{"abstract":"In large venues like shopping malls and airports, knowledge on the indoor populations fuels applications such as business analytics, venue management, and safety control. In this work, we provide means of modeling populations in partitions of indoor space offline and of monitoring indoor populations continuously, by using indoor positioning data. However, the low-sampling rates of indoor positioning render the data temporally and spatially sparse, which in turn renders the offline capture of indoor populations challenging. It is even more challenging to continuously monitor indoor populations, as positioning data may be missing or not ready yet at the current moment. To address these challenges, we first enable probabilistic modeling of populations in indoor space partitions as Normal distributions. Based on that, we propose two learning-based estimators for on-the-fly prediction of population distributions. Leveraging the prediction-based schemes, we provide a unified continuous query processing framework for a type of query that enables continuous monitoring of populated partitions. The framework encompasses caching and result validity mechanisms to reduce cost and maintain monitoring effectiveness. Extensive experiments on two real data sets show that the proposed estimators are able to outperform the state-of-the-art alternatives and that the query processing framework is effective and efficient.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Li, Xiao","Li, Huan","Lu, Hua","Jensen, Christian S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782505"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Indoor positioning data","Uncertainty"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and monitoring of indoor populations using sparse positioning data","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/107443356/CMPP_TKDE_Nov_2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782505","identifier":[{"id":"85208382036","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-69668b1e-6523-49bc-a7aa-74a2f0c64ad7"],"keyword":["Indoor population","indoor positioning data","uncertainty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF126DFF611F8059057C2386129090E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/107443356/CMPP_TKDE_Nov_2024.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Programming, Logic and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Xiao","key":"lixiaopau","last":"Li","locid":"8b86b24d-5f2f-42ea-84c1-ce252da514d9","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Huan","key":"lihuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Huan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Hua","key":"luhuapau","last":"Lu","locid":"23598038-5481-490e-961c-2c4af8e04f5d","name":"Lu, Hua","orcid":"0000-0003-1199-6678","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christian S.","key":"jensenchristianspau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Christian S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tkde.2024.3489796","issn":["10414347","15582191"],"issn_org":["10414347"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering","pages":"794-809","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Knowledge and Data Engineering","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208382036"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-69668b1e-6523-49bc-a7aa-74a2f0c64ad7"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Modeling and Monitoring of Indoor Populations using Sparse Positioning Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782505","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Conventional fundamental frequency zero-sequence voltage (FFZSV) injection-based fault-tolerant operation methods cause power reversion under submodule (SM) failure conditions with low-power factor, which leads to overcharge risk in the cascaded H-bridge converter-based battery energy storage system (CHB-BESS). To solve this issue, a novel fault-tolerant operation approach has been proposed for the CHB-BESS. First, the power reversion mechanism and overcharge risk are analyzed with the conventional FFZSV injection-based methods. On this basis, the operation conditions of the CHB-BESS are divided into three stages according to the safe FFZSV injection region, the FFZSV is modified, and the negative sequence current is injected when necessary. As a result, the power flow of battery packs among the three phases can maintain the same direction, and the power reversion and overcharge risk can be avoided. Experimental results under various conditions verify that the proposed fault-tolerant operation approach of the CHB-BESS can achieve uninterrupted operation and avoid overcharge risk.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Xiao, Qian","Yu, Haolin","Jin, Yu","Jia, Hongjie","Mu, Yunfei","Liu, Huiqiao","Li, Wenhua","Teodorescu, Remus","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786020"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Jin, Yu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hebei University of Technology","The State Key Laboratory of Reliability and Intelligence of Electrical Equipment","Tianjin University"],"keyword":["Battery energy storage system BESS","Cascaded H bridge CHB","Fault tolerant operation","submodule SM failure"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel fault tolerant operation approach for cascaded h bridge converter based battery energy storage systems to avoid overcharge","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85207351100&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported in part by the National Natural Science Foundation of China under Grant 52477117, Grant 52107121, Grant 52407135, Grant 52222704, and Grant U2066213; in part by the State Key Laboratory of Reliability and Intelligence of Electrical Equipment, Hebei University of Technology under Grant EERI_KF2021008; in part by the Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation under Grant 2022A1515240047; in part by the Youth Talent Program of the China Association for Science and Technology under Grant XMSB20240711043; in part by the China Postdoctoral Science Foundation under Grant 2023TQ0242; and in part by the Tianjin Enterprise Science and Technology Commissioner Project under Grant 23YDTPJC00090. Received 17 April 2024; revised 7 August 2024 and 9 September 2024; accepted 8 October 2024. This work was supported in part by the National Natural Science Foundation of China under Grant 52477117, Grant 52107121, Grant 52407135, Grant 52222704, and Grant U2066213; in part by the State Key Laboratory of Reliability and Intelligence of Electrical Equipment, Hebei University of Technology under Grant EERI_KF2021008; in part by the Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation under Grant 2022A1515240047; in part by the Youth Talent Program of the China Association for Science and Technology under Grant XMSB20240711043; in part by the China Postdoctoral Science Foundation under Grant 2023TQ0242; and in part by the Tianjin Enterprise Science and Technology Commissioner Project under Grant 23YDTPJC00090. (Corresponding author: Yu Jin.) Qian Xiao is with the Key Laboratory of Smart Grid of Ministry of Education, Tianjin University, Tianjin 300072, China, and also with the State Key Laboratory of Reliability and Intelligence of Electrical Equipment, Hebei University of Technology, Tianjin 300401, China (e-mail: xiaoqian@tju. edu.cn)."],"id":"S01-000.00-786020","identifier":[{"id":"85207351100","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7eaca766-68ce-474f-9753-d0f647fff06e"],"keyword":["Battery energy storage system (BESS)","cascaded H-bridge (CHB)","fault-tolerant operation","submodule (SM) failure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC698164D3B5B96B8E96492A867D12EA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tianjin university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"the state key laboratory of reliability and intelligence of electrical equipment","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"The State Key Laboratory of Reliability and Intelligence of Electrical Equipment","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"hebei university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hebei University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Batteries","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Center for Research on Smart Battery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Photovoltaic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronics System Integration and Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Qian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Haolin","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Haolin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"jinpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Yu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongjie","key":"jiapau","last":"Jia","name":"Jia, Hongjie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunfei","key":"mupau","last":"Mu","name":"Mu, Yunfei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huiqiao","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Huiqiao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenhua","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wenhua","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescupau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tie.2024.3485716","issn":["02780046","15579948"],"issn_org":["02780046"],"issue":"6","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","pages":"5497-5506","publisher":"IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207351100"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7eaca766-68ce-474f-9753-d0f647fff06e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Novel Fault-Tolerant Operation Approach for Cascaded H-Bridge Converter-Based Battery Energy Storage Systems to Avoid Overcharge","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786020","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Virtual power plant (VPP) serves as an effective solution for maintaining internal power balance and participating in external peak shaving auxiliary services within grid-connected microgrid involved in multi-type flexible resources (FRs). However, with increasing prominence of the feature heterogeneity in response behaviors of diverse FRs and their coupling in peak shaving poses challenges in the accurate decomposition of VPP scheduling commands. This paper proposes a de-aggregation strategy, utilizing discrete choice model and feature matching methods, to dynamically sequence FRs responses while optimizing VPP's peak shaving capability. Initially, heterogeneous features are refined and modeled to characterize the response capability of multi-type FRs in meeting the scheduled demand of grid-connected microgrid (SDGM). Subsequently, a feature difference quantification model and matching priority criterion are formulated to describe the feature mapping relationship and guide dynamic decision-making process. On this basis, the multi-type FRs are co-scheduled in the considered VPP to form a dynamic response sequence achieving peak shaving objectives. Case studies based on real data from a region-connected microgrid demonstrate the proposed strategy's performance in improving return on investment by 6.1 %, reducing peak shaving deviation and power exchange with main grid by 70 % and 13.1 %, respectively, and effectively improve the ability of grid-connected microgrid to balance the power and participate in peaking auxiliary services.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Zheng, Zixuan","Li, Jie","Liu, Xiaoming","Huang, Chunjun","Hu, Wenxi","Xiao, Xianyong","Zhang, Shu","Zhou, Yongjun","Yue, Song","Zong, Yi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798178"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hu, Wenxi"],"country":["China","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Sichuan University","State Grid Tibet Electric Power Company, Co. Ltd."],"keyword":["Discrete choice model","Feature matching","Virtual power plant"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a de aggregation strategy based optimal co scheduling of heterogeneous flexible resources in virtual power plant","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85215832836","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798178","identifier":[{"id":"85215832836","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8b53b712-da16-4ef7-9553-6178631c24e6"],"keyword":["Discrete choice model","Feature matching","Flexible resources","VPP de-aggregation","Virtual power plant"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2EC0AA0835FA2B3B14EE2A0E803AF805"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state grid tibet electric power company co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Grid Tibet Electric Power Company, Co. Ltd.","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind and Energy Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind and Energy Systems, Power and Energy Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind and Energy Systems, Power and Energy Systems, Power-to-X and Storage"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zixuan","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Zixuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoming","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xiaoming","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chunjun","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Chunjun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenxi","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Wenxi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianyong","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xianyong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shu","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Shu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongjun","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yongjun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Song","key":"yuepau","last":"Yue","name":"Yue, Song","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yi","key":"zongpau","last":"Zong","locid":"3063028d-1dc8-4394-8afb-e1b09eb39672","name":"Zong, Yi","orcid":"0000-0003-1262-3558","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2025.125404","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","paperid":"125404","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"383"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215832836"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8b53b712-da16-4ef7-9553-6178631c24e6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A De-aggregation strategy based optimal co-scheduling of heterogeneous flexible resources in virtual power plant","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798178","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"哺乳动物的气味腺体分泌的化学信号对物种之间特异性交流至关重要,但趋同的麝香合成机制仍未完全理解。有趣的是，林麝和麝鼠都独立进化出了能够产生麝香化合物的香腺，代表了一个典型的趋同进化案例。通过整合多组学方法，我们发现两个物种的麝香中都含有重要的前体物质—环十五酮，同时在下游代谢物中表现出物种特异性的差异。单细胞RNA测序揭示这些特化顶浆分泌腺体具有独特的分泌结构，并表现出与周期性麝香产生相关的转录谱，这与常规顶浆腺体不同。这种趋同性延伸到细胞水平，在关键的上皮细胞亚型（腺泡细胞、导管细胞和基底细胞）中观显示出平行的分子特征。值得注意的是，两个物种的腺泡细胞都表达参与脂肪酸和甘油脂代谢的共同基因（如 ACSBG1、 HSD17B12、 HACD2、 HADHA），表明麝香前体物质生物合成具有保守的分子框架。对麝香样本的宏基因组分析进一步揭示了由棒状杆菌主导并富含脂质代谢通路的平行微生物群落结构。这些发现表明麝香生物合成在多个层面上存在趋同，从分子通路到微生物群落，为哺乳动物化学信号研究和人工麝香生产提供了新见解。.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Sun, Yi Shan","Zhao, Lei","Zheng, Cheng Li","Yan, Xiao Ting","Li, Ye","Gao, Xue Li","Xue, Ting Feng","Zhang, Yi Ming","Li, Zhi Peng","Heller, Rasmus","Feng, Chen Guang","Xu, Chao","Wang, Kun","Qiu, Qiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809017"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jilin Agricultural University","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","Sichuan Institute for Drug Control"],"keyword":["Convergence","Microbiota","Multi omics approach"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"convergent musk biosynthesis across host and microbiota in musk deer and muskrat","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24272/j.issn.2095-8137.2025.094","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809017","identifier":[{"id":"40259731","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003896602","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-06c43f98-2d7f-4845-b8ce-63f76c53b151"],"keyword":["Convergence","Microbiota","Multi-omics approach","Musk biosynthesis","Musk gland"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-78C22EDC7AE7A2850DF4A276198798A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24272/j.issn.2095-8137.2025.094","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/449940756/Convergent_musk_biosynthesis_across_host_and_microbiota_in_musk_deer_and_muskrat.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northwestern polytechnical university xian","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"sichuan institute for drug control","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan Institute for Drug Control","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jilin agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jilin Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yi Shan","key":"sunyishanpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yi Shan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"zhaoleipau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Lei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Cheng Li","key":"zhengchenglipau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Cheng Li","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Ting","key":"yanxiaotingpau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Xiao Ting","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ye","key":"liyepau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ye","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xue Li","key":"gaoxuelipau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Xue Li","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ting Feng","key":"xuetingfengpau","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Ting Feng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yi Ming","key":"zhangyimingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yi Ming","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Zhi Peng","key":"lizhipengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhi Peng","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Rasmus","key":"hellerrasmuspau","last":"Heller","locid":"efbe80a4-e869-43e8-b962-989c40c79f93","name":"Heller, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-6583-6923","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chen Guang","key":"fengchenguangpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Chen Guang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Chao","key":"xuchaopau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Chao","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kun","key":"wangkunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Kun","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Qiang","key":"qiuqiangpau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, Qiang","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40259731"],"pub":{"doi":"10.24272/j.issn.2095-8137.2025.094","issn":["20958137"],"issue":"3","journal":"Zoological research","pages":"505-517","status":"p","title":"Zoological research","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003896602"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-06c43f98-2d7f-4845-b8ce-63f76c53b151"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Convergent musk biosynthesis across host and microbiota in musk deer and muskrat","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809017","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Importance: The relationship between butter and plant-based oil intakes and mortality remains unclear, with conflicting results from previous studies. Long-term dietary assessments are needed to clarify these associations. Objective: To investigate associations of butter and plant-based oil intakes with risk of total and cause-specific mortality among US adults. Design, Setting, and Participants: This prospective population-based cohort study used data from 3 large cohorts: the Nurses' Health Study (1990-2023), the Nurses' Health Study II (1991-2023), and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (1990-2023). Women and men who were free of cancer, cardiovascular disease (CVD), diabetes, or neurodegenerative disease at baseline were included. Exposures: Primary exposures included intakes of butter (butter added at the table and from cooking) and plant-based oil (safflower, soybean, corn, canola, and olive oil). Diet was assessed by validated semiquantitative food frequency questionnaires every 4 years. Main Outcomes and Measures: Total mortality was the primary outcome, and mortality due to cancer and CVD were secondary outcomes. Deaths were identified through the National Death Index and other sources. A physician classified the cause of death based on death certificates and medical records. Results: During up to 33 years of follow-up among 221054 adults (mean [SD] age at baseline: 56.1 [7.1] years for Nurses' Health Study, 36.1 [4.7] years for Nurses' Health Study II, and 56.3 [9.3] years for Health Professionals Follow-up Study), 50932 deaths were documented, with 12241 due to cancer and 11240 due to CVD. Participants were categorized into quartiles based on their butter or plant-based oil intake. After adjusting for potential confounders, the highest butter intake was associated with a 15% higher risk of total mortality compared to the lowest intake (hazard ratio [HR], 1.15; 95% CI, 1.08-1.22; P for trend <.001). In contrast, the highest intake of total plant-based oils compared to the lowest intake was associated with a 16% lower total mortality (HR, 0.84; 95% CI, 0.79-0.90; P for trend <.001). There was a statistically significant association between higher intakes of canola, soybean, and olive oils and lower total mortality, with HRs per 5-g/d increment of 0.85 (95% CI, 0.78-0.92), 0.94 (95% CI, 0.91-0.96), and 0.92 (95% CI, 0.91-0.94), respectively (all P for trend <.001). Every 10-g/d increment in plant-based oils intake was associated with an 11% lower risk of cancer mortality (HR, 0.89; 95% CI, 0.85-0.94; P for trend <.001) and a 6% lower risk of CVD mortality (HR, 0.94; 95% CI, 0.89-0.99; P for trend =.03), whereas a higher intake of butter was associated with higher cancer mortality (HR, 1.12; 95% CI, 1.04-1.20; P for trend <.001). Substituting 10-g/d intake of total butter with an equivalent amount of total plant-based oils was associated with an estimated 17% reduction in total mortality (HR, 0.83; 95% CI, 0.79-0.86; P <.001) and a 17% reduction in cancer mortality (HR, 0.83; 95% CI, 0.76-0.90; P <.001). Conclusions and Relevance: In this cohort study, higher intake of butter was associated with increased mortality, while higher plant-based oils intake was associated with lower mortality. Substituting butter with plant-based oils may confer substantial benefits for preventing premature deaths.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Zhang, Yu","Chadaideh, Katia S.","Li, Yanping","Li, Yuhan","Gu, Xiao","Liu, Yuxi","Guasch-Ferré, Marta","Rimm, Eric B.","Hu, Frank B.","Willett, Walter C.","Stampfer, Meir J.","Wang, Dong D."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818633"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Veterans Affairs","Harvard University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["D