ltural Ecology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Crop Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xiangnan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiangnan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Fulai","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"dc299ce8-5a4c-46f4-9af0-4d935f7cf190","name":"Liu, Fulai","orcid":"0000-0002-5006-8965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dong","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Dong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jia.2025.05.026","issn":["20953119"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Integrative Agriculture","pages":"2885-2887","status":"p","title":"Journal of Integrative Agriculture","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012094823"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c59db15f-547b-4b8d-b627-ce084d82fa06"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Innovative pathways to sustainable wheat production","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829838","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The widespread use of plasticizers like phthalate esters (PAEs) has led to environmental and health concerns. The neurobehavioral toxicity of these compounds in marine environments, particularly regulated by the “brain-gut” axis, remains unclear, especially concerning wild demersal fish of high ecological value. Our investigation into the behavioral effects of three common PAEs, i.e., dimethyl phthalate (DMP), di-n-butyl phthalate (DBP), and di(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate (DEHP), and their molecular mechanisms on juvenile Sebastes schlegelii, revealed alarming results from molecular to population levels. After a 20-day foodborne exposure at a low marine environmental concentration (1.0 μg g −1), we observed that all three PAEs significantly increased the thigmotaxis (behavioral tendency to stay close to physical boundaries) and mobility of juvenile fish by 28.2–59.4 % and 23.3–74.5 %, respectively, indicating anxiety-like behavior of fish. DEHP exhibited the most pronounced effects, followed by DBP and DMP. PAEs accumulated in the juvenile fish in the order of brain > liver > gut > muscle, with DEHP showing the highest brain concentrations (23.2 ± 2.98 μg g −1). This accumulation led to oxidative damage, inflammatory responses, and neurodegenerative changes in the optic tectum, resulting in cholinergic system dysfunction. In the gut, PAEs caused inflammatory lesions, disrupted the gut barrier, and altered the gut microbiome, exacerbating the neurotoxicity via “brain-gut” communication. These findings underscore the significant neurobehavioral toxicity of PAEs, emphasizing their critical impact on fish behavior. We also stress the crucial need for further research on fish and other marine species beyond the laboratory scale to fully understand the broader implications of PAE exposure in marine ecosystems and to guide future conservation efforts.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Liu, Liuqingqing","Li, Xinyao","Luo, Xianxiang","Wang, Xiao","Liu, Linjia","Yuan, Zixi","Sun, Cuizhu","Zheng, Hao","Xu, Elvis Genbo","Li, Fengmin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-791972"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Luo, Xianxiang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ocean University of China"],"keyword":["Behavioral ecology","Brain gut axis","Endocrine disrupting chemicals","Gut microbiome","Neurotoxicity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phthalates esters disrupt demersal fish behavior unveiling the brain gut axis impact","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoenv.2024.117470","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-791972","identifier":[{"id":"39647374","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85211151648","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-87a22f8e-e917-474e-a7ec-1627678db3f0"],"keyword":["Anxiety behavior","Behavioral ecology","Brain-gut axis","Endocrine disrupting chemicals","Gut microbiome","Neurotoxicity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D7FD55088D6AF91B3DA66150CA1DA27C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoenv.2024.117470","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/281036269/1-s2.0-S014765132401546X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"ocean university of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ocean University of China","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liuqingqing","key":"liuliuqingqingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Liuqingqing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinyao","key":"lixinyaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xinyao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianxiang","key":"luoxianxiangpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Xianxiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"wangxiaopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Linjia","key":"liulinjiapau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Linjia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zixi","key":"yuanzixipau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Zixi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cuizhu","key":"suncuizhupau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Cuizhu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao","key":"zhenghaopau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Hao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elvis Genbo","key":"xuelvisgenbopau","last":"Xu","locid":"6d6ca13b-421e-4ab9-a6ce-df92da56c683","name":"Xu, Elvis Genbo","orcid":"0000-0002-4414-1978","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengmin","key":"lifengminpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Fengmin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39647374"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ecoenv.2024.117470","issn":["01476513","10902414"],"issn_org":["01476513"],"journal":"Ecotoxicology and Environmental Safety","paperid":"117470","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Ecotoxicology and Environmental Safety","volume":"289"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211151648"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-87a22f8e-e917-474e-a7ec-1627678db3f0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Phthalates esters disrupt demersal fish behavior: Unveiling the brain-gut axis impact","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-791972","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"High-frequency and high-precision dissolved oxygen (DO) monitoring is essential for lake health assessment, but it is limited by equipment and methods. This study developed a novel ground-based hyperspectral proximal sensing system (GHPSs) combined with machine learning methods for continuous monitoring of DO with an observation interval of 20 s. Five machine learning and deep learning models were calibrated and validated to estimate DO based on four combination scenarios of the GHPSs reflectance of 420-830 nm, chlorophyll-a (Chl-a), and water temperature (WTR). The results showed that a support vector machine model was preferred for DO estimation with satisfactory accuracy (R2 = 0.84, mean absolute percentage error = 0.12, and root mean square error = 1.15 mg/L) based on 11,131 in situ measurements. Multitemporal changes of DO concentration in Lake Taihu were obtained from October 2021 to December 2023 by applying the model, which suggested that the surface of Lake Taihu was hypoxic in 2.1% out of 754 days. Finally, the potential significance of monitoring real-time DO dynamics was elaborated under global warming. This study highlights the effectiveness, accuracy, and high frequency of novel GHPSs in real-time DO monitoring, which is crucial for predicting and early warning of lake pollution.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Luo, Xiayang","Li, Na","Zhang, Yunlin","Zhang, Yibo","Shi, Kun","Qin, Boqiang","Zhu, Guangwei","Jeppesen, Erik","Brookes, Justin D.","Sun, Xiao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-795569"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Na","Zhang, Yunlin"],"country":["Australia","China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","Liaocheng University","Middle East Technical University","University of Adelaide","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Dissolved oxygen","Lake Taihu","Machine learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real time monitoring of dissolved oxygen using a novel ground based hyperspectral proximal sensing system","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85214337222","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-795569","identifier":[{"id":"85214337222","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0a18d9d7-759f-4f7f-8342-0e1b9533cbcc"],"keyword":["Lake Taihu","dissolved oxygen","ground-based hyperspectral proximal sensing","machine learning","multitemporal dynamics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4F7F0CFD021D7CE1432852191F9F2D07"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas nanjing institute of geography and limnology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"au","key":"university of adelaide","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Adelaide","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"liaocheng university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Liaocheng University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiayang","key":"luoxiayangpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Xiayang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Na","key":"linapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Na","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunlin","key":"zhangyunlinpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yunlin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yibo","key":"zhangyibopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yibo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kun","key":"shikunpau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Kun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Boqiang","key":"qinboqiangpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Boqiang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guangwei","key":"zhuguangweipau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Guangwei","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Justin D.","key":"brookesjustindpau","last":"Brookes","name":"Brookes, Justin D.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"sunxiaopau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Xiao","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsestwater.4c00896","issn":["26900637"],"issue":"2","journal":"ACS ES and T Water","pages":"825-837","publisher":"AMER CHEMICAL SOC","status":"p","title":"ACS ES and T Water","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214337222"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0a18d9d7-759f-4f7f-8342-0e1b9533cbcc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Real-Time Monitoring of Dissolved Oxygen Using a Novel Ground-Based Hyperspectral Proximal Sensing System","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-795569","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This study presents an experimental investigation on the feasibility of adopting micro-cellulose fiber as not only internal curing but also micro-reinforcement agents for high-performance cement composites (HPCs). The effect of micro-cellulose fiber on the ballistic impact resistance, in terms of penetration depth, crater diameter, volume, profile and cracking pattern, as well as physical, mechanical and shrinkage properties is explored. It was found that the incorporation of micro-cellulose fiber in HPCs leads to a significant decrease of the penetration depth (13.6 %), crater diameter and volume (27.6 %). The autogenous and drying shrinkage of HPCs at various ages up to 91 days are significantly reduced due to the addition of micro-cellulose fiber. Furthermore, incorporating micro-cellulose fiber does not have a significant effect on the early-age compressive and flexural strengths, but increases the late-age compressive and flexural strengths. With the aid of micro-cellulose fiber, HPCs with excellent ballistic impact resistance and volume stability can be successfully fabricated. The results of this study contribute towards the implementation of HPCs in in-situ application for protective structures where autogenous shrinkage and related cracking are highly problematic.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Fengling","Pang, Kai","Li, Jinglong","Xu, Wenlong","Du, Junjie","Wang, Jialiang","Zhang, Jie","Liu, Qifang","Xiao, Huigang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-796312"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Fengling"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harbin Institute of Technology","Shandong University","Taiyuan University of Technology"],"keyword":["Autogenous shrinkage","High performance concrete","Internal curing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of micro cellulose fiber on the mechanical shrinkage properties and ballistic impact resistance of high performance cement composites","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85215827875","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-796312","identifier":[{"id":"85215827875","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6462174e-58fc-4afa-9202-88e36cca6415"],"keyword":["Autogenous shrinkage","Cellulose fiber","High performance concrete","Internal curing","Projectile impact"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2B8168FDBEF70118247B06C532DFF26C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Civil and Architectural Engineering, Department of Civil and Architectural Engineering - Structural Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"taiyuan university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Taiyuan University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengling","key":"zhangfenglingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Fengling","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai","key":"pangkaipau","last":"Pang","name":"Pang, Kai","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinglong","key":"lijinglongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jinglong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenlong","key":"xuwenlongpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Wenlong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Junjie","key":"dujunjiepau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Junjie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jialiang","key":"wangjialiangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"d87a997f-978c-47e5-be94-6a39eb84cfb5","name":"Wang, Jialiang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"zhangjiepau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qifang","key":"liuqifangpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Qifang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Huigang","key":"xiaohuigangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Huigang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.conbuildmat.2025.139963","issn":["09500618"],"journal":"Construction and Building Materials","paperid":"139963","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Construction and Building Materials","volume":"463"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85215827875"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6462174e-58fc-4afa-9202-88e36cca6415"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effect of micro-cellulose fiber on the mechanical, shrinkage properties and ballistic impact resistance of high-performance cement composites","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-796312","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Enzymatic biofuel cells are energy conversion devices utilizing biocatalysts to directly convert chemical energy to electricity. Due to their biocompatible, sustainable and maintenance-free properties, they hold the promise as attractive energy sources for powering next generation medical electronics for personalized healthcare. Low current and power output are main bottlenecks of enzymatic biofuel cells to hinder their practical applications. Supercapacitors are able to harness ambitious energy and deliver high-power pulses. Combining enzymatic biofuel cells with supercapacitors to establish self-charging energy-conversion/energy-storage hybrid systems are considered as an effective strategy to improve the current and power output. This design enables the hybrid electric devices to scavenge ambient energy and simultaneously store it and thus increases the efficiency and facilitates the miniaturization for practical application. In this review, we first discuss various structural configurations of these self-charging hybrid systems, and then focus on explaining their charge storage mechanisms, including electrochemical double-layer capacitance, pseudocapacitance and hybrids. Several proof-of-concept applications as implantable and wearable power sources are enumerated. Finally, we provide an overview of challenges and opportunities for research and development of self-charging hybrid devices.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Shen, Fei","Xiao, Xinxin","Dai, Qiming","Li, Hailin","Zhang, Xinyang","Huang, Kang","Zhou, Yuanbo","Xue, Songlin","Zhao, Xiaohui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-804887"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xue, Songlin","Zhao, Xiaohui"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangsu University","Soochow University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combining enzymatic biofuel cells with supercapacitors to self charging hybrid devices","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=105002168981&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was financially supported by QINGLAN Project of Jiangsu Province of China, National Natural Science Foundation of China (22301108), Pre-research project of Suzhou City University (2022SGY007), International Talent Cultivation Brand Program in New Energy Materials and Devices of Suzhou City University and Suzhou Basic Research Project (SJC2023003), National College Students\\u2032 Innovation and Entrepreneurship Training Program (202413983023Z, 202413983016), Jiangsu Provincial College Students\\u2032 Innovation and Entrepreneurship Training Program (202413983085Y) and Novo Nordisk Foundation Start Package grant (0081331). This work was financially supported by QINGLAN Project of Jiangsu Province of China, National Natural Science Foundation of China (22301108), Pre\\u2010research project of Suzhou City University (2022SGY007), International Talent Cultivation Brand Program in New Energy Materials and Devices of Suzhou City University and Suzhou Basic Research Project (SJC2023003), National College Students\\u2032 Innovation and Entrepreneurship Training Program (202413983023Z, 202413983016), Jiangsu Provincial College Students\\u2032 Innovation and Entrepreneurship Training Program (202413983085Y) and Novo Nordisk Foundation Start Package grant (0081331)."],"id":"S01-000.00-804887","identifier":[{"id":"105002168981","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3e19c34f-dc90-4f43-9259-8e3e90ec8ebc"],"keyword":["Biosupercapacitors","Enzymatic biofuel cells","Implantable power supply","Wearable application"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CF4880E39206D9130D775B62ED0F999B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-04-08","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"soochow university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Soochow University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, [Mission] A Sustainable Danish Energy System"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jiangsu university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangsu University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fei","key":"shenpau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Fei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"fd69114c-9434-44ba-b01b-e9ecb3831cae","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiming","key":"daipau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Qiming","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hailin","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hailin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinyang","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xinyang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kang","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Kang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuanbo","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yuanbo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Songlin","key":"xuepau","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Songlin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaohui","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Xiaohui","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/tcr.202400248","issn":["15278999","15280691"],"issn_org":["15278999"],"issue":"5","journal":"Chemical Record","paperid":"e202400248","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Chemical Record","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002168981"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3e19c34f-dc90-4f43-9259-8e3e90ec8ebc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Combining enzymatic biofuel cells with supercapacitors to self-charging hybrid devices","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-804887","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Nicotiana tabacum is an allotetraploid hybrid of Nicotiana sylvestris and Nicotiana tomentosiformis and a model organism in genetics. However, features of subgenome evolution, expression coordination, genetic diversity and complex traits regulation of N. tabacum remain unresolved. Here we present chromosome-scale assemblies for all three species, and genotype and phenotypic data for 5,196 N. tabacum germplasms. Chromosome rearrangements and epigenetic modifications are associated with genome evolution and expression coordination following polyploidization. Two subgenomes and genes biased toward one subgenome contributed unevenly to complex trait variation. Using 178 marker–trait associations, a reference genotype-to-phenotype map was built for 39 morphological, developmental and disease resistance traits, and a novel gene regulating leaf width was validated. Signatures of positive and polygenic selection during the process of selective breeding were detected. Our study provides insights into genome evolution, complex traits regulation in allotetraploid N. tabacum and the use of GeneBank-scale resources for advancing genetic and genomic research.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Zan, Yanjun","Chen, Shuai","Ren, Min","Liu, Guoxiang","Liu, Yutong","Han, Yu","Dong, Yang","Zhang, Yao","Si, Huan","Liu, Zhengwen","Liu, Dan","Zhang, Xingwei","Tong, Ying","Li, Yuan","Jiang, Caihong","Wen, Liuying","Xiao, Zhiliang","Sun, Yangyang","Geng, Ruimei","Ji, Yan","Feng, Quanfu","Wang, Yuanying","Ye, Guoyou","Fang, Lingzhao","Chen, Yong","Cheng, Lirui","Yang, Aiguo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806207"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Yong","Cheng, Lirui","Yang, Aiguo","Zan, Yanjun"],"country":["China","Philippines","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Institutes of Life Science","CAS - 