{"abstract":"This letter has developed an electrical circuit analogy-based maximum latency calculation (MLC) method of the internet data center (IDC) in power-communication network. Firstly, by analogy with the circuit model, the basic concepts to describe information flow are defined, including information current, information resistance, information conductivity, and information voltage. Based on these concepts, the information processing model considering both channel blocking and user priority is established. By analogy with the electrical circuit, the information flow calculation laws are introduced to calculate the maximum latency of IDCs. Verification results show that the maximum latency of IDCs in power-communication network can be accurately calculated by the proposed MLC method.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Xiao, Qian","Li, Tianxiang","Jia, Hongjie","Mu, Yunfei","Jin, Yu","Qiao, Ji","Pu, Tianjiao","Blaabjerg, Frede","Guerrero, Josep M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786157"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Tianxiang"],"country":["China","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Electric Power Research Institute","Polytechnic University of Catalonia","Tianjin University","Tsinghua University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrical circuit analogy based maximum latency calculation method of internet data centers in power communication network","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85207358709&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported in part by the National Natural Science Foundation of China under Grant U2066213, Grant 52477117, Grant 52107121, Grant 52407135, and Grant 52222704; in part by the Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation under Grant 2022A1515240047; in part by the State Key Laboratory of Power System Operation and Control under Grant SKLD23KZ04; in part by the Youth Talent Program of the China Association for Science and Technology under Grant XMSB20240711043; in part by the China Postdoctoral Science Foundation under Grant 2023TQ0242; and in part by the Tianjin Enterprise Science and Technology Commissioner Project under Grant 23YDTPJC00090. This work was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (No. U2066213, 52477117, 52107121, 52407135, 52222704), Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation (No. 2022A1515240047), State Key Laboratory of Power System Operation and Control(No.SKLD23KZ04),YouthTalentProgramoftheChinaAssociation for Science and Technology (No. XMSB20240711043), China Postdoctoral Science Foundation (No. 2023TQ0242), and Tianjin Enterprise Science and TechnologyCommissionerProject(No.23YDTPJC00090).Paperno.PESL-00104-2024.(Correspondingauthor:TianxiangLi.) QianXiaoiswiththeKeyLaboratoryofSmartGridofTianjin University and also with the State Key Laboratory of Power System Operation and Control of Tsinghua University. Tianxiang Li, Hongjie Jia, Yunfei Mu, and Yu Jin are with the Key Laboratory of Smart Grid of Tianjin University. Ji Qiao and Tianjiao Pu are with the China Electric Power Research Institute. FredeBlaabjergiswiththeAalborgUniversity.JosepM.Guerreroiswiththe TechnicalUniversityofCatalonia.(e-mail:txl@tju.edu.cn)"],"id":"S01-000.00-786157","identifier":[{"id":"85207358709","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a1ec5d4d-86f9-46bc-8175-4af185e4b783"],"keyword":["Internet data centers","electrical circuit analogy-based model","maximum latency","power-communication network"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4527FCF2434B99CACE13027A0ED54919"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tianjin university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"china electric power research institute","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Electric Power Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Applied Power Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, E-Mobility and Drives","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, EMI/EMC in Power Electronics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Photovoltaic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Control, Reliability and System Optimization","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Wind Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"polytechnic university of catalonia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Catalonia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Qian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianxiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Tianxiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongjie","key":"jiapau","last":"Jia","name":"Jia, Hongjie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunfei","key":"mupau","last":"Mu","name":"Mu, Yunfei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"jinpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Yu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ji","key":"qiaopau","last":"Qiao","name":"Qiao, Ji","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianjiao","key":"pupau","last":"Pu","name":"Pu, Tianjiao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tsg.2024.3478844","issn":["19493053"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Smart Grid","pages":"449-452","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Smart Grid","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207358709"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a1ec5d4d-86f9-46bc-8175-4af185e4b783"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Electrical Circuit Analogy-Based Maximum Latency Calculation Method of Internet Data Centers in Power-Communication Network","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786157","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Mantle peridotites and pyroxenites from arc crust root record vital information about petrogenetic processes in supra–subduction environments, which are commonly obscured by subsequent metamorphic and/or metasomatic overprints. The Heigou Complex from the western Central Qilian arc root (NE Tibet, China) includes peridotites and pyroxenites. Petrography, bulk–rock and mineral geochemistry, zircon and titanite U–Pb ages, and bulk–rock Sr–Nd–Hf isotopes are presented to decipher its petrogenetic and metasomatic history. The peridotites display highly refractory compositions of low SiO2, Al2O3, CaO, but high MgO contents. Geochemical modeling indicates that these are the residues after up to ~22% melt extraction. The geochemical and isotopic data (87Sr/86Sr i = 0.7116–0.7179, εNd(t) = −4.2 to −7.1 and εHf(t) = −5.3 to −5.4) suggest the pyroxenitic protoliths were derived from a subduction-metasomatized mantle source. Combining petrographic and fractional crystallization simulation, the pyroxenites formed as cumulates through 50% to 80% differentiation of primitive basaltic magma in the arc root at ca. 523 Ma. Elevated LILEs (Rb, Sr, Pb, etc.) and LREE in bulk-rock and mineral compositions, together with microstructure evidence, suggest that mantle peridotite experienced mantle metasomatism. Subsequent hydrous melt (fluid) metasomatism during exhumation then reacted with the preexisting clinopyroxenite, leading to local Mg-hornblende, titanite and epidote formation. The timing of retrograde melt infiltration is constrained by a titanite U–Pb crystallization age of ca. 485 Ma. The combined evidence reveals a picture of continental arc magmatism and metasomatism at arc crust roots. Dehydration of the Proto-Tethys oceanic slab could induce flux melting in the mantle wedge that had undergone metasomatism, resulting in the generation of hydrous arc magmas. These arc magmas intruded the overlying lithospheric mantle, segregating pyroxenite cumulates. The ultramafic rocks at the arc crust root were subsequently modified by hydrous melt (fluid).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Sun, Xiao Kui","Wang, Chao","Scott, James M.","Liu, Liang","Yu, Zun Pu","Yang, Wen Qiang","Li, Hang","Liu, Ke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797072"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northwest University China"],"keyword":["Metasomatism","Pyroxenite"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tracking magmatism and metasomatism in continental arc crust root significance from western central qilian belt in ne tibet china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85217760043","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-797072","identifier":[{"id":"85217760043","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c9c64faf-7e08-489d-acd1-63489012e9b7"],"keyword":["Central Qilian belt","Heigou complex","continental arc crust root","metasomatism","pyroxenite"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8CBE9E39A1B795EF23D67A26FE25C992"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northwest university china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest University China","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Kui","key":"sunxiaokuipau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Xiao Kui","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Chao","key":"wangchaopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"James","key":"scottjamesmpau","last":"Scott","locid":"854d453b-009a-4ac6-8d6c-b33db9e95c24","name":"Scott, James M.","name_org":"Scott, James","orcid":"0000-0001-5185-6261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liang","key":"liuliangpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Liang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zun Pu","key":"yuzunpupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Zun Pu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen Qiang","key":"yangwenqiangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Wen Qiang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hang","key":"lihangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"liukepau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Ke","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/petrology/egaf006","issn":["00223530","14602415"],"issn_org":["00223530"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Petrology","paperid":"egaf006","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Petrology","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217760043"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c9c64faf-7e08-489d-acd1-63489012e9b7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tracking Magmatism and Metasomatism in Continental Arc Crust Root : Significance from Western Central Qilian Belt in NE Tibet, China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797072","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Trophic interactions in micro-food webs, such as those between nematodes and their bacterial prey, affect nitrogen cycling in soils, potentially changing nitrous oxide (N2O) production and consumption. However, how nematode-mediated changes in soil bacterial community composition affect soil N2O emissions is largely unknown. Here, microcosm experiments are performed with the bacterial feeding nematode Protorhabditis to explore the potential of nematodes in regulating microbial communities and thereby soil N2O emissions. Removal of nematodes by defaunation resulted in increased N2O emissions, with the removal of Protorhabditis contributing most to this increase. Further, inoculation with Protorhabditis altered bacterial community composition and increased the relative abundance of Bacillus, and the abundance of the nosZ gene in soil. In vitro experiments indicated that Protorhabditis reinforce the reduction in N2O emissions by Bacillus due to suppressing competitors and producing bacteria growth stimulating substances such as betaine. The results indicate that interactions between nematodes and bacteria modify N2O emissions providing the perspective for the mitigation of greenhouse gas emissions via manipulating trophic interactions in soil.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Xu, Xu","Wang, Xinling","Sun, Ting","Liu, Shanshan","Dong, Menghui","Yue, Yang","Min, Yi","Jousset, Alexandre","Xiao, Xian","Liu, Shuwei","Geisen, Stefan","Krashevska, Valentyna","Shen, Qirong","Scheu, Stefan","Li, Rong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797109"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Rong"],"country":["China","Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Changzhou University","Nanjing Agricultural University","Senckenberg Biodiversity and Climate Research Institute","University of Göttingen","Utrecht University","Wageningen University & Research"],"keyword":["Nematoda","Soil microbial communities","Trophic interaction","nosZ gene"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactions between bacterivorous nematodes and bacteria reduce n sub 000000000002 sub o emissions","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202413227","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-797109","identifier":[{"id":"105001638306","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39887670","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11948072","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-d005cbb6-50a9-43f8-9c1b-ddecb30e2327"],"keyword":["nematoda","nosZ gene","selective predation","soil microbial communities","trophic interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3759B2B895B57D05AB89F6B1084EBA39"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202413227","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Plant Pathology and Microbiology"],"no