{"abstract":"With the rapid increase of human exploration and utilization of ocean space, awareness of threats posed by extreme wave events elevates significantly. To protect man-made structures, breakwaters are widely used and they can be classified according to bottom fixed and floating ones. Compared to bottom fixed breakwaters, floating breakwaters can have the advantages such as low cost, easy installation, and environmental friendliness. The relevant technology has not been thoroughly studied yet. Recently, we performed a sequence of preliminary experimental and numerical investigations. The experimental tests were conducted in a wave flume at the Shanghai Jiao Tong University with image processing techniques. The numerical simulations were implemented with a Reynolds averaged Navier–Stokes equation code. We investigated the performance of porous floating breakwaters with different input wave states. In addition, we examined and discussed the wave attenuation performance of floating breakwaters with different moment of inertia and length scale. The results will enhance the scientific understanding and guide the feasibility studies of using floating breakwaters to protect the coast of Asian cities.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhang, Zitan","Chow, Kwok Wing","Li, Ye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827446"],"event":{"end":"2025-12-04","place":"hk","start":"2025-12-02","title":"4th World Conference on Floating Solutions","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Zitan"],"country":["China","Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","The University of Hong Kong"],"keyword":["Floating breakwater","Laboratory experiment","Transmission coefficient"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation on wave attenuation performance of a flexible porous floating breakwater","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010032369","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827446","identifier":[{"id":"105010032369","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-2b242cfd-d7c2-40c8-afa9-23c28067647e"],"keyword":["Coast protection","Floating breakwater","Laboratory experiment","RANS equation","Transmission coefficient"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5D44F35D01B2415CE3A75EC74D567A9B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"the university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind and Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zitan","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zitan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kwok Wing","key":"chowpau","last":"Chow","name":"Chow, Kwok Wing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ye","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"d3ed0364-dfae-4741-ace7-c3481b4b7c1d","name":"Li, Ye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao Lin","key":"zhaopedh","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Xiao Lin","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian-Guo","key":"daipedh","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Jian-Guo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Siwei","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Siwei","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Soon Heng","key":"limpedh","last":"Lim","name":"Lim, Soon Heng","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-981-96-4569-5_99","eisbn":["9789819645695"],"isbn":["9789819645688","9789819645718"],"issn":["23662557"],"pages":"955-964","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Civil Engineering","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Fourth World Conference on Floating Solutions: WCFS 2024; 2–4 December; Hong Kong","volume":"597"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105010032369"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2b242cfd-d7c2-40c8-afa9-23c28067647e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Investigation on Wave Attenuation Performance of a Flexible Porous Floating Breakwater","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827446","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Production of recombinant proteins is regarded as an important breakthrough in the field of biomedicine and industrial biotechnology. Due to the complexity of the protein secretory pathway and its tight interaction with cellular metabolism, the application of traditional metabolic engineering tools to improve recombinant protein production faces major challenges. A systematic approach is required to generate novel design principles for superior protein secretion cell factories. Here, we applied a proteome-constrained genome-scale protein secretory model of the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae (pcSecYeast) to simulate α-amylase production under limited secretory capacity and predict gene targets for downregulation and upregulation to improve α-amylase production. The predicted targets were evaluated using high-throughput screening of specifically designed CRISPR interference/activation (CRISPRi/a) libraries and droplet microfluidics screening. From each library, 200 and 190 sorted clones, respectively, were manually verified. Out of them, 50% of predicted downregulation targets and 34.6% predicted upregulation targets were confirmed to improve α-amylase production. By simultaneously fine-tuning the expression of three genes in central carbon metabolism, i.e. LPD1, MDH1, and ACS1, we were able to increase the carbon flux in the fermentative pathway and α-amylase production. This study exemplifies how model-based predictions can be rapidly validated via a high-throughput screening approach. Our findings highlight novel engineering targets for cell factories and furthermore shed light on the connectivity between recombinant protein production and central carbon metabolism.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Chen, Xiao","Li, Feiran","Li, Xiaowei","Otto, Maximilian","Chen, Yu","Siewers, Verena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-788757"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Genome scale model","High throughput screening","Microfluidics","Recombinant protein production","Yeast cell factories"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model assisted crispri a library screening reveals central carbon metabolic targets for enhanced recombinant protein production in yeast","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ymben.2024.11.010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-788757","identifier":[{"id":"39615667","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85210652065","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1f4bb513-1a17-4a08-99c2-a87746baf059"],"keyword":["CRISPRi/a library","Genome-scale model","High-throughput screening","Microfluidics","Recombinant protein production","Yeast cell factories"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FEA7E7FC1231BA7A3E3C08D4BAC0A60A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ymben.2024.11.010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386884398/1-s2.0-S1096717624001526-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2