{"abstract":"Urbanisation has been considered to promote exotic plant invasion. Ecophysiology predicts phenotypic variation and potential evolution following urbanisation and can be used to evaluate plant invasiveness. However, few studies have included the role of ecophysiological traits for such invasiveness in urban ecosystems. Traditional plant functional traits have been used but have their limitations. Novel approaches such as metabolomics may potentially be useful. The present study explored the invasiveness of the cosmopolitan noxious invasive plant Alternanthera philoxeroides in urban and periurban areas of a megacity city in China using both traditional leaf functional traits and novel leaf metabolome as indicators. We found that traditional leaf functional traits, including specific leaf area, nitrogen concentration, carbon:nitrogen ratio and construction costs, did not differ between urban and periurban A. philoxeroides populations. However, metabolomic profiling showed that the urban populations had an up-regulated expression of zeatin and purine, two cytokinins correlated with plant growth and a down-regulated expression of isoflavonoids, a defensive metabolite for herbivory. Leaf metabolome may, therefore, be sensitive in deciphering the facilitative effects of urbanisation on plant invasion. We also found that the urban populations of A. philoxeroides accumulated more beneficial microbes, which might enhance their invasiveness. Urbanisation likely promotes exotic plants invasion through generation of metabolites, which stimulates growth via modification of the soil microbiome. Our results indicate that leaf metabolome may be used for interpreting plant invasiveness and predicting plant invasion.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Huang, Xiaolong","Yang, Jinming","Yang, Xue","Wang, Tong","Meng, Jie","Guo, Xiao","Wang, Yang","Xiong, Wen","Zeng, Jin","Wu, Zhaoshi","Li, Kuanyi","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-797327"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Tong"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","Hubei Normal University","Middle East Technical University","Qingdao Agricultural University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Wuhan Institute of Technology","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Ecophysiology","Soil microbiome","Urbanisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"leaf metabolomic traits decipher the invasiveness of i alternanthera philoxeroides i in urban wetlands","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85218234629","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-797327","identifier":[{"id":"39987825","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85218234629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-eb00ac83-fcd4-4d7e-8e9e-416087c3ad09"],"keyword":["Ecophysiology","Invasion mechanism","Soil microbiome","Urbanisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9AD29794036FC1D731E9692CAFC4C15F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas nanjing institute of geography and limnology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Nanjing Institute of Geography and Limnology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"qingdao agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"wuhan institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"hubei normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hubei Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaolong","key":"huangxiaolongpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Xiaolong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinming","key":"yangjinmingpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Jinming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xue","key":"yangxuepau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xue","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tong","key":"wangtongpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Tong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"mengjiepau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Jie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"guoxiaopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yang","key":"wangyangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen","key":"xiongwenpau","last":"Xiong","name":"Xiong, Wen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin","key":"zengjinpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Jin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhaoshi","key":"wuzhaoshipau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Zhaoshi","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kuanyi","key":"likuanyipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Kuanyi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6 7 8","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39987825"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2025.178888","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"178888","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"968"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218234629"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eb00ac83-fcd4-4d7e-8e9e-416087c3ad09"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Leaf metabolomic traits decipher the invasiveness of <i>Alternanthera philoxeroides</i> in urban wetlands","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797327","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Ergothioneine (EGT), a histidine derivative with diverse physiological functions, has broad applications in food, cosmetics, and pharmaceuticals. Fermentative production of EGT using recombinant Saccharomyces cerevisiae is widely considered the most cost-effective and direct method. However, no previous studies have explored improving EGT production in S. cerevisiae through protein fusion technology. In this study, we present the first successful construction of a fungal EGT biosynthesis pathway in S. cerevisiae, coupled with enzyme fusion techniques and optimization of gene copy integration. The engineered strain, SZA011, achieved a record EGT production of 122.5 mg/L under optimized shake flask fermentation conditions. Moreover, in a 10 L fed-batch fermentation system, SZA011 produced 626.24 mg/L of EGT. This study introduces a novel strategy for enhancing microbial EGT generation through protein and genetic engineering, potentially enabling industrial applications.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Chen, Shuzhen","Lin, Wenjing","Zhang, Yan","Cai, Fan","Lin, Wei","Xiao, Jianbin","Chen, Xingtong","Li, Qin","Zhang, Huaidong","Zhang, Mingliang","Li, Li"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806491"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Li","Zhang, Mingliang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fujian Normal University"],"keyword":["Bioprocess optimization","Ergothioneine","Flexible linkers","Metabolic engineering","Saccharomyces cerevisiae"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing ergothioneine production in saccharomyces cerevisiae via protein fusion technology and gene integration optimization","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105004079214","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806491","identifier":[{"id":"105004079214","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5682ca22-a17b-466a-9233-99311a8114d7"],"keyword":["Bioprocess optimization","Ergothioneine","Flexible linkers","Metabolic engineering","Saccharomyces cerevisiae"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8FE45D7B46D914BE1B8B0AE3A152D273"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"fujian normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fujian Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering, Department of Biological and Chemical Engineering - Industrial Biotechnology - Gustav Wieds Vej 10D"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuzhen","key":"chenshuzhenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Shuzhen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjing","key":"linwenjingpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Wenjing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"zhangyanpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"251ea212-fcf4-4249-8672-42fcf09ea051","name":"Zhang, Yan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fan","key":"caifanpau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Fan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"linweipau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianbin","key":"xiaojianbinpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jianbin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xingtong","key":"chenxingtongpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xingtong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qin","key":"liqinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huaidong","key":"zhanghuaidongpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Huaidong","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingliang","key":"zhangmingliangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Mingliang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"lilipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Li","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fbio.2025.106745","issn":["22124292","22124306"],"issn_org":["22124292"],"journal":"Food Bioscience","paperid":"106745","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Food Bioscience","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004079214"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5682ca22-a17b-466a-9233-99311a8114d7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Enhancing ergothioneine production in Saccharomyces cerevisiae via protein fusion technology and gene integration optimization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806491","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Compared to classical ion-selective electrodes (ISEs) with internal reference solutions, potential stability remains one of the greatest challenges for all-solid-state ISEs. In this paper, a highly stable all-solid-state potassium ISE was developed using thin egg-shell hollow carbon nanospheres (ESHCNs) synthesized via one-pot hydrothermal method as an ion-to-electron transducing layer. The electrodes’ properties were examined by means of cyclic voltammetry, electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, and chronopotentiometry, proving the superior hydrophobicity as well as large interfacial capacitance for these ESHCNs. These characteristics effectively prevented the formation of a water layer between the conducting substrate and polymer film, therefore stabilizing their electrode potential. The prepared electrode exhibited good linearity within potassium ion concentration range of 5.0 × 10-6 ∼ 1.0 × 10-2 mol/L, with a Nernst slope of 55.11 ± 1.6 mV/decade and a detection limit of 1.41 × 10-6 mol/L. It showed excellent long-term stability, with only a decrease of 12.02 % in response-slope after over 18 months of use. For quality control in industrial settings, the amount of K+ contents determined in actual cigarette paper using this electrode was consistent with ion chromatography results, demonstrating its potential for rapid, accurate, and reliable on-site K+ detection with promising industrial applications.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Yu, Saibo","Li, Bin","Chen, Pengfei","Lian, Wenliu","Jiang, Lamei","Jin, Yong","Wu, Ling","Xiao, Zhongliang","Yu, Donghong","Cao, Zhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-814834"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Cao, Zhong","Jin, Yong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Changsha University of Science and Technology","State Tobacco Monopoly Administration, China Tobacco Corporation"],"keyword":["Potassium ion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an all solid state polymeric membrane potassium ion selective electrode with egg shell hollow carbon nanospheres as ion to electron transducing layer","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=105008127044&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-814834","identifier":[{"id":"105008127044","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c162bd6c-54d4-4fe7-8e4a-1c42df8d94fb"],"keyword":["All-solid-state ion-selective electrode","Cigarette paper analysis","Egg-shell hollow carbon nanospheres","Ion-to-electron transducing layer","Potassium ion","Potentiometric sensor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-48A794F7ADAE64CD882817A6EC3224D6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"changsha university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Changsha University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state tobacco monopoly administration china tobacco corporation","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Tobacco Monopoly Administration, China Tobacco Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Saibo","key":"yusaibopau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Saibo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"libinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengfei","key":"chenpengfeipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Pengfei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenliu","key":"lianwenliupau","last":"Lian","name":"Lian, Wenliu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lamei","key":"jianglameipau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Lamei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong","key":"jinyongpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Yong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ling","key":"wulingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Ling","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongliang","key":"xiaozhongliangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Zhongliang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yudonghongpau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong","key":"caozhongpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhong","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.microc.2025.114287","issn":["0026265X","10959149"],"issn_org":["0026265X"],"journal":"Microchemical Journal","paperid":"114287","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Microchemical Journal","volume":"215"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008127044"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c162bd6c-54d4-4fe7-8e4a-1c42df8d94fb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An all-solid-state polymeric membrane potassium ion-selective electrode with egg-shell hollow carbon nanospheres as ion-to-electron transducing layer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814834","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Cassava is a highly resilient tropical crop that produces large, starchy storage roots and high biomass. However, how did cassava's remarkable environmental adaptability and key economic traits evolve from its wild species remain unclear. In this study, we obtained near complete telomere-to-telomere genome assemblies and their haplotype forms for the cultivar AM560, the wild ancestors FLA4047 and W14, constructed a graphic pan-genome of 30 representatives with a size of 1.15 Gb, and built a clarified evolutionary tree of 486 accessions. A comparison of structural variations and single-nucleotide variations between the ancestors and cultivated cassavas reveals predominant expansions and contractions of numbers of genes and gene families, which are mainly driven by transposons. Significant selective sweeping occurred in 122 footprints of genomes and affects 1,519 domesticated genes. We identify selective mutations in MeCSK and MeFNR2 that could promote photoreactions associated with MeNADP-ME in C4 photosynthesis in modern cassava. Coevolution of retard floral primordia and initiation of storage roots may arise from MeCOL5 variants with altered bindings to MeFT1, MeFT2, and MeTFL2. Mutations in MeMATE1 and MeGTR occur in sweet cassava, and MeAHL19 has evolved to regulate the biosynthesis, transport, and endogenous remobilization of cyanogenic glucosides in cassava. These extensive genomic and gene resources provided here, along with the findings on the evolutionary mechanisms responsible for beneficial traits in modern cultivars, lay a strong foundation for future breeding improvements of cassava.","author_count":48,"contributors":["Xia, Zhiqiang","Du, Zhenglin","Zhou, Xincheng","Jiang, Sirong","Zhu, Tingting","Wang, Le","Chen, Fei","Carvalho, Luiz","Zou, Meiling","Becerra Lopez-Lavalle, Luis Augusto","Zhang, Xiaofei","Xu, Liangye","Wang, Zhenyu","Chen, Meili","Guo, Xin","Wang, Shujuan","Li, Mengtao","Li, Yuanchao","Wang, Haiyan","Liu, Shisheng","Bao, Yuting","Zhao, Long","Zhang, Chenji","Xiao, Jianjia","Guo, Fengguang","Shen, Xu","Li, Haozheng","Lu, Cheng","Qiao, Fei","Ceballos, Hernan","Yan, Huabing","Qin, Xiaochun","Ma, Ling","Zhang, Huaifang","He, Shuang","Zhao, Wenming","Wan, Yinglang","Chen, Yinhua","Huang, Dongyi","Li, Kaimian","Liu, Bin","Peng, Ming","Zhang, Weixiong","Møller, Birger Lindberg","Chen, Xin","Luo, Ming Cheng","Xiao, Jingfa","Wang, Wenquan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819072"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","China","Colombia","Hong Kong","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Brazilian Agricultural Research Corporation","Centro Internacional de Agricultura Tropical","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Chinese Academy of Tropical Agricultural Sciences","Guangxi Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Guangxi University","Hainan University","Hong Kong Polytechnic University","Institute of Nanfan & Seed Industry, Guangdong Academy of Sciences","Qinghai University","University of California at Davis","University of Jinan"],"keyword":["Cassava","Genome","Pan genome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pan genome and haplotype map of cassava cultivars and wild ancestors provide insights into its adaptive evolution and domestication","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.molp.2025.05.014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819072","identifier":[{"id":"40437759","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105008021995","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4fb5f560-0ef2-4e4d-a1e3-930df99cf1e9"],"keyword":["cassava","evolution and domestication","genome","pan-gen