{"abstract":"Antibiotic pollution in natural water bodies has reached alarming levels, posing a significant threat to the delicate balance of aquatic ecosystems. Bacteria and phytoplankton are foundational components of these ecosystems, playing crucial roles as decomposers and primary producers, respectively, and their symbiotic relationships are essential for maintaining ecological stability. Despite accumulating research focusing on the direct toxic effects of antibiotics, disruptions of complex bacteria–phytoplankton symbioses remain largely underexplored. In this review, we first introduce the symbiotic mechanisms between bacteria and phytoplankton, highlighting the processes underlying the formation of these relationships. We then examine the antibiotic sensitivity of bacteria and phytoplankton, highlighting the heightened vulnerability of bacteria. Finally, we explore the mechanism by which antibiotics disrupt bacteria, leading to altered interactions with phytoplankton. These disruptions cause shifts in phytoplankton population community structure and dynamics with implications for ecosystem functions, including higher risk of exacerbation of harmful algal blooms. Our study reveals that even if environmental concentrations of antibiotics do not directly impact phytoplankton populations, they can affect phytoplankton populations and communities by altering symbiotic bacteria. Understanding bacteria–phytoplankton symbioses is thus essential for unraveling the ecological impacts of antibiotics. This underexplored field demands greater attention from pollution ecology researchers, as it is key to defining environmental thresholds for pollutants.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Liu, Xiao Xuan","Li, Jun Mei","Wang, Ruo Bing","Ni, Rongting","Duan, Changqun","Yu, Jiacheng","Jeppesen, Erik","Pan, Ying"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-807687"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Pan, Ying"],"country":["China","Turkey"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Middle East Technical University","Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Phytoplankton"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"antibiotics disrupt bacteria phytoplankton symbioses unveiling ecological risks in aquatic ecosystems","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85219599804","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-807687","identifier":[{"id":"85219599804","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e1a7521b-08b2-4cdb-8495-448000d2c2e5"],"keyword":["antibiotic pollution","bacteria","bacteria-phytoplankton system","interspecies relationships","lethal effect","phytoplankton"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4302EA091FA32C281E52FB84F12F21C9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Freshwater Ecology","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology - WATEC Aarhus University Centre for Water Technology, C.F. Møllers Allé 3"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"sino danish centre for education and research","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"tr","key":"middle east technical university","loc":["Turkey","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Middle East Technical University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Xuan","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xiao Xuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun Mei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jun Mei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruo Bing","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ruo Bing","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rongting","key":"nipau","last":"Ni","name":"Ni, Rongting","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Changqun","key":"duanpau","last":"Duan","name":"Duan, Changqun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiacheng","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Jiacheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"panpau","last":"Pan","locid":"78fc621c-f03d-4569-a6bd-b240ff642b0a","name":"Pan, Ying","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/oik.11201","issn":["00301299","16000706"],"issn_org":["00301299"],"issue":"7","journal":"Oikos","paperid":"e11201","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Oikos","volume":"2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219599804"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e1a7521b-08b2-4cdb-8495-448000d2c2e5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Antibiotics disrupt bacteria-phytoplankton symbioses : unveiling ecological risks in aquatic ecosystems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-807687","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Biodegradation is crucial for the removal and remediation of sulfonamide antibiotic (SA) contamination. Comprehensively understanding the thermophilic degradation mechanism is essential for the application of SA-biodegrading isolates in engineered systems, such as composting. In this study, we explored the thermophilic biodegradation mechanism of Geobacillus sp. S-07 on sulfamethazine (SMZ). Targeted metabolite analysis unveiled that strain S-07 effectively detoxifies SMZ by modifying the amino moiety and disassembling the sulfonamide bridge moiety. By integrating genomic and proteomic analysis, enzymes potentially involved in the SMZ biotransformation were further proposed, including an adenine deaminase, a dimethylsulfone monooxygenase, and a putative heme-containing peroxidase. Genomic analysis indicated that S-07 carries five antibiotic resistance genes, presenting a low mobility in horizontal transfer, implying its low resistance pollution risk in bioremediation application. This study offers novel insights into the thermophilic SA biodegradation mechanism, and provides biological resources for the development of thermophilic bioremediation technologies aimed at enhanced SA removal.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pan, Ting","Zhou, Yan-Yan","Huang, Xu","Xu, Jianxin","Guo, Xiao-Yu","Su, Jian-Qiang","Li, Hu","Yang, Xiao-Ru"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-808761"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Su, Jian-Qiang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Antibiotic biodegradation","Antibiotic resistance genes","Proteomic","Sulfonamides","Thermophile"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thermophilic degradation of sulfamethazine by i geobacillus i sp s 000000000007 pathway and mechanism","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-808761","identifier":[{"id":"40355059","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-c80d8387-23a4-4419-8cd8-bce64290960e"],"keyword":["Antibiotic biodegradation","Antibiotic resistance genes","Proteomic","Sulfonamides","Thermophile"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-020972F518D7A623FC25FA66AD7FE628"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ting","key":"panpau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Ting","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan-Yan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yan-Yan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xu","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Xu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jian-Xin","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"1dbdd379-7c13-4006-bcdc-7bdc6556562f","name":"Xu, Jianxin","name_org":"Xu, Jian-Xin","orcid":"0000-0003-2021-1211","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Yu","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao-Yu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian-Qiang","key":"supau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Jian-Qiang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Ru","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao-Ru","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40355059"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.envres.2025.121823","issn":["00139351","10960953"],"issn_org":["00139351"],"issue":"Part 2","journal":"Environmental Research","paperid":"121823","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Environmental Research","volume":"279"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005080411"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c80d8387-23a4-4419-8cd8-bce64290960e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Thermophilic degradation of sulfamethazine by <i>Geobacillus</i> sp. S-07: pathway and mechanism","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-808761","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Bacteriophages play important roles in the regulation of bacterial communities and may thus impact human health. However, the scarcity of genomic data of oral microorganism has limited information on oral phages. We collected data on 5427 metagenomic samples and 2178 cultivated bacterial genomes across different geographical areas and populations, generating the Oral Phage Database (OPD), comprising 189,859 representative phage genome sequences, including 3416 huge phages (genome size > 200 kbp). OPD reveals that most oral viruses are unknown and encode an enormous variety of dark proteins. Numerous oral phages infecting a broad range of hosts carry anti-defense genes, auxiliary metabolic genes, and virulence factors that may affect bacterial metabolism and influence human health. The composition of oral phages varies among different populations, and several phages have the potential to act as biomarkers for disease. OPD expands our knowledge of phage-bacteria interactions, huge phages diversity, and potential impacts on human health.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Jie, Zhuye","Liang, Hewei","Meng, Yanzheng","Zhang, Jiahao","Zhang, Tao","Li, Wenxi","Lin, Xiaoqian","Hu, Tongyuan","Han, Mo","Liang, Weiting","Ju, Yanmei","Tong, Xin","Jin, Xin","Xu, Xun","Zhang, Wenwei","Wang, Jian","Yang, Huanming","Kristiansen, Karsten","Xiao, Liang","Zou, Yuanqiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828818"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","James D. Watson Institute of Genome Sciences","National Institute of Biological Sciences, Beijing","South China University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrating metagenomics and cultivation unveils oral phage diversity and potential impact on hosts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41522-025-00773-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828818","identifier":[{"id":"105011719457","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40715125","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12297358","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-48f0390a-3369-44e9-8a3d-e3a089ba93d0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6C152E8A2254DBA1DD0E6932BA60BF6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41522-025-00773-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/459804025/s41522-025-00773-z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"national institute of biological sciences beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"National Institute of Biological Sciences, Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"james d watson institute of genome sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"James D. Watson Institute of Genome Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg un