{"abstract":"The carbon sinks of North American boreal forests have been threatened by global warming and forest disturbances in recent decades, but knowledge about the carbon balance of these forests in recent years remains unknown. We tracked annual aboveground carbon (AGC) changes from 2016 to 2021 across the forest regions of NASA's Arctic Boreal Vulnerability Experiment (ABoVE) core study domain, using Vegetation Optical Depth derived from low-frequency passive microwave observations. The results showed that these forests showed a net AGC increase of + 28.49 Tg C/yr during the study period, with total AGC gains of + 219.34 Tg C/yr counteracting total AGC losses of −190.86 Tg C/yr. Forest degradation (-162.21 Tg C/yr), defined as a reduction in the capacity of forest to provide goods and services, contributes 5 times more to the total AGC loss than forest cover loss (-28.65 Tg C/yr), defined as the complete removal of tree cover. This indicates that degradation has dominated AGC loss in the region.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Yu, Ling","Fan, Lei","Ciais, Philippe","Xiao, Jingfeng","Frappart, Frédéric","Sitch, Stephen","Chen, Jingming","Xiao, Xiangming","Fensholt, Rasmus","Chang, Zhongbing","Fang, Hongqian","Li, Xiaojun","Cui, Tiangxiang","Ma, Mingguo","Wigneron, Jean Pierre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738790"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China","France","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing Forestry University","Paris-Saclay University","Southwest University","Surveying and Mapping Institute Lands and Resource Department of Guangdong Province","University of Exeter","University of New Hampshire","University of Oklahoma","University of Toronto","Université de Bordeaux"],"keyword":["Carbon balance","Forest degradation","Remote sensing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forest degradation contributes more to carbon loss than forest cover loss in north american boreal forests","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jag.2024.103729","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-738790","identifier":[{"id":"85187662475","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1e37e8a1-894e-4eaf-9813-49485fe9954e"],"keyword":["Canadian boreal forests","Carbon balance","Forest degradation","Remote sensing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DD59F3E7EF7A70DAFC4AD2319CFC61C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jag.2024.103729","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/389595074/1_s2.0_S1569843224000839_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"paris saclay university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Saclay University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of new hampshire","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of New Hampshire","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"université de bordeaux","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université de Bordeaux","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography, Land, Environment and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"cn","key":"surveying and mapping institute lands and resource department of guangdong province","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Surveying and Mapping Institute Lands and Resource Department of Guangdong Province","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"cn","key":"nanjing forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Forestry University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ling","key":"yulingpau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Ling","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"fanleipau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Lei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Philippe","key":"ciaisphilippepau","last":"Ciais","name":"Ciais, Philippe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jingfeng","key":"xiaojingfengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jingfeng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Frédéric","key":"frappartfrédéricpau","last":"Frappart","name":"Frappart, Frédéric","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Stephen","key":"sitchstephenpau","last":"Sitch","name":"Sitch, Stephen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jingming","key":"chenjingmingpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Jingming","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Xiangming","key":"xiaoxiangmingpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xiangming","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","f