i","key":"houpau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Chengyi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"ulstruppau","last":"Ulstrup","locid":"a7bf8f77-fd81-4dce-8592-8c7bec26750b","name":"Ulstrup, Jens","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38048721"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bios.2023.115890","issn":["09565663","18734235"],"issn_org":["09565663"],"journal":"Biosensors and Bioelectronics","paperid":"115890","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biosensors and Bioelectronics","volume":"246"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178554104"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a16c53ad-b61f-4eda-a56b-e74e35b27149","dtu-300f89b0-87b0-4e24-b96e-f9e054840f1d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Electrochemical sensing fibers for wearable health monitoring devices","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-703768","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Biological hydrogen-methane conversion technology can combine Power-to-Gas technology with biogas engineering and showed great potential in breaking through the limitations of both hydrogen storage and CO2 removal for biogas upgrading. However, the low gas–liquid mass transfer rate of hydrogen greatly limited its conversion efficiency and actual application. This study used a biotrickling filter (BTF) to address this limiting factor, and the effects of temperature and packing materials on hydrogen-methane conversion were investigated. Results showed that higher temperature was beneficial for hydrogen-methane conversion, and the highest conversion efficiency of 8.3 L/Lw·d was obtained at 55 °C with the archaeal community dominated by Methanothermobacter (99.97 %). The reactor using activated carbon as packing material showed the best hydrogen-methane conversion efficiency of 91.9 %, with the most methanogens fixed on the surface. Due to the electronic conductor property of activated carbon, the microbial communities of the biofilm were also different from the other two packing materials. Finally, the H2/CO2 ratio of the gas inflow was optimized, and the most suitable result was 2.5:1 (H2/CO2, v/v), which was far below the previously reported results and indicated higher efficiency in carbon dioxide removal. This study provided a promising way for biogas upgrading.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Huang, Jie-Hua","Fan, Xiao-Lei","Li, Rui","Sun, Meng-Ting","Zou, Hua","Zhang, Yifeng","Guo, Rong-Bo","Fu, Shan-Fei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-711552"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Fu, Shan-Fei"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Jiangnan University","Qingdao University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Biogas upgrading","Biotrickling filter","Temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biogas upgrading by biotrickling filter effects of temperature and packing materials","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85181666835","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-711552","identifier":[{"id":"85181666835","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7ea3dc4c-b8fc-4497-aa73-6e828b2d6e6b"],"keyword":["Biogas upgrading","Biotrickling filter","Hydrogen-methane conversion","Packing material","Temperature"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6DE7003C2E58B5EA229A1BF269212286"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-01-03","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"qingdao university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Water Technology & Processes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie-Hua","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jie-Hua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Lei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Xiao-Lei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Rui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Meng-Ting","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Meng-Ting","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hua","key":"zoupau","last":"Zou","name":"Zou, Hua","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yi-Feng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"ce49a7e7-7f82-427b-babf-27d0549e1f8f","name":"Zhang, Yifeng","name_org":"Zhang, Yi-Feng","orcid":"0000-0002-2832-2277","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rong-Bo","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Rong-Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shan-Fei","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Shan-Fei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cej.2023.148367","issn":["13858947","18733212"],"issn_org":["13858947"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering Journal","paperid":"148367","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering Journal","volume":"481"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181666835"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7ea3dc4c-b8fc-4497-aa73-6e828b2d6e6b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Biogas upgrading by biotrickling filter : Effects of temperature and packing materials","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-711552","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Nanoporous materials have attracted great attention for gas storage, but achieving high volumetric storage capacity remains a challenge. Here, by using neutron powder diffraction, volumetric gas adsorption, inelastic neutron scattering and first-principles calculations, we investigate a magnesium borohydride framework that has small pores and a partially negatively charged non-flat interior for hydrogen and nitrogen uptake. Hydrogen and nitrogen occupy distinctly different adsorption sites in the pores, with very different limiting capacities of 2.33 H 2 and 0.66 N 2 per Mg(BH 4) 2. Molecular hydrogen is packed extremely densely, with about twice the density of liquid hydrogen (144 g H 2 per litre of pore volume). We found a penta-dihydrogen cluster where H 2 molecules in one position have rotational freedom, whereas H 2 molecules in another position have a well-defined orientation and a directional interaction with the framework. This study reveals that densely packed hydrogen can be stabilized in small-pore materials at ambient pressures.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Oh, Hyunchul","Tumanov, Nikolay","Ban, Voraksmy","Li, Xiao","Richter, Bo","Hudson, Matthew R","Brown, Craig M","Iles, Gail N","Wallacher, Dirk","Jorgensen, Scott W","Daemen, Luke","Balderas-Xicohténcatl, Rafael","Cheng, Yongqiang","Ramirez-Cuesta, Anibal J","Heere, Michael","Posada-Pérez, Sergio","Hautier, Geoffroy","Hirscher, Michael","Jensen, Torben René","Filinchuk, Yaroslav"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-717418"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Filinchuk, Yaroslav","Hirscher, Michael","Jensen, Torben René"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Germany","South Korea","Spain","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","General Motors","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems","National Institute of Standards and Technology","Oak Ridge National Laboratory","Royal Melbourne Institute of Technology University","Technical University of Braunschweig","Ulsan National Institute of Science and Technology","Universite Catholique de Louvain","University of Girona"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"small pore hydridic frameworks store densely packed hydrogen","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41557-024-01443-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-717418","identifier":[{"id":"38321236","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11087247","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85184179802","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3fa5389f-a8b3-4430-abfc-dd1b9f3cef82"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-62C4355AD8BE84694E53E15683578968"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41557-024-01443-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"kr","key":"ulsan national institute of science and technology","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Ulsan National Institute of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"universite catholique de louvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite Catholique de Louvain","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","