f the human-derived isolates of Faecalibacterium","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-748906","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Solid oral controlled release formulations feature numerous clinical advantages for drug candidates with adequate solubility and dissolution rate. However, most new chemical entities exhibit poor water solubility, and hence are exempt from such benefits. Although combining drug amorphization with controlled release formulation is promising to elevate drug solubility, like other supersaturating systems, the problem of drug recrystallization has yet to be resolved, particularly within the dosage form. Here, we explored the potential of an emerging, non-leachable terpolymer nanoparticle (TPN) pore former as an internal recrystallization inhibitor within controlled release amorphous solid dispersion (CRASD) beads comprising a poorly soluble drug (celecoxib) reservoir and insoluble polymer (ethylcellulose) membrane. Compared to conventional pore former, polyvinylpyrrolidone (PVP), TPN-containing membranes exhibited superior structural integrity, less crystal formation at the CRASD bead surface, and greater extent of celecoxib release. All-atom molecular dynamics analyses revealed that in the presence of TPN, intra-molecular bonding, crystal formation tendency, diffusion coefficient, and molecular flexibility of celecoxib were reduced, while intermolecular H-bonding was increased as compared to PVP. This work suggests that selection of a pore former that promotes prolonged molecular separation within a nanoporous controlled release membrane structure may serve as an effective strategy to enhance amorphicity preservation inside CRASD.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Lugtu-Pe, Jamie Anne","Zhang, Xuning","Mirzaie, Sako","Chang, Hao Han R.","AL-Mousawi, Nour","Chen, Kuan","Li, Yongqiang","Kane, Anil","Bar-Shalom, Daniel","Wu, Xiao Yu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749209"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Candoo Pharmatech Company Inc.","Thermo Fisher Scientific, Inc.","University of Toronto"],"keyword":["Molecular Dynamics Simulation","Poorly soluble drug"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an emerging terpolymeric nanoparticle pore former as an internal recrystallization inhibitor of celecoxib in controlled release amorphous solid dispersion beads experimental studies and molecular dynamics analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apsb.2024.03.026","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749209","identifier":[{"id":"38828156","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85190145298","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11143779","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d27432b4-5067-4c69-abf0-d48b5515d3c0"],"keyword":["Controlled release amorphous solid dispersion","Drug-polymer interactions","Effect of pore formers","Internal recrystallization","Membrane-reservoir coated beads","Molecular dynamics simulation","Poorly soluble drug","Terpolymer nanogel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A8AD4D7A845F4BEEF3002FA3D2C7738E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apsb.2024.03.026","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/393838831/1_s2.0_S2211383524001072_main_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"candoo pharmatech company inc","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Candoo Pharmatech Company Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"thermo fisher scientific inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Thermo Fisher Scientific, Inc.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jamie Anne","key":"lugtupepau","last":"Lugtu-Pe","name":"Lugtu-Pe, Jamie Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xuning","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xuning","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sako","key":"mirzaiepau","last":"Mirzaie","name":"Mirzaie, Sako","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hao Han R.","key":"changpau","last":"Chang","name":"Chang, Hao Han R.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nour","key":"almousawipau","last":"AL-Mousawi","name":"AL-Mousawi, Nour","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kuan","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Kuan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Yongqiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yongqiang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Anil","key":"kanepau","last":"Kane","name":"Kane, Anil","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniel","key":"barshalompau","last":"Bar-Shalom","locid":"e2009817-c8f5-4ad5-937d-bd5e2811997a","name":"Bar-Shalom, Daniel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Yu","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xiao Yu","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38828156"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apsb.2024.03.026","issn":["22113835"],"issue":"6","journal":"Acta Pharmaceutica Sinica B","pages":"2669-2684","status":"p","title":"Acta Pharmaceutica Sinica B","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190145298"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d27432b4-5067-4c69-abf0-d48b5515d3c0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An emerging terpolymeric nanoparticle pore former as an internal recrystallization inhibitor of celecoxib in controlled release amorphous solid dispersion beads : Experimental studies and molecular dynamics analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749209","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Antimony contamination in aquatic environment raises tremendous concerns for human health and ecosystem safety, while there is a lack of methods for efficient and selective adsorption of antimony. In this study, an adsorbent for trivalent antimony (Sb(III)) removal is obtained by cross-linking polyethyleneimine (PEI) onto phosphoric acid-modified lignin-based porous biochar (PPLB). PPLB exhibits efficient adsorption of Sb(III) with a maximum value of 371.7 mg/g, which is also highly selective as the Sb(III) removal capability by PPLB remains unaffected under the common co-existing anions (Cl -, NO 3 –, PO 4 3-, and CO 3 2–) and less affected with the co-existing cations (Cd 2+, Zn 2+, Cu 2+, and Pb 2+). Such a performance is validated in three simulated Sb(III)-contaminated water bodies (Zijiang River water, industrial wastewater, and mining area water). Understanding of the adsorption mechanisms is further established via density functional theory calculations, revealing the dominant adsorption site of Sb(III) on PPLB is –NH- groups. It's finally concluded that the removal of Sb(III) by PPLB is governed by complexation, with also the contribution from ligand exchange and hydrogen bonding. As a proof of concept, the spent PPLB adsorbed with Sb(III) is valorized into an active material of sodium ion battery, demonstrating a specific capacity of 192.4 mA h/g for 1000 cycles with a good long-term stability.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Huang, Wei","Yang, Zhixuan","Hu, Junguang","Chen, Xin","Li, Wei","Wang, Zhiguo","Zhang, Chun","Wang, Qiongchao","Xiao, Xinxin","Yu, Peng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762127"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Xinxin","Yu, Peng"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Biochar","Removal mechanism","Selective adsorption","Valorization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mechanisms and valorization of selective adsorption of sb iii by amino functionalized lignin based porous biochar","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.156262","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by the Hunan Provincial Natural Science Foundation of China (2023JJ40330 & 2023JJ50322), Provincial Science and Technology Project of Nonggao District, Jinggangshan (20222-051245), Research Foundation of Education Bureau of Hunan Province, China (22B0184) and Postgraduate Scientific Research Innovation Project of Hunan Province (CX20240669). X.X. acknowledges a Novo Nordisk Foundation Start Package grant (0081331)."],"id":"S01-000.00-762127","identifier":[{"id":"85205391774","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1905e3b5-562a-4948-98c4-49cdc945a681"],"keyword":["Biochar","Removal mechanism","Selective adsorption","Trivalent antimony","Valorization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BFC084B2223CEEA99DD4EB2267B4FC81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/764123791/1-s2.0-S1385894724077532-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.156262","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"hunan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, [Mission] A Sustainable Danish Energy System"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"huangweipau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhixuan","key":"yangzhixuanpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Zhixuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Junguang","key":"hujunguangpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Junguang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin","key":"chenxinpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhiguo","key":"wangzhiguopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zhiguo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chun","key":"zhangchunpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Chun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiongchao","key":"wangqiongchaopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Qiongchao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaoxinxinpau","last":"Xiao","locid":"fd69114c-9434-44ba-b01b-e9ecb3831cae","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng","key":"yupengpau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Peng","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cej.2024.156262","issn":["13858947","18733212"],"issn_org":["13858947"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering Journal","paperid":"156262","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering Journal","title_org":"Chemical engineering journal","volume":"499"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205391774"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1905e3b5-562a-4948-98c4-49cdc945a681"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Mechanisms and valorization of selective adsorption of Sb(III) by amino-functionalized lignin-based porous biochar","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-762127","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
