Ana","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Lei","key":"fanleipau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Lei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Gabriel","key":"gaticagabrielpau","last":"Gatica","name":"Gatica, Gabriel","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Rahul","key":"kashyaprahulpau","last":"Kashyap","name":"Kashyap, Rahul","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiangzhuo","key":"liuxiangzhuopau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xiangzhuo","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Stephen","key":"sitchstephenpau","last":"Sitch","name":"Sitch, Stephen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Shengli","key":"taoshenglipau","last":"Tao","name":"Tao, Shengli","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Xiangming","key":"xiaoxiangmingpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xiangming","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"Hui","key":"yanghuipau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Hui","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","first":"Jhan Carlo Espinoza","key":"villarjhancarloespinozapau","last":"Villar","name":"Villar, Jhan Carlo Espinoza","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederic","key":"frappartfredericpau","last":"Frappart","name":"Frappart, Frederic","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15","first":"Wei","key":"liweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Yuanwei","key":"qinyuanweipau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Yuanwei","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16","first":"Aurélien","key":"detruchisaurélienpau","last":"De Truchis","name":"De Truchis, Aurélien","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rasmus","key":"fensholtrasmuspau","last":"Fensholt","locid":"26fbbb5c-3853-4be9-8cab-3dce86446363","name":"Fensholt, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-3067-4527","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/frsen.2024.1338618","issn":["26736187"],"journal":"Frontiers in Remote Sensing","paperid":"1338618","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Remote Sensing","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193942083"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-533abd0f-2c4f-4f8a-b050-77a71c8f3944"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Global carbon balance of the forest : satellite-based L-VOD results over the last decade","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777713","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Previous studies revealed extensive genetic introgression between Ovis species, which affects genetic adaptation and morphological traits. However, the exact evolutionary scenarios underlying the hybridization between sheep and allopatric wild relatives remain unknown. To address this problem, we here integrate the reference genomes of several ovine and caprine species: domestic sheep, argali, bighorn sheep, snow sheep, and domestic goats. Additionally, we use 856 whole genomes representing 169 domestic sheep populations and their six wild relatives: Asiatic mouflon, urial, argali, snow sheep, thinhorn sheep, and bighorn sheep. We implement a comprehensive set of analyses to test introgression among these species. We infer that the argali lineage originated ∼3.08 to 3.35 Mya and hybridized with the ancestor of Pachyceriforms (e.g. bighorn sheep and snow sheep) at ∼1.56 Mya. Previous studies showed apparent introgression from North American Pachyceriforms into the Bashibai sheep, a Chinese native sheep breed, despite of their wide geographic separation. We show here that, in fact, the apparent introgression from the Pachyceriforms into Bashibai can be explained by the old introgression from Pachyceriforms into argali and subsequent recent introgression from argali into Bashibai. Our results illustrate the challenges of estimating complex introgression histories and provide an example of how indirect and direct introgression can be distinguished.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lv, Feng-Hua","Wang, Dong-Feng","Zhao, Si-Yi","Lv, Xiao-Yang","Sun, Wei","Nielsen, Rasmus","Li, Meng-Hua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779119"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Zoology","China Agricultural University","University of California at Berkeley","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Yangzhou University"],"keyword":["Demographic history","Genomes","Sheep"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep ancestral introgressions between ovine species shape sheep genomes via argali mediated gene flow","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msae212","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-779119","identifier":[{"id":"39404100","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11542629","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85208771918","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cf0c82b0-2ae1-4a39-84ae-6ed17797f71c"],"keyword":["Ovis genus","ancestral introgression","argali","demographic history","genomes","sheep"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-879CF67CF8A35E54502276CA9088C041"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msae212","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/412775564/msae212.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas institute of zoology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Institute of Zoology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"yangzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yangzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Feng-Hua","key":"lvfenghuapau","last":"Lv","name":"Lv, Feng-Hua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Dong-Feng","key":"wangdongfengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Dong-Feng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Si-Yi","key":"zhaosiyipau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Si-Yi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Xiao-Yang","key":"lvxiaoyangpau","last":"Lv","name":"Lv, Xiao-Yang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Wei","key":"sunweipau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenrasmuspau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"68905e51-280a-4c0b-bc94-469bb52de9b6","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-0513-6591","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Meng-Hua","key":"limenghuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Meng-Hua","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39404100"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/molbev/msae212","issn":["07374038","15371719"],"issn_org":["07374038"],"issue":"11","journal":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","paperid":"msae212","status":"p","title":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208771918"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cf0c82b0-2ae1-4a39-84ae-6ed17797f71c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Ancestral Introgressions between Ovine Species Shape Sheep Genomes via Argali-Mediated Gene Flow","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779119","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have identified more than 200 common genetic variants independently associated with colorectal cancer (CRC) risk, but the causal variants and target genes are mostly unknown. We sought to fine-map all known CRC risk loci using GWAS data from 100,204 cases and 154,587 controls of East Asian and European ancestry. Our stepwise conditional analyses revealed 238 independent association signals of CRC risk, each with a set of credible causal variants (CCVs), of which 28 signals had a single CCV. Our cis-eQTL/mQTL and colocalization analyses using colorectal tissue-specific transcriptome and methylome data separately from 1299 and 321 individuals, along with functional genomic investigation, uncovered 136 putative CRC susceptibility genes, including 56 genes not previously reported. Analyses of single-cell RNA-seq data from colorectal tissues revealed 17 putative CRC susceptibility genes with distinct expression patterns in specific cell types. Analyses of whole exome sequencing data provided additional support for several target genes identified in this study as CRC susceptibility genes. Enrichment analyses of the 136 genes uncover pathways not previously linked to CRC risk. Our study substantially expanded association signals for CRC and provided additional insight into the biological mechanisms underlying CRC development.","author_count":51,"contributors":["Chen, Zhishan","Guo, Xingyi","Tao, Ran","Huyghe, Jeroen R","Law, Philip J","Fernandez-Rozadilla, Ceres","Ping, Jie","Jia, Guochong","Long, Jirong","Li, Chao","Shen, Quanhu","Xie, Yuhan","Timofeeva, Maria","Thomas, Minta","Schmit, Stephanie L","Díez-Obrero, Virginia","Devall, Matthew","Moratalla-Navarro, Ferran","Fernandez-Tajes, Juan","Palles, Claire","Sherwood, Kitty","Briggs, Sarah E W","Svinti, Victoria","Donnelly, Kevin","Farrington, Susan M","Blackmur, James","Vaughan-Shaw, Peter G","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Lu, Yingchang","Broderick, Peter","Studd, James","Harrison, Ta