{"abstract":"The extreme dry and hot 2015/16 El Niño episode caused large losses in tropical live aboveground carbon (AGC) stocks. Followed by climatic conditions conducive to high vegetation productivity since 2016, tropical AGC are expected to recover from large losses during the El Niño episode; however, the recovery rate and its spatial distribution remain unknown. Here, we used low-frequency microwave satellite data to track AGC changes, and showed that tropical AGC stocks returned to pre-El Niño levels by the end of 2020, resulting in an AGC sink of (Formula presented.) Pg C year−1 during 2014–2020. This sink was dominated by strong AGC increases ((Formula presented.) Pg C year−1) in non-forest woody vegetation during 2016–2020, compensating the forest AGC losses attributed to the El Niño event, forest loss, and degradation. Our findings highlight that non-forest woody vegetation is an increasingly important contributor to interannual to decadal variability in the global carbon cycle.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Fan, Lei","Cui, Tianxiang","Wigneron, Jean-Pierre","Ciais, Philippe","Sitch, Stephen","Brandt, Martin","Li, Xin","Niu, Shuli","Xiao, Xiangming","Chave, Jérome","Wu, Chaoyang","Li, Wei","Yuan, Wenping","Xing, Zanpin","Li, Xiaojun","Wang, Mengjia","Liu, Xiangzhuo","Chen, Xiuzhi","Qin, Yuanwei","Yang, Hui","Tang, Qiang","Li, Yuechen","Ma, Mingguo","Fensholt, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754538"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique (CNRS)","Chinese Academy of Sciences","INRAE","Max Planck Institute for Biogeochemistry","Nanjing Forestry University","Paris-Saclay University","Peking University","Southwest University","Sun Yat-Sen University","Tsinghua University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Exeter","University of Oklahoma","Zhengzhou University"],"keyword":["El Niño","Non forest woody vegetation","Recovery","Remote sensing","Tropics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dominant role of the non forest woody vegetation in the post 000000002015 000000000016 el niño tropical carbon recovery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-754538","identifier":[{"id":"39010751","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85198626603","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6f774d0b-75d4-4911-aae0-8e553a2ca280"],"keyword":["El Niño","aboveground carbon","non-forest woody vegetation","recovery","remote sensing","tropics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F32F0ACFDF0146BB5CDC3419F0D7D9F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"nanjing forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"inrae","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRAE","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"paris saclay university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Saclay University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, 