{"affno":"1","first":"Yuechen","key":"liyuechenpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yuechen","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mingguo","key":"mamingguopau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Mingguo","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Rasmus","key":"fensholtrasmuspau","last":"Fensholt","locid":"26fbbb5c-3853-4be9-8cab-3dce86446363","name":"Fensholt, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-3067-4527","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39010751"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/gcb.17423","issn":["13541013","13652486"],"issn_org":["13541013"],"issue":"7","journal":"Global Change Biology","paperid":"e17423","status":"p","title":"Global Change Biology","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198626603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6f774d0b-75d4-4911-aae0-8e553a2ca280"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dominant role of the non-forest woody vegetation in the post 2015/16 El Niño tropical carbon recovery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754538","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The scale of electric vehicles (EVs) in microgrids is growing prominently. However, the stochasticity of EV charging behavior poses formidable obstacles to exploring their dispatch potential. To solve this issue, an optimization strategy for EV-integrated microgrids considering peer-to-peer (P2P) transactions has been proposed in this paper. This research strategy contributes to the sustainable development of microgrids under large-scale EV integration. Firstly, a novel cooperative operation framework considering P2P transactions is established, in which the impact factors of EV charging are regarded to simulate its stochasticity and the energy trading process of the EV-integrated microgrid participating in P2P transactions is defined. Secondly, cost models for the EV-integrated microgrid are established. Thirdly, a three-stage optimization strategy is proposed to simplify the solving process. It transforms the scheduling problem into three solvable subproblems and restructures them with Lagrangian relaxation. Finally, case studies demonstrate that the proposed strategy optimizes EV load distribution, reduces the overall operational cost of the EV-integrated microgrid, and enhances the economic efficiency of each microgrid participating in P2P transactions.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Tian, Sen","Xiao, Qian","Li, Tianxiang","Jin, Yu","Mu, Yunfei","Jia, Hongjie","Li, Wenhua","Teodorescu, Remus","Guerrero, Josep M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-770530"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Qian"],"country":["China","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hebei University of Technology","Polytechnic University of Catalonia","Tianjin University"],"keyword":["Cooperative operation","Demand response","Energy interaction","Lagrange relaxation","Multi agent","Renewable energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an optimization strategy for ev integrated microgrids considering peer to peer transactions","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su16208955","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-770530","identifier":[{"id":"85207330293","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-77294df1-ee9b-4906-8d12-f0ba561e7114"],"keyword":["EV-integrated microgrid","Lagrange relaxation","cooperative operation","demand response","dispatch optimization","energy interaction","multi agent","peer-to-peer transactions","renewable energy","time-sharing tariff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F8A577C21AF7AABAC80F627511F80AE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/752947164/sustainability-16-08955.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/su16208955","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tianjin university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hebei university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hebei University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Batteries","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Center for Research on Smart Battery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Photovoltaic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronics System Integration and Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"polytechnic university of catalonia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Catalonia","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sen","key":"tiansenpau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Sen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"xiaoqianpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Qian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianxiang","key":"litianxiangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Tianxiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"jinyupau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Yu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunfei","key":"muyunfeipau","last":"Mu","name":"Mu, Yunfei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongjie","key":"jiahongjiepau","last":"Jia","name":"Jia, Hongjie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenhua","key":"liwenhuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wenhua","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Remus","key":"teodorescuremuspau","last":"Teodorescu","locid":"fd2ad1e5-313f-45d9-a445-53a24f644768","name":"Teodorescu, Remus","orcid":"0000-0002-2617-7168","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Josep M.","key":"guerrerojosepmpau","last":"Guerrero","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/su16208955","issn":["20711050"],"issue":"20","journal":"Sustainability","paperid":"8955","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"Sustainability","title_org":"Sustainability (Switzerland)","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207330293"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-77294df1-ee9b-4906-8d12-f0ba561e7114"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An Optimization Strategy for EV-Integrated Microgrids Considering Peer-to-Peer Transactions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-770530","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In large venues like shopping malls and airports, knowledge on the indoor populations fuels applications such as business analytics, venue management, and safety control. In this work, we provide means of modeling populations in partitions of indoor space offline and of monitoring indoor populations continuously, by using indoor positioning data. However, the low-sampling rates of indoor positioning render the data temporally and spatially sparse, which in turn renders the offline capture of indoor populations challenging. It is even more challenging to continuously monitor indoor populations, as positioning data may be missing or not ready yet at the current moment. To address these challenges, we first enable probabilistic modeling of populations in indoor space partitions as Normal distributions. Based on that, we propose two learning-based estimators for on-the-fly prediction of population distributions. Leveraging the prediction-based schemes, we provide a unified continuous query processing framework for a type of query that enables continuous monitoring of populated partitions. The framework encompasses caching and result validity mechanisms to reduce cost and maintain monitoring effectiveness. Extensive experiments on two real data sets show that the proposed estimators are able to outperform the state-of-the-art alternatives and that the query processing framework is effective and efficient.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Li, Xiao","Li, Huan","Lu, Hua","Jensen, Christian S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-771073"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and monitoring of indoor populations using sparse positioning data extension","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.21142","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-771073","ids":["aau-cae39f1a-9d8a-4105-8b23-b3717fec2248"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-758E73775EF039940D65858FF3D9A06A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.21142","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/759393893/2410.21142v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Daisy - Center for Data-intensive Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data Engineering, Science and Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"lixiaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Huan","key":"lihuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Huan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hua","key":"luhuapau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Hua","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian S.","key":"jensenchristianspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"56b675d6-bbf5-4dec-a799-50327f3fc66a","name":"Jensen, Christian S.","orcid":"0000-0002-9697-7670","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2410.21142","pages":"16","publisher":"arXiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cae39f1a-9d8a-4105-8b23-b3717fec2248"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling and Monitoring of Indoor Populations using Sparse Positioning Data (Extension)","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-771073","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: With the implementation of the 11th edition of the International Classification of Diseases (ICD-11) and the publication of the metabolic dysfunction-associated fatty liver disease (MAFLD) nomenclature in 2020, it is important to establish consensus for the coding of MAFLD in ICD-11. This will inform subsequent revisions of ICD-11. Methods: Using the Qualtrics XM and WJX platforms, questionnaires were sent online to MAFLD-ICD-11 coding collaborators, authors of papers, and relevant association members. Results: A total of 890 international experts in various fields from 61 countries responded to the survey. We also achieved full coverage of provincial-level administrative regions in China. 77.1% of respondents agreed that MAFLD should be represented in ICD-11 by updating NAFLD, with no significant regional differences (77.3% in Asia and 76.6% in non-Asia, p = 0.819). Over 80% of respondents agreed or somewhat agreed with the need to assign specific codes for progressive stages of MAFLD (i.e. steatohepatitis) (92.2%), MAFLD combined with comorbidities (84.1%), or MAFLD subtypes (i.e., lean, overweight/obese, and diabetic) (86.1%). Conclusions: This global survey by a collaborative panel of clinical, coding, health management and policy experts, indicates agreement that MAFLD should be coded in ICD-11. The data serves as a foundation for corresponding adjustments in the ICD-11 revision.","author_count":95,"contributors":["Zhang, Huai","Targher, Giovanni","Byrne, Christopher D","Kim, Seung Up","Wong, Vincent Wai-Sun","Valenti, Luca","Glickman, Myer","Ponce, Jaime","Mantzoros, Christos S","Crespo, Javier","Gronbaek, Henning","Yang, Wah","Eslam, Mohammed","Wong, Robert J","Machado, Mariana Verdelho","Yu, Ming-Lung","Ghanem, Omar M","Okanoue, Takeshi","Liu, Jun-Feng","Lee, Yong-Ho","Xu, Xiao-Yuan","Pan, Qiuwei","Sui, Meili","Lonardo, Amedeo","Yilmaz, Yusuf","Zhu, Li-Yong","Moreno, Christophe","Miele, Luca","Lupsor-Platon, Monica","Zhao, Lei","LaMasters, Teresa LeAnn","Gish, Robert G","Zhang, Huijie","Nedelcu, Marius","Chan, Wah Kheong","Xia, Ming-Feng","Bril, Fernando","Shi, Jun-Ping","Datz, Christian","Romeo, Stefano","Sun, Jian","Liu, Dan","Sookoian, Silvia","Mao, Yi-Min","Méndez-Sánchez, Nahum","Wang, Xiao-Yan","Pyrsopoulos, Nikolaos T","Fan, Jian-Gao","Fouad, Yasser","Sun, Dan-Qin","Giannini, Cosimo","Chai, Jin","Xia, Ze-Feng","Jun, Dae Won","Li, Guo-Jing","Treeprasertsuk, Sombat","Li, Ying-Xu","Cheung, Tan To","Zhang, Faming","Goh, George Boon-Bee","Furuhashi, Masato","Seto, Wai-Kay","Huang, Hui","Di Sessa, Anna","Li, Qing-Hong","Cholongitas, Evangelos","Zhang, Le","Silveira, Themis Reverbel","Sebastiani, Giada","Adams, Leon A","Chen, Wei","Qi, Xiaolong","Rankovic, Ivan","De Ledinghen, Victor","Lv, Wen-Jie","Hamaguchi, Masahide","Kassir, Radwan","Müller-Wieland, Dirk","Romero-Gomez, Manuel","Xu, Ying","Xu, Yi-Cong","Chen, Shi-Yao","Kermansaravi, Mohammad","Kuchay, Mohammad Shafi","Lefere, Sander","Parmar, Chetan","Lip, Gregory Y H","Liu, Chun-Jen","Åberg, Fredrik","Lau, George","George, Jacob","Sarin, Shiv Kumar","Zhou, Jing-Ya","Zheng, Ming-Hua"],"cuid":["S02-093.38-751619"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["MAFLD ICD-11 coding collaborators"],"corresponding_author":["Zheng, Ming-Hua","Zhou, Jing-Ya"],"country":["Argentina","Australia","Austria","Belgium","China","Finland","Germany","Hong Kong","India","Iran","Italy","Japan","Malaysia","Mexico","Netherlands","Romania","Singapore","Slovakia","South Korea","Spain","Sweden","Taiwan","Thailand","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Capital Institute of Pediatrics","Catholic University in Ruzomberok","Central South University","China-Japan Friendship