{"abstract":"Compared to the particle-gas partition coefficients (KPG), the rain-gas (KRG) and snow-gas (KSG) partition coefficients are also essential in studying the environmental behavior and fate of chemicals in the atmosphere. While the temperature dependence for the KPG have been extensively studied, the study for KRG and KSG are still lacking. Adsorption coefficients between water surface-air (KIA) and snow surface-air (KJA), as well as partition coefficients between water-air (KWA) and octanol-air (KOA) are vital in calculating KRG and KSG. These four basic adsorption and partition coefficients are also temperature-dependent, given by the well-known two-parameters Antoine equation logKXY = AXY + BXY/T, where KXY is the adsorption or partition coefficients, AXY and BXY are Antoine parameters (XY stand for IA, JA, WA, and OA), and T is the temperature in Kelvin. In this study, the parameters AXY and BXY are calculated for 943 chemicals, and logKXY can be estimated at any ambient temperature for these chemicals using these Antoine parameters. The results are evaluated by comparing these data with published experimental and modeled data, and the results show reasonable accuracy. Based on these coefficients, temperature-dependence of logKRG and logKSG is studied. It is found that both logKRG and logKSG are linearly related to 1/T, and Antoine parameters for logKRG and logKSG are also estimated. Distributions of the 943 chemicals in the atmospheric phases (gas, particle, and rain/snow), are illustrated in a Chemical Space Map. The findings reveal that, at environmental temperatures and precipitation days, the dominant state for the majority of chemicals is the gaseous phase. All the AXY and BXY values for logKSG, logKRG, and basic adsorption and partition coefficients, both modeled by this study and collected from published work, are systematically organized into an accessible dataset for public utilization.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Yang, Pu Fei","Ma, Wan Li","Xiao, Hang","Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","Wang, Liang","Sun, Jing Jing","Liu, Li Yan","Zhang, Zi Feng","Jia, Hong Liang","Li, Yi Fan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745080"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Yi Fan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Dalian Maritime University","Harbin Institute of Technology","Heilongjiang University","Third Institute of Oceanography, Ministry of Natural Resources"],"keyword":["Partition coefficients","Temperature dependent"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temperature dependence of the rain gas and snow gas partition coefficients for nearly a thousand chemicals","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85196168882","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745080","identifier":[{"id":"85196168882","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38871187","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ad1d1c37-2307-46db-b583-a31ebef4ab76"],"keyword":["Adsorption coefficients","Antoine parameters","Partition coefficients","Rain-gas partition","Snow-gas partition","Temperature-dependent"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4BBBBECDDAAFF97CA43925C7D146C18B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"heilongjiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Heilongjiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Environmental Science, Department of Environmental Science - Atmospheric Emissions & Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"third institute of oceanography ministry of natural resources","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Third Institute of Oceanography, Ministry of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"dalian maritime university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Dalian Maritime University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pu Fei","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Pu Fei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wan Li","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Wan Li","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hang","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Hang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaj M.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"85f79280-93e9-4d5f-aaec-c245958a6b24","name":"Hansen, Kaj Mantzius","name_org":"Hansen, Kaj M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Liang","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Liang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing Jing","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Jing Jing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Li Yan","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Li Yan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zi Feng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zi Feng","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong Liang","key":"jiapau","last":"Jia","name":"Jia, Hong Liang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi Fan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yi Fan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38871187"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2024.142565","issn":["00456535","18791298"],"issn_org":["00456535"],"journal":"Chemosphere","paperid":"142565","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Chemosphere","volume":"362"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196168882"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ad1d1c37-2307-46db-b583-a31ebef4ab76"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Temperature dependence of the rain-gas and snow-gas partition coefficients for nearly a thousand chemicals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745080","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Soil microbes regulate various biogeochemical cycles on Earth and respond rapidly to climate change, which is accompanied by changes in soil pH. However, the long-term patterns of these changes under future climate scenarios remain unclear. We propose a core-bacteria-forecast model (CoBacFM) to model soil pH changes by shifts of core bacterial groups under future scenarios using a curated soil microbiota dataset of global grasslands. Our model estimates that soil pH will increase in 63.8%–67.0% of grassland regions and decrease in 10.1%–12.4% of regions. Approximately 32.5%–32.9% of regions will become more alkaline by 5.6%, and these areas expand in all future scenarios. These results were supported by 14 warming simulation experiments. Using bacterial responses as bioindicators of soil pH, the CoBacFM method can accurately forecast pH changes in future scenarios, and the changing global climate is likely to result in the alkalization of grasslands.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Feng, Kai","Wang, Shang","He, Qing","Bonkowski, Michael","Bahram, Mohammad","Yergeau, Etienne","Wang, Zhujun","Peng, Xi","Wang, Danrui","Li, Shuzhen","Wang, Yingcheng","Ju, Zhicheng","Du, Xiongfeng","Yan, Chengliang","Gu, Songsong","Li, Tong","Yang, Xingsheng","Shen, Wenli","Wei, Ziyan","Hu, Qiulong","Li, Pengfei","Zhu, Yanmei","Lu, Guangxin","Qin, Clara","Zhang, Gengxin","Xiao, Chunwang","Yang, Yunfeng","Zhou, Jizhong","Deng, Ye"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752722"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Deng, Ye"],"country":["Canada","China","Estonia","Germany","Hong Kong","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Microbiology","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Chinese Research Academy of Environmental Sciences","Hainan University","Hong Kong University of Science and Technology","Hunan Agricultural University","Institut National de la Recherche Scientifique - Canada","Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory","Minzu University of China","Qinghai University","Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences","Tsinghua University","University of California at Santa Cruz","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Cologne","University of Oklahoma","University of Tartu"],"keyword":["Alkaline","Bacteria","Biogeography","Climate change","Soil pH","Warming","model prediction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cobacfm core bacteria forecast model for global grassland ph dynamics under future climate warming scenarios","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oneear.2024.06.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752722","identifier":[{"id":"85198594077","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-30fc4650-3db8-4c75-bed2-f9f6a4e410b0"],"keyword":["alkaline","bacteria","biogeography","climate change","grassland microbiome","model prediction","soil pH","warming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C24C58C5644B5461581474299F3A6147"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.oneear.2024.06.002","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese research academy of environmental sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Research Academy of Environmental Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of cologne","loc":["Ger