e":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Gengxin","key":"zhanggengxinpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Gengxin","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15","corresponding":null,"first":"Chunwang","key":"xiaochunwangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Chunwang","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"16","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunfeng","key":"yangyunfengpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Yunfeng","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"17 18","corresponding":null,"first":"Jizhong","key":"zhoujizhongpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Jizhong","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ye","key":"dengyepau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Ye","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.oneear.2024.06.002","issn":["25903322","25903330"],"issn_org":["25903330"],"issue":"7","journal":"One Earth","pages":"1275-1287","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"One Earth","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198594077"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-30fc4650-3db8-4c75-bed2-f9f6a4e410b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"CoBacFM : Core bacteria forecast model for global grassland pH dynamics under future climate warming scenarios","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752722","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Stinels are a novel class of N-methyl-D-aspartate glutamate receptor (NMDAR) positive allosteric modulators. We explored mechanism of action and NR2 subtype specificity of the stinel zelquistinel (ZEL) in HEK 293 cells expressing recombinant NMDARs. ZEL potently enhanced NMDAR current at NR2A (EC50 = 9.9 ± 0.5 nM) and NR2C-containing (EC50 = 9.7 ± 0.6 nM) NMDARs, with a larger ceiling enhancement at NR2B-NMDAR (EC50 = 35.0 ± 0.7 nM), while not affecting NR2D-containing NMDARs. In cells expressing NR2A and NR2C-containing NMDARs, ZEL exhibited an inverted-U dose-response relation, with a low concentration enhancement and high concentration suppression of NMDAR currents. Extracellular application of ZEL potentiated NMDAR receptor activity via prolongation of NMDAR currents. Replacing the slow Ca2+ intracellular chelator EGTA with the fast chelator BAPTA blocked ZEL potentiation of NMDARs, suggesting an action on intracellular Ca2+-calmodulin-dependent inactivation (CDI). Consistent with this mechanism of action, removal of the NR1 intracellular C-terminus, or intracellular infusion of a calmodulin blocking peptide, blocked ZEL potentiation of NMDAR current. In contrast, BAPTA did not prevent high-dose suppression of current, indicating this effect has a different mechanism of action. These data indicate ZEL is a novel positive allosteric modulator that binds extracellularly and acts through a unique long-distance mechanism to reduce NMDAR CDI, eliciting enhancement of NMDAR current. The critical role that NMDARs play in long-term, activity-dependent synaptic plasticity, learning, memory and cognition, suggests dysregulation of CDI may contribute to psychiatric disorders such as depression, schizophrenia and others, and that the stinel class of drugs can restore NMDAR-dependent synaptic plasticity by reducing activity-dependent CDI.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhang, Xiao lei","Li, Yong Xin","Berglund, Nils A.","Burgdorf, Jeffrey S.","Donello, John E.","Moskal, Joseph R.","Stanton, Patric K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-758582"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stanton, Patric K."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["AbbVie Inc","All Global Affiliations","Gate Neurosciences Inc.","New York Medical College","Northwestern University"],"keyword":["Calmodulin","N methyl D aspartate receptor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"zelquistinel acts at an extracellular binding domain to modulate intracellular calcium inactivation of n methyl d aspartate receptors","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuropharm.2024.110100","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-758582","identifier":[{"id":"39117105","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85200801492","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-daade65c-1861-441f-8584-deda59d05418"],"keyword":["Calcium-dependent inactivation","Calmodulin","HEK cell","Long-term plasticity","N-Methyl-D-aspartate receptor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65F823BB6F456C1B6156397C8FBDF134"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neuropharm.2024.110100","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"new york medical college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York Medical College","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"abbvie inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"AbbVie Inc","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"gate neurosciences inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Gate Neurosciences Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"northwestern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northwestern University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao lei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong Xin","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yong Xin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils","key":"berglundpau","last":"Berglund","locid":"7f7ccb56-0069-487e-a8ef-e0b7e429f81a","name":"Berglund, Nils A.","name_org":"Berglund, Nils","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeffrey S.","key":"burgdorfpau","last":"Burgdorf","name":"Burgdorf, Jeffrey S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"John E.","key":"donellopau","last":"Donello","name":"Donello, John E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph R.","key":"moskalpau","last":"Moskal","name":"Moskal, Joseph R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patric K.","key":"stantonpau","last":"Stanton","name":"Stanton, Patric K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39117105"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.neuropharm.2024.110100","issn":["00283908","18737064"],"issn_org":["00283908"],"journal":"Neuropharmacology","paperid":"110100","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Neuropharmacology","volume":"259"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200801492"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-daade65c-1861-441f-8584-deda59d05418"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Zelquistinel acts at an extracellular binding domain to modulate intracellular calcium inactivation of N-methyl-D-aspartate receptors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-758582","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, many reviews have been made for MXenes and their derivatives, but a systematic overview specifically dedicated to MXenes/bismuth-related composites (i.e., MXenes/Bi-rcs) is still missing. Here we present the recent progress on the design, synthesis, and photo- /electrocatalytic properties of MXenes/Bi-rcs, as well as their applications, aiming to offer new insights and guidance for their future development. We begin by disclosing the synthesis methods of MXenes/Bi-rcs and highlighting the preparation strategies of MXenes which are an important first step in achieving the MXenes/Bi-rcs. Then, we disclose the photo- /electrocatalytic properties and applications of MXenes/Bi-rcs, with a focus of particular concern on the interplay of Bi element with the functional groups of MXenes and for the mechanisms that account for the enhanced photo- /electroactivity and durability. Finally, we show the promising opportunities of MXenes/Bi-rcs associated with the potential challenges of this emerging research branch.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Li, Dongsheng","Wang, Guanyu","Ye, Yuanfeng","Boutinaud, Philippe","Zheng, Xu","Xu, Jie","Li, Dongzhe","He, Zhiyu","Huang, Wei","Xiao, Sanshui","Kang, Fengwen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764231"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kang, Fengwen"],"country":["China","France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paul Sabatier University - Toulouse III","Sichuan University","Southwest Medical University","Université Clermont Auvergne"],"keyword":["Electrocatalysis","MXenes","Photocatalysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recent advances in the synthesis photo electrocatalytic properties and applications of mxenes bismuth related composites","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85203417689","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764231","identifier":[{"id":"85203417689","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001313821700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-6062ee6d-1510-4096-9ee1-3dab0dca8796"],"keyword":["Bismuth (Bi)","Electrocatalysis","MXenes","MXenes/Bi composites","Photocatalysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-767EC62489AE80B4DB83519B799F9802"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-09-10","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"université clermont auvergne","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université Clermont Auvergne","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"southwest medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"paul sabatier university toulouse iii","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paul Sabatier University - Toulouse III","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Quantum Photonics of Low-dimensional Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongsheng","key":"lidongshengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Dongsheng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guanyu","key":"wangguanyupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Guanyu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuanfeng","key":"yeyuanfengpau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Yuanfeng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philippe","key":"boutinaudphilippepau","last":"Boutinaud","name":"Boutinaud, Philippe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xu","key":"zhengxupau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Xu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"xujiepau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Jie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongzhe","key":"lidongzhepau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Dongzhe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhiyu","key":"hezhiyupau","last":"He","name":"He, Zhiyu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"huangweipau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Wei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sanshui","key":"xiaosanshuipau","last":"Xiao","locid":"c516dded-c5eb-40a6-b2dd-37be55b893c8","name":"Xiao, Sanshui","orcid":"0000-0001-6529-5047","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengwen","key":"kangfengwenpau","last":"Kang","name":"Kang, Fengwen","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cej.2024.155098","issn":["13858947","18733212"],"issn_org":["13858947"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering Journal","paperid":"155098","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering Journal","volume":"498"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203417689"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6062ee6d-1510-4096-9ee1-3dab0dca8796"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Recent advances in the synthesis, photo-/electrocatalytic properties and applications of MXenes/bismuth-related composites","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764231","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Habitat degradation is one of the most serious environmental problems worldwide, which threatens human wellbeing and sustainable development. Exploring how to protect natural habitats has become a research hotspot in the environmental management field. Ecological zoning has been widely used in habitat protection, but its actual effectiveness has been rarely revealed, especially with the robust and reliable causal inference method. Therefore, taking the Yangtze River Economic Belt (YREB) in China as the study area, we first quantified habitat quality and changes at the district/county scale during 2005–2019. Then, we used the National Key Ecological Function Zone (NKEFZ) as a representative ecological zone scheme, and explored the effectiveness of the NKEFZ in protecting habitat quality with the Propensity Score Matching and Difference-in-Difference combined method, which is a representative causal inference method. We found that habitat quality showed an uneven distribution during the study period, and habitat quality of districts/counties within the NKEFZ was higher than that outside the NKEFZ with statistical significance. Most districts/counties experienced a habitat quality decrease, but the decrease within the NKEFZ is less than that outside the NKEFZ. We observed that the NKEFZ can protect habitat quality from the causal relationship perspective, but there was the spatio-temporal heterogeneity of the NKEFZ effectiveness. In terms of the spatial dimension, the NKEFZ was the most effective in the Lower Reach of the YREB. In terms of the temporal dimension, there was a 1-year time-lag effect of the NKEFZ effectiveness, and NKEFZ effectiveness experienced a sharp increase from 2016. The NKEFZ contributed to protecting habitat quality through multiple management strategies such as urban land quota, high pollution industry prohibition, and ecological compensation. Overall, this study verified that the ecological zone scheme can contribute to habitat quality protection, and emphasizes that the effectiveness of ecological zoning may vary across time and space. This work can support ecological zoning implementation with robust evidence, and provides a novel perspective for understanding the effectiveness of ecological zoning.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Li, Kai","Yan, Xiao Lei","Hou, Ying","Lv, Bingyang","Huang, Youyou","Liu, Jing","Han, Haiting","Li, Xi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765137"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","King's College London","Nanjing Normal University","Sichuan Agricultural University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Causal inference","Ecological protection","Habitat quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can ecological zoning act as an environmental management tool for protecting regional habitat quality causal evidence from the national key ecological function zone in china","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-765137","identifier":[{"id":"85203785848","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7e698528-dfe1-4bc3-9cd5-970d677d9fec"],"keyword":["Causal inference","Ecological protection","Ecological zoning","Effectiveness evaluation","Habitat quality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8537653D5BD2AFCBD33B2419290B12D8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sichuan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"nanjing normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Normal University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kai","key":"likaipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Kai","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xiao Lei","key":"yanxiaoleipau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Xiao Lei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Ying","key":"houyingpau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Ying","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bingyang","key":"lvbingyangpau","last":"Lv","name":"Lv, Bingyang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Youyou","key":"huangyouyoupau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Youyou","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jing","key":"liujingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","first":"Haiting","key":"hanhaitingpau","last":"Han","locid":"2ec73c63-a398-4a0b-8f9e-7b8d6a617dcf","name":"Han, Haiting","orcid":"0000-0001-9468-1094","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xi","key":"lixipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jclepro.2024.143623","issn":["09596526"],"journal":"Journal of Cleaner Production","paperid":"143623","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cleaner Production","volume":"475"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203785848"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7e698528-dfe1-4bc3-9cd5-970d677d9fec"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Can ecological zoning act as an environmental management tool for protecting regional habitat quality : Causal evidence from the national key ecological function zone in China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765137","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Pangenomes are collections of annotated genome sequences of multiple individuals of a species1. The structural variants uncovered by these datasets are a major asset to genetic analysis in crop plants2. Here we report a pangenome of barley comprising long-read sequence assemblies of 76 wild and domesticated genomes and short-read sequence data of 1,315 genotypes. An expanded catalogue of sequence variation in the crop includes structurally complex loci that are rich in gene copy number variation. To demonstrate the utility of the pangenome, we focus on four loci involved in disease resistance, plant architecture, nutrient release and trichome development. Novel allelic variation at a powdery mildew resistance locus and population-specific copy number gains in a regulator of vegetative branching were found. Expansion of a family of starch-cleaving enzymes in elite malting barleys was linked to shifts in enzymatic activity in micro-malting trials. Deletion of an enhancer motif is likely to change the developmental trajectory of the hairy appendages on barley grains. Our findings indicate that allelic diversity at structurally complex loci may have helped crop plants to adapt to new selective regimes in agricultural ecosystems.","author_count":80,"contributors":["Jayakodi, Murukarthick","Lu, Qiongxian","Pidon, Hélène","Rabanus-Wallace, M Timothy","Bayer, Micha","Lux, Thomas","Guo, Yu","Jaegle, Benjamin","Badea, Ana","Bekele, Wubishet","Brar, Gurcharn S","Braune, Katarzyna","Bunk, Boyke","Chalmers, Kenneth J","Chapman, Brett","Jørgensen, Morten Egevang","Feng, Jia-Wu","Feser, Manuel","Fiebig, Anne","Gundlach, Heidrun","Guo, Wenbin","Haberer, Georg","Hansson, Mats","Himmelbach, Axel","Hoffie, Iris","Hoffie, Robert E","Hu, Haifei","Isobe, Sachiko","König, Patrick","Kale, Sandip M.","Kamal, Nadia","Keeble-Gagnère, Gabriel","Keller, Beat","Knauft, Manuela","Koppolu, Ravi","Krattinger, Simon G","Kumlehn, Jochen","Langridge, Peter","Li, Chengdao","Marone, Marina 