{"abstract":"Designing anodic electrocatalysts with high activity and robust stability for acidic oxygen evolution reaction (OER) is significant for the large-scale promotion of sustainable proton exchange membrane water electrolysis (PEMWE). Most reported Ru-based electrocatalysts tend to further improve activity at the expense of stability. Herein, we report the synthesis of crystalline Mn 3O 4 supported Ru-RuO 2 nano-heterostructures as the anodic electrocatalyst that only requires a low overpotential of 182 mV (10 mA cm −2) for acidic OER, accompanied with a record stability of 400 h in 0.5 M H 2SO 4. The results of XPS, ICP-MS, and XAS indicate that the Mn 3O 4 substrate plays a crucial role in stabilizing Ru-RuO 2 nano-heterostructure by preventing Ru from over-oxidation and dissolution. Meanwhile, DEMS with isotope labeling reveals that the Ru-RuO 2 nano-heterostructure contributes to suppressing lattice oxygen oxidation mechanism (LOM) and concurrently expediting the involvement of adsorbate evolution mechanism (AEM) for boosting the acidic OER performance.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Long, Xin","Zhao, Bin","Zhao, Qianqian","Wu, Xuexian","Zhu, Meng-Nan","Feng, Renfei","Shakouri, Mohsen","Zhang, Yu","Xiao, Xinxin","Zhang, Jiujun","Fu, Xian-Zhu","Luo, Jing-Li"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705289"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai University","Shenzhen University","University of Alberta","University of Saskatchewan"],"keyword":["Heterostructure","Stability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ru ruo000000000002 nano heterostructures stabilized by the sacrificing oxidation strategy of mn000000000003o000000000004 substrate for boosting acidic oxygen evolution reaction","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/764681575/SSRN-id4565665.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors acknowledge the financial support of Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation (No. 2023A1515010940 ), Shenzhen Natural Science Fund (the Stable Support Plan Program No. 20220809160022001 ), National Natural Science Foundation of China (No. 21805187, 21975163 ), and the Shenzhen Science and Technology Programs (No. ZDSYS20220527171401003, KQTD20190929173914967 ). The authors also thank Shiyanjia Lab (www.shiyanjia.com) for the XPS characterizations."],"id":"S01-000.00-705289","identifier":[{"id":"85178112818","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5f00ad17-1efa-48d0-9af5-1c695c0ab39c"],"keyword":["MnO substrate","Ru-based electrocatalysts","acidic OER","heterostructure","stability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A76DBCC6607CEB198FEA0B50BA1E2B1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/764681575/SSRN-id4565665.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shenzhen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shenzhen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of alberta","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Alberta","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university of saskatchewan","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Saskatchewan","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, [Mission] A Sustainable Danish Energy System"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"shanghai university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin","key":"longxinpau","last":"Long","name":"Long, Xin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"zhaobinpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Bin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qianqian","key":"zhaoqianqianpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Qianqian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xuexian","key":"wuxuexianpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xuexian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Meng-Nan","key":"zhumengnanpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Meng-Nan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Renfei","key":"fengrenfeipau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Renfei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"shakourimohsenpau","last":"Shakouri","name":"Shakouri, Mohsen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"zhangyupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaoxinxinpau","last":"Xiao","locid":"fd69114c-9434-44ba-b01b-e9ecb3831cae","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiujun","key":"zhangjiujunpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jiujun","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xian-Zhu","key":"fuxianzhupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Xian-Zhu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing-Li","key":"luojinglipau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Jing-Li","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apcatb.2023.123559","issn":["09263373","18733883"],"issn_org":["09263373"],"journal":"Applied Catalysis B: Environmental","paperid":"123559","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Catalysis B: Environmental","volume":"343"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178112818"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5f00ad17-1efa-48d0-9af5-1c695c0ab39c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Ru-RuO2 nano-heterostructures stabilized by the sacrificing oxidation strategy of Mn3O4 substrate for boosting acidic oxygen evolution reaction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705289","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"It is long observed that females tend to live longer than males in nearly every country. However, the underlying mechanism remains elusive. In this study, we discovered that genetic associations with longevity are on average stronger in females than in males through bio-demographic analyses of genome-wide association studies (GWAS) dataset of 2178 centenarians and 2299 middle-age controls of Chinese Longitudinal Healthy Longevity Study (CLHLS). This discovery is replicated across North and South regions of China, and is further confirmed by North-South discovery/replication analyses of different and independent datasets of Chinese healthy aging candidate genes with CLHLS participants who are not in CLHLS GWAS, including 2972 centenarians and 1992 middle-age controls. Our polygenic risk score analyses of eight exclusive groups of sex-specific genes, analyses of sex-specific and not-sex-specific individual genes, and Genome-wide Complex Trait Analysis using all SNPs all reconfirm that genetic associations with longevity are on average stronger in females than in males. Our discovery/replication analyses are based on genetic datasets of in total 5150 centenarians and compatible middle-age controls, which comprises the worldwide largest sample of centenarians. The present study's findings may partially explain the well-known male-female health-survival paradox and suggest that genetic variants may be associated with different reactions between males and females to the same vaccine, drug treatment and/or nutritional intervention. Thus, our findings provide evidence to steer away from traditional view that “one-size-fits-all” for clinical interventions, and to consider sex differences for improving healthcare efficiency. We suggest future investigations focusing on effects of interactions between sex-specific genetic variants and environment on longevity as well as biological function.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Zeng, Yi","Chen, Huashuai","Liu, Xiaomin","Song, Zijun","Lei, Xiaoyan","Lv, Xiaozhen","Cheng, Lingguo","Chen, Zhihua","Bai, Chen","Yin, Zhaoxue","Lv, Yuebin","Lu, Jiehua","Li, Jianxin","Land, Kenneth C","Yashin, Anatoli I","O'Rand, Angela M","Sun, Liang","Yang, Ze","Tao, Wei","Gu, Jun","Gottschalk, William","Tan, Qihua","Christensen, Kaare","Hesketh, Therese","Tian, Xiao-Li","Yang, Huanming","Egidi, Viviana","Caselli, Graziella","Robine, Jean-Marie","Wang, Hualin","Shi, Xiaoming","Vaupel, James W.","Lutz, Michael W","Nie, Chao","Min, Junxia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-723675"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zeng, Yi"],"country":["China","France","Italy","Singapore","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","BGI Shenzhen","Beijing Hospital","Business School of Xiangtan University","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Chinese Center for Disease Control and Prevention","College of Information Science and Electronic Engineering, Zhejiang University","Duke University","Duke-National University of Singapore","Ecole Pratique des Hautes Etudes (EPHE)","French National Institute of Health","Institut National de la Sante et de la Recherche Medicale (INSERM)","Nanchang University","Nanjing University","Peking University","Sapienza University of Rome","University College London"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic associations with longevity are on average stronger in females than in males","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2023.e23691","version":"Publ