{"abstract":"Mitochondria, the versatile organelles crucial for cellular and organismal viability, play a pivotal role in meeting the energy requirements of cells through the respiratory chain located in the inner mitochondrial membrane, concomitant with the generation of reactive oxygen species (ROS). A wealth of evidence derived from contemporary investigations on reproductive longevity strongly indicates that the aberrant elevation of ROS level constitutes a fundamental factor in hastening the aging process of reproductive systems which are responsible for transmission of DNA to future generations. Constant changes in redox status, with a pro-oxidant shift mainly through the mitochondrial generation of ROS, are linked to the modulation of physiological and pathological pathways in gametes and reproductive tissues. Furthermore, the quantity and quality of mitochondria essential to capacitation and fertilization are increasingly associated with reproductive aging. The article aims to provide current understanding of the contributions of ROS derived from mitochondrial respiration to the process of reproductive aging. Moreover, understanding the impact of mitochondrial dysfunction on both female and male fertility is conducive to finding therapeutic strategies to slow, prevent or reverse the process of gamete aging, and thereby increase reproductive longevity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Song, Jiangbo","Xiao, Li","Zhang, Zhehao","Wang, Yujin","Kouis, Panayiotis","Rasmussen, Lene Juel","Dai, Fangyin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730267"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Southwest University"],"keyword":["Aging","Fertility","Gamete quality","Mitochondria","ROS","Reproductive health"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of reactive oxygen species and mitochondrial dysfunction on reproductive aging","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcell.2024.1347286","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730267","identifier":[{"id":"85186911897","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38465288","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10920300","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-00f5c30d-8b57-458b-88a5-d5b533c6eda6"],"keyword":["ROS","aging","fertility","gamete quality","mitochondria","reproductive health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D163A295EE07B694758699F92EA1018"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385230289/fcell_12_1347286.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcell.2024.1347286","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jiangbo","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Jiangbo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Li","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Li","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhehao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhehao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yujin","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yujin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Panayiotis","key":"kouispau","last":"Kouis","name":"Kouis, Panayiotis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene Juel","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"54d5267c-3c91-45bc-ace5-1d0edb1b250d","name":"Rasmussen, Lene Juel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fangyin","key":"daipau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Fangyin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38465288"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fcell.2024.1347286","issn":["2296634X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Cell and Developmental Biology","paperid":"1347286","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Cell and Developmental Biology","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186911897"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-00f5c30d-8b57-458b-88a5-d5b533c6eda6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of reactive oxygen species and mitochondrial dysfunction on reproductive aging","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730267","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"DC power flow controller (DCPFC) is regarded as an effective technology to improve the power distribution capability in a complex dc power grid. Among different types of DCPFCs, the interline dc power flow controller (IDCPFC) can realize multiline power flow control functions in a complex dc grid. In this paper, a modular interline dc power flow controller based on switch isolation (ISO-IDCPFC) and a decoupling and phase shift control method of ISO-IDCPFC are proposed. ISO-IDCPFC has the advantages of modularity, scalability and multi-level outputs. By utilizing the dual-target decoupling and multi-carrier phase shift control method, ISO-IDCPFC can realize flexible and economical line current adjustment. Based on these, simulation models built in PLECS and downscaled experiment setup are used to validate the effectiveness of the proposed topology and the control method.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Tuo, Chaoqun","Xu, Qianming","Hu, Jiayu","Guo, Peng","Li, Yuze","Xiao, Muxuan","Guerrero, Josep M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-735653"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Hu, Jiayu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan University","State Grid Corporation of China","Xiamen University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"decoupling and phase shift control method of modular interline dc power flow controller","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85179084830&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-735653","identifier":[{"id":"85179084830","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-09adfbd3-3927-4bc2-a53d-77ba1f958658"],"keyword":["DC power grid","dual-target decoupling","interline dc power flow controller","multi-carrier phase shift","multi-level output"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09C6CCEA16833E480BFC3FD025566B31"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"hunan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state grid corporation of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Grid Corporation of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"xiamen university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xiamen University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Center for Research on Microgrids​","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chaoqun","key":"tuopau","last":"Tuo","name":"Tuo, Chaoqun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qianming","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Qianming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiayu","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Jiayu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Peng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuze","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yuze","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Muxuan","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Muxuan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Josep M.","key":"guerreropau","last":"Guerrero","locid":"07d2eed6-2177-4f61-b812-a08c55b2e8af","name":"Guerrero, Josep M.","orcid":"0000-0001-5236-4592","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tpwrd.2023.3337240","issn":["08858977"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Power Delivery","pages":"661-674","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Power Delivery","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179084830"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-09adfbd3-3927-4bc2-a53d-77ba1f958658"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Decoupling and Phase Shift Control Method of Modular Interline DC Power Flow Controller","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-735653","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Contamination of rice by the potent neurotoxin methylmercury (MeHg) originates from microbe-mediated Hg methylation in soils. However, the high diversity of Hg methylating microorganisms in soils hinders the prediction of MeHg formation and challenges the mitigation of MeHg bioaccumulation via regulating soil microbiomes. Here we explored the roles of various cropland microbial communities in MeHg formation in the potentials leading to MeHg accumulation in rice and reveal that Geobacteraceae are the key predictors of MeHg bioaccumulation in paddy soil systems. We characterized Hg methylating microorganisms from 67 cropland ecosystems across 3,600 latitudinal kilometres. The simulations of a rice-paddy biogeochemical model show that MeHg accumulation in rice is 1.3–1.7-fold more sensitive to changes in the relative abundance of Geobacteraceae compared to Hg input, which is recognized as the primary parameter in controlling MeHg exposure. These findings open up a window to predict MeHg formation and accumulation in human food webs, enabling more efficient mitigation of risks to human health through regulations of key soil microbiomes.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Zhong, Huan","Tang, Wenli","Li, Zizhu","Sonne, Christian","Lam, Su Shiung","Zhang, Xiao","Kwon, Sae Yun","Rinklebe, Jörg","Nunes, Luís M.","Yu, Ri Qing","Gu, Baohua","Hintelmann, Holger","Tsui, Martin Tsz Ki","Zhao, Jiating","Zhou, Xin Quan","Wu, Mengjie","Liu, Beibei","Hao, Yunyun","Chen, Long","Zhang, Baogang","Tan, Wenfeng","Zhang, Xu Xiang","Ren, Hongqiang","Liu, Yu Rong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736687"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chen, Long","Liu, Yu Rong","Sonne, Christian","Zhong, Huan"],"country":["Canada","China","Germany","Hong Kong","India","Malaysia","Portugal","South Korea","United States"],"glorg":[