e":"pau"}],"pmid":["38658746"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-024-07324-0","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"8013","journal":"Nature","pages":"843-850","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"629"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85191337518"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-034f2c25-7cf4-4ba3-99dc-280c9fea2d5f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Phylogenomics and the rise of the angiosperms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743555","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Extant Old World camels (genus Camelus) contributed to the economic and cultural exchanges between the East and West for thousands of years.1 , 2 Although many remains have been unearthed,3 , 4 , 5 we know neither whether the prevalent hybridization observed between extant Camelus species2 , 6 , 7 also occurred between extinct lineages and the ancestors of extant Camelus species nor why some populations became extinct while others survived. To investigate these questions, we generated paleogenomic and stable isotope data from an extinct two-humped camel species, Camelus knoblochi. We find that in the mitochondrial phylogeny, all C. knoblochi form a paraphyletic group that nests within the diversity of modern, wild two-humped camels (Camelus ferus). In contrast, they are clearly distinguished from both wild and domesticated (Camelus bactrianus) two-humped camels on the nuclear level. Moreover, the divergence pattern of the three camel species approximates a trifurcation, because the most common topology is only slightly more frequent than the two other possible topologies. This mito-nuclear phylogenetic discordance likely arose due to interspecific gene flow between all three species, suggesting that interspecific hybridization is not exclusive to modern camels but a recurrent phenomenon throughout the evolutionary history of the genus Camelus. These results suggest that the genomic complexity of Old World camels’ evolutionary history is underestimated when considering data from only modern species. Finally, we find that C. knoblochi populations began declining prior to the last glacial maximum and, by integrating palaeoecological evidence and stable isotope data, suggest that this was likely due to failure to adapt to a changing environment.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Yuan, Junxia","Hu, Jiaming","Liu, Wenhui","Chen, Shungang","Zhang, Fengli","Wang, Siren","Zhang, Zhen","Wang, Linying","Xiao, Bo","Li, Fuqiang","Hofreiter, Michael","Lai, Xulong","Westbury, Michael V.","Sheng, Guilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-748615"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China University of Geosciences, Wuhan","Daqing Museum","National Museum of China","University of Potsdam","Zhaoyuan Museum"],"keyword":["Ancient DNA","Evolution","Extinction","Interspecific hybridization","Nucleotide diversity","Phylogenetic tree","Pleistocene","Stable isotope"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i camelus knoblochi i genome reveals the complex evolutionary history of old world camels","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-748615","identifier":[{"id":"38754423","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85194330866","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-904eb82e-3154-4ff0-b4e8-3f688da4f174"],"keyword":["Camelus knoblochi","Pleistocene","ancient DNA","evolution","extinction","interspecific hybridization","nucleotide diversity","phylogenetic tree","stable isotope","two-humped camel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2200453A52BCBFAF8BF665134972B672"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china university of geosciences wuhan","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Geosciences, Wuhan","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"national museum of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"National Museum of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"daqing museum","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Daqing Museum","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"zhaoyuan museum","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhaoyuan Museum","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"university of potsdam","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Potsdam","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Molecular Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Junxia","key":"yuanjunxiapau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Junxia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiaming","key":"hujiamingpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Jiaming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Wenhui","key":"liuwenhuipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Wenhui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shungang","key":"chenshungangpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Shungang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Fengli","key":"zhangfenglipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Fengli","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Siren","key":"wangsirenpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Siren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Zhen","key":"zhangzhenpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Linying","key":"wanglinyingpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Linying","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"xiaobopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Bo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fuqiang","key":"lifuqiangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Fuqiang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Michael","key":"hofreitermichaelpau","last":"Hofreiter","name":"Hofreiter, Michael","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xulong","key":"laixulongpau","last":"Lai","name":"Lai, Xulong","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Michael V.","key":"westburymichaelvpau","last":"Westbury","locid":"db6371bf-5fd0-47fc-8f4d-1536e797be00","name":"Westbury, Michael V.","orcid":"0000-0003-0478-3930","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guilian","key":"shengguilianpau","last":"Sheng","name":"Sheng, Guilian","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38754423"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cub.2024.04.050","issn":["09609822","18790445"],"issn_org":["09609822"],"issue":"11","journal":"Current Biology","status":"p","title":"Current Biology","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194330866"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-904eb82e-3154-4ff0-b4e8-3f688da4f174"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"<i>Camelus knoblochi</i> genome reveals the complex evolutionary history of Old World camels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-748615","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Global climate change is predicted to influence both precipitation amount and frequency in many regions. However, little is known about how precipitation changes affect soil aggregates and soil organic carbon (SOC) in alpine wetlands. Plots of an alpine wetland on the Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau were subjected to two precipitation frequencies (high vs. low, i.e., 1 and 3 times of nature rainfall intervals) crossed with two precipitation amounts (high vs. low, i.e., 100 % and 70 % of the amount of natural rainfall). Two years later, we investigated changes of soil aggregates (silt + clay, < 53 μm; microaggregates, 53∼250 μm; and macroaggregates, >250 μm) and SOC in three soil depths, i.e., 0–15 cm, 15–30 cm and 30–50 cm. Averaged across the three soil depths, the content of SOC and dissolved organic carbon (DOC) in the simulated natural precipitation (high amount, high frequency treatment) were 127.22 g kg−1 and 0.19 g kg−1, respectively. Reducing precipitation amount or frequency led to a 19.6 %-26.2 % increase in SOC, and 28.7 %-44.4 % increase in DOC. Microbial biomass carbon in natural precipitation was 1.33 g kg−1 across the three soil depths, and its response to precipitation varied with soil depths. The fraction of macroaggregates in the 0–15 cm soil depth was 63.5 % in the simulated natural precipitation treatment, and decreased by 18.6 %–21.9 % in response to reduced precipitation amount or frequency. Aggregate fractions in the 15–30 cm soil depth did not respond significantly to the changes of precipitation patterns. Reducing precipitation frequency or amount decreased the contribution of macroaggregate-associated organic carbon to SOC compared to the simulated natural precipitation, but increased the contribution of microaggregate-associated organic carbon, especially in the 0–15 cm soil depth. Structural equation models revealed that SOC was regulated by soil aggregate composition and microbial biomass carbon. The buffering of the surface soil weakened the effects of precipitation changes on aggregates and aggregate-associated organic carbon in the deep soil. These results suggest that reducing precipitation frequency or amount can decrease the fraction of macroaggregates in the surface soil, and weaken the physical protection of macroaggregates for SOC. Thus, changes in precipitation patterns may have a significant impact on SOC storage and stability in alpine wetlands through their influence on soil aggregate composition.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Li, Qian Wei","Zhang, Xiao Ya","Gao, Jun Qin","Rinnan, Riikka","Jiao, Yi","Liang, Jin Feng","Yu, Fei Hai"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754753"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Forestry University","Hainan Tropical Ocean University","Jiangxi Normal University","National Forestry and Grassland Administration","TaiZhou University"],"keyword":["Precipitation","Soil organic carbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"precipitation patterns impact soil aggregates and organic carbon of an alpine wetland on the qinghai tibetan plateau","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-754753","identifier":[{"id":"85199257454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ab7e2ff7-3dc7-479f-9a8d-d53d5508fb3e"],"keyword":["Aggregate associated organic carbon","Alpine wetland","Precipitation","Soil aggregate","Soil organic carbon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25A7574E7CC41349EE87CF0D2A6E92BA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"hainan tropical ocean university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hainan Tropical Ocean University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"national forestry and grassland administration","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"National Forestry and Grassland Administration","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"jiangxi normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangxi Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"taizhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"TaiZhou University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Qian Wei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qian Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Xiao Ya","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"753e7dff-866d-434a-84fe-20c5a479fd8c","name":"Zhang, Xiao Ya","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Jun Qin","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Jun Qin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Riikka","key":"rinnanpau","last":"Rinnan","locid":"aacf3cda-4ceb-4d53-a6cc-ac39022f1208","name":"Rinnan, Riikka","orcid":"0000-0001-7222-700X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yi","key":"jiaopau","last":"Jiao","locid":"b93fcb7b-15db-4332-89c9-d9ad6b0b00ce","name":"Jiao, Yi","orcid":"0000-0001-5027-3144","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Jin Feng","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Jin Feng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Fei Hai","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Fei Hai","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.catena.2024.108249","issn":["03418162","18726887"],"issn_org":["03418162"],"journal":"Catena","paperid":"108249","status":"p","title":"Catena","volume":"244"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199257454"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab7e2ff7-3dc7-479f-9a8d-d53d5508fb3e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Precipitation patterns impact soil aggregates and organic carbon of an alpine wetland on the Qinghai-Tibetan Plateau","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754753","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Both controllable regulation of the conformational structure of a polypeptide and specific recognition of an amino acid are still arduous challenges. Here, a novel dual-mode (electrochemical and colorimetric) biosensor was built for arginine (Arg) recognition based on a conformation switch, utilizing controllable and synergistic self-assembly of a ferrocene-grafted hexadecapeptide (P16Fc) with gold nanoparticles (AuNPs). Benefiting from the flexibility and unique topological structure of P16Fc formed nanospheres, the assembly and disassembly can undergo a conformation transition induced by Arg through controlling the distance and number of Fc detached from the gold surface, producing on-off electrical signals. Also, they can induce aggregation and dispersion of AuNPs in solution, causing a color change. The mechanism of Arg recognition with polypeptide conformation regulation was well explored by combining microstructure characterizations with molecular mechanics calculations. The electrochemical and colorimetric assays for Arg were successfully established in sensitive and selective manner, not only obtaining a very low detection limit, but also effectively eliminating the interference from other amino acids and overcoming the limitation of AuNP aggregation. Notably, the conformational change-based assay with the peptide regulated by the target will make a powerful tool for the amino acid biosensing and health diagnosis.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wu, Ling","Zhu, Kaijie","Xue, Shulei","Wu, Bowen","Xiao, Zhongliang","Feng, Zemeng","Yin, Yulong","Li, Jishan","Yu, Donghong","Cao, Zhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-757459"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Cao, Zhong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Subtropical Agriculture","Changsha University of Science and Technology","Hunan University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dual mode arginine assay based on the conformation switch of a ferrocene grafted polypeptide","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85196948294&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-757459","identifier":[{"id":"85196948294","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ef27f35d-42e8-4be6-ae60-5864ebee4e89"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-30A6711142EC5EAC5C0EA2E14AEB2820"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"changsha university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Changsha University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas institute of subtropical agriculture","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Institute of Subtropical Agriculture","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"hunan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ling","key":"wulingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Ling","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaijie","key":"zhukaijiepau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Kaijie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shulei","key":"xueshuleipau","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Shulei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bowen","key":"wubowenpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Bowen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongliang","key":"xiaozhongliangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Zhongliang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zemeng","key":"fengzemengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Zemeng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yulong","key":"yinyulongpau","last":"Yin","name":"Yin, Yulong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jishan","key":"lijishanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jishan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yudonghongpau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong","key":"caozhongpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhong","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.4c01050","issn":["00032700","15204782"],"issn_org":["00032700"],"issue":"27","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","pages":"10943-10952","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Analytical Chemistry","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196948294"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ef27f35d-42e8-4be6-ae60-5864ebee4e89"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Dual-Mode Arginine Assay Based on the Conformation Switch of a Ferrocene-Grafted Polypeptide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-757459","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Hyperlipidemia, obesity and gut dysbiosis are pivotal risk factors for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ACVD). Supplementation of Akkermansia muciniphila (AKK) has also been proven to be effective in the prevention and treatment of obesity and other metabolic disorders. Here we found that AKK was more abundant in healthy control than ACVD patients via metagenomic sequencing on fecal samples. Subsequently, we investigated the role and underlying mechanism of AKK on obesity-associated atherosclerosis. AKK intervention partially reversed the exacerbation of atherosclerotic lesion formation in ApoE-/- mice by improving dyslipidemia. Interestingly, replenishment with AKK significantly enhanced cardiac function and reduced the body weight. It also reduced pro-inflammatory cytokine IL-6 and increased anti-inflammatory IL-10 in the circulation. Additionally, AKK colonization dramatically regulated gut microbiota and increased the abundance of Lactobacillaceae. Our findings have provided novel insights into the therapeutic potential of AKK as a beneficial microbe for treating atherosclerotic-associated cardiovascular diseases.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Xiao, Xiao","Wu, Yuanyuan","Jie, Zhuye","Lin, Lu","Li, Yangchen","Hu, Weixian","Li, Yong","Zhong, Shilong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765657"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangdong Provincial People's Hospital","South China University of Technology"],"keyword":["Atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease","Cardiac function","Dyslipidemia","Gut microbiota","Inflammation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i akkermansia muciniphila i supplementation improves hyperlipidemia cardiac function and gut microbiota in high fat fed apolipoprotein e deficient mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-765657","identifier":[{"id":"39265779","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85203649326","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ee866bff-989a-4ea3-9625-f7de4972768a"],"keyword":["Atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease","Cardiac function","Dyslipidemia","Gut microbiota","Inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52812005208B654B2CB275199A7E5E46"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"guangdong provincial people s hospital","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong Provincial People's Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao","key":"xiaoxiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Yuanyuan","key":"wuyuanyuanpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Yuanyuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Zhuye","key":"jiezhuyepau","last":"Jie","locid":"2fd7fb85-ecfc-4a78-b546-2596c302b583","name":"Jie, Zhuye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lu","key":"linlupau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Lu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yangchen","key":"liyangchenpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yangchen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Weixian","key":"huweixianpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Weixian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yong","key":"liyongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Shilong","key":"zhongshilongpau","last":"Zhong","name":"Zhong, Shilong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39265779"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.prostaglandins.2024.106906","issn":["10988823"],"journal":"Prostaglandins & Other Lipid Mediators","paperid":"106906","status":"p","title":"Prostaglandins & Other Lipid Mediators","title_org":"Prostaglandins and Other Lipid Mediators","volume":"175"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203649326"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ee866bff-989a-4ea3-9625-f7de4972768a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"<i>Akkermansia Muciniphila</i> supplementation improves hyperlipidemia, cardiac function, and gut microbiota in high fat fed apolipoprotein E–deficient mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765657","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Evolutionary Agroecology theory predicts that the relationship between population yield and individual fitness among genotypes of a crop species is unimodal, and experimental evidence supports this. We test the theory further by investigating the role of resource availability on this relationship by comparing growth and reproductive output of three old and three modern cultivars of wheat (Triticum aestivum) in mixture and monocultures grown at three resource levels. The relationship between population grain yield and individual fitness (mean individual grain yield in mixture) of genotypes was resource dependent in a way that is consistent with the theory: when resource levels are low and limit individual growth directly, individual and population yield are positively correlated. When resource levels are high and the growth of individual plants is limited by competition for these resources, the relationship between individual fitness and population yield becomes negative. There was evidence for the unimodal relationship at the intermediate resource level. Old cultivars had higher fitness than newer cultivars at all three resource levels. Old cultivars had higher yields at low resource levels, but the newer cultivars yielded more when resource levels were high. Evaluating individual fitness and population yield in different environments may help wheat breeders to develop locally adapted, cooperative cultivars to increase production across large wheat-producing areas.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Yang, Xiao Wei","Weiner, Jacob","Fan, Jing Wei","Ren, Jie Ying","Luo, Wen Yuan","Li, Feng Min","Du, Yan Lei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777230"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lanzhou University","Nanjing Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Plant Breeding","Population performance","Tragedy of the commons"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolutionary agroecology individual fitness population yield and resource availability in wheat","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.baae.2024.10.004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777230","identifier":[{"id":"001348396700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85207718939","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-28a2628c-8e01-49e7-9aed-ae62465d8222"],"keyword":["Darwinian agriculture","Plant breeding","Population performance","Tragedy of the commons"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0CF6F18B81AF57EC0491A736969B374"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.baae.2024.10.004","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411853692/1_s2.0_S0924977X24001858_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"lanzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Lanzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Organismal Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"nanjing agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Agricultural University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Wei","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"weinerpau","last":"Weiner","locid":"dd3c08ff-333b-4591-9968-3957845a6fa1","name":"Weiner, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-0736-7943","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jing Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Jing Wei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jie Ying","key":"renpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Jie Ying","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wen Yuan","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Wen Yuan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Feng Min","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Feng Min","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yan Lei","key":"dupau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Yan Lei","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.baae.2024.10.004","issn":["14391791","16180089"],"issn_org":["14391791"],"journal":"Basic and Applied Ecology","pages":"53-58","status":"p","title":"Basic and Applied Ecology","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207718939"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-28a2628c-8e01-49e7-9aed-ae62465d8222"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolutionary Agroecology : Individual fitness, population yield and resource availability in wheat","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777230","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"An outstanding fact (OF) is a striking claim by which some entities stand out from their peers on some attribute. OFs serve data journalism, fact checking, and recommendation. However, one could jump to conclusions by selecting truthful OFs while intentionally or inadvertently ignoring lateral contexts and data that render them less striking. This jumping conclusion bias from unstable OFs may disorient the public, including voters and consumers, raising concerns about fairness and transparency in political and business competition. It is thus ethically imperative for several stakeholders to measure the robustness of OFs with respect to lateral contexts and data. Unfortunately, a capacity for such inspection of OFs mined from knowledge graphs (KGs) is missing. In this paper, we propose a methodology that inspects the robustness of OFs in KGs by perturbation analysis. We define (1) entity perturbation, which detects outlying contexts by perturbing context entities in the OF; and (2) data perturbation, which considers plausible data that render an OF less striking. We compute the expected strikingness scores of OFs over perturbation relevance distributions and assess an OF as robust if its measured strikingness does not deviate significantly from the expected. We devise a suite of exact and sampling algorithms for perturbation analysis on large KGs. Extensive experiments reveal that our methodology accurately and efficiently detects frail OFs generated by existing mining approaches on KGs. We also show the effectiveness of our approaches through case and user studies.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Xiao, Hanhua","Li, Yuchen","Wang, Yanhao","Karras, Panagiotis","Mouratidis, Kyriakos","Avlona, Natalia Rozalia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777495"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-29","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2024-08-25","title":"30th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining, KDD 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"country":["China","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","East China Normal University","Singapore Management University"],"keyword":["Knowledge Graphs","Perturbation analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to avoid jumping to conclusions measuring the robustness of outstanding facts in knowledge graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3637528.3671763","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777495","identifier":[{"id":"85203689956","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3f0cd3db-b38b-4c5f-be64-7ea830a2c9e6"],"keyword":["knowledge graphs","outstanding facts","perturbation analysis","robustness measurement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3ED32AC0BE12515F8A4C5DAB8F4C3164"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/414380906/How_to_Avoid_Jumping_to_Conclusions.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3637528.3671763","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"sg","key":"singapore management university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Singapore Management University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"east china normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hanhua","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Hanhua","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuchen","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yuchen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yanhao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yanhao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Panagiotis","key":"karraspau","last":"Karras","locid":"cbf789a0-42be-4b2a-9827-3b7130aeb50c","name":"Karras, Panagiotis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kyriakos","key":"mouratidispau","last":"Mouratidis","name":"Mouratidis, Kyriakos","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Natalia Rozalia","key":"avlonapau","last":"Avlona","locid":"be82e151-8b78-4656-8f1b-78e2bb512e1e","name":"Avlona, Natalia Rozalia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3637528.3671763","eisbn":["9798400704901"],"issn":["2154817X"],"pages":"3539-3550","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the ACM SIGKDD International Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining","status":"p","title":"KDD 2024 - Proceedings of the 30th ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203689956"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3f0cd3db-b38b-4c5f-be64-7ea830a2c9e6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to Avoid Jumping to Conclusions : Measuring the Robustness of Outstanding Facts in Knowledge Graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777495","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"China's terrestrial ecosystems are pivotal in upholding the global carbon balance, with their recognized capacity for carbon sequestration holding significant importance on a global scale, but there are still challenges in accurately monitoring its spatial-temporal patterns. SMOSMAP-IB L-VOD, a recently developed low-frequency L-band Vegetation Optical Depth (L-VOD) product, was employed to monitor the fluctuations in aboveground vegetation carbon stock over China between 2015 and 2021, and to investigate the influence of forest age and ecological restoration projects on China's carbon sink capacity. The carbon sink of above-ground vegetation in China was +169.98+135.59+179.44 Tg C yr-1 during 2015–2021. Southwest and northeast China's forests exhibit higher carbon sink capacity, contrasting with lower values per unit area are mainly found in northwestern China. The forest served as the foremost contributor to the carbon sink of above-ground vegetation in China, although their carbon density peaked in the middle-aged forests and then gradually decreased as the age of the forest grew. Furthermore, carbon sink areas were observed in most regions where ecological restoration projects were implemented, indicating that the execution of afforestation and ecological restoration initiatives has proven effective in carbon sequestration, creating a sink in these areas. Our results provide an improved foundation for formulating new afforestation policies in the future.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Fang, Hongqian","Fan, Lei","Ciais, Philippe","Xiao, Jingfeng","Fensholt, Rasmus","Chen, Jingming","Frappart, Frédéric","Ju, Weimin","Niu, Shuli","Xiao, Xiangming","Yuan, Wenping","Xia, Jiangzhou","Li, Xin","Liu, Liangyun","Qin, Yuanwei","Chang, Zhongbing","Yu, Ling","Dong, Guanyu","Cui, Tianxiang","Li, Xiaojun","Wigneron, Jean Pierre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779349"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China","France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Aerospace Information Research Institute","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Nanjing Forestry University","Nanjing University","Paris-Saclay University","Southwest University","Sun Yat-Sen University","Surveying and Mapping Institute Lands and Resource Department of Guangdong Province","Tianjin Normal University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of New Hampshire","University of Oklahoma","University of Toronto","Université de Bordeaux"],"keyword":["Aboveground biomass","Carbon sink","China","Ecological restoration","Forest growth","Remote sensing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"satellite based monitoring of china s above ground biomass carbon sink from 000000002015 to 000000002021","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-779349","identifier":[{"id":"85199390839","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e6f607e7-9200-4ee2-b868-3a7c9fbf212b"],"keyword":["Aboveground biomass","Carbon sink","China","Ecological restoration","Forest growth","Remote sensing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-65387C284E05DCCF669E979A048E398E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"paris saclay university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Saclay University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of new hampshire","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of New Hampshire","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l