"loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Forestry University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hongqian","key":"fanghongqianpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Hongqian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"fanleipau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Lei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Philippe","key":"ciaisphilippepau","last":"Ciais","name":"Ciais, Philippe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jingfeng","key":"xiaojingfengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jingfeng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Rasmus","key":"fensholtrasmuspau","last":"Fensholt","locid":"26fbbb5c-3853-4be9-8cab-3dce86446363","name":"Fensholt, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-3067-4527","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Jingming","key":"chenjingmingpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Jingming","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Frédéric","key":"frappartfrédéricpau","last":"Frappart","name":"Frappart, Frédéric","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Weimin","key":"juweiminpau","last":"Ju","name":"Ju, Weimin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Shuli","key":"niushulipau","last":"Niu","name":"Niu, Shuli","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Xiangming","key":"xiaoxiangmingpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xiangming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Wenping","key":"yuanwenpingpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Wenping","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Jiangzhou","key":"xiajiangzhoupau","last":"Xia","name":"Xia, Jiangzhou","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Xin","key":"lixinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xin","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"Liangyun","key":"liuliangyunpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Liangyun","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Yuanwei","key":"qinyuanweipau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Yuanwei","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","first":"Zhongbing","key":"changzhongbingpau","last":"Chang","name":"Chang, Zhongbing","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ling","key":"yulingpau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Ling","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guanyu","key":"dongguanyupau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Guanyu","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"15","first":"Tianxiang","key":"cuitianxiangpau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Tianxiang","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Xiaojun","key":"lixiaojunpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaojun","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Jean Pierre","key":"wigneronjeanpierrepau","last":"Wigneron","name":"Wigneron, Jean Pierre","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.agrformet.2024.110172","issn":["01681923","18732240"],"issn_org":["01681923"],"journal":"Agricultural and Forest Meteorology","paperid":"110172","status":"p","title":"Agricultural and Forest Meteorology","volume":"356"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199390839"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e6f607e7-9200-4ee2-b868-3a7c9fbf212b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Satellite-based monitoring of China's above-ground biomass carbon sink from 2015 to 2021","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779349","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"As a sulfur containing α-amino acid in nature, L-cysteine plays a crucial role in a variety of metabolic pathways with many important physiological functions. However, it is still a great challenge to construct a simple and rapid approach for L-cysteine up to now. In this paper, a simple, rapid and enzyme-free method was developed for potentiometric determination of L-cysteine by using meso-2,3-dimercaptosuccinic acid self-assembled monolayer on gold electrode. The surface morphology and property of self-assembled membrane with and without L-cysteine combined were characterized by means of scanning electron microscopy, X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, electrochemical impedance spectroscopy, and cyclic voltammetry, respectively. The recognition mechanism may be attributed to formation of hydrogen bonds between meso-2,3-dimercaptosuccinic acid and the target molecule of L-cysteine, producing a double electric layer at the sensing interface, that the membrane potential decreases with increasing concentration of L-cysteine. The assay results showed that good linear potential response to L-cysteine in Tris-HCl buffer solution (pH=7.0) was obtained in a range of 1.0 × 10-8 to 1.0 × 10-3 mol/L, with a slope of −57.00 ± 0.63 mV/-pc (25 °C) and a detection limit of 7.9 × 10-9 mol/L. The electrode possessed fast response time (45 s), good reproducibility, and strong anti-interference performance. Moreover, the electrode can be well applied to the detection of L-cysteine in pig serums with a recovery rate of 94.3 ∼ 106.3%, indicating a promising application prospect.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wu, Yuan Qing","Xiao, Hong Shu","Peng, Yu Yu","Wu, Bo Wen","Li, Bin","Ding, Yi Chao","Li, Dan","Wu, Ling","Yu, Donghong","Cao, Zhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786319"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Dan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Changsha University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Electrochemical sensor","Enzyme free","L cysteine","Membrane potential"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simple rapid and enzyme free assay for potentiometric determination of l cysteine based on meso 000000000002 000000000003 dimercaptosuccinic acid self assembled gold electrode","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85204593186&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-786319","identifier":[{"id":"85204593186","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ca2d5239-e905-48bf-83c4-c3d37ce5bbf1"],"keyword":["Electrochemical sensor","Enzyme-free","L-cysteine","Membrane potential","Meso-2,3-dimercaptosuccinic acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-018E0EF7E993EB8DFEE37221D399FD09"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"changsha university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Changsha University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Applied Supramolecular Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuan Qing","key":"wuyuanqingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Yuan Qing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong Shu","key":"xiaohongshupau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Hong Shu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu Yu","key":"pengyuyupau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Yu Yu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo Wen","key":"wubowenpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Bo Wen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bin","key":"libinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi Chao","key":"dingyichaopau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Yi Chao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"lidanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Dan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ling","key":"wulingpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Ling","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yudonghongpau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong","key":"caozhongpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhong","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.microc.2024.111548","issn":["0026265X","10959149"],"issn_org":["0026265X"],"journal":"Microchemical Journal","paperid":"111548","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Microchemical Journal","volume":"206"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204593186"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ca2d5239-e905-48bf-83c4-c3d37ce5bbf1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Simple, rapid and enzyme-free assay for potentiometric determination of L-cysteine based on meso-2,3-dimercaptosuccinic acid self-assembled gold electrode","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786319","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Aligned Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable performance across various tasks. However, LLMs remain susceptible to jailbreak adversarial attacks, where adversaries manipulate prompts to elicit malicious responses that aligned LLMs should have avoided. Identifying these vulnerabilities is crucial for understanding the inherent weaknesses of LLMs and preventing their potential misuse. One pioneering work in jailbreaking is the GCG attack, a discrete token optimization algorithm that seeks to find a suffix capable of jailbreaking aligned LLMs. Despite the success of GCG, we find it suboptimal, requiring significantly large computational costs, and the achieved jailbreaking performance is limited. In this work, we propose Faster-GCG, an efficient adversarial jailbreak method by delving deep into the design of GCG. Experiments demonstrate that Faster-GCG can surpass the original GCG with only 1/10 of the computational cost, achieving significantly higher attack success rates on various open-source aligned LLMs. In addition, We demonstrate that Faster-GCG exhibits improved attack transferability when testing on closed-sourced LLMs such as ChatGPT.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Xiao","Li, Zhuhong","Li, Qiongxiu","Lee, Bingze","Cui, Jinghao","Hu, Xiaolin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794370"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Tsinghua University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"faster gcg efficient discrete optimization jailbreak attacks against aligned large language models","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.15362","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-794370","ids":["aau-3c7b66cd-e9a0-46f0-8e94-e4fe514fb9a3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2FDA7F705D455F642232960D94B06619"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.15362","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Center for Communication, Media and Information Technologies","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Cyber Security Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"lixiaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhuhong","key":"lizhuhongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhuhong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qiongxiu","key":"liqiongxiupau","last":"Li","locid":"f880b285-6c3f-4145-94ec-59cceb843c48","name":"Li, Qiongxiu","orcid":"0000-0002-2487-5149","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bingze","key":"leebingzepau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Bingze","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinghao","key":"cuijinghaopau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Jinghao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaolin","key":"huxiaolinpau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Xiaolin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2410.15362","pages":"12","publisher":"arXiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3c7b66cd-e9a0-46f0-8e94-e4fe514fb9a3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Faster-GCG : Efficient discrete optimization jailbreak attacks against aligned large language models","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794370","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This review discusses the critical role of fundamentals of battery recycling in addressing the challenges posed by the increasing number of spent lithium-ion batteries (LIBs) due to the widespread use of electric vehicles and portable electronics, by providing the theoretical basis and technical support for recycling spent LIBs, including battery classification, ultrasonic flaw detection, pretreatment (e.g., discharging, mechanical crushing, and physical separation), electrolyte recovery, direct regeneration, and theoretical calculations and simulations. Physical chemistry principles are essential for achieving effective separation of different components through methods like screening, magnetic separation, and flotation. Electrolyte recovery involves separation and purification of electrolytes through advanced physical and chemical techniques. Direct regeneration technology restores the structure of electrode materials at the microscopic scale, requiring precise control of the physical state and crystal structure of the material. Physical processes such as phase changes, solubility, and diffusion are fundamental to techniques like solid-state sintering, eutectic-salt treatment, and hydrothermal methods. Theoretical calculations and simulations help predict the behaviour of materials during recycling, guiding process optimization. This review provides insights into understanding and improving the recycling process, emphasizing the central role of physical chemistry principles in addressing environmental and energy issues. It is valuable for promoting innovation in spent LIB recycling processes and is expected to stimulate interest among researchers and manufacturers.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Li, Pengwei","Luo, Shaohua","Lin, Yicheng","Xiao, Jiefeng","Xia, Xiaoning","Liu, Xin","Wang, Li","He, Xiangming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794700"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["He, Xiangming","Luo, Shaohua","Wang, Li"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huaqiao University","Northeastern University China","Tsinghua University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fundamentals of the recycling of spent lithium ion batteries","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85209208257&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-794700","identifier":[{"id":"39471089","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85209208257","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-79c11e47-9023-456d-a724-984125afc4d1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-893E11C69635F8AB181677781156BE54"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northeastern university china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeastern University China","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"huaqiao university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huaqiao University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Operations and Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengwei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Pengwei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shaohua","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Shaohua","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yicheng","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Yicheng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiefeng","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jiefeng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoning","key":"xiapau","last":"Xia","locid":"8f73aed8-9e77-4a91-bfd8-6f2e45a4953c","name":"Xia, Xiaoning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Li","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiangming","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Xiangming","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39471089"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d4cs00362d","issn":["03060012","14604744"],"issn_org":["03060012"],"issue":"24","journal":"Chemical Society Reviews","pages":"11967-12013","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Chemical Society Reviews","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209208257"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-79c11e47-9023-456d-a724-984125afc4d1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Fundamentals of the recycling of spent lithium-ion batteries","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794700","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Meaning-making systems underlie perceptions of the efficacy of threat-mitigating behaviors. Religion and science both offer threat mitigation, yet these meaning-making systems are often considered incompatible. Do such epistemological conflicts swamp the desire to employ diverse precautions against threats? Or do individuals—particularly individuals who are highly reactive to threats—hedge their bets by using multiple threat-mitigating practices despite their potential epistemological incompatibility? Complicating this question, perceptions of conflict between religion and science likely vary across cultures; likewise, pragmatic features of precautions prescribed by some religions make them incompatible with some scientifically-based precautions. The COVID-19 pandemic elicited diverse precautions thus providing an opportunity to investigate these questions. Across 27 societies from five continents (N = 7,844), in the majority of countries, individuals’ practice of religious precautions such as prayer correlates positively with their use of scientifically-based precautions. Prior work indicates that greater adherence to tradition likely reflects greater reactivity to threats. Unsurprisingly given associations between many traditions and religion, valuing tradition is predictive of employing religious precautions. However, consonant with its association with threat reactivity, we also find that traditionalism predicts adherence to public health precautions—a pattern that underscores threat-avoidant individuals’ apparent tolerance for epistemological conflict in pursuit of safety.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Samore, Theodore","Fessler, Daniel M.T.","Sparks, Adam Maxwell","Holbrook, Colin","Aarøe, Lene","Baeza, Carmen Gloria","Barbato, María Teresa","Barclay, Pat","Berniūnas, Renatas","Contreras-Garduño, Jorge","Costa-Neves, Bernardo","del Pilar Grazioso, Maria","Elmas, Pınar","Fedor, Peter","Fernandez, Ana Maria","Fernández-Morales, Regina","Garcia-Marques, Leonel","Giraldo-Perez, Paulina","Gul, Pelin","Habacht, Fanny","Hasan, Youssef","Hernandez, Earl John","Jarmakowski, Tomasz","Kamble, Shanmukh","Kameda, Tatsuya","Kim, Bia","Kupfer, Tom R.","Kurita, Maho","Li, Norman P.","Lu, Junsong","Luberti, Francesca R.","Maegli, María Andrée","Mejia, Marinés","Morvinski, Coby","Naito, Aoi","Ng’ang’a, Alice","de Oliveira, Angélica Nascimento","Posner, Daniel N.","Prokop, Pavol","Shani, Yaniv","Solorzano, Walter Omar Paniagua","Stieger, Stefan","Suryani, Angela Oktavia","Tan, Lynn K.L.","Tybur, Joshua M.","Viciana, Hugo","Visine, Amandine","Wang, Jin","Wang, Xiao Tian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-796024"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Samore, Theodore"],"country":["Austria","Canada","Chile","France","Guatemala","Hong Kong","India","Indonesia","Israel","Japan","Lithuania","Mexico","Netherlands","New Zealand","Poland","Portugal","Qatar","Singapore","Slovakia","South Korea","Spain","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Adnan Menderes University","All Global Affiliations","Atma Jaya Catholic University of Indonesia","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","Chinese University of Hong Kong","Comenius University","Francisco Marroquin University","Hokkaido University","Institute of Science Tokyo","Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","Karl Landsteiner University of Health Sciences","Karnatak University","Montpellier SupAgro","Nicolaus Copernicus University in Torun","Nipissing University","Nottingham Trent University","Pusan National University","Qatar University","Singapore Management University","Slovak Academy of Sciences","Tamagawa University","Tel Aviv University","Universidad Nacional Autonoma de Mexico","Universidad Rafael Landívar","Universidad de Sa