{"abstract":"A novel thionocarbonate-coumarin-thiourea triad-based probe with dual recognition sites for sensing mercury (Hg2+) ion was developed. The synthesized probe possessed both fluorogenic (“off-on”) and chromogenic (from colorless to blackish brown) sensing performance towards Hg2+ ions. The fluorescence intensity was increased by 70 fold after the addition of Hg2+. As expected, the probe exhibited excellent selectivity and sensitivity for Hg2+ compared to other common competitive metal ions. The fluorescence intensity of the probe improved linearly with the increase of the concentration of Hg2+ (0–40 μM). Also, the minimum limit of detection (LOD) of the synthesized probe was 0.12 μM. Considering the importance of test feasibility in the harsh environment, the developed probe was applicable for detecting Hg2+ ions over a broad working pH range of 3–11. It is reliable and qualifies for the quantitative determination of Hg2+ concentrations in actual water samples. Finally, the probe achieved the bioimaging performance of Hg2+ in living cells and plants with good biocompatibility.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Li, Hongqi","Li, Jiayin","Pan, Zhixiu","Zheng, Tao","Song, Yanxi","Zhang, Jian","Xiao, Zhongwen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-359575"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Hongqi"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Donghua University"],"keyword":["Bioimaging","Coumarin","Fluorescent probe","Mercury II","Thiourea"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"highly selective and sensitive detection of hg sup 000000000002 sup by a novel fluorescent probe with dual recognition sites","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85146734920","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The financial support by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC, No. 52276103) is acknowledged."],"id":"S01-000.00-359575","identifier":[{"id":"36682255","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146734920","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b807e735-bda0-4d59-ac20-a7193c0b94ac"],"keyword":["Bioimaging","Coumarin","Fluorescent probe","Mercury(II)","Thionocarbonate","Thiourea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD4162BF3522859369D6AA0E344E8ADB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"donghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Donghua University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biotherapeutic Engineering and Drug Targeting","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Biotherapeutic Engineering and Drug Targeting, Nanomaterials and Nanobiosensors"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongqi","key":"lihongqipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hongqi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiayin","key":"lijiayinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jiayin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhixiu","key":"panzhixiupau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Zhixiu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tao","key":"zhengtaopau","last":"Zheng","locid":"7a0aa044-70ce-4040-90e5-39f111c36657","name":"Zheng, Tao","orcid":"0000-0002-0626-4344","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanxi","key":"songyanxipau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Yanxi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"zhangjianpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongwen","key":"xiaozhongwenpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Zhongwen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36682255"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.saa.2023.122379","issn":["13861425","18733557"],"issn_org":["13861425"],"journal":"Spectrochimica Acta Part A: Molecular and Biomolecular Spectroscopy","paperid":"122379","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Spectrochimica Acta Part A: Molecular and Biomolecular Spectroscopy","title_org":"Spectrochimica Acta - Part A: Molecular and Biomolecular Spectroscopy","volume":"291"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146734920"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b807e735-bda0-4d59-ac20-a7193c0b94ac"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Highly selective and sensitive detection of Hg<sup>2+</sup> by a novel fluorescent probe with dual recognition sites","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-359575","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The oral microbiome has been implicated in a growing number of diseases; however, determinants of the oral microbiome and their roles remain elusive. Here, we investigated the oral (saliva and tongue dorsum) metagenome, the whole genome, and other omics data in a total of 4,478 individuals and demonstrated that the oral microbiome composition and its major contributing host factors significantly differed between sexes. We thus conducted a sex-stratified metagenome-genome-wide-association study (M-GWAS) and identified 11 differential genetic associations with the oral microbiome (psex-difference < 5 × 10−8). Furthermore, we performed sex-stratified Mendelian randomization (MR) analyses and identified abundant causalities between the oral microbiome and serum metabolites. Notably, sex-specific microbes-hormonal interactions explained the mostly observed sex hormones differences such as the significant causalities enrichments for aldosterone in females and androstenedione in males. These findings illustrate the necessity of sex stratification and deepen our understanding of the interplay between the oral microbiome and serum metabolites.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Liu, Xiaomin","Tong, Xin","Jie, Zhuye","Zhu, Jie","Tian, Liu","Sun, Qiang","Ju, Yanmei","Zou, Leying","Lu, Haorong","Qiu, Xuemei","Li, Qiang","Liao, Yunli","Lian, Heng","Zuo, Yong","Chen, Xiaomin","Rao, Weiqiao","Ren, Yan","Wang, Yuan","Zi, Jin","Wang, Rong","Xu, Xun","Yang, Huanming","Wang, Jian","Zong, Yang","Liu, Weibin","Hou, Yong","Jin, Xin","Xiao, Liang","Kristiansen, Karsten","Jia, Huijue","Zhang, Tao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462001"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["Canada","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","James D. Watson Institute of Genome Sciences","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Toronto"],"keyword":["Microbial metabolism","Microbiome","Oral microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex differences in the oral microbiome host traits and their causal relationships","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2022.105839","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-462001","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9843272","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36660475","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146072275","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-72bf8629-e292-4b66-94dd-298bbe8fadb0"],"keyword":["Microbial metabolism","Microbiome","Oral microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4557B88C64CA052D8225B6C6D7C49362"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/334257596/1_s2.0_S2589004222021125_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2022.105839","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto"