{"abstract":"This paper introduces a novel analytical model for the accurate inductance calculation of rounded rectangular coils in wireless power transfer systems (WPTSs). Comprehensive analysis is conducted for the rounded rectangular coil and a new parametric model is proposed to precisely define its structure. A new inductance calculation model is proposed for the rounded rectangular coils based on Neumann's formula and the obtained parametric structure model. The Geometric Mean Distance method is introduced to reduce the complexity and difficulty of self-inductance modeling. The image current method is adopted to achieve accurate inductance modeling for rounded rectangular coils with ferrite plates. Finally, the accuracy of the proposed analytical model is validated and compared with two other traditional methods. It turns out that the proposed models can achieve high calculation accuracy in self-inductance and mutual inductance calculation. The proposed model exhibits the merits of high accuracy and fast calculation speed which makes it promising for future coil designing and optimization.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jiang, Yongbin","Wu, Yue","Li, Yaohua","Xiao, Ziheng","Wang, Ning","Wu, Min","Wang, Xiaohua","Tang, Yi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756471"],"event":{"end":"2023-10-19","place":"Singapore, sg","start":"2023-10-16","title":"49th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society, IECON 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"country":["China","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanyang Technological University","Xi'an Jiaotong University"],"keyword":["Analytical modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"precise modeling for the inductance of rounded rectangular coils in wireless power transfer systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85179524284&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-756471","identifier":[{"id":"85179524284","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1cab7fce-eda2-4a26-ae74-a6b090c18da4"],"keyword":["Wireless power transfer system (WPTS)","analytical modeling","high accuracy calculation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2051292F1D2F17DB16647BD2C0FDFDB2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"sg","key":"nanyang technological university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Nanyang Technological University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"xi an jiaotong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xi'an Jiaotong University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongbin","key":"jiangyongbinpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Yongbin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yue","key":"wuyuepau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Yue","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaohua","key":"liyaohuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yaohua","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ziheng","key":"xiaozihengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Ziheng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ning","key":"wangningpau","last":"Wang","locid":"f63f0a35-0e1b-446d-b3a1-cf6fce60eede","name":"Wang, Ning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"wuminpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Min","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaohua","key":"wangxiaohuapau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaohua","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"tangyipau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Yi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iecon51785.2023.10312669","eisbn":["9798350331820"],"issn":["21624704"],"publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IECON Proceedings","status":"p","title":"IECON 2023 - 49th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179524284"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1cab7fce-eda2-4a26-ae74-a6b090c18da4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Precise Modeling for the Inductance of Rounded Rectangular Coils in Wireless Power Transfer Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-756471","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Suicidal behavior is heritable and is a major cause of death worldwide. Two large-scale genome-wide association studies (GWASs) recently discovered and crossvalidated genome-wide significant (GWS) loci for suicide attempt (SA). The present study leveraged the genetic cohorts from both studies to conduct the largest GWAS metaanalysis of SA to date. Multi-ancestry and admixture-specific meta-analyses were conducted within groups of significant African, East Asian, and European ancestry admixtures. Methods: This study comprised 22 cohorts, including 43,871 SA cases and 915,025 ancestry-matched controls. Analytical methods across multi-ancestry and individual ancestry admixtures included inverse variance-weighted fixed-effects meta-analyses, followed by gene, gene-set, tissue-set, and drug-target enrichment, as well as summary-data-based Mendelian randomization with brain expression quantitative trait loci data, phenome-wide genetic correlation, and genetic causal proportion analyses. Results: Multi-ancestry and European ancestry admixture GWAS meta-analyses identified 12 risk loci at p values <5×10-8. These loci were mostly intergenic and implicated DRD2, SLC6A9, FURIN, NLGN1, SOX5, PDE4B, and CACNG2. The multi-ancestry SNP-based heritability estimate of SA was 5.7% on the liability scale (SE=0.003, p=5.7×10-80). Significant brain tissue gene expression and drug set enrichment were observed. There was shared genetic variation of SA with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, smoking, and risk tolerance after conditioning SA on both major depressive disorder and posttraumatic stress disorder. Genetic causal proportion analyses implicated shared genetic risk for specific health factors. Conclusions: This multi-ancestry analysis of suicide attempt identified several loci contributing to risk and establishes significant shared genetic covariation with clinical phenotypes. These findings provide insight into genetic factors associated with suicide attempt across ancestry admixture populations, in veteran and civilian populations, and in attempt versus death.","author_count":248,"contributors":["Docherty, Anna R.","Mullins, Niamh","Ashley-Koch, Allison E.","Qin, Xuejun","Coleman, Jonathan R.I.","Shabalin, Andrey","Kang, Joo Eun","Murnyak, Balasz","Wendt, Frank","Adams, Mark","Campos, Adrian I.","DiBlasi, Emily","Fullerton, Janice M.","Kranzler, Henry R.","Bakian, Amanda V.","Monson, Eric T.","Rentería, Miguel E.","Walss-Bass, Consuelo","Andreassen, Ole A.","Behera, Chittaranjan","Bulik, Cynthia M.","Edenberg, Howard J.","Kessler, Ronald C.","John Mann, J.","Nurnberger, John I.","Pistis, Giorgio","Streit, Fabian","Ursano, Robert J.","Polimanti, Renato","Dennis, Michelle","Garrett, Melanie","Hair, Lauren","Harvey, Philip","Hauser, Elizabeth R.","Hauser, Michael A.","Huffman, Jennifer","Jacobson, Daniel","Madduri, Ravi","McMahon, Benjamin","Oslin, David W.","Trafton, Jodie","Awasthi, Swapnil","Berrettini, Wade H.","Bohus, Martin","Chang, Xiao","Chen, Hsi Chung","Chen, Wei J.","Christensen, Erik D.M.D.","Crow, Scott","Duriez, Philibert","Edwards, Alexis C.","Fernández-Aranda, Fernando","Galfalvy, Hanga","Gandal, Michael","Gorwood, Philip","Guo, Yiran","Hafferty, Jonathan D.","Hakonarson, Hakon","Halmi, Katherine A.","Hishimoto, Akitoyo","Jain, Sonia","Jamain, Stéphane","Jiménez-Murcia, Susana","Johnson, Craig","Kaplan, Allan S.","Kaye, Walter H.","Keel, Pamela K.","Kennedy, James L.","Kim, Minsoo","Klump, Kelly L.","Levey, Daniel F.","Li, Dong","Liao, Shih Cheng","Lieb, Klaus","Lilenfeld, Lisa","Marshall, Christian R.","Mitchell, James E.","Okazaki, Satoshi","Otsuka, Ikuo","Pinto, Dalila","Powers, Abigail","Ramoz, Nicolas","Ripke, Stephan","Roepke, Stefan","Rozanov, Vsevolod","Scherer, Stephen W.","Schmahl, Christian","Sokolowski, Marcus","Starnawska, Anna","Strober, Michael","Su, Mei Hsin","Thornton, Laura M.","Treasure, Janet","Ware, Erin B.","Watson, Hunna J.","Witt, Stephanie H.","Blake Woodside, D.","Yilmaz,