Virginia","rank":244,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 192","first":"Hilary","key":"coonhilarypau","last":"Coon","name":"Coon, Hilary","rank":245,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 45","first":"Jean C.","key":"beckhamjeancpau","last":"Beckham","name":"Beckham, Jean C.","rank":246,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 45","first":"Nathan A.","key":"kimbrelnathanapau","last":"Kimbrel","name":"Kimbrel, Nathan A.","rank":247,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Douglas M.","key":"ruderferdouglasmpau","last":"Ruderfer","name":"Ruderfer, Douglas M.","rank":248,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37777856"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1176/appi.ajp.21121266","issn":["0002953X","11393475"],"issn_org":["0002953X"],"issue":"10","journal":"American Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"723-738","publisher":"Grupo Ars XXI de Comunicacion, SA","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Psychiatry","volume":"180"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85176353814"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Lundbeck Pharma","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-321a664c-f29b-43b3-ac1a-fae88ad60e44","ku-2d1a3b43-8fac-48fc-a5b2-ae7572e7d948"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GWAS Meta-Analysis of Suicide Attempt : Identification of 12 Genome-Wide Significant Loci and Implication of Genetic Risks for Specific Health Factors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.78-755987","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Although species can arise through hybridization, compelling evidence for hybrid speciation has been reported only rarely in animals. Here, we present phylogenomic analyses on genomes from 12 macaque species and show that the fascicularis group originated from an ancient hybridization between the sinica and silenus groups ~3.45 to 3.56 million years ago. The X chromosomes and low-recombination regions exhibited equal contributions from each parental lineage, suggesting that they were less affected by subsequent backcrossing and hence could have played an important role in maintaining hybrid integrity. We identified many reproduction-associated genes that could have contributed to the development of the mixed sexual phenotypes characteristic of the fascicularis group. The phylogeny within the silenus group was also resolved, and functional experimentation confirmed that all extant Western silenus species are susceptible to HIV-1 infection. Our study provides novel insights into macaque evolution and reveals a hybrid speciation event that has occurred only very rarely in primates.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Zhang, Bao Lin","Chen, Wu","Wang, Zefu","Pang, Wei","Luo, Meng Ting","Wang, Sheng","Shao, Yong","He, Wen Qiang","Deng, Yuan","Zhou, Long","Chen, Jiawei","Yang, Min Min","Wu, Yajiang","Wang, Lu","Fernández-Bellon, Hugo","Molloy, Sandra","Meunier, Hélène","Wanert, Fanélie","Kuderna, Lukas","Marques-Bonet, Tomas","Roos, Christian","Qi, Xiao Guang","Li, Ming","Liu, Zhijin","Schierup, Mikkel Heide","Cooper, David N.","Liu, Jianquan","Zheng, Yong Tang","Zhang, Guojie","Wu, Dong Dong"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-672731"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Germany","Ireland","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Autonomous 