azarus, Philip","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"31","first":"Matthew B.","key":"schabathmatthewbpau","last":"Schabath","name":"Schabath, Matthew B.","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"32","first":"Melinda C.","key":"aldrichmelindacpau","last":"Aldrich","name":"Aldrich, Melinda C.","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paul","key":"brennanpaulpau","last":"Brennan","name":"Brennan, Paul","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yong","key":"liyongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yong","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olga","key":"gorlovaolgapau","last":"Gorlova","name":"Gorlova, Olga","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ivan","key":"gorlovivanpau","last":"Gorlov","name":"Gorlov, Ivan","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher I.","key":"amoschristopheripau","last":"Amos","name":"Amos, Christopher I.","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37150255"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtho.2023.05.001","issn":["15560864","15561380"],"issn_org":["15560864"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of Thoracic Oncology","pages":"1003-1016","status":"p","title":"Journal of Thoracic Oncology","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163295925"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b109f2ec-ff28-4049-8675-70384d1f2cc1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mosaic Chromosomal Alterations Are Associated With Increased Lung Cancer Risk : Insight From the INTEGRAL-ILCCO Cohort Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690226","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Indoor location-based services rely on the availability of sufficiently accurate positioning in indoor spaces. A popular approach to positioning relies on so-called radio maps that contain pairs of a vector of Wi-Fi signal strength indicator values (RSSIs), called a fingerprint, and a location label, called a reference point (RP), in which the fingerprint was observed. The positioning accuracy depends on the quality of the radio maps and their fingerprints. Radio maps are often sparse, with many pairs containing vectors missing many RSSIs as well as RPs. Aiming to improve positioning accuracy, we present a complete set of techniques to impute such missing values in radio maps. We differentiate two types of missing RSSIs: missing not at random (MNAR) and missing at random (MAR). Specifically, we design a framework encompassing a missing RSSI differentiator followed by a data imputer for missing values. The differentiator identifies MARs and MNARs via clustering-based fingerprint analysis. Missing RSSIs and RPs are then imputed jointly by means of a novel encoder-decoder architecture that leverages temporal dependencies in data collection as well as correlations among fingerprints and RPs. A time-lag mechanism is used to consider the aging of data, and a sparsity-friendly attention mechanism is used to focus attention score calculation on observed data. Extensive experiments with real data from two buildings show that our proposal outperforms the alternatives with significant advantages in terms of imputation accuracy and indoor positioning accuracy","author_count":5,"contributors":["Li, Xiao","Li, Huan","Chan, Harry Kai-Ho","Lu, Hua","Jensen, Christian S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705963"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sheffield","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data imputation for sparse radio maps in indoor positioning extended version","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2302.13022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-705963","ids":["aau-cd845efc-f463-406c-8ac5-277e172cc217"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6BA2524F7ED29B4E9305FF573AA53E60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.13022","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2302.13022","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of sheffield","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sheffield","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, CITS","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Daisy - Center for Data-intensive Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data Engineering, Science and Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"lixiaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Huan","key":"lihuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Huan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Harry Kai-Ho","key":"chanharrykaihopau","last":"Chan","name":"Chan, Harry Kai-Ho","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hua","key":"luhuapau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Hua","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian S.","key":"jensenchristianspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"56b675d6-bbf5-4dec-a799-50327f3fc66a","name":"Jensen, Christian S.","orcid":"0000-0002-9697-7670","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2302.13022","publisher":"arXiv","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cd845efc-f463-406c-8ac5-277e172cc217"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Data Imputation for Sparse Radio Maps in Indoor Positioning (Extended Version)","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705963","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Polygenic risk scores (PRS) have great potential to guide precision colorectal cancer (CRC) prevention by identifying those at higher risk to undertake targeted screening. However, current PRS using European ancestry data have sub-optimal performance in non-European ancestry populations, limiting their utility among these populations. Towards addressing this deficiency, we expand PRS development for CRC by incorporating Asian ancestry data (21,731 cases; 47,444 controls) into European ancestry training datasets (78,473 cases; 107,143 controls). The AUC estimates (95% CI) of PRS are 0.63(0.62-0.64), 0.59(0.57-0.61), 0.62(0.60-0.63), and 0.65(0.63-0.66) in independent datasets including 1681-3651 cases and 8696-115,105 controls of Asian, Black/African American, Latinx/Hispanic, and non-Hispanic White, respectively. They are significantly better than the European-centric PRS in all four major US racial and ethnic groups (p-values < 0.05). Further inclusion of non-European ancestry populations, especially Black/African American and Latinx/Hispanic, is needed to improve the risk prediction and enhance equity in applying PRS in clinical practice.","author_count":128,"contributors":["Thomas, Minta","Su, Yu Ru","Rosenthal, Elisabeth A.","Sakoda, Lori C.","Schmit, Stephanie L.","Timofeeva, Maria","Chen, Zhishan","Fernandez-Rozadilla, Ceres","Law, Philip J.","Murphy, Neil","Carreras-Torres, Robert","Diez-Obrero, Virginia","van Duijnhoven, Franzel J.B.","Jiang, Shangqing","Shin, Aesun","Wolk, Alicja","Phipps, Amanda I.","Burnett-Hartman, Andrea","Gsur, Andrea","Chan, Andrew T.","Zauber, Ann G.","Wu, Anna H.","Lindblom, Annika","Um, Caroline Y.","Tangen, Catherine M.","Gignoux, Chris","Newton, Christina","Haiman, Christopher A.","Qu, Conghui","Bishop, D. Timothy","Buchanan, Daniel D.","Crosslin, David R.","Conti, David V.","Kim, Dong Hyun","Hauser, Elizabeth","Siegel, Erin","Schumacher, Fredrick R.","Rennert, Gad","Giles, Graham G.","Hampel, Heather","Brenner, Herm