{"abstract":"Nitrogen was introduced into TiAl pre-alloyed powder using high-temperature gas nitriding, and Ti2AlN/TiAl composites with a continuous network structure of the reinforced phase were prepared via spark plasma sintering. The results show that the hardness of the composite is significantly higher than that of TiAl alloy, and increases with the increase of nitriding time. The strengthening effect is originated from the synergistic effect of the solid-solution strengthening caused by the nitriding of the powder, the continuous network of the Ti2AlN phase with high hardness and elastic modulus, and the increase of dislocation density. Additionally, the compressive strength of the Ti2AlN/TiAl composites is lower than that of the TiAl alloy, which is related to a part of Ti2AlN particles that are directly formed after nitriding and excessive reinforcement content.","author_count":6,"contributors":["JIANG, Min jin","SUN, Hong liang","LIU, Rui","JIANG, Xiao song","ZHANG, Ya li","Sun, Daming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-735843"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["JIANG, Xiao song","SUN, Hong liang"],"country":["China","South Korea"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ministry of Education, China","Southwest Jiaotong University","Sungkyunkwan University"],"keyword":["Mechanical properties","Microstructure","Nitriding"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fabrication and mechanical properties of ti sub 000000000002 sub aln tial composite with continuous network structure","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1003-6326(23)66194-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-735843","identifier":[{"id":"85161569515","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3b37e0c7-20e2-429b-b922-9df193cb93cc"],"keyword":["TiAlN/TiAl composite","continuous network structure","mechanical properties","microstructure","nitriding","pre-alloyed powder"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2CFA01CB2D5C2A75AE8A2E6FCF549930"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1003-6326(23)66194-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/706507748/1-s2.0-S1003632623661941-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southwest jiaotong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest Jiaotong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"ministry of education china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ministry of Education, China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"kr","key":"sungkyunkwan university","loc":["South Korea","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Sungkyunkwan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Disordered Materials","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Min jin","key":"jiangminjinpau","last":"JIANG","name":"JIANG, Min jin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong liang","key":"sunhongliangpau","last":"SUN","name":"SUN, Hong liang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui","key":"liuruipau","last":"LIU","name":"LIU, Rui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao song","key":"jiangxiaosongpau","last":"JIANG","name":"JIANG, Xiao song","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ya li","key":"zhangyalipau","last":"ZHANG","name":"ZHANG, Ya li","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Da ming","key":"sundamingpau","last":"SUN","locid":"21d36ad0-99b9-4e18-a3df-aca270113829","name":"Sun, Daming","name_org":"SUN, Da ming","orcid":"0000-0002-4469-1187","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s1003-6326(23)66194-1","issn":["10036326","22103384"],"issn_org":["10036326"],"issue":"5","journal":"Transactions of Nonferrous Metals Society of China","pages":"1437-1451","publisher":"Nonferrous Metals Society of China","status":"p","title":"Transactions of Nonferrous Metals Society of China","title_org":"Transactions of Nonferrous Metals Society of China (English Edition)","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161569515"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3b37e0c7-20e2-429b-b922-9df193cb93cc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Fabrication and mechanical properties of Ti<sub>2</sub>AlN/TiAl composite with continuous network structure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-735843","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Human aging is invariably accompanied by a decline in renal function, a process potentially exacerbated by uremic toxins originating from gut microbes. Based on a registered household Chinese Guangxi longevity cohort (n = 151), we conducted comprehensive profiling of the gut microbiota and serum metabolome of individuals from 22 to 111 years of age and validated the findings in two independent East Asian aging cohorts (Japan aging cohort n = 330, Yunnan aging cohort n = 80), identifying unique age-dependent differences in the microbiota and serum metabolome. We discovered that the influence of the gut microbiota on serum metabolites intensifies with advancing age. Furthermore, mediation analyses unveiled putative causal relationships between the gut microbiota (Escherichia coli, Odoribacter splanchnicus, and Desulfovibrio piger) and serum metabolite markers related to impaired renal function (p-cresol, N-phenylacetylglutamine, 2-oxindole, and 4-aminohippuric acid) and aging. The fecal microbiota transplantation experiment demonstrated that the feces of elderly individuals could influence markers related to impaired renal function in the serum. Our findings reveal novel links between age-dependent alterations in the gut microbiota and serum metabolite markers of impaired renal function, providing novel insights into the effects of microbiota-metabolite interplay on renal function and healthy aging.","author_count":56,"contributors":["Sun, Liang","Li, Zhiming","Hu, Caiyou","Ding, Jiahong","Zhou, Qi","Pang, Guofang","Wu, Zhu","Yang, Ruiyue","Li, Shenghui","Li, Jian","Cai, Jianping","Sun, Yuzhe","Li, Rui","Zhen, Hefu","Sun, Shuqin","Zhang, Jianmin","Fang, Mingyan","Chen, Zhihua","Lv, Yuan","Cao, Qizhi","Sun, Yanan","Gong, Ranhui","Huang, Zezhi","Duan, Yong","Liu, Hengshuo","Dong, Jun","Li, Junchun","Ruan, Jie","Lu, Haorong","He, Benjin","Li, Ninghu","Li, Tao","Xue, Wenbin","Li, Yan","Shen, Juan","Yang, Fan","Zhao, Cheng","Liang, Qinghua","Zhang, Mingrong","Chen, Chen","Gong, Huan","Hou, Yong","Wang, Jian","Zhang, Ying","Yang, Huanming","Zhu, Shida","Xiao, Liang","Jin, Zhen","Guo, Haiyun","Zhao, Peng","Brix, Susanne","Xu, Xun","Jia, Huijue","Kristiansen, Karsten","Yang, Ze","Nie, Chao"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716228"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Kristiansen, Karsten","Nie, Chao","Sun, Liang","Yang, Ze"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","BGI Group","Binzhou Medical College","Binzhou Medical University","China Agricultural University","China National GeneBank","Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","Department of Environment Science and Engineering, Fudan University","Jiangbin Hospital","Kunming Medical College","People's Government of Yongfu County","Qingdao-Europe Advanced Institute for Life Sciences","Yunnan Key Laboratory of Laboratory Medicine"],"keyword":["Aging","Gut microbiota","Renal function","Serum metabolome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"age dependent changes in the gut microbiota and serum metabolome correlate with renal function and human aging","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/acel.14028","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716228","identifier":[{"id":"85177775152","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10726799","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38015106","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-5c0b574c-fe0a-4a05-abd2-44f6592b81fb","ku-f5cd9ac6-8517-4534-ac81-76a63dbf298f"],"keyword":["Aging","Gut microbiota","Renal function","Serum metabolome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"no