ccess","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455007","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"People vary both in their embrace of their society’s traditions, and in their perception of hazards as salient and necessitating a response. Over evolutionary time, traditions have offered avenues for addressing hazards, plausibly resulting in linkages between orientations toward tradition and orientations toward danger. Emerging research documents connections between traditionalism and threat responsivity, including pathogen-avoidance motivations. Additionally, because hazard-mitigating behaviors can conflict with competing priorities, associations between traditionalism and pathogen avoidance may hinge on contextually contingent tradeoffs. The COVID-19 pandemic provides a real-world test of the posited relationship between traditionalism and hazard avoidance. Across 27 societies (N = 7844), we find that, in a majority of countries, individuals’ endorsement of tradition positively correlates with their adherence to costly COVID-19-avoidance behaviors; accounting for some of the conflicts that arise between public health precautions and other objectives further strengthens this evidence that traditionalism is associated with greater attention to hazards.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Samore, Theodore","Fessler, Daniel M.T.","Sparks, Adam Maxwell","Holbrook, Colin","Aarøe, Lene","Baeza, Carmen Gloria","Barbato, María Teresa","Barclay, Pat","Berniūnas, Renatas","Contreras-Garduño, Jorge","Costa-Neves, Bernardo","del Pilar Grazioso, Maria","Elmas, Pınar","Fedor, Peter","Fernandez, Ana Maria","Fernández-Morales, Regina","Garcia-Marques, Leonel","Giraldo-Perez, Paulina","Gul, Pelin","Habacht, Fanny","Hasan, Youssef","Hernandez, Earl John","Jarmakowski, Tomasz","Kamble, Shanmukh","Kameda, Tatsuya","Kim, Bia","Kupfer, Tom R.","Kurita, Maho","Li, Norman P.","Lu, Junsong","Luberti, Francesca R.","Maegli, María Andrée","Mejia, Marinés","Morvinski, Coby","Naito, Aoi","Ng’ang’a, Alice","de Oliveira, Angélica Nascimento","Posner, Daniel N.","Prokop, Pavol","Shani, Yaniv","Solorzano, Walter Omar Paniagua","Stieger, Stefan","Suryani, Angela Oktavia","Tan, Lynn K.L.","Tybur, Joshua M.","Viciana, Hugo","Visine, Amandine","Wang, Jin","Wang, Xiao Tian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-668489"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Samore, Theodore"],"country":["Austria","Canada","Chile","France","Guatemala","Hong Kong","India","Indonesia","Israel","Japan","Lithuania","Mexico","Netherlands","New Zealand","Poland","Portugal","Qatar","Singapore","Slovakia","South Korea","Spain","Turkey","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Adnan Menderes University","All Global Affiliations","Atma Jaya Catholic University of Indonesia","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","Chinese University of Hong Kong","Comenius University","Francisco Marroquin University","Hokkaido University","Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","Karl Landsteiner University of Health Sciences","Karnatak University","Montpellier SupAgro","Nicolaus Copernicus University in Torun","Nipissing University","Nottingham Trent University","Pusan National University","Qatar University","Singapore Management University","Slovak Academy of Sciences","Tamagawa University","Tel Aviv University","Universidad Nacional Autonoma de Mexico","Universidad Rafael Landívar","Universidad de Santiago de Chile","University of Auckland","University of California Merced","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Groningen","University of Guelph","University of Lisbon","University of Seville","University of Tokyo","University of the Valley of Guatemala","VU University Amsterdam","Vilnius University","Wilfrid Laurier University"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI