iyu","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Sassan","key":"saatchipau","last":"Saatchi","name":"Saatchi, Sassan","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Peter","key":"boucherpau","last":"Boucher","name":"Boucher, Peter","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jenia","key":"singhpau","last":"Singh","name":"Singh, Jenia","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Simon","key":"taugourdeaupau","last":"Taugourdeau","name":"Taugourdeau, Simon","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Morgane","key":"dendonckerpau","last":"Dendoncker","name":"Dendoncker, Morgane","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Xiao-Peng","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Xiao-Peng","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole","key":"mertzpau","last":"Mertz","locid":"83caa189-6757-469a-ac6f-39578f4355ff","name":"Mertz, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3876-6779","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","first":"Compton J.","key":"tuckerpau","last":"Tucker","name":"Tucker, Compton J.","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"fensholtpau","last":"Fensholt","locid":"26fbbb5c-3853-4be9-8cab-3dce86446363","name":"Fensholt, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0003-3067-4527","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37130845"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-023-37880-4","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"2258","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85158003568"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-74abca4b-66eb-4537-b517-3bf99ed0c391"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"More than one quarter of Africa's tree cover is found outside areas previously classified as forest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-670393","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Anthropogenic discharge of nutrients, metals, and antibiotics poses multiple threats to the health of aquatic ecosystems and humans, e.g., causing eutrophication, and introduction of resistance genes into human pathogens. The potential link between microbial communities, resistance genes, and eutrophication levels in urban lakes is complex and remains unclear, which is crucial for ecological and human health risk assessment. Here, five urban lakes of different trophic conditions were investigated to quantify their microbial diversity, and high-resolution profiles of antibiotic resistance genes (ARGs) and metal resistance genes (MRGs) were established. Metagenome and multivariance analyses indicated that the microbial structures, distribution of resistance genes and mobile genetic elements (MGEs), and virulence factor genes (VFGs) significantly differed between the lakes. The hypereutrophic lake Nanhu harbored the lowest microbial diversity but the highest level of resistance genes. Microbial communities and MGEs were identified as the main drivers in shaping the profiles of ARGs and MRGs, while external environmental factors played an indirect role in the changing resistance genes. Two members of Proteobacteria, Aestuariivirga and Limnohabitans were identified as predominant bacterial hosts of ARGs in most samples. In addition, the resistome risk scores were found positively correlated with water quality factors and negatively correlated with microbial diversity in the urban lakes. Our study provides novel insights into the link between microbial diversity, MGEs, and the potential dissemination risk of ARGs in urban lakes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mao, Chengzhi","Wang, Xiao","Li, Xinghao","Kong, Qiaoyi","Xu, Elvis Genbo","Huang, Jie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671570"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xu, Elvis Genbo"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Hubei University of Technology","Ocean University of China","University of Chinese Academy of Science"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbial communities resistance genes and resistome risks in urban lakes of different trophic states internal links and external influences","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100233","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-671570","identifier":[{"id":"85151470813","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3a70fcc3-cb7c-4716-9337-590eb14edf90"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ADBCEB0CC5FCF92B8C23FBF34DF5BBCA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100233","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/220169430/1_s2.0_S2772416623000049_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"ocean university of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ocean University of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"hubei university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hubei University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of science","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Science","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecotoxicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chengzhi","key":"maopau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Chengzhi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinghao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xinghao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiaoyi","key":"kongpau","last":"Kong","name":"Kong, Qiaoyi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Elvis Genbo","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"6d6ca13b-421e-4ab9-a6ce-df92da56c683","name":"Xu, Elvis Genbo","orcid":"0000-0002-4414-1978","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.hazadv.2023.100233","issn":["27724166"],"journal":"Journal of Hazardous Materials Advances","paperid":"100233","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hazardous Materials Advances","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151470813"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3a70fcc3-cb7c-4716-9337-590eb14edf90"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Microbial communities, resistance genes, and resistome risks in urban lakes of different trophic states : internal links and external influences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671570","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this letter, a leaky-wave antenna (LWA) based on double-layer (DL) slow-wave structure, possessing high-scanning rate and wide-scanning angle features is investigated. The DL unit structure consists of a top-layer structure with cross-shaped unit and a bottom-layer structure with slot-shaped unit. The DL units realize the property of controlling the cutoff frequency and slope of dispersion curves independently by independently changing the unit slow-wave property of top and bottom layers. The radiation of LWA is achieved by triangularly modulating the cross-shaped units of top layer. Due to the existence of the slot-shaped units of bottom layer, strong slow-wave property is introduced to increase the growth rate of period phase shift, thus achieving high-scanning rate. Meanwhile, the n = -2 space harmonic (SH) of the LWA is separated from the fast-wave region of n = -1 SH, thus enlarging scanning angle in forward quadrant. A prototype of the proposed LWA is fabricated and measured. The LWA can achieve a wide-scanning angle from -68 ° to +74 ° in a narrow frequency band of 9 to 10.75 GHz.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zhang, Hong-Hao","Li, Rui","Ren, Jian","Du, Xiaoyu","Zhang, Chenghao","Sun, Xiao-Yuan","Yin, YingZeng","Shen, Ming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674007"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Xidian University"],"keyword":["Cutoff frequency","Dispersion","Leaky wave antenna","Metals","Power transmission lines","Substrates","Transmission line measurements","high scanning rate","wide scanning angle"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high scanning rate and wide scanning angle leaky wave antenna based on double layer slow wave structure","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85161039009&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-674007","identifier":[{"id":"85161039009","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ae362092-1d8d-45ba-a8b0-0dba5249268b"],"keyword":["Cutoff frequency","Dispersion","Double-layer slow-wave structure","Leaky wave antennas","Metals","Power transmission lines","Substrates","Transmission line measurements","high scanning rate","leaky-wave antenna","wide scanning angle"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6354B07D4B557946E621DBB6C6263241"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"xidian university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xidian University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, AI RF-sensors","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong-Hao","key":"zhanghonghaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Hong-Hao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui","key":"liruipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Rui","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"renjianpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Jian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoyu","key":"duxiaoyupau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Xiaoyu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chenghao","key":"zhangchenghaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Chenghao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Yuan","key":"sunxiaoyuanpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Xiao-Yuan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"YingZeng","key":"yinyingzengpau","last":"Yin","name":"Yin, YingZeng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ming","key":"shenmingpau","last":"Shen","locid":"fef97c7d-c5df-4fce-a27f-aff2429975c7","name":"Shen, Ming","orcid":"0000-0002-9388-3513","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lawp.2023.3278863","issn":["15361225"],"issue":"9","journal":"IEEE Antennas and Wireless Propagation Letters","pages":"2145-2149","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Antennas and Wireless Propagation Letters","title_org":"I E E E Antennas and Wireless Propagation Letters","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161039009"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ae362092-1d8d-45ba-a8b0-0dba5249268b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"High-Scanning-Rate and Wide-Scanning-Angle Leaky-Wave Antenna Based on Double-Layer Slow-Wave Structure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674007","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Development of high-performance materials for the capture and separation of CO2 from the gas mixture is significant to alleviate carbon emission and mitigate the greenhouse effect. In this work, a novel structure of C9N7 slit was developed to explore its CO2 adsorption capacity and selectivity using Grand Canonical Monte Carlo (GCMC) and Density Functional Theory (DFT) calculations. Among varying slit widths, C9N7 with the slit width of 0.7 nm exhibited remarkable CO2 uptake with superior CO2/N2 and CO2/CH4 selectivity. At 1 bar and 298 K, a maximum CO2 adsorption capacity can be obtained as high as 7.06 mmol/g, and the selectivity of CO2/N2 and CO2/CH4 was 41.43 and 18.67, respectively. In the presence of H2O, the CO2 uptake of C9N7 slit decreased slightly as the water content increased, showing better water tolerance. Furthermore, the underlying mechanism of highly selective CO2 adsorption and separation on the C9N7 surface was revealed. The closer the adsorption distance, the stronger the interaction energy between the gas molecule and the C9N7 surface. The strong interaction between the C9N7 nanosheet and the CO2 molecule contributes to its impressive CO2 uptake and selectivity performance, suggesting that the C9N7 slit could be a promising candidate for CO2 capture and separation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Liu, Zilong","Li, Xue","Shi, Di","Guo, Fengzhi","Zhao, Ge","Hei, Yanxiao","Xiao, Yufei","Zhang, Xiao","Peng, Yun Lei","Sun, Weichao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-676661"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Zilong","Zhang, Xiao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China University of Petroleum - Beijing","Jiangxi Normal University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"superior selective co sub 000000000002 sub adsorption and separation over n sub 000000000002 sub and ch sub 000000000004 sub of porous carbon nitride nanosheets insights from gcmc and dft simulations","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85156237391","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank Prof. Xiaofang Li and Dr. Xiao Chang (China University of Petroleum, Qingdao) for their active discussions and valuable suggestions. The computations were performed on Materials Studio at the Shenzhen Supercomputing Center. This work was supported by the Open Project Program of the State–Province Joint Engineering Laboratory of Zeolite Membrane Materials (no. SPJELZMM-202207), the Science Foundation of the China University of Petroleum, Beijing (no. 2462020BJRC007 and 2462022YXZZ007), and the State Key Laboratory of Petroleum Resources and Prospecting, China University of Petroleum (no. PRP/DX-2216). The authors thank Prof. Xiaofang Li and Dr. Xiao Chang (China University of Petroleum, Qingdao) for their active discussions and valuable suggestions. The computations were performed on Materials Studio at the Shenzhen Supercomputing Center. This work was supported by the Open Project Program of the State-Province Joint Engineering Laboratory of Zeolite Membrane Materials (no. SPJELZMM-202207), the Science Foundation of the China University of Petroleum, Beijing (no. 2462020BJRC007 and 2462022YXZZ007), and the State Key Laboratory of Petroleum Resources and Prospecting, China University of Petroleum (no. PRP/DX-2216)."],"id":"S01-000.00-676661","identifier":[{"id":"37098239","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85156237391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-49668332-84e3-49f8-b976-692d1e215622"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F424DD282C2D1B53E4AA96172D23AFEE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china university of petroleum beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Petroleum - Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"jiangxi normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangxi Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Physical and Biophysical Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zilong","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zilong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xue","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xue","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Di","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Di","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fengzhi","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Fengzhi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ge","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Ge","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanxiao","key":"heipau","last":"Hei","name":"Hei, Yanxiao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yufei","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Yufei","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yun Lei","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Yun Lei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Weichao","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","locid":"7852fe34-1c57-4afd-97f3-36ba2a963101","name":"Sun, Weichao","orcid":"0000-0002-8597-7501","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37098239"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.langmuir.3c00595","issn":["07437463","15205827"],"issn_org":["07437463"],"issue":"18","journal":"Langmuir","pages":"6613-6622","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Langmuir","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85156237391"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-49668332-84e3-49f8-b976-692d1e215622"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Superior Selective CO<sub>2</sub> Adsorption and Separation over N<sub>2</sub> and CH<sub>4</sub> of Porous Carbon Nitride Nanosheets : Insights from GCMC and DFT Simulations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-676661","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Atmospheric nitrogen (N) deposition is altering grassland productivity and community structure worldwide. Deposited N comes in different forms, which can have different consequences for productivity due to differences in their fertilization and acidification effects. We hypothesize that these effects may be mediated by changes in plant functional traits. We investigated the responses of aboveground primary productivity and community functional composition to addition of three nitrogen compounds (NH4NO3, [NH4]2SO4, and CO[NH2]2) at the rates of 0, 5, 10, 20 g N m−2 yr−1. We used structural equation modeling (SEM) to evaluate how functional structure influences the responses of productivity to the three N compounds. Nitrogen addition increased community-level leaf chlorophyll content but decreased leaf dry matter content and phosphorus concentration. These changes were mainly due to intra-specific variation. Functional dispersion of traits was reduced by N addition through changes in species composition. SEM revealed that fertilization effects were more important than soil acidification for the responses of productivity to CO(NH2)2 addition, which enhanced productivity by decreasing functional trait dispersion. In contrast, the effects of (NH4)2SO4 and NH4NO3 were primarily due to soil acidification, influencing productivity via community-weighted means of functional traits. Our results suggest that N forms with different fertilizing and acidifying effects influence productivity via different functional traits pathways. Our study also emphasizes the need for in situ experiments with the relevant N compounds to accurately understand and predict the ecological effects of atmospheric N deposition on ecosystems.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Cai, Jiangping","Weiner, Jacob","Luo, Wentao","Feng, Xue","Yang, Guojiao","Lu, Jiayu","Lü, Xiao Tao","Li, Mai He","Jiang, Yong","Han, Xingguo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683835"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Botany","CAS - Shenyang Institute of Applied Ecology","Hebei University","Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research"],"keyword":["Functional structure","Grassland productivity","Intraspecific variation","Nitrogen deposition","Species turnover"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional structure mediates the responses of productivity to addition of three nitrogen compounds in a meadow steppe","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/425362567/Cai_2023_Functional_structure_mediates_the_responses_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-683835","identifier":[{"id":"85146678886","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36688977","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000917327700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-3269679f-e23a-4f06-9caf-b0c7a011473a"],"keyword":["Functional structure","Grassland productivity","Intraspecific variation","Nitrogen deposition","Species turnover"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E683192FD6C1B72BA93A2B3B75B5BF73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/425362567/Cai_2023_Functional_structure_mediates_the_responses_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas shenyang institute of applied ecology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Shenyang Institute of Applied Ecology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas institute of botany","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Institute of Botany","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Organismal Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute for forest snow and landscape research","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute for Forest, Snow and Landscape Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"hebei university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hebei University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jiangping","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Jiangping","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"weinerpau","last":"Weiner","locid":"dd3c08ff-333b-4591-9968-3957845a6fa1","name":"Weiner, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-0736-7943","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wentao","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Wentao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xue","key":"fengpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Xue","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guojiao","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Guojiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiayu","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Jiayu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Tao","key":"lüpau","last":"Lü","name":"Lü, Xiao Tao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Mai He","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Mai He","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Yong","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Yong","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xingguo","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Xingguo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36688977"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00442-022-05310-9","issn":["00298549","14321939"],"issn_org":["00298549"],"journal":"Oecologia","pages":"575-584","status":"p","title":"Oecologia","volume":"201"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146678886"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3269679f-e23a-4f06-9caf-b0c7a011473a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Functional structure mediates the responses of productivity to addition of three nitrogen compounds in a meadow steppe","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-683835","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The role of microbial interactions and the underlying mechanisms that shape complex biofilm communities are poorly understood. Here we employ a microfluidic chip to represent porous subsurface environments and show that cooperative microbial interactions between free-living and biofilm-forming bacteria trigger active spatial segregation to promote their respective dominance in segregated microhabitats. During initial colonization, free-living and biofilm-forming microbes are segregated from the mixed planktonic inoculum to occupy the ambient fluid and grain surface. Contrary to spatial exclusion through competition, the active spatial segregation is induced by cooperative interactions which improves the fitness of both biofilm and planktonic populations. We further show that free-living Arthrobacter induces the surface colonization by scavenging the biofilm inhibitor, D-amino acids and receives benefits from the public goods secreted by the biofilm-forming strains. Collectively, our results reveal how cooperative microbial interactions may contribute to microbial coexistence in segregated microhabitats and drive subsurface biofilm community succession.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Wu, Yichao","Fu, Chengxia","Peacock, Caroline L.","Sørensen, Søren Johannes","Redmile-Gordon, Marc A.","Xiao, Ke Qing","Gao, Chunhui","Liu, Jun","Huang, Qiaoyun","Li, Zixue","Song, Peiyi","Zhu, Yongguan","Zhou, Jizhong","Cai, Peng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-684345"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Huazhong Agricultural University","Huazhong University of Science and Technology","Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory","Royal Horticultural Society","Tsinghua University","University of Leeds","University of Oklahoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cooperative microbial interactions drive spatial segregation in porous environments","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39991-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-684345","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10349867","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85164754809","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37454222","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a43019b4-3817-4c7a-b200-bb540d434cf0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C90C000DC763B81993BAD00BFFDEEBAD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360248716/s41467_023_39991_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39991-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"huazhong agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of leeds","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Leeds","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"royal horticultural society","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Horticultural Society","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"cas research center for eco environmental sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"huazhong university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"lawrence berkeley national laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yichao","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Yichao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chengxia","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Chengxia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Caroline L.","key":"peacockpau","last":"Peacock","name":"Peacock, Caroline L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Søren J.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1a8a144e-52fd-4508-b364-6e3ea6cfaa8a","name":"Sørensen, Søren Johannes","name_org":"Sørensen, Søren J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6227-9906","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Marc A.","key":"redmilegordonpau","last":"Redmile-Gordon","name":"Redmile-Gordon, Marc A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Ke Qing","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Ke Qing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Chunhui","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Chunhui","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jun","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Qiaoyun","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Qiaoyun","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Zixue","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zixue","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Peiyi","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Peiyi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 7","first":"Yongguan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yongguan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9 10","first":"Jizhong","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Jizhong","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peng","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Peng","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37454222"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-023-39991-4","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"4226","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164754809"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a43019b4-3817-4c7a-b200-bb540d434cf0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cooperative microbial interactions drive spatial segregation in porous environments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-684345","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Globally, reducing carbon emissions and mitigating soil heavy metal pollution pose pressing challenges. We evaluated the effects of lead (Pb) and cadmium (Cd) contamination in the field over 20 years. The five treatment groups featured Pb concentrations of 40 and 250 mg/kg, Cd concentrations of 10 and 60 mg/kg, and a combination of Pb and Cd (60 and 20 mg/kg, respectively); we also included a pollution-free control group. After 20 years, soil pH decreased notably in all treatments, particularly by 1.02 in Cd10-treated soil. In addition to the increase of SOC in Cd10 and unchanged in Pb40 treatment, the SOC was reduced by 9.62%–12.98% under the other treatments. The α diversities of bacteria and fungi were significantly changed by Cd10 pollution (both p < 0.05) and the microbial community structure changed significantly. However, there were no significant changes in bacterial and fungal communities under other treatments. Cd10 pollution reduced the numbers of Ascomycota and Basidiomycota fungi, and enhanced SOC accumulation. Compared to the control, long-term heavy Cd, Pb, and Pb–Cd composite pollution caused SOC loss by increasing Basidiomycota which promoting carbon degradation, and decreasing Proteobacteria which promoting carbon fixation via the Krebs cycle. Our findings demonstrate that heavy metal pollution mediates Carbon-cycling microorganisms and genes, impacting SOC storage.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Xiao, Zhineng","Duan, Changqun","Li, Shiyu","Chen, Ji","Peng, Changhui","Che, Rongxiao","Liu, Chang'e","Huang, Yin","Mei, Runran","Xu, Liangliang","Luo, Pengfei","Yu, Yadong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-687579"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Shiyu"],"country":["Canada","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Université du Québec à Montréal","Yunnan University"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Carbon cycle","Carbon reduction","Fungi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the microbial mechanisms by which long term heavy metal contamination affects soil organic carbon levels","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85168082987","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-687579","identifier":[{"id":"37562505","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85168082987","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-35ebcbd9-3f8b-49f8-99e1-ccf83b98f15b"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Carbon cycle","Carbon reduction","Fungi","Soil heavy metal pollution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB97625CA2B4BF7AAF63A39ACF5456DA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"yunnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Yunnan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Climate and Water"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"université du québec à montréal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Université du Québec à Montréal","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhineng","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Zhineng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Changqun","key":"duanpau","last":"Duan","name":"Duan, Changqun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shiyu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shiyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ji","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"05f23b9e-16c0-478d-840b-18a8d914c393","name":"Chen, Ji","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Changhui","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Changhui","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rongxiao","key":"chepau","last":"Che","name":"Che, Rongxiao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chang'e","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Chang'e","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yin","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Yin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Runran","key":"meipau","last":"Mei","name":"Mei, Runran","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liangliang","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Liangliang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengfei","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Pengfei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yadong","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Yadong","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37562505"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.chemosphere.2023.139770","issn":["00456535","18791298"],"issn_org":["00456535"],"journal":"Chemosphere","paperid":"139770","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Chemosphere","volume":"340"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168082987"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-35ebcbd9-3f8b-49f8-99e1-ccf83b98f15b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The microbial mechanisms by which long-term heavy metal contamination affects soil organic carbon levels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-687579","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Lung adenocarcinoma is the most common type of lung cancer. Known risk variants explain only a small fraction of lung adenocarcinoma heritability. Here, we conducted a two-stage genome-wide association study of lung adenocarcinoma of East Asian ancestry (21,658 cases and 150,676 controls; 54.5% never-smokers) and identified 12 novel susceptibility variants, bringing the total number to 28 at 25 independent loci. Transcriptome-wide association analyses together with colocalization studies using a Taiwanese lung expression quantitative trait loci dataset (n = 115) identified novel candidate genes, including FADS1 at 11q12 and ELF5 at 11p13. In a multi-ancestry meta-analysis of East Asian and European studies, four loci were identified at 2p11, 4q32, 16q23, and 18q12. At the same time, most of our findings in East Asian populations showed no evidence of association in European populations. In our studies drawn from East Asian populations, a polygenic risk score based on the 25 loci had a stronger association in never-smokers vs. individuals with a history of smoking (Pinteraction = 0.0058). These findings provide new insights into the etiology of lung adenocarcinoma in individuals from East Asian populations, which could be important in developing translational applications.","author_count":222,"contributors":["Shi, Jianxin","Shiraishi, Kouya","Choi, Jiyeon","Matsuo, Keitaro","Chen, Tzu Yu","Dai, Juncheng","Hung, Rayjean J.","Chen, Kexin","Shu, Xiao Ou","Kim, Young Tae","Landi, Maria Teresa","Lin, Dongxin","Zheng, Wei","Yin, Zhihua","Zhou, Baosen","Song, Bao","Wang, Jiucun","Seow, Wei Jie","Song, Lei","Chang, I. Shou","Hu, Wei","Chien, Li Hsin","Cai, Qiuyin","Hong, Yun Chul","Kim, Hee Nam","Wu, Yi Long","Wong, Maria Pik","Richardson, Brian Douglas","Funderburk, Karen M.","Li, Shilan","Zhang, Tongwu","Breeze, Charles","Wang, Zhaoming","Blechter, Batel","Bassig, Bryan A.","Kim, Jin Hee","Albanes, Demetrius","Wong, Jason Y.Y.","Shin, Min Ho","Chung, Lap Ping","Yang, Yang","An, She Juan","Zheng, Hong","Yatabe, Yasushi","Zhang, Xu Chao","Kim, Young Chul","Caporaso, Neil E.","Chang, Jiang","Ho, James Chung Man","Kubo, Michiaki","Daigo, Yataro","Song, Minsun","Momozawa, Yukihide","Kamatani, Yoichiro","Kobayashi, Masashi","Okubo, Kenichi","Honda, Takayuki","Hosgood, Dean H.","Kunitoh, Hideo","Patel, Harsh","Watanabe, Shun ichi","Miyagi, Yohei","Nakayama, Haruhiko","Matsumoto, Shingo","Horinouchi, Hidehito","Tsuboi, Masahiro","Hamamoto, Ryuji","Goto, Koichi","Ohe, Yuichiro","Takahashi, Atsushi","Goto, Akiteru","Minamiya, Yoshihiro","Hara, Megumi","Nishida, Yuichiro","Takeuchi, Kenji","Wakai, Kenji","Matsuda, Koichi","Murakami, Yoshinori","Shimizu, Kimihiro","Suzuki, Hiroyuki","Saito, Motonobu","Ohtaki, Yoichi","Tanaka, Kazumi","Wu, Tangchun","Wei, Fusheng","Dai, Hongji","Machiela, Mitchell J.","Su, Jian","Kim, Yeul Hong","Oh, In Jae","Lee, Victor Ho Fun","Chang, Gee Chen","Tsai, Ying Huang","Chen, Kuan Yu","Huang, Ming Shyan","Su, Wu Chou","Chen, Yuh Min","Seow, Adeline","Park, Jae Yong","Kweon, Sun Seog","Chen, Kun Chieh","Gao, Yu Tang","Qian, Biyun","Wu, Chen","Lu, Daru","Liu, Jianjun","Schwartz, Ann G.","Houlston, Richard","Spitz, Margaret R.","Gorlov, Ivan P.","Wu, Xifeng","Yang, Ping","Lam, Stephen","Tardon, Adonina","Chen, Chu","Bojesen, Stig E","Johansson, Mattias","Risch, Angela","Bickeböller, Heike","Ji, Bu Tian","Wichmann, H. Erich","Christiani, David C.","Rennert, Gadi","Arnold, Susanne","Brennan, Paul","McKay, James","Field, John K.","Shete, Sanjay S.","Le Marchand, Loic","Liu, Geoffrey","Andrew, Angeline","Kiemeney, Lambertus A.","Zienolddiny-Narui, Shan","Grankvist, Kjell","Johansson, Mikael","Cox, Angela","Taylor, Fiona","Yuan, Jian Min","Lazarus, Philip","Schabath, Matthew B.","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Jeon, Hyo Sung","Jiang, Shih Sheng","Sung, Jae Sook","Chen, Chung Hsing","Hsiao, Chin Fu","Jung, Yoo Jin","Guo, Huan","Hu, Zhibin","Burdett, Laurie","Yeager, Meredith","Hutchinson, Amy","Hicks, Belynda","Liu, Jia",