{"abstract":"An effective cancer therapy requires both killing cancer cells and targeting tumor-promoting pathways or cell populations within the tumor microenvironment (TME). We purposely search for molecules that are critical for multiple tumor-promoting cell types and identified nuclear receptor subfamily 4 group A member 1 (NR4A1) as one such molecule. NR4A1 has been shown to promote the aggressiveness of cancer cells and maintain the immune suppressive TME. Using genetic and pharmacological approaches, we establish NR4A1 as a valid therapeutic target for cancer therapy. Importantly, we have developed the first-of-its kind proteolysis-targeting chimera (PROTAC, named NR-V04) against NR4A1. NR-V04 effectively degrades NR4A1 within hours of treatment in vitro and sustains for at least 4 days in vivo, exhibiting long-lasting NR4A1-degradation in tumors and an excellent safety profile. NR-V04 leads to robust tumor inhibition and sometimes eradication of established melanoma tumors. At the mechanistic level, we have identified an unexpected novel mechanism via significant induction of tumor-infiltrating (TI) B cells as well as an inhibition of monocytic myeloid derived suppressor cells (m-MDSC), two clinically relevant immune cell populations in human melanomas. Overall, NR-V04-mediated NR4A1 degradation holds promise for enhancing anti-cancer immune responses and offers a new avenue for treating various types of cancer.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Wang, Lei","Xiao, Yufeng","Luo, Yuewan","Master, Rohan P","Mo, Jiao","Kim, Myung-Chul","Liu, Yi","Patel, Urvi M","Li, Xiangming","Shaffer, Donald","Guertin, Kevin R","Moser, Emily","Smalley, Keiran S","Zhou, Daohong","Zheng, Guangrong","Zhang, Weizhou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798913"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sanofi","University of Florida","University of Texas at San Antonio"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unleashing the power of nr000000000004a000000000001 degradation as a novel strategy for cancer immunotherapy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.08.09.552650","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-798913","identifier":[{"id":"37609171","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10441411","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-10147e1a-3935-4af1-83f9-001b7030cd93"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2ADF65A996C3DB33D5D54230D3900F30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.08.09.552650","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/448203228/Liwei_Lyu.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of florida","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Florida","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Andersen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"sanofi","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sanofi","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of texas at san antonio","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas at San Antonio","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yufeng","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Yufeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yuewan","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","locid":"92676be6-d2a7-48a1-92ac-98eade80fb46","name":"Luo, Yuewan","orcid":"0000-0002-8964-5301","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rohan P","key":"masterpau","last":"Master","name":"Master, Rohan P","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiao","key":"mopau","last":"Mo","name":"Mo, Jiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Myung-Chul","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","name":"Kim, Myung-Chul","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yi","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Urvi M","key":"patelpau","last":"Patel","name":"Patel, Urvi M","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Xiangming","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiangming","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Donald","key":"shafferpau","last":"Shaffer","name":"Shaffer, Donald","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kevin R","key":"guertinpau","last":"Guertin","name":"Guertin, Kevin R","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emily","key":"moserpau","last":"Moser","name":"Moser, Emily","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Keiran S","key":"smalleypau","last":"Smalley","name":"Smalley, Keiran S","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Daohong","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Daohong","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guangrong","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Guangrong","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Weizhou","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Weizhou","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37609171"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/2023.08.09.552650","issn":["26928205"],"pages":"46","series":"bioRxiv","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-10147e1a-3935-4af1-83f9-001b7030cd93"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unleashing the Power of NR4A1 Degradation as a Novel Strategy for Cancer Immunotherapy","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798913","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Comparative analysis of primate genomes within a phylogenetic context is essential for understanding the evolution of human genetic architecture and primate diversity. We present such a study of 50 primate species spanning 38 genera and 14 families, including 27 genomes first reported here, with many from previously less well represented groups, the New World monkeys and the Strepsirrhini. Our analyses reveal heterogeneous rates of genomic rearrangement and gene evolution across primate lineages. Thousands of genes under positive selection in different lineages play roles in the nervous, skeletal, and digestive systems and may have contributed to primate innovations and adaptations. Our study reveals that many key genomic innovations occurred in the Simiiformes ancestral node and may have had an impact on the adaptive radiation of the Simiiformes and human evolution.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Shao, Yong","Zhou, Long","Li, Fang","Zhao, Lan","Zhang, Bao Lin","Shao, Feng","Chen, Jia Wei","Chen, Chun Yan","Bi, Xupeng","Zhuang, Xiao Lin","Zhu, Hong Liang","Hu, Jiang","Sun, Zongyi","Li, Xin","Wang, Depeng","Rivas-González, Iker","Wang, Sheng","Wang, Yun Mei","Chen, Wu","Li, Gang","Lu, Hui Meng","Liu, Yang","Kuderna, Lukas F.K.","Farh, Kyle Kai How","Fan, Peng Fei","Yu, Li","Li, Ming","Liu, Zhi Jin","Tiley, George P.","Yoder, Anne D.","Roos, Christian","Hayakawa, Takashi","Marques-Bonet, Tomas","Rogers, Jeffrey","Stenson, Peter D.","Cooper, David N.","Schierup, Mikkel Heide","Yao, Yong Gang","Zhang, Ya Ping","Wang, Wen","Qi, Xiao Guang","Zhang, Guojie","Wu, Dong Dong"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-672772"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Germany","Japan","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Autonomous University of Barcelona","BGI","BGI-Shenzhen","Barcelona Institute of Science and Technology (BIST)","Baylor College of Medicine","Beijing Grandomics Biosciences Co., Ltd (Biz)","CAS - Institute of Zoology","CAS - Kunming Institute of Zoology","Capital Normal University","Cardiff University","Centre for Genomic Regulation","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Duke University","German Primate Center - Leibniz Institute for Primate Research","Guangzhou Wildlife Research Center","Hokkaido University","ICREA","Illumina","Japan Monkey Centre","Northwest University China","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","Pompeu Fabra University","Shaanxi Normal University","Southwest University","Sun Yat-Sen University","The Spanish National Research Council (CSIC)","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Yunnan University","Zhejiang University","Zhejiang Wanli University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phylogenomic analyses provide insights into primate evolution","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/406082273/Flagship_Manuscript_20221216_GZ_SY1_2_38.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-672772","identifier":[{"id":"85160631037","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37262173","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b439427f-2337-4b8e-83c5-897bfca53dc3","ku-d9bb4561-ecd3-4999-8079-32e8bb7645ff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E219E4F5208201AA173302A8135EC7D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/406082273/Flagship_Manuscript_20221216_GZ_SY1_2_38.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas kunming institute of 