ournal of Hazardous Materials","paperid":"131160","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Hazardous Materials","volume":"451"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149758724"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1d99c5f8-8e35-4f3c-8548-6986f1da6c1f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Meta-analysis reveals cyanotoxins risk across African inland waters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146277","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Long-read sequencing (LRS) facilitates both the genome assembly and the discovery of structural variants (SVs). Here, we built a graph-based pig pangenome by incorporating 11 LRS genomes with an average of 94.01% BUSCO completeness score, revealing 206-Mb novel sequences. We discovered 183,352 nonredundant SVs (63% novel), representing 12.12% of the reference genome. By genotyping SVs in an additional 196 short-read sequencing samples, we identified thousands of population stratified SVs. Particularly, we detected 7,568 Tibetan specific SVs, some of which demonstrate significant population differentiation between Tibetan and low-altitude pigs, which might be associated with the high-altitude hypoxia adaptation in Tibetan pigs. Further integrating functional genomic data, the most promising candidate genes within the SVs that might contribute to the high-altitude hypoxia adaptation were discovered. Overall, our study generates a benchmark pangenome resource for illustrating the important roles of SVs in adaptive evolution, domestication, and genetic improvement of agronomic traits in pigs.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Jiang, Yi Fan","Wang, Sheng","Wang, Chong Long","Xu, Ru Hai","Wang, Wen Wen","Jiang, Yao","Wang, Ming Shan","Jiang, Li","Dai, Li He","Wang, Jie Ru","Chu, Xiao Hong","Zeng, Yong Qing","Fang, Lingzhao","Wu, Dong Dong","Zhang, Qin","Ding, Xiang Dong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-190061"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Ding, Xiang Dong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anhui Academy of Agricultural Sciences","CAS - Kunming Institute of Zoology","China Agricultural University","Shandong Agricultural University","Zhejiang Academy of Agricultural Sciences"],"keyword":["Animals","Genomics","Phylogenetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pangenome obtained by long read sequencing of 000000000011 genomes reveal hidden functional structural variants in pigs","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2023.106119","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-190061","identifier":[{"id":"85148041417","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9958381","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36852268","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6a7242eb-4a50-4f68-814c-8d5e7e8d8bbb"],"keyword":["Animals","Genomics","Phylogenetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A99CF1325A045FA1FE26B41FD76670CD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2023.106119","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas kunming institute of zoology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Kunming Institute of Zoology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"anhui academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Anhui Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"shandong agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi Fan","key":"jiangyifanpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Yi Fan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheng","key":"wangshengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Sheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chong Long","key":"wangchonglongpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chong Long","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ru Hai","key":"xuruhaipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Ru Hai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen Wen","key":"wangwenwenpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wen Wen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yao","key":"jiangyaopau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Yao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ming Shan","key":"wangmingshanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ming Shan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"jianglipau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Li","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Li He","key":"dailihepau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Li He","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie Ru","key":"wangjierupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jie Ru","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Hong","key":"chuxiaohongpau","last":"Chu","name":"Chu, Xiao Hong","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong Qing","key":"zengyongqingpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Yong Qing","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ling Zhao","key":"fanglingzhaopau","last":"Fang","locid":"4e548f18-1d3b-4395-b7ad-6c7b7d1d1f79","name":"Fang, Lingzhao","name_org":"Fang, Ling Zhao","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong Dong","key":"wudongdongpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Dong Dong","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Qin","key":"zhangqinpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Qin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiang Dong","key":"dingxiangdongpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Xiang Dong","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36852268"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.isci.2023.106119","issn":["25890042"],"issue":"3","journal":"iScience","paperid":"106119","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"iScience","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148041417"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6a7242eb-4a50-4f68-814c-8d5e7e8d8bbb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pangenome obtained by long-read sequencing of 11 genomes reveal hidden functional structural variants in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-190061","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The combination of nitrogen (N) fertilization and straw incorporation has complex influences on soil N transformations and derived nitrous oxide (N2O) emissions. This study aimed to reveal the coupled effects of straw returning forms and N fertilizer management on soil N2O emissions. Here, carbon (C) sources with varied availabilities were supplied by different straw returning forms, including straw, charred straw, and combined application of straw and charred straw. The time gaps between additions of exogenous N and C sources were carried out by managing the timing of N fertilization, including N application simultaneous with or delayed after straw return. Soil N2O emissions under different straw returning forms and their response relationships to soil C, N, microbial biomass, as well as soil pH and oxygen (O2) were explored. Co-application of straw and N fertilizer provided sufficient C and N sources, enhanced the microbial biomass, and consequently increased N2O emissions. Delayed N fertilization could decouple the response of N2O emissions to straw addition, because of constrained N availability and limited pH decline, which decreased the cumulative N2O emissions significantly. Possibly due to straw induced N immobilization coupled with charred straw induced pH elevation, the combined application of straw and charred straw constrained soil N2O emissions compared with straw only application, regardless of N fertilizer management. By shaping the microbial biomass and soil C, N, and O2 dynamics, delayed application of N fertilizer could further enhance the inhibition effect of the charred straw and straw combination on soil N2O emissions. Therefore, the varied straw returning forms and the timing of N fertilization could affect the supply of available C and N, influencing the hot moments of N2O emissions, and the joint addition of straw and charred straw with a few weeks delayed N application could possibly reduce the risk of soil N2O emissions from straw return systems. Such mitigation potential should be evaluated further under field conditions. Highlights: Delayed N fertilization attenuated the magnitude of N2O emissions after straw additions. Combination of charred straw with straw mitigated N2O emissions, further enhanced by delayed N fertilization. Soil pH was the chief regulator for N2O emissions under different straw returning forms and N application.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ye, Xin","Ran, Hongyu","Wang, Xiao","Li, Guitong","Ambus, Per Lennart","Wang, Gang","Zhu, Kun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-399178"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Biochar","NO emission factor","Soil pH"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"delayed nitrogen application after straw and charred straw addition altered the hot moment of soil n sub 000000000002 sub o emissions","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359553878/AASA_European_J_Soil_Science_2023_Ye_Delayed_nitrogen_application_after_straw_and_charred_straw_addition_altered_the_hot.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-399178","identifier":[{"id":"85148864757","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-098c0f13-4892-44f1-a1af-666f7fe62989"],"keyword":["NO emission factor","biochar","charred straw","soil pH","straw returning forms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59D9A105D4DE29D65BCE6D43AC426F50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359553878/AASA_European_J_Soil_Science_2023_Ye_Delayed_nitrogen_application_after_straw_and_charred_straw_addition_altered_the_hot.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xin","key":"yexinpau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Xin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hongyu","key":"ranhongyupau","last":"Ran","name":"Ran, Hongyu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao","key":"wangxiaopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guitong","key":"liguitongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Guitong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per","key":"ambusperlennartpau","last":"Ambus","locid":"e3fc10b5-9fcd-494b-a3bc-dcfbede40f90","name":"Ambus, Per Lennart","name_org":"Ambus, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-7580-524X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gang","key":"wanggangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Gang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kun","key":"zhukunpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Kun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejss.13349","issn":["13510754","13652389"],"issn_org":["13510754"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Soil Science","paperid":"e13349","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Soil Science","volume":"74"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148864757"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-098c0f13-4892-44f1-a1af-666f7fe62989"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Delayed nitrogen application after straw and charred straw addition altered the hot moment of soil N<sub>2</sub>O emissions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-399178","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This brief provides a mutual coupling suppression network for antenna arrays with high frequency selectivity. The proposed network is composed of three-order (denoting three decoupling bridges established by transmission lines) decoupling networks and unequal power dividers consisting of complementary split-ring resonators featuring bandpass and harmonic suppression responses. All the decoupling structures are highly integrated. A design example of a 2×4 patch antenna array, working at 4.9 GHz and integrated with the proposed decoupling network, is constructed and fabricated. Simulated and measured results indicate that the antenna array is well-decoupled involving the suppression of vertical, horizontal, and diagonal coupling paths. The measured common bandwidth of impedance matching (|Sii| < ‒10 dB) and isolation (> 25 dB) is from 4.8 to 5.1 GHz. A small insertion loss of 0.35 dB is introduced. Moreover, a filtering response is observed, and gain nulls are generated at the two sides of the operating band. As for the demonstrator, spurious up to 11 GHz is well suppressed and the peak gain at the harmonic band is reduced by over 20 dB, exhibiting a good harmonic suppression performance.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Yiming","Li, Xu","Zhang, Shuai","Xiao, Shaoqiu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674074"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Shaoqiu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sun Yat-Sen University"],"keyword":["Antenna arrays","Antenna decoupling","Bandpass","Bridge circuits","Couplings","Filtering","Harmonic suppression","Harmonics suppression","Large scale array","Mutual coupling","Power dividers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"decoupling network integrated with csrr based filtering power dividers for antenna arrays","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/540783720/Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Guangdong Basic and Applied Basic Research Foundation under Grant 2023A1515011412."],"id":"S01-000.00-674074","identifier":[{"id":"85164801904","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bdbd95ed-e662-4e0d-94a7-0da387a70da3"],"keyword":["Antenna arrays","Bridge circuits","Couplings","Filtering","Harmonics suppression","Multiple input multiple output antennas","Mutual coupling","Power dividers","antenna decoupling","bandpass","harmonic suppression","large-scale array"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A78A9F49C526EFFE15F9035ECE26E088"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/540783720/Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yiming","key":"zhangyimingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yiming","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xu","key":"lixupau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shuai","key":"zhangshuaipau","last":"Zhang","locid":"c97f8895-893d-4895-bc19-d7bf7d5fe6d9","name":"Zhang, Shuai","orcid":"0000-0002-9003-2879","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shaoqiu","key":"xiaoshaoqiupau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Shaoqiu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tcsii.2023.3294907","issn":["15497747"],"issue":"12","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems. Part 2: Express Briefs","pages":"4334-4338","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Circuits and Systems. Part 2: Express Briefs","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Circuits and Systems. Part 2: Express Briefs","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164801904"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bdbd95ed-e662-4e0d-94a7-0da387a70da3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Decoupling Network Integrated With CSRR-Based Filtering Power Dividers for Antenna Arrays","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-674074","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"By a survey of metagenome-wide association studies (MWAS), we found a robust depletion of Bacteroides cellulosilyticus, Faecalibacterium prausnitzii, and Roseburia intestinalis in individuals with atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ACVD). From an established collection of bacteria isolated from healthy Chinese individuals, we selected B. cellulosilyticus, R. intestinalis, and Faecalibacterium longum, a bacterium related to F. prausnitzii, and tested the effects of these bacteria in an Apoe/− atherosclerosis mouse model. We show that administration of these three bacterial species to Apoe−/− mice robustly improves cardiac function, reduces plasma lipid levels, and attenuates the formation of atherosclerotic plaques. Comprehensive analysis of gut microbiota, plasma metabolome, and liver transcriptome revealed that the beneficial effects are associated with a modulation of the gut microbiota linked to a 7α-dehydroxylation–lithocholic acid (LCA)–farnesoid X receptor (FXR) pathway. Our study provides insights into transcriptional and metabolic impact whereby specific bacteria may hold promises for prevention/treatment of ACVD.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Jie, Zhuye","Zhu, Qian","Zou, Yuanqiang","Wu, Qili","Qin, Min","He, Dongdong","Lin, Xiaoqian","Tong, Xin","Zhang, Jiahao","Jie, Zhu","Luo, Wenwei","Xiao, Xiao","Chen, Shiyu","Wu, Yonglin","Guo, Gongjie","Zheng, Shufen","Li, Yong","Lai, Weihua","Yang, Huanming","Wang, Jian","Xiao, Liang","Chen, Jiyan","Zhang, Tao","Kristiansen, Karsten","Jia, Huijue","Zhong, Shilong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677756"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","James D. Watson Institute of Genome Sciences","South China University of Technology","Southern Medical University"],"keyword":["Bacteriology","Human metabolism","Microbial metabolism","Microbiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a consortium of three bacteria isolated from human feces inhibits formation of atherosclerotic deposits and lowers lipid levels in a mouse model","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2023.106960","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677756","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10291474","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85161545611","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37378328","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-261cc084-be59-4a7b-8934-7ddd260725d9"],"keyword":["Bacteriology","Human metabolism","Microbial metabolism","Microbiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AEAA8ED209FFAEE4A7EA6F3C09C68515"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2023.106960","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357066184/1_s2.0_S2589004223010374_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"southern medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology",