0908"],"issn_org":["17520894"],"journal":"Nature Geoscience","pages":"56-62","status":"p","title":"Nature Geoscience","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143789938"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-978141d2-526a-4cc0-b6bd-7307466e0874"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Siberian carbon sink reduced by forest disturbances","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-678733","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The programmed cell death protein 1 (PD-1) is an inhibitory receptor on T cells and plays an important role in promoting cancer immune evasion. While ubiquitin E3 ligases regulating PD-1 stability have been reported, deubiquitinases governing PD-1 homeostasis to modulate tumor immunotherapy remain unknown. Here, we identify the ubiquitin-specific protease 5 (USP5) as a bona fide deubiquitinase for PD-1. Mechanistically, USP5 interacts with PD-1, leading to deubiquitination and stabilization of PD-1. Moreover, extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK) phosphorylates PD-1 at Thr234 and promotes PD-1 interaction with USP5. Conditional knockout of Usp5 in T cells increases the production of effector cytokines and retards tumor growth in mice. USP5 inhibition in combination with Trametinib or anti-CTLA-4 has an additive effect on suppressing tumor growth in mice. Together, this study describes a molecular mechanism of ERK/USP5-mediated regulation of PD-1 and identifies potential combinatorial therapeutic strategies for enhancing anti-tumor efficacy.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Xiao, Xiangling","Shi, Jie","He, Chuan","Bu, Xia","Sun, Yishuang","Gao, Minling","Xiang, Bolin","Xiong, Wenjun","Dai, Panpan","Mao, Qi","Xing, Xixin","Yao, Yingmeng","Yu, Haisheng","Xu, Gaoshan","Li, Siqi","Ren, Yan","Chen, Baoxiang","Jiang, Congqing","Meng, Geng","Lee, Yu Ru","Wei, Wenyi","Freeman, Gordon J.","Xie, Conghua","Zhang, Jinfang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-678790"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Taiwan","United States"],"glorg":["Academia Sinica - Institute of Biomedical Sciences","All Global Affiliations","China Agricultural University","Harvard University","Shanghai University of Traditional Chinese Medicine","Wuhan University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"erk and usp000000000005 govern pd 000000000001 homeostasis via deubiquitination to modulate tumor immunotherapy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-38605-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-678790","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10199079","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37208329","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85159671957","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9e32b5d2-79b7-4001-9ac9-35a80ec63bdb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C6CD858CAC8F898B5BB8F1F1E3A0D828"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/347804919/s41467_023_38605_3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-38605-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"wuhan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shanghai university of traditional chinese medicine","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai University of Traditional Chinese Medicine","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, E