{"abstract":"A flux switching permanent magnet (FSPM) motor is designed and optimized in this article to achieve high torque density and expanded speed regulation range from a design viewpoint of pole-changing (PC). Based on the field modulation theory, the PM field in the FSPM motor is modulated by the stator and rotor teeth, generating rich harmonics with different pole-pair numbers in the air-gap flux density. By adopting an appropriate slot pole combination, working harmonics with different slot pitch angles are obtained to establish a basis for the PC-FSPM motor. Then, different working harmonics can be used to achieve different energy conversions with different winding configurations, so the PC operation can be performed to realize the high torque and wide speed regulation range by switching the working modes. Based on the field modulation theory, the operation principle of conventional and PC-FSPM motors is analyzed and compared. Then, according to the design principle of the PC-FSPM motor, a 24/22-pole PC-FSPM motor with the E-core is designed and optimized by a multilevel optimization method. Finally, the electromagnetic performances are analyzed by finite-element analysis and the test results of the prototype have verified the feasibility of the motor.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mao, Yi","Du, Yi","Xiao, Feng","Zhu, Xiaoyong","Quan, Li","Zhou, Dao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-681796"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangsu University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design and optimization of a pole changing flux switching permanent magnet motor","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/634048375/TPEL_Design_and_Optimization_of_SPMM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-681796","identifier":[{"id":"85147301618","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-54ce1332-9667-41e9-afe8-c404eb1a0f7d"],"keyword":["Air-gap field modulation","flux switching permanent magnet (FSPM) motor","pole changing (PC)","wide speed regulation range"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3720BEAE0EC8CE3458B259E6753ED02C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/634048375/TPEL_Design_and_Optimization_of_SPMM.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangsu university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangsu University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Mechatronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Reliability of Power Electronic Components","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Wind Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"maopau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Yi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"dupau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Yi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Feng","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Feng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoyong","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Xiaoyong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"quanpau","last":"Quan","name":"Quan, Li","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dao","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","locid":"8cf08fe2-24d6-4224-aaa2-f7e03a45debb","name":"Zhou, Dao","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-4309","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tie.2023.3237886","issn":["02780046","15579948"],"issn_org":["02780046"],"issue":"12","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","pages":"12636-12647","publisher":"IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Industrial Electronics","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147301618"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-54ce1332-9667-41e9-afe8-c404eb1a0f7d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Design and Optimization of a Pole Changing Flux Switching Permanent Magnet Motor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-681796","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this work, a new type of H2S sensor was fabricated by means of drop-coating of an Au/SnO-SnO2 nanosheet material, which was prepared by a one-pot hydrothermal reaction, onto a gold electrode in an alumina ceramic tube with the formation of a thin nanocomposite film. The microstructure and morphology of the nanosheet composites were characterized by scanning electron microscopy (SEM) and transmission electron microscopy (TEM). A gas-sensitivity study presented good H2S-sensing performance of such Au/SnO-SnO2 nanosheet composites. At an optimal operating temperature of 240 °C and ambient temperature of 25 °C, the resulting sensor showed a good linear response to H2S in a range of 1.0 to 100 ppm with a low detection limit of 0.7 ppm, and a very fast response-recovery time of 22 s for response and 63 s for recovery, respectively. The sensor was also unaffected by ambient humidity and had good reproducibility and selectivity. When being applied to the monitoring of H2S in an atmospheric environment in a pig farm, the response signal to H2S was only attenuated by 4.69% within 90 days, proving that the sensor had a long and stable service lifetime for continuous running and showing its important practical application prospects.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zou, Hao Yun","Li, Lin Xuan","Huang, Ying","Tang, Yi","Wu, Jian Ping","Xiao, Zhong Liang","Zeng, Ju Lan","Yu, Donghong","Cao, Zhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-681879"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Cao, Zhong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Changsha University of Science and Technology","SINOPEC","Sino-Danish Center for Education and Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an au sno sno sub 000000000002 sub nanosheet based composite used for rapid detection of hydrogen sulphide","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85149073183&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was financially supported by the projects of the National Natural Science Foundation of China (No. 21275022 and 22073011), Natural Science Foundation of Hunan Province, China (No. 2020JJ4599), Scientific Research Fund of Hunan Provincial Education Department of China (No. 21A0182), and Postgraduate Scientific Research Innovation Project of Hunan Province (No. CX2018B570). Support from the Sino-Danish Center for Education and Research is fully acknowledged."],"id":"S01-000.00-681879","identifier":[{"id":"36802289","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85149073183","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-866604a0-4578-4816-a647-426cfb187f40"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39396A35B0D3CD3A1EB07EE50F4274D2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"changsha university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Changsha University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"sinopec","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"SINOPEC","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"sino danish center for education and research","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sino-Danish Center for Education and Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao Yun","key":"zoupau","last":"Zou","name":"Zou, Hao Yun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lin Xuan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Lin Xuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Ying","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Yi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian Ping","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Jian Ping","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong Liang","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Zhong Liang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ju Lan","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Ju Lan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong","key":"caopau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhong","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36802289"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d2ay01891h","issn":["17599660","17599679"],"issn_org":["17599660"],"journal":"Analytical Methods","pages":"1315-1322","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Analytical Methods","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149073183"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-866604a0-4578-4816-a647-426cfb187f40"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An Au/SnO-SnO<sub>2</sub> nanosheet based composite used for rapid detection of hydrogen sulphide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-681879","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"High-fat diet (HFD)-induced insulin resistance (IR) in skeletal muscle is often accompanied by mitochondrial dysfunction and oxidative stress. Boosting nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide (NAD) using nicotinamide riboside (NR) can effectively decrease oxidative stress and increase mitochondrial function. However, whether NR can ameliorate IR in skeletal muscle is still inconclusive. We fed male C57BL/6J mice with an HFD (60% fat) ± 400 mg/kg·bw NR for 24 weeks. C2C12 myotube cells were treated with 0.25 mM palmitic acid (PA) ± 0.5 mM NR for 24 h. Indicators for IR and mitochondrial dysfunction were analyzed. NR treatment alleviated IR in HFD-fed mice with regard to improved glucose tolerance and a remarkable decrease in the levels of fasting blood glucose, fasting insulin and HOMA-IR index. NR-treated HFD-fed mice also showed improved metabolic status regarding a significant reduction in body weight and lipid contents in serum and the liver. NR activated AMPK in the skeletal muscle of HFD-fed mice and PA-treated C2C12 myotube cells and upregulated the expression of mitochondria-related transcriptional factors and coactivators, thereby improving mitochondrial function and alleviating oxidative stress. Upon inhibiting AMPK using Compound C, NR lost its ability in enhancing mitochondrial function and protection against IR induced by PA. In summary, improving mitochondrial function through the activation of AMPK pathway in skeletal muscle may play an important role in the amelioration of IR using NR.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Li, Qiuyan","Jiang, Xuye","Zhou, Yujia","Gu, Yingying","Ding, Yijie","Luo, Jing","Pang, Nengzhi","Sun, Yan","Pei, Lei","Pan, Jie","Gao, Mengqi","Ma, Sixi","Xiao, Ying","Hu, De","Wu, Feilong","Yang, Lili"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-683956"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sun Yat-Sen University"],"keyword":["Insulin Resistance","Mitochondrial dysfunction","NAD","Oxidative stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving mitochondrial function in skeletal muscle contributes to the amelioration of insulin resistance by nicotinamide riboside","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms241210015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-683956","identifier":[{"id":"85163962990","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001017145300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"37373163","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10297940","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4d559596-47c2-4306-8bee-29bec2f5eabf"],"keyword":["AMPK activation","NAD","insulin resistance","mitochondrial dysfunction","nicotinamide riboside (NR)","oxidative stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0F59A6AF652C80BBD02872C1287CFD0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/360692058/ijms_24_10015.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms241210015","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Kilpeläinen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Qiuyan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qiuyan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Xuye","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","locid":"ff0f81d4-8e53-4552-b950-b2d296e5ffbc","name":"Jiang, Xuye","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yujia","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Yujia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yingying","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Yingying","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yijie","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Yijie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jing","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Jing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nengzhi","key":"pangpau","last":"Pang","name":"Pang, Nengzhi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yan","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"peipau","last":"Pei","name":"Pei, Lei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jie","key":"panpau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Jie","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mengqi","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Mengqi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sixi","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Sixi","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ying","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Ying","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"De","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, De","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Feilong","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Feilong","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Lili","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37373163"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijms241210015","issn":["14220067","16616596"],"issn_org":["16616596"],"issue":"12","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","paperid":"10015","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163962990"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4d559596-47c2-4306-8bee-29bec2f5eabf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Improving Mitochondrial Function in Skeletal Muscle Contributes to the Amelioration of Insulin Resistance by Nicotinamide Riboside","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-683956","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: This study was performed in the frame of a more extensive study dedicated to the integrated analysis of the single-cell transcriptome and chromatin accessibility datasets of peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) with a large-scale GWAS of 45 complex traits in Chinese Holstein cattle. Lipopolysaccharide (LPS) is a crucial mediator of chronic inflammation to modulate immune responses. PBMCs include primary T and B cells, natural killer (NK) cells, monocytes (Mono), and dendritic cells (DC). How LPS stimulates PBMCs at the single-cell level in dairy cattle remains largely unknown. Data description: We sequenced 30,756 estimated single cells and mapped 26,141 of them (96.05%) with approximately 60,075 mapped reads per cell after quality control for four whole-blood treatments (no, 2 h, 4 h, and 8 h LPS) by single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) and single-cell sequencing assay for transposase-accessible chromatin (scATAC-seq). Finally, 7,107 (no), 9,174 (2 h), 6,741 (4 h), and 3,119 (8 h) cells were generated with ~ 15,000 total genes in the whole population. Therefore, the single-cell transcriptome and chromatin accessibility datasets in this study enable a further understanding of the cell types and functions of PBMCs and their responses to LPS stimulation in vitro.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Wang, Xiao","Gao, Yahui","Li, Cong jun","Fang, Lingzhao","Liu, George E.","Zhao, Xiuxin","Zhang, Yuanpei","Cai, Gaozhan","Xue, Guanghui","Liu, Yan","Wang, Lingling","Zhang, Fan","Wang, Kun","Zhang, Miao","Li, Rongling","Gao, Yundong","Li, Jianbin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-687352"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gao, Yundong","Li, Jianbin"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shandong Academy of Agricultural Sciences","US Dept Agriculture"],"keyword":["Chinese Holstein cattle","Chromatin","Lipopolysaccharide","Peripheral blood mononuclear cell","Transcriptome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the single cell transcriptome and chromatin accessibility datasets of peripheral blood mononuclear cells in chinese holstein cattle","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12863-023-01139-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-687352","identifier":[{"id":"85166784314","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37550629","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10408222","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-02110e8c-a2c4-49e4-baa0-0af5b1c3a608"],"keyword":["Chinese Holstein cattle","Chromatin","Lipopolysaccharide","Peripheral blood mononuclear cell","Single-cell accessibility dataset","Transcriptome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B75367CA20E8A107BD44F75D3AE7DCE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12863-023-01139-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"us dept agriculture","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"US Dept Agriculture","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Center for Quantitative Genetics and Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affn