9411a9-baf9-4c60-89ea-266562a5ae12"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Narcolepsy risk loci outline role of T cell autoimmunity and infectious triggers in narcolepsy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695464","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The cell membrane is characterized by a rich variety of topographical features such as local protrusions or invaginations. Curvature-sensing proteins, including the Bin/Amphiphysin/Rvs (BAR) or epsin N-terminal homology (ENTH) family proteins, sense the bending sharpness and the positive/negative sign of these topographical features to induce subsequent intracellular signaling. A number of assays have been developed to study curvature-sensing properties of proteins in vitro, but it is still challenging to probe low curvature regime with the diameter of curvature from hundreds of nanometers to micrometers. It is particularly difficult to generate negative membrane curvatures with well-defined curvature values in the low curvature regime. In this work, we develop a nanostructure-based curvature sensing (NanoCurvS) platform that enables quantitative and multiplex analysis of curvature-sensitive proteins in the low curvature regime, in both negative and positive directions. We use NanoCurvS to quantitatively measure the sensing range of a negative curvature-sensing protein IRSp53 (an I-BAR protein) and a positive curvature-sensing protein FBP17 (an F-BAR protein). We find that, in cell lysates, the I-BAR domain of IRSp53 is able to sense shallow negative curvatures with the diameter-of-curvature up to 1500 nm, a range much wider than previously expected. NanoCurvS is also used to probe the autoinhibition effect of IRSp53 and the phosphorylation effect of FBP17. Therefore, the NanoCurvS platform provides a robust, multiplex, and easy-to-use tool for quantitative analysis of both positive and negative curvature-sensing proteins.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lu, Chih Hao","Tsai, Ching Ting","Jones IV, Taylor","Chim, Vincent","Klausen, Lasse Hyldgaard","Zhang, Wei","Li, Xiao","Jahed, Zeinab","Cui, Bianxiao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-707462"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cui, Bianxiao","Jahed, Zeinab"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a nanocurvs platform for quantitative and multiplex analysis of curvature sensing proteins","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10809791/pdf/nihms-1957808.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-707462","identifier":[{"id":"85163998110","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10809791","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37337788","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-42ac2749-687e-46da-81a2-27c6a07369c8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0D8B01AD3AFBFE4886E29373C7CE1D35"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10809791/pdf/nihms-1957808.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chih Hao","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Chih Hao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ching Ting","key":"tsaipau","last":"Tsai","name":"Tsai, Ching Ting","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Taylor","key":"jonesivpau","last":"Jones IV","name":"Jones IV, Taylor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincent","key":"chimpau","last":"Chim","name":"Chim, Vincent","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lasse H.","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","locid":"37adddc1-94cb-4230-a0db-a51c19e2e97b","name":"Klausen, Lasse Hyldgaard","name_org":"Klausen, Lasse H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3004-5958","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Wei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zeinab","key":"jahedpau","last":"Jahed","name":"Jahed, Zeinab","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bianxiao","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Bianxiao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37337788"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d2bm01856j","issn":["20474830","20474849"],"issn_org":["20474830"],"issue":"15","journal":"Biomaterials Science","pages":"5205-5217","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Biomaterials Science","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-42ac2749-687e-46da-81a2-27c6a07369c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A NanoCurvS platform for quantitative and multiplex analysis of curvature-sensing proteins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-707462","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Conventional design and optimization methods for resonant coils in wireless power transfer systems (WPTSs) heavily rely on finite element simulations, which are very time-consuming and complex. In this paper, a novel Universal Coil Structure Design (UCSD) method is proposed to accelerate and optimize the design process of rounded rectangular coils in WPTSs. First, the analytical model of the resonant coil’s self-inductance is derived when no ferrite plate is added. Second, the image current method is adopted to calculate coil’s self-inductance when ferrite plates are added. Accurate numerical calculation methods are used for the derived analytical model to calculate the coil’s self-inductance quickly and precisely. Next, the working principle of the UCSD method is presented. The UCSD method can calculate the self-inductances of rectangular coils with the proposed analytical model and pinpoint the most possible range of optimal coil structure according to the given requirements from different WPTSs. Subsequently, the proposed UCSD method is applied to determine the optimal coil structures for two case studies with much less time consumption. Finally, a 1.5-kW WPT system prototype is built to verify the effectiveness of the proposed UCSD method. With the coupling coefficient k = 0.2, the maximum transfer efficiency reaches 95.57% and 94.91% for Case I and Case II while k = 0.15, the maximum transfer efficiency reaches 96.07% and 95.37% for Case I and Case II.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wu, Yue","Jiang, Yongbin","Li, Yaohua","He, Zhou","Wang, Chang","Xiao, Ziheng","Wang, Xiaohua","Tang, Yi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-711931"],"event":{"end":"2023-11-02","place":"Nashville, us","start":"2023-10-29","title":"2023 IEEE Energy Conversion Congress and Exposition (ECCE)","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"country":["China","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanyang Technological University","Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University"],"keyword":["Analytical models","Coils","Couplings","Design methodology","Ferrites","Inductance","Prototypes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a universal coil structure design method with accurate numerical computation in wireless power transfer systems","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85182927936","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-711931","identifier":[{"id":"85182927936","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b27d8784-6f54-4109-a169-c9ee25acd33f"],"keyword":["Analytical models","Coils","Couplings","Design methodology","Ferrites","Inductance","Prototypes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C09B18DDD0FAB20BCBC75CA1F5B732A7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"xi an jiaotong liverpool university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"nanyang technological university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Nanyang Technological University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Electronics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first"