{"abstract":"Plant-mediated CH4 emission is an important part of the ecosystem CH4 emission from vegetated wetlands. Inundation depth may alter the potential magnitude of CH4 releases by changing CH4 production and plant transport, but the relationships between plant-mediated CH4 emissions and inundation depth are still uncertain, especially for estuarine wetlands with changeable hydrological processes. Besides, there are conflicting results regarding the role of inundation depth in plant-mediated CH4 emissions. Here we conducted a novel inundation depth experiment (0, 5, 10, 20, 30 and 40 cm inundation depth) dominated by Phragmites australis in the Yellow River estuary, China. Soil CH4 emissions, ecosystem CH4 emissions, net ecosystem CO2 exchange (NEE), soil organic carbon (SOC) and plant traits were measured during the growing seasons of 2018, 2019 and 2020. Plant-mediated CH4 emissions were the difference between ecosystem CH4 emissions and soil CH4 emissions. The results showed that inundation depth decreased soil CH4 emissions but increased ecosystem CH4 emissions. Plant-mediated CH4 transport from Phragmites australis accounted for 99% of total ecosystem CH4 emissions under different inundation depths. Inundation depth strongly stimulated plant-mediated CH4 emission from 0 to 20 cm during the growing seasons. The increased NEE enhanced plant-mediated CH4 emissions by altering production, suggesting that carbon components derived from photosynthetic carbon input may benefit CH4 production. Additionally, the increased plant height promoted CH4 emission by regulating plant transport, indicating that plant traits may play an important role in transport of CH4. Our findings indicated that NEE and plant height play an important role in plant-mediated CH4 emissions under different inundation depths in estuarine wetland. This study also highlights that hydrological regimes and plant traits are essential for the estimation of CH4 emissions in future projections of global wetland changes. Read the free Plain Language Summary for this article on the Journal blog.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Zhao, Mingliang","Li, Peiguang","Song, Weimin","Chu, Xiaojing","Eller, Franziska","Wang, Xiaojie","Liu, Jingtao","Xiao, Leilei","Wei, Siyu","Li, Xinge","Han, Guangxuan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-184073"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Han, Guangxuan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Binzhou University","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Estuarine wetland","plant height"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inundation depth stimulates plant mediated ch sub 000000000004 sub emissions by increasing ecosystem carbon uptake and plant height in an estuarine wetland","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85147428019","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-184073","identifier":[{"id":"85147428019","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5fe653c0-f368-4480-8738-0b4732354452"],"keyword":["estuarine wetland","inundation depth","net ecosystem CO exchange","plant height","plant-mediated CH emissions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A585E6AC4EDBB975C28AE32E84F392D7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"binzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Binzhou University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingliang","key":"zhaomingliangpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Mingliang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peiguang","key":"lipeiguangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Peiguang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Weimin","key":"songweiminpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Weimin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaojing","key":"chuxiaojingpau","last":"Chu","name":"Chu, Xiaojing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaojie","key":"wangxiaojiepau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaojie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingtao","key":"liujingtaopau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jingtao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leilei","key":"xiaoleileipau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Leilei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyu","key":"weisiyupau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Siyu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinge","key":"lixingepau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xinge","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guangxuan","key":"hanguangxuanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Guangxuan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1365-2435.14258","issn":["02698463","13652435"],"issn_org":["02698463"],"issue":"3","journal":"Functional Ecology","pages":"536-550","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Functional Ecology","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147428019"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5fe653c0-f368-4480-8738-0b4732354452"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Inundation depth stimulates plant-mediated CH<sub>4</sub> emissions by increasing ecosystem carbon uptake and plant height in an estuarine wetland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-184073","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In response to the COVID-19 pandemic, the Psychological Science Accelerator coordinated three large-scale psychological studies to examine the effects of loss-gain framing, cognitive reappraisals, and autonomy framing manipulations on behavioral intentions and affective measures. The data collected (April to October 2020) included specific measures for each experimental study, a general questionnaire examining health prevention behaviors and COVID-19 experience, geographical and cultural context characterization, and demographic information for each participant. Each participant started the study with the same general questions and then was randomized to complete either one longer experiment or two shorter experiments. Data were provided by 73,223 participants with varying completion rates. Participants completed the survey from 111 geopolitical regions in 44 unique languages/dialects. The anonymized dataset described here is provided in both raw and processed formats to facilitate re-use and further analyses. The dataset offers secondary analytic opportunities to explore coping, framing, and self-determination across a diverse, global sample obtained at the onset of the COVID-19 pandemic, which can be merged with other time-sampled or geographic data.","author_count":340,"contributors":["Buchanan, Erin M.","Lewis, Savannah C.","Paris, Bastien","Forscher, Patrick S.","Pavlacic, Jeffrey M.","Beshears, Julie E.","Drexler, Shira Meir","Gourdon-Kanhukamwe, Amélie","Mallik, Peter R.","Silan, Miguel Alejandro A.","Miller, Jeremy K.","IJzerman, Hans","Moshontz, Hannah","Beaudry, Jennifer L.","Suchow, Jordan W.","Chartier, Christopher R.","Coles, Nicholas A.","Sharifian, Mohammad Hasan","Todsen, Anna Louise","Levitan, Carmel A.","Azevedo, Flávio","Legate, Nicole","Heller, Blake","Rothman, Alexander J.","Dorison, Charles A.","Gill, Brian P.","Wang, Ke","Rees, Vaughan W.","Gibbs, Nancy","Goldenberg, Amit","Thi Nguyen, Thuy vy","Gross, James J.","Kaminski, Gwenaêl","von Bastian, Claudia C.","Paruzel-Czachura, Mariola","Mosannenzadeh, Farnaz","Azouaghe, Soufian","Bran, Alexandre","Ruiz-Fernandez, Susana","Santos, Anabela Caetano","Reggev, Niv","Zickfeld, Janis H.","Akkas, Handan","Pantazi, Myrto","Ropovik, Ivan","Korbmacher, Max","Arriaga, Patrícia","Gjoneska, Biljana","Warmelink, Lara","Alves, Sara G.","de Holanda Coelho, Gabriel Lins","Stieger, Stefan","Schei, Vidar","Hanel, Paul H.P.","Szaszi, Barnabas","Fedotov, Maksim","Antfolk, Jan","Marcu, Gabriela Mariana","Schrötter, Jana","Kunst, Jonas R.","Geiger, Sandra J.","Adetula, Adeyemi","Kocalar, Halil Emre","Kielińska, Julita","Kačmár, Pavol","Bokkour, Ahmed","Galindo-Caballero, Oscar J.","Djamai, Ikhlas","Pöntinen, Sara Johanna","Agesin, Bamikole Emmanuel","Jernsäther, Teodor","Urooj, Anum","Rachev, Nikolay R.","Koptjevskaja-Tamm, Maria","Kurfalı, Murathan","Pit, Ilse L.","Li, Ranran","Çoksan, Sami","Dubrov, Dmitrii","Paltrow, Tamar Elise","Baník, Gabriel","Korobova, Tatiana","Studzinska, Anna","Jiang, Xiaoming","Aruta, John Jamir Benzon R.","Vintr, Jáchym","Chiu, Faith","Kaliska, Lada","Berkessel, Jana B.","Tümer, Murat","Morales-Izquierdo, Sara","Chuan-Peng, Hu","Vezirian, Kevin","Rosa, Anna Dalla","Bialobrzeska, Olga","Vasilev, Martin R.","Beitner, Julia","Kácha, Ondřej","Žuro, Barbara","Westerlund, Minja","Nedelcheva-Datsova, Mina","Findor, Andrej","Krupić, Dajana","Kowal, Marta","Askelund, Adrian Dahl","Pourafshari, Razieh","Đorđević, Jasna Milošević","Schmidt, Nadya Daniela","Baklanova, Ekaterina","Szala, Anna","Zakharov, Ilya","Vranka, Marek A.","Ihaya, Keiko","Grano, Caterina","Cellini, Nicola","Białek, Michał","Anton-Boicuk, Lisa","Dalgar, Ilker","Adıgüzel, Arca","Verharen, Jeroen P.H.","Maturan, Princess Lovella G.","Kassianos, Angelos P.","Oliveira, Raquel","Čadek, Martin","Adoric, Vera Cubela","Özdoğru, Asil Ali","Sverdrup, Therese E.","Aczel, Balazs","Zambrano, Danilo","Ahmed, Afroja","Tamnes, Christian K.","Yamada, Yuki","Volz, Leonhard","Sunami, Naoyuki","Su