{"abstract":"Over the past 2 to 3 decades, Chinese forests are estimated to act as a large carbon sink, yet the magnitude and spatial patterns of this sink differ considerably among studies. Using 3 microwave (L- and X-band vegetation optical depth [VOD]) and 3 optical (normalized difference vegetation index, leaf area index, and tree cover) remote-sensing vegetation products, this study compared the estimated live woody aboveground biomass carbon (AGC) dynamics over China between 2013 and 2019. Our results showed that tree cover has the highest spatial consistency with 3 published AGC maps (mean correlation value R = 0.84), followed by L-VOD (R = 0.83), which outperform the other VODs. An AGC estimation model was proposed to combine all indices to estimate the annual AGC dynamics in China during 2013 to 2019. The performance of the AGC estimation model was good (root mean square error = 0.05 Pg C and R2 = 0.90 with a mean relative uncertainty of 9.8% at pixel scale [0.25°]). Results of the AGC estimation model showed that carbon uptake by the forests in China was about +0.17 Pg C year−1 from 2013 to 2019. At the regional level, provinces in southwest China including Guizhou (+22.35 Tg C year−1), Sichuan (+14.49 Tg C year−1), and Hunan (+11.42 Tg C year−1) provinces had the highest carbon sink rates during 2013 to 2019. Most of the carbon-sink regions have been afforested recently, implying that afforestation and ecological engineering projects have been effective means for carbon sequestration in these regions.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Chang, Zhongbing","Fan, Lei","Wigneron, Jean-Pierre","Wang, Ying-Ping","Ciais, Philippe","Chave, Jérôme","Fensholt, Rasmus","Chen, Jing M.","Yuan, Wenping","Ju, Weimin","Li, Xin","Jiang, Fei","Wu, Mousong","Chen, Xiuzhi","Qin, Yuanwei","Frappart, Frédéric","Li, Xiaojun","Wang, Mengjia","Liu, Xiangzhuo","Tang, Xuli","Hobeichi, Sanaa","Yu, Mengxiao","Ma, Mingguo","Wen, Jianguang","Xiao, Qing","Shi, Weiyu","Liu, Dexin","Yan, Junhua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739729"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","China","France","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Normal University","CSIRO","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Fujian Normal University","Henan University","Nanjing Normal University","Nanjing University","Paris-Saclay University","Southern Marine Science and Engineering Guangdong Laboratory - Guanzhou","Southwest University","Sun Yat-Sen University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of New South Wales","University of Oklahoma","University of Toronto","Université Paul Sabatier Toulouse III","Université de Bordeaux"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimating aboveground carbon dynamic of china using optical and microwave remote sensing datasets from 000000002013 to 000000002019","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34133/remotesensing.0005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739729","identifier":[{"id":"85152145188","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ba7bcb48-aabd-4bda-93bd-4d2fb6828d6b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F86D3C2AD5441C5141D2E9DD63CE2A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.34133/remotesensing.0005","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/390999369/remotesensing.0005.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of scien