abjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6 7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Weihao","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","locid":"6a8d73a0-43d8-4b65-a4d0-4f62e2cc4315","name":"Hu, Weihao","orcid":"0000-0003-3816-7263","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fmre.2023.05.004","issn":["26673258"],"issn_org":["20969457"],"journal":"Fundamental Research","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"i","title":"Fundamental Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163118700"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["In Press"]},"sid":["aau-af438dc4-3726-4680-a2ec-b666605a7e5a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"AI-aided power electronic converters automatic online real-time efficiency optimization method","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786221","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The temporal partitioning hypothesis refers to the promotion of stable species’ coexistence by reducing the likelihood of competitive exclusion, such as when species are active at different months of the year. However, the studies confirming the mechanisms of species’ coexistence focus on spatial scale, and temporal partitioning hypothesis for species’ coexistence remains underexplored. Fungal sporophores that are sensitive to seasonality change are ideal candidates for studying the role of temporal differentiation hypothesis in species’ coexistence. In this study, a field survey of fungal sporocarps was conducted from May to October, and the entity and abundance of different species of fungal sporocarps in a 5‐hectare forest dynamic plot in a temperate, deciduous broad‐leaved forest were recorded. The results showed that the emergence of fungal sporocarps based on month was highly specialized and uneven. The torus‐translation test showed that 56 species exhibited ecological habitat preferences for different months (47/100, 47%). The distribution of soil fungal sporocarps (35/75, 46.67%) based on months showed higher specialization compared with that of rotten‐wood fungal sporocarps (9/22, 40.90%). The findings suggest the importance of temporal partitioning in maintaining local diversity in the fungal community.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zhou, Ziyu","Man, Xiao","Wang, Senlin","Wang, Xueying","Li, Wang","Chen, Yun","Yuan, Zhiliang","Guo, Erhui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-144452"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Erhui"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Henan Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Species diversity","forest dynamics plot"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal partitioning of fungal sporophores in a temperate deciduous broad leaved forest","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/d14060483","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-144452","identifier":[{"id":"85132576550","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1a5d3381-2c48-419b-a19e-9ad56c095c0e"],"keyword":["forest dynamics plot","fungal sporocarps","month","species’ diversity","temporal partitioning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-694BB187CD7F24F98F6CC3F21F458B9E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/d14060483","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"henan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Henan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Ecoinformatics and Biodiversity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ziyu","key":"zhouziyupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Ziyu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"manxiaopau","last":"Man","name":"Man, Xiao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Senlin","key":"wangsenlinpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Senlin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xueying","key":"wangxueyingpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xueying","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wang","key":"liwangpau","last":"Li","locid":"b7453bd7-2b7e-4e87-8f44-f9bca94a7525","name":"Li, Wang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yun","key":"chenyunpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhiliang","key":"yuanzhiliangpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Zhiliang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erhui","key":"guoerhuipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Erhui","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/d14060483","issn":["14242818"],"issue":"6","journal":"Diversity","paperid":"483","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Diversity","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132576550"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1a5d3381-2c48-419b-a19e-9ad56c095c0e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Temporal Partitioning of Fungal Sporophores in a Temperate Deciduous Broad-Leaved Forest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-144452","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Link here: https://wiki.digitalmethods.net/Dmi/SummerSchool2022chugginguhg This project investigates two competing 4chan groups concerned with the war in Ukraine. We follow the pro-Ukrainian (/uhg/) and the pro-Russian (/chug/) threads and their fandomized war reporting. A journalistic register dominates the /uhg/ sets, and a strategic-logistic register dominates the /chug/ sets. The two threads fandomize the Ukrainian war through anthropomorphising and fictionalising nations and militaries in the form of memes. Surprisingly, there is a lack in the differential political positioning of the threads. Their sensemaking is antisemitic in nature. The differences are more stylistic than substantial. /chug/ is more conscious about the community’s identity, reflected in the abundance of logos, while /uhg/ images are more evidentiary, indicating a greater emphasis on reportage and points at original journalistic endeavours. There is a relative (in)visibility of memes to the mainstream web. The vernacularity of hyper-specific online discourse emerges through absence, especially so in /chug/, which represents a vernacular within a vernacular. The organizational practices and structures differ heavily between the pro-Ukrainian /uhg/ and the pro-Russian /chug/ threads. The analysis methods reinforce the interest difference between the /uhg/ and /chug/ threads. /uhg/ is more scrappy, having no discernable strategy in their aesthetic or storytelling. /uhg/ is reactionary, whilst /chug/ drives the story. Text analysis of OP greentext showcased the lack of organisation in /ugh/ which is a more noisy and less coherent discussion forum. /uhg/ focus more on direct war reportage and external rivalry against /chug/ /chug/ is more organized than /uhg/. /chug/ community appear to have their story straight, offering a well-rounded arsenal of strategies to convince /pol/ of their authenticity and truthfulness. Text analysis of OP greentext showcased the organizational capacities of /chug/. As a schismatic outcrop of pro-Russian segments of early /uhg/ threads, /chug/ quickly became more systematized. For example, in baking strategies and cultivation of shared intercultural iconography. /chug/ focus more internally oriented around inter-group reinforcement and performativity. From distinct visual methodologies, we can infer that: /uhg/ OP images present a more extensive set of evidentiary war images that might be instances of original journalism /chug/ focuses more on establishing its identity through logo branding. The cultural sophistication of /chug/ in relation to /uhg/ in the sense that the notable amount of non-web entities on /chug/ suggest a deeper, more differentiated visual vernacular distinct from specific labels known by the Google Vision API. The predominance of sexualization of warfare, portraying it in terms of the trope of female sexual dominance and subjugation, or war as threatening the innocence of the female subject, who in turn need saving from it. Methodological findings: The shared image analysis presented a novel method for uncovering internal and inter-group rivalry and shilling, contingent community formation, grassroots reportage and a way to contextualize anomalies in the dataset. Analysis of country flag metadata reveals the influence of a national and regional context in terms of user activity, thread partiality, and discursive input, opening up an as-of yet under-researched area of 4chan.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Baun, Phillip Stenmann","Schlüter, Maximilian","Bach, Daniel","Tuters, Marc","Li, Yuening","Keye, Wade","Zhou, Xin","Rajhans, Anunaya","Li, Yuru","Xiao, Fan","Ward, Sean","Westling, Carina","Pilati, Federico","Aversa, Elena","Omena, Janna Joceli","Watson, Grace","Valli, Marco","Gobbo, Beatrice","Trans, Martin Broholt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-154988"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["4chan","Disinformation","Memes","War"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"let s play war inside 000000000004chan s intergroup rivalry contingent community formation and fandomized war reporting","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://wiki.digitalmethods.net/Dmi/SummerSchool2022chugginguhg","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-154988","ids":["au-2cd9ef26-f4b3-4381-a338-e9018144f711"],"keyword":["4chan","disinformation","memes","war"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D7F5751AAA3F6B0AAAEC8A049C348187"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Global Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Phillip Stenmann","key":"baunphillipstenmannpau","last":"Baun","locid":"aaeedafe-bb67-4286-bae2-28aa9d3f9a8f","name":"Baun, Phillip Stenmann","orcid":"0000-0002-2433-8212","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maximilian","key":"schlütermaximilianpau","last":"Schlüter","locid":"b2fdc675-ca58-4c61-b166-ce2226fea79d","name":"Schlüter, Maximilian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"bachdanielpau","last":"Bach","name":"Bach, Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"tutersmarcpau","last":"Tuters","name":"Tuters, Marc","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuening","key":"liyueningpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yuening","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wade","key":"keyewadepau","last":"Keye","name":"Keye, Wade","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xin","key":"zhouxinpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Xin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anunaya","key":"rajhansanunayapau","last":"Rajhans","name":"Rajhans, Anunaya","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuru","key":"liyurupau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yuru","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fan","key":"xiaofanpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Fan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sean","key":"wardseanpau","last":"Ward","name":"Ward, Sean","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina","key":"westlingcarinapau","last":"Westling","name":"Westling, Carina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Federico","key":"pilatifedericopau","last":"Pilati","name":"Pilati, Federico","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"aversaelenapau","last":"Aversa","name":"Aversa, Elena","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Janna Joceli","key":"omenajannajocelipau","last":"Omena","name":"Omena, Janna Joceli","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Grace","key":"watsongracepau","last":"Watson","name":"Watson, Grace","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"vallimarcopau","last":"Valli","name":"Valli, Marco","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Beatrice","key":"gobbobeatricepau","last":"Gobbo","name":"Gobbo, Beatrice","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Broholt","key":"transmartinbroholtpau","last":"Trans","locid":"4912e505-4c93-4bc8-bf7b-5bb530ecd7c2","name":"Trans, Martin Broholt","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2cd9ef26-f4b3-4381-a338-e9018144f711"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Let's Play War : Inside 4chan’s intergroup rivalry, contingent community formation, and fandomized war reporting","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-154988","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Molybdenum dioxide (MoO2) with high theoretical capacity and low cost has triggered extensive interest as a renowned anode for lithium ion batteries (LIBs). However, the sluggish diffusion kinetics and severe capacity decay obstructed its practical application. Herein, hierarchical spherical Mo2C-MXene@MoO2@C was fabricated through a self-assembly and carbonization strategy. DFT calculations and experimental results revealed that the incorporation of metallic Mo2C-MXene and carbon into MoO2 not only modulated the charge distribution and weakened Mo-O bond of MoO2, but also promoted the adsorption of Li+ on MoO2 and lowered the migration energy barrier for Li+, thereby accelerating the electrochemical kinetics, inducing a strong diffusion-controlled charge storage behavior and improving the electrochemical reversibility. In addition, the introduction of MXene reinforced the structural integrity of MoO2 during ion insertion and extraction, which ameliorated the electrochemical stability. Beneficiating from the above synergistic effect, the optimized Mo2C-MXene@MoO2@C delivered remarkable cycling capacity (854.5 mAh g−1 after 500 cycles at 0.5 A g−1) and superior rate capacity (644.4 mAh g−1 at 1 A g−1) for lithium storage. This work disclosed the charge storage mechanism of MoO2 and provided new guidance for the rational design of novel electrode materials for secondary batteries.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Liu, Guilong","Xiao, Fangyuan","Zhang, Ting","Gu, Yingying","Li, Jin","Guo, Donglei","Xu, Maowen","Wu, Naiteng","Cao, Ang","Liu, Xianming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-361721"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Xianming","Wu, Naiteng","Xu, Maowen"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luoyang Normal University","Southwest University"],"keyword":["Lithium ion battery"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in situ growth of moo000000000002 n doped carbon on mo000000000002c mxene for superior lithium storage","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85130826494","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-361721","identifier":[{"id":"000807242200004","type":"wos"},{"id":"85130826494","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-bf439826-0d89-43fa-8c57-97928defc6b8"],"keyword":["Lithium ion battery","Mo2CTx MXene","MoO2 anode","Pseudo-capacitance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DB8D288790A0576F2B57DC00A91F768B"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"luoyang normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Luoyang Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Catalysis Theory Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guilong","key":"liuguilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guilong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fangyuan","key":"xiaofangyuanpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Fangyuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ting","key":"zhangtingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ting","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yingying","key":"guyingyingpau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Yingying","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin","key":"lijinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Donglei","key":"guodongleipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Donglei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maowen","key":"xumaowenpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Maowen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Naiteng","key":"wunaitengpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Naiteng","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ang","key":"caoangpau","last":"Cao","locid":"bcb0a893-26f0-4e9c-84d6-ec895a5d3a7b","name":"Cao, Ang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianming","key":"liuxianmingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xianming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apsusc.2022.153688","issn":["01694332","18735584"],"issn_org":["01694332"],"journal":"Applied Surface Science","paperid":"153688","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Surface Science","volume":"597"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130826494"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bf439826-0d89-43fa-8c57-97928defc6b8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"In-situ growth of MoO2@N doped carbon on Mo2C-MXene for superior lithium storage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-361721","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In order to understand and minimize microbial contaminants spread from animal to raw pork products, we explored the diversity of antibiotic resistance genes (ARGs), virulence factors (VFs), mobile genetic elements (MGEs) and the bacterial community composition in feces of pigs, processing areas as well as the end pork products in a large-scale pig slaughterhouse in China using metagenomics. The abundance and diversity of microbial community was higher in arrival and slaughtering room area and decreased sharply in the end pork products. Furthermore, the relative abundance of some clinically relevant pathogens and opportunity pathogens were greater in the end pork products and cutter samples. We identified 1412 subtypes of ARGs related to 30 antibiotic classes, in which ARGs related to multidrug resistance and β-lactamase were dominant. Resistance determinants to clinically critical important antibiotics, including sequences related to mcr, optrA, poxtA, tetX and β-lactamase genes (i.e. blaOXA, blaVIM, blaIMP, blaGES, blaNDM, blaKPC and blaSME) were detected. More than 42 general virulence features, mainly adherence, secretion system, iron uptake, toxin, antiphagocytosis and immune evasion, were identified. A total of 1922 types of MGEs, mainly plasmids were observed. Most of the ARGs are predicted to be associated with MGEs. The prevalence of ARGs, VFs and MGEs decreased over subsequential processing steps. Most of the remaining ARGs, VFs and MGEs in end pork products were also present on other samples, indicating the flow of these genes through the production line. These results broaden our understanding of the global ARGs, VFs and MGEs diversity along the pork production chain, with the suggestion of implementing improved control measures to reduce the risk of spread of pathogenic bacteria and their associated resistome, virulome and mobilome from animal to the food chain and the surrounding environment.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Lili","Xiao, Yawen","Wang, Chong","Olsen, Rikke Heidemann","Meng, Hecheng","Shi, Lei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504855"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jinan University","Shandong New Hope Liuhe Group","South China University of Technology"],"keyword":["Metagenomic","Microbiome","Pork production","Resistome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the resistome virulome mobilome and microbiome along pork production chain using metagenomics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-504855","identifier":[{"id":"85127810847","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35413521","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-baa10a71-85b5-4527-9427-b3a40744a044"],"keyword":["Metagenomic","Microbiome","Pork production","Resistome","Virulome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-72141CCAFF0C7752A844495CB4CD5492"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jinan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jinan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shandong new hope liuhe group","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong New Hope Liuhe Group","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Lili","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yawen","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Yawen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Chong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rikke Heidemann","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8bc39fd7-fa38-4eb8-8c84-01b4682efd79","name":"Olsen, Rikke Heidemann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Hecheng","key":"mengpau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Hecheng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Lei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35413521"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijfoodmicro.2022.109674","issn":["01681605","18793460"],"issn_org":["01681605"],"journal":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","paperid":"109674","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Food Microbiology","volume":"371"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127810847"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-baa10a71-85b5-4527-9427-b3a40744a044"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring the resistome, virulome, mobilome and microbiome along pork production chain using metagenomics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-504855","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A search with minimal model dependence for physics beyond the Standard Model in events featuring three or four charged leptons (3ℓ and 4ℓ, ℓ=e,μ) is presented. The analysis aims to be sensitive to a wide range of potential new-physics theories simultaneously. This analysis uses data from pp collisions delivered by the Large Hadron Collider at a centre-of-mass energy of s=13 TeV and recorded with the ATLAS detector, corresponding to the full Run 2 dataset of 139 fb−1. The 3ℓ and 4ℓ phase space is divided into 22 event categories according to the number of leptons in the event, the missing transverse momentum, the invariant mass of the leptons, and the presence of leptons originating from a Z-boson candidate. These event categories are analysed independently for the presence of deviations from the Standard Model. No statistically significant deviations from the Standard Model predictions are observed. Upper limits for all signal regions are reported in terms of the visible cross-section.","author_count":2825,"contributors":["Aad, G.","Abbott, B.","Abbott, D. C.","Abed Abud, A.","Abeling, K.","Abhayasinghe, D. K.","Abidi, S. H.","AbouZeid, Ossama Sherif Alexander","Abramowicz, H.","Abreu, H.","Abulaiti, Y.","Abusleme Hoffman, A. C.","Acharya, B. S.","Achkar, B.","Adam, L.","Adam Bourdarios, C.","Adamczyk, L.","Adamek, L.","Adelman, J.","Adiguzel, A.","Adorni, S.","Adye, T.","Affolder, A. A.","Afik, Y.","Agapopoulou, C.","Agaras, M. N.","Agarwala, J.","Aggarwal, A.","Agheorghiesei, C.","Aguilar-Saavedra, J. A.","Ahmad, A.","Ahmadov, F.","Ahmed, W. S.","Ai, X.","Aielli, G.","Akatsuka, S.","Akbiyik, M.","Åkesson, T. P.A.","Akimov, A. V.","Al Khoury, K.","Alberghi, G. L.","Albert, J.","Alconada Verzini, M. J.","Alderweireldt, S.","Aleksa, M.","Aleksandrov, I. N.","Alexa, C.","Alexopoulos, T.","Alfonsi, A.","Alfonsi, F.","Alhroob, M.","Ali, B.","Ali, S.","Aliev, M.","Alimonti, G.","Allaire, C.","Allbrooke, B. M.M.","Allport, P. P.","Aloisio, A.","Alonso, F.","A