{"abstract":"In this paper, a shared-radiator dual-polarized wideband antenna for 5G applications is proposed. It consists of a shared-radiator and a ground plane together with two orthogonal feeding plates. The feeding structure is formed by a microstrip power divider and a coupling slot opened on the ground to perform as a balun. The operating frequency range of the proposed antenna is 3.2 GHz to 3.7 GHz. Simulation results show that the antenna reaches reflection coefficient < -10 dB in the operating frequency band with and port isolation better than 30 dB. The antenna not only possesses good electromagnetic properties in terms of high gain, wide bandwidth, but also has simple physical structure for potential production, which makes the antenna proposed in this paper to be suitable for 5G applications.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Chen, Min","Zhang, Zhong-Qi","Li, Xiao-Dong","Liu, Hao-Lei","Huang, Guan-Long","Fan, Wei","Sim, Chow-Yen-Desmond"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-673319"],"event":{"end":"2022-12-18","place":"Haidian, China","start":"2022-12-17","title":"2022 Cross Strait Radio Science &amp; Wireless Technology Conference (CSRSWTC)","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China","Taiwan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Feng Chia University","Foshan University"],"keyword":["5G mobile communication","Adaptive arrays","Reflection coefficient","Reflector antennas","Scattering parameters","Simulation","Wireless communication"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a shared radiator dual polarized wideband antenna for 000000000005g application","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10098350/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-673319","identifier":[{"id":"85156100887","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-099668c5-693f-44fa-a78a-e4441bd22ba8"],"keyword":["5G mobile communication","Adaptive arrays","Reflection coefficient","Reflector antennas","Scattering parameters","Simulation","Wireless communication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BC002CD1E199B63146439851C6856603"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"foshan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Foshan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, Propagation and Millimetre-Wave Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Wireless propagation and Over the Air testing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"tw","key":"feng chia university","loc":["Taiwan","Asia, East"],"name":"Feng Chia University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Min","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhong-Qi","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhong-Qi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Dong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao-Dong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao-Lei","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Hao-Lei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guan-Long","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Guan-Long","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","locid":"196e035b-e3db-4c94-b288-03dcd3119fda","name":"Fan, Wei","orcid":"0000-0002-9835-4485","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chow-Yen-Desmond","key":"simpau","last":"Sim","name":"Sim, Chow-Yen-Desmond","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/csrswtc56224.2022.10098350","isbn":["9781665460972"],"issn":["23778512"],"pages":"1-2","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Cross Strait Quad-Regional Radio Science and Wireless Technology Conference","status":"p","title":"2022 Cross Strait Radio Science &amp; Wireless Technology Conference (CSRSWTC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85156100887"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-099668c5-693f-44fa-a78a-e4441bd22ba8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Shared-Radiator Dual-Polarized Wideband Antenna for 5G Application","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673319","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Addressing global environmental challenges requires access to biodiversity data across wide spatial, temporal and taxonomic scales. Availability of such data has increased exponentially recently with the proliferation of biodiversity databases. However, heterogeneous coverage, protocols, and standards have hampered integration among these databases. To stimulate the next stage of data integration, here we present a synthesis of major databases, and investigate (a) how the coverage of databases varies across taxonomy, space, and record type; (b) what degree of integration is present among databases; (c) how integration of databases can increase biodiversity knowledge; and (d) the barriers to database integration. Location: Global. Time period: Contemporary. Major taxa studied: Plants and vertebrates. Methods: We reviewed 12 established biodiversity databases that mainly focus on geographic distributions and functional traits at global scale. We synthesized information from these databases to assess the status of their integration and major knowledge gaps and barriers to full integration. We estimated how improved integration can increase the data coverage for terrestrial plants and vertebrates. Results: Every database reviewed had a unique focus of data coverage. Exchanges of biodiversity information were common among databases, although not always clearly documented. Functional trait databases were more isolated than those pertaining to species distributions. Variation and potential incompatibility of taxonomic systems used by different databases posed a major barrier to data integration. We found that integration of distribution databases could lead to increased taxonomic coverage that corresponds to 23 years’ advancement in data accumulation, and improvement in taxonomic coverage could be as high as 22.4% for trait databases. Main conclusions: Rapid increases in biodiversity knowledge can be achieved through the integration of databases, providing the data necessary to address critical environmental challenges. Full integration across databases will require tackling the major impediments to data integration: taxonomic incompatibility, lags in data exchange, barriers to effective data synchronization, and isolation of individual initiatives.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Feng, Xiao","Enquist, Brian J.","Park, Daniel S.","Boyle, Brad","Breshears, David D.","Gallagher, Rachael V.","Lien, Aaron","Newman, Erica A.","Burger, Joseph R.","Maitner, Brian S.","Merow, Cory","Li, Yaoqi","Huynh, Kimberly M.","Ernst, Kacey","Baldwin, Elizabeth","Foden, Wendy","Hannah, Lee","Jørgensen, Peter M.","Kraft, Nathan J.B.","Lovett, Jon C.","Marquet, Pablo A.","McGill, Brian J.","Morueta-Holme, Naia","Neves, Danilo M.","Núñez-Regueiro, Mauricio M.","Oliveira-Filho, Ary T.","Peet, Robert K.","Pillet, Michiel","Roehrdanz, Patrick R.","Sandel, Brody","Serra-Diaz, Josep M.","Šímová, Irena","Svenning, Jens Christian","Violle, Cyrille","Weitemier, Trang D.","Wiser, Susan","López-Hoffman, Laura"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-017619"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Feng, Xiao"],"country":["Argentina","Australia","Brazil","Chile","China","Czechia","France","New Zealand","South Africa","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charles University","Consejo Nacional de Investigaciones Científicas y Técnicas","Conservation International","Conservation International (USA)","Czech Academy of Sciences","Florida State University","International Union for Conservation of Nature","International Union for Conservation of Nature and Natural Resources","Landcare Research","Manaaki Whenua - Landcare Research","Missouri Botanical Garden","Montpellier University","Pontificia Universidad Catolica de Chile","Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile","Purdue University","Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew","Santa Clara University","Santa Fe Institute","South African National Parks","Southern Connecticut State University","Universidad Austral de Chile","Universidad de Chile","Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais","Universite de Lorraine","Universite de Montpellier","University of Arizona","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Connecticut","University of Kentucky","University of Leeds","University of Lorraine","University of Maine","University of North Carolina","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Stellenbosch","Western Sydney University","Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University"],"keyword":["Big data","Biodiversity informatics","Biogeography","Functional trait","database integration","taxonomic system"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a review of the heterogeneous landscape of biodiversity databases opportunities and challenges for a synthesized biodiversity knowledge base","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/geb.13497","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-017619","identifier":[{"id":"85128256664","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000783348000001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-442fa546-11b2-46ce-bec6-cabd943b34ce","ku-470d14c8-1fd2-4971-b169-ae009add63a3"],"keyword":["big data","biodiversity informatics","biogeography","database integration","functional trait","taxonomic system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-095FF00001B5686935F62A157F53521A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi