{"affno":"2","first":"Wei","key":"zhangweipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Wei","rank":31,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xiao","key":"liuxiaopau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xiao","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yang","key":"zongyangpau","last":"Zong","name":"Zong, Yang","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Weibin","key":"liuweibinpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Weibin","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Liang","key":"xiaoliangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Liang","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yong","key":"houyongpau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Yong","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xun","key":"xuxunpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xun","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Huanming","key":"yanghuanmingpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Huanming","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Jian","key":"wangjianpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jian","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenkarstenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"941041b1-1b8f-4be5-9a65-5e98f662c07e","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","orcid":"0000-0002-6024-0917","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Huijue","key":"jiahuijuepau","last":"Jia","name":"Jia, Huijue","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34118463"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.gpb.2021.01.005","issn":["16720229"],"issue":"2","journal":"Genomics, Proteomics and Bioinformatics","pages":"304-321","status":"p","title":"Genomics, Proteomics and Bioinformatics","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112448779"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5638c923-6727-40f9-9cd9-4b8ef6128101"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Life History Recorded in the Vagino-cervical Microbiome Along with Multi-omes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-444957","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Efficient CO2/C2H2 separation at ambient conditions is an essential but challenging process owing to their similar molecular sizes and physical properties. In this work, a novel approach of charge/strain-regulated gas capture and separation was proposed, which offered the advantages of reversibility and controllable kinetics. Highly selective CO2 separation from CO2/C2H2 with porous g-C9N7 nanosheets were demonstrated with varying charge densities and strains using molecular dynamics (MD) simulations and first-principle density function theory (DFT) calculations. The remarkable CO2 permeance up to 5.85 x 10(7) GPU can be achieved by charge engineering. Under the condition of tensile strain, a controllable CO2 separation performance was exhibited, whose CO2 permeance increased with increasing the applied strain. The maximum permeance was 3.44 x 10(7) GPU with 9% strained g-C9N7 membrane. More interestingly, a promising approach combining the charge regulation with strain engineering was explored to investigate the synergistic effect. Under conditions of 2 e(-) charge and 3% tensile strain on g-C9N7 membrane, the CO2 permeance reached 4.24 x 107 GPU, which was 1.6 times of CO2 permeability when only 2 e(-) was added and 10 times of CO2 permeance when only 3% strain was added. Additionally, the energy barrier of CO2 decreased with the increasing degree of regulation (charge and strain engineering) on the g-C9N7 membrane, indicating that the g-C9N7 membrane can be served as an excellent candidate for CO2/C2H2 separation. These results provide useful guidance for developing advanced materials and applying new regulation techniques to realize highly tunable and selective CO2/C2H2 separation.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Li, Xue","He, Wenhao","Liu, Zilong","Zhang, Xiao","Zhao, Li","Hou, Xiaonan","Liu, Yueliang","Zhu, Jianwei","Li, Xiaofang","Zhang, Suian","Sun, Weichao","Xie, Enze","Lu, Guiwu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-536583"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China University of Petroleum - Beijing"],"keyword":["Adsorption","CO2 capture","Carbon materials","Charge regulation","Covalent organic frameworks","Helium separation","Insights","Membrane","Nitride","Performance","Permeance","Strain engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["State Key Lab Coal & Coalbed Methane Coprod"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"highly selective co sub 000000000002 sub c sub 000000000002 sub h sub 000000000002 sub separation with porous g c sub 000000000009 sub n sub 000000000007 sub nanosheets by charge and strain engineering","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-536583","identifier":[{"id":"85123842578","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000774915800002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-efe48f01-26fa-429b-a983-0db866d02ce5"],"keyword":["ACETYLENE STORAGE","ADSORPTION","CARBON MATERIALS","CO2 CAPTURE","CO2 capture and separation","COVALENT ORGANIC FRAMEWORKS","Charge regulation","HELIUM SEPARATION","INSIGHTS","MONOLAYER MEMBRANE","Membrane","NITRIDE","PERFORMANCE","Permeance","Strain engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FBF92072F35537B5BC5E802DB1D35497"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china university of petroleum beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Petroleum - Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["State Key Lab Coal & Coalbed Methane Coprod"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Xue","key":"lixuepau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xue","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wenhao","key":"hewenhaopau","last":"He","name":"He, Wenhao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zilong","key":"liuzilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zilong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao","key":"zhangxiaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Li","key":"zhaolipau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Li","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaonan","key":"houxiaonanpau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Xiaonan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yueliang","key":"liuyueliangpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yueliang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jianwei","key":"zhujianweipau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Jianwei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaofang","key":"lixiaofangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaofang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Suian","key":"zhangsuianpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Suian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Weichao","key":"sunweichaopau","last":"Sun","locid":"728793c2-52fc-4c6d-b1be-14dc08be63b6","name":"Sun, Weichao","orcid":"0000-0002-8597-7501","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Enze","key":"xieenzepau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Enze","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guiwu","key":"luguiwupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Guiwu","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cej.2022.134737","issn":["13858947","18733212"],"issn_org":["13858947"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering Journal","paperid":"134737","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering Journal","volume":"435"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123842578"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-efe48f01-26fa-429b-a983-0db866d02ce5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Highly selective CO<sub>2</sub>/C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>2</sub> separation with porous g-C<sub>9</sub>N<sub>7</sub> nanosheets by charge and strain engineering","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-536583","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Black carbon is ubiquitous in the marine environment. However, whether it accumulates in the deepest ocean region, the hadal zone, is unknown. Here we measure the concentration and carbon isotopes (δ13C and Δ14C) of black carbon and total organic carbon in sediments from six hadal trenches. Black carbon constituted 10% of trench total organic carbon, and its δ13C and Δ14C were more negative than those of total organic carbon, suggesting that the black carbon was predominantly derived from terrestrial C3 plants and fossil fuels. The contribution of fossil carbon to the black carbon pool was spatially heterogeneous, which could be related to differences in the distance to landmass, land cover and socioeconomic development. Globally, we estimate a black carbon burial rate of 1.0 ± 0.5 Tg yr−1 in the hadal zone, which is seven-fold higher than the global ocean average per unit area. We propose that the hadal zone is an important, but overlooked, sink of black carbon in the ocean.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Zhang, Xi","Xu, Yunping","Xiao, Wenjie","Zhao, Meixun","Wang, Zicheng","Wang, Xuchen","Xu, Liping","Luo, Min","Li, Xinxin","Fang, Jiasong","Fang, Yin","Wang, Yasong","Oguri, Kazumasa","Wenzhöfer, Frank","Rowden, Ashley A.","Mitra, Siddhartha","Glud, Ronnie N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-600611"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Xu, Yunping"],"country":["China","Germany","Japan","New Zealand","United States"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute","All Global Affiliations","East Carolina University","Japan Agency for Marine Earth-Science and Technology","Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research","Ocean University of China","Qingdao National Laboratory for Marine Science and Technology","Shanghai Ocean University","Southern University of Science and Technology","Tokyo University of Marine Science and Technology","Victoria University of Wellington"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hadal zone is an important and heterogeneous sink of black carbon in the ocean","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43247-022-00351-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-600611","identifier":[{"id":"85130474122","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-5fce4131-9981-4b23-99d7-9e89edd28a61"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-731B30EB31D7522CF750B3E26867B976"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43247-022-00351-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/200115115/s43247_022_00351_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai ocean university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Ocean University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, HADAL","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Nordcee"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"southern university of science and technology","lo