{"abstract":"Although inclusive innovation has been regarded as a process according to prior studies, this complex process remains relatively under-researched, particularly when the process is successfully completed by entrepreneurial firms from emerging economies. This paper therefore seeks to explore, from a holistically dynamic view, how inclusive innovation process of entrepreneurial firms evolves in the “Bottom of the Pyramid” (BOP) markets. Based on the multi-dimensional details of a Chinese entrepreneurial firms conducting inclusive innovation in African BOP market, this exploratory case study suggests that inclusive innovation information management consists of three important consecutive stages: BOP market gap identification, market cultivation, and intensive market developing. We also unexpectedly reveal that the key capabilities in these three stages are distinctive.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wang, Xiao","Zheng, Leven J.","Li, Peter Ping","Dong, Jianing"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700575"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zheng, Leven J."],"country":["China","Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hong Kong Metropolitan University","University of Nottingham Ningbo China","Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University"],"keyword":["Born global firm","Inclusive innovation process","Interplay","Organizational capability","Synergy"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"international inclusive innovation of entrepreneurial firms toward a process model","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4018/JGIM.299321","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700575","ids":["cbs-e08a2136-697f-43ed-82b3-7fe43261343c"],"keyword":["Born-global firm","Inclusive innovation process","Interplay","Organizational capability","Synergy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-71C921BF57C5338F4E187A0AFEDA7DF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/98745703/wang_xiao_et_al_international_inclusive_innovation_of_entrepreneurial_firms_publisherversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4018/JGIM.299321","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"xi an jiaotong liverpool university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xi'an Jiaotong-Liverpool University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"hong kong metropolitan university","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Hong Kong Metropolitan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of International Economics, Government and Business"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"university of nottingham ningbo china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Nottingham Ningbo China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Leven J.","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Leven J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Ping","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"e37e0ae5-c775-414a-b958-81a2adf8ff38","name":"Li, Peter Ping","orcid":"0000-0002-0170-2050","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jianing","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Jianing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4018/jgim.299321","issn":["10627375","15337995"],"issn_org":["10627375"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Global Information Management","publisher":"IGI Publishing","status":"p","title":"Journal of Global Information Management","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-e08a2136-697f-43ed-82b3-7fe43261343c"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"International Inclusive Innovation of Entrepreneurial Firms : Toward a Process Model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700575","year":"2022","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present an observational study of the luminous red nova (LRN) AT 2021biy in the nearby galaxy NGC 4631. The field of the object was routinely imaged during the pre-eruptive stage by synoptic surveys, but the transient was detected only at a few epochs from similar to 231 days before maximum brightness. The LRN outburst was monitored with unprecedented cadence both photometrically and spectroscopically. AT 2021biy shows a short-duration blue peak, with a bolometric luminosity of similar to 1.6 x 10(41) erg s(-1), followed by the longest plateau among LRNe to date, with a duration of 210 days. A late-time hump in the light curve was also observed, possibly produced by a shell-shell collision. AT 2021biy exhibits the typical spectral evolution of LRNe. Early-time spectra are characterised by a blue continuum and prominent H emission lines. Then, the continuum becomes redder, resembling that of a K-type star with a forest of metal absorption lines during the plateau phase. Finally, late-time spectra show a very red continuum (T-BB approximate to 2050 K) with molecular features (e.g., TiO) resembling those of M-type stars. Spectropolarimetric analysis indicates that AT 2021biy has local dust properties similar to those of V838 Mon in the Milky Way Galaxy. Inspection of archival Hubble Space Telescope data taken on 2003 August 3 reveals a similar to 20 M-circle dot progenitor candidate with log (L/L-circle dot)= 5.0 dex and T-eff = 5900 K at solar metallicity. The above luminosity and colour match those of a luminous yellow supergiant. Most likely, this source is a close binary, with a 17-24 M(circle dot)( )primary component.","author_count":83,"contributors":["Cai, Y-Z","Pastorello, A.","Fraser, M.","Wang, X-F","Filippenko, A.","Reguitti, A.","Patra, K. C.","Goranskij, V. P.","Barsukova, E. A.","Brink, T. G.","Elias-Rosa, N.","Stevance, H. F.","Zheng, W.","Yang, Y.","Atapin, K. E.","Benetti, S.","de Boer, T. J. L.","Bose, S.","Burke, J.","Byrne, R.","Cappellaro, E.","Chambers, K. C.","Chen, W-L","Emami, N.","Gao, H.","Hiramatsu, D.","Howell, D. A.","Huber, M. E.","Kankare, E.","Kelly, P. L.","Kotak, R.","Kravtsov, T.","Lander, V. Yu","Li, Z-T","Lin, C-C","Lundqvist, P.","Magnier, E. A.","Malygin, E. A.","Maslennikova, N. A.","Matilainen, K.","Mazzali, P. A.","McCully, C.","Mo, J.","Moran, S.","Newsome, M.","Oparin, D.","Gonzalez, E. Padilla","Reynolds, T. M.","Shatsky, N.","Smartt, S. J.","Smith, K. W.","Stritzinger, M. D.","Tatarnikov, A. M.","Terreran, G.","Uklein, R.","Valerin, G.","Vallely, P. J.","Vozyakova, O. V.","Wainscoat, R.","Yan, S-Y","Zhang, J-J","Zhang, T-M","Zheltoukhov, S. G.","Dastidar, R.","Fulton, M.","Galbany, L.","Gangopadhyay, A.","Ge, H-W","Gutierrez, C. P.","Lin, H.","Misra, K.","Ou, Z-W","Salmaso, Nico","Tartaglia, L.","Xiao, L.","Zhang, X-H"],"cuid":["S02-086.57-021301"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Chile","China","Finland","Germany","India","Ireland","Italy","Japan","Russia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Administrative Headquarters of the Max Planck Society","All Global Affiliations","Aryabhatta Research Institute of Observational Sciences","Cumbres Observ","Hiroshima University","Institut d'Estudis Espacials de Catalunya (IEEC)","Istituto Nazionale di Astrofisica","Lomonosov Moscow State University","Millennium Inst Astrophys MAS","NSF AI Inst Artificial Intelligence & Fundamental","Ohio State University","Queen's University Belfast","Russian Academy of Sciences","Stockholm University","Sun Yat-Sen University","Tsinghua University","University College Dublin","University of California at Berkeley","University of California at Santa Barbara","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Minnesota Twin Cities","University of Padua","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Binaries close","DATA RELEASE","ELECTRON CAPTURE SUPERNOVAE","Evolution","RICH CIRCUMSTELLAR MEDIUM","SN HUNT 248","Stars winds outflows","Stellar mergers","Transient","V838 MONOCEROTIS","astro ph GA","astro ph HE","astro ph SR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forbidden hugs in pandemic times iii observations of the luminous red nova at 000000002021biy in the nearby galaxy ngc 000000004631","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202244393","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.57-021301","identifier":[{"id":"000875299200003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85142878213","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-761b2c3c-2b8a-4b8c-af3a-e9f03529e83d","ku-18ea49c2-0c30-4c73-98ab-84f4ba576acb"],"keyword":["DATA RELEASE","DUSTY AFTERMATH","ELECTRON-CAPTURE SUPERNOVAE","EVOLUTION","RICH CIRCUMSTELLAR MEDIUM","SN HUNT 248","STELLAR MERGERS","TRANSIENT","V4332 SAGITTARII","V838 MONOCEROTIS","astro-ph.GA","astro-ph.HE","astro-ph.SR","binaries: close","stars: individual: AT 2021biy","stars: winds, outflows"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AA2F4E9E28FED061329904C912197A39"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202244393","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/326352649/aa44393_22.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/296647599/2207.00734v2.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technolog