"affno":"20","first":"Nico","key":"salmasonicopau","last":"Salmaso","name":"Salmaso, Nico","rank":73,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L.","key":"xiaolpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, L.","rank":75,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"X-H","key":"zhangxhpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, X-H","rank":76,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1051/0004-6361/202244393","issn":["00046361","14320746"],"issn_org":["00046361"],"journal":"Astronomy & Astrophysics","paperid":"A4","publisher":"EDP Sciences","status":"p","title":"Astronomy & Astrophysics","title_org":"Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)","volume":"667"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142878213"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-761b2c3c-2b8a-4b8c-af3a-e9f03529e83d","ku-18ea49c2-0c30-4c73-98ab-84f4ba576acb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Forbidden hugs in pandemic times III. Observations of the luminous red nova AT 2021biy in the nearby galaxy NGC 4631","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.57-021301","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Increasing consumer demand for high-quality, additive-free fruit and vegetable products with ‘fresh-like’ sensory properties has led to the development of novel ‘minimal processing’ technologies. As a prime example, high pressure processing (HPP) is increasingly applied as an alternative to thermal processing (TP) to maintain the properties of fresh fruit-based juices and smoothies. However, the resulting products need to be validated from a sensory standpoint. Situated within this context, this paper provides a narrative review of sensory studies focused on high pressure treated fruit juices and smoothies published in the last ≈25 years (1995 to 2021), centered around three objectives: (i) to review methods used for assessing the sensory quality, (ii) to review knowledge of the effect of HPP on sensory quality, and (iii) to understand consumers’ acceptability towards these products. Overall, most sensory studies concluded that a combination of HPP and low temperature storage preserved the sensory properties better than TP, and thereby enables the production of products with ‘fresh-like’ quality. Yet, most published studies employed very small panel sizes and often showed a mismatch between test type and assessors employed (for example, using consumers for analytic tests and trained assessors for affective tests), which might lead to biased results. In future research, a clearer focus on experimental conditions, proper sensory methods, and more focus on the relationship between sensory quality and consumer perception are needed to better understand the effect of HPP on the sensory quality of fruit juices and smoothies.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Song, Qiushuang","Li, Renjie","Song, Xiao","Clausen, Mathias P.","Orlien, Vibeke","Giacalone, Davide"],"cuid":["S02-095.92-041206"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Giacalone, Davide"],"keyword":["Consumer acceptability","Fruit juice","High pressure processing","Sensory quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-DUP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-DUP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of high pressure processing on sensory quality and consumer acceptability of fruit juices and smoothies a review","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foodres.2022.111250","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.92-041206","identifier":[{"id":"000830158700006","type":"wos"},{"id":"35761562","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85128432871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-2e266ccf-02fb-4bb6-a56d-f32f46c8bbd6","sdu-330e14e0-a3ce-445a-9607-419a350482ac"],"keyword":["Consumer acceptability","Fruit juice","High pressure processing","Minimal processing methods","Sensory quality","Smoothies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FC3809E1C6928C42665BAADED2AB1CB4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/201700937/The_effect_of_high_pressure_processing_on_sensory_quality_and_consumer_acceptability_of_fruit_juices_and_smoothies_A_review_Elsevier_Enhanced_Reader.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foodres.2022.111250","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/305177283/1_s2.0_S0963996922003076_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation, SDU Innovation and Design Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Design and Consumer Behavior"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dupont","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-DUP","l3nn":"DuPont","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DuPont","namevar":["DuPont Nutrition Biosciences ApS (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-DUP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiushuang","key":"songqiushuangpau","last":"Song","locid":"1a03af4e-70f8-4aa6-ab19-2ac1df139b7c","name":"Song, Qiushuang","orcid":"0000-0003-0187-7608","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Renjie","key":"lirenjiepau","last":"Li","locid":"9ce6bc81-dfb3-452f-9735-4e1e9c538966","name":"Li, Renjie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Xiao","key":"songxiaopau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias Porsmose","key":"clausenmathiasppau","last":"Clausen","locid":"dad6e7b1-6013-461d-b9a6-367b146f5d86","name":"Clausen, Mathias P.","name_org":"Clausen, Mathias Porsmose","orcid":"0000-0003-1196-6241","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vibeke","key":"orlienvibekepau","last":"Orlien","locid":"05a112c3-5a29-42d3-b0ed-cbe2cc68fae3","name":"Orlien, Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0003-4354-6591","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Davide","key":"giacalonedavidepau","last":"Giacalone","locid":"da9e1744-4cb6-419e-bd02-ef7b74513323","name":"Giacalone, Davide","orcid":"0000-0003-2498-0632","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35761562"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.foodres.2022.111250","issn":["09639969","18737145"],"issn_org":["09639969"],"journal":"Food Research International","paperid":"111250","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Food Research International","volume":"157"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85128432871"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2e266ccf-02fb-4bb6-a56d-f32f46c8bbd6","sdu-330e14e0-a3ce-445a-9607-419a350482ac"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The effect of high-pressure processing on sensory quality and consumer acceptability of fruit juices and smoothies : A review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.92-041206","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Genetics and biology may influence the age of onset of anorexia nervosa (AN). The aims of this study were to determine whether common genetic variation contributes to age of onset of AN and to investigate the genetic associations between age of onset of AN and age at menarche. Methods: A secondary analysis of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium genome-wide association study (GWAS) of AN was performed, which included 9335 cases and 31,981 screened controls, all from European ancestries. We conducted GWASs of age of onset, early-onset AN (<13 years), and typical-onset AN, and genetic correlation, genetic risk score, and Mendelian randomization analyses. Results: Two loci were genome-wide significant in the typical-onset AN GWAS. Heritability estimates (single nucleotide polymorphism–h2) were 0.01–0.04 for age of onset, 0.16–0.25 for early-onset AN, and 0.17–0.25 for typical-onset AN. Early- and typical-onset AN showed distinct genetic correlation patterns with putative risk factors for AN. Specifically, early-onset AN was significantly genetically correlated with younger age at menarche, and typical-onset AN was significantly negatively genetically correlated with anthropometric traits. Genetic risk scores for age of onset and early-onset AN estimated from independent GWASs significantly predicted age of onset. Mendelian randomization analysis suggested a causal link between younger age at menarche and early-onset AN. Conclusions: Our results provide evidence consistent with a common variant genetic basis for age of onset and implicate biological pathways regulating menarche and reproduction.","author_count":177,"contributors":["Watson, Hunna J.","Thornton, Laura M.","Yilmaz, Zeynep","Baker, Jessica H.","Coleman, Jonathan R.I.","Adan, Roger A.H.","Alfredsson, Lars","Andreassen, Ole A.","Ask, Helga","Berrettini, Wade H.","Boehnke, Michael","Boehm, Ilka","Boni, Claudette","Buehren, Katharina","Bulant, Josef","Burghardt, Roland","Chang, Xiao","Ci