{"abstract":"Crops are exposed to the environment and are able to adapt their development and physiology to multiple occurring stress types and events. “Priming”—exposing plants to moderate abiotic stress during vegetative growth in order to induce plant resistance to a severe stress episodes occurring during generative growth has improved stress tolerance within the same generation as well as between generations. This chapter presents our understanding of the complex physiological and molecular mechanisms involved in induced stress tolerance to abiotic stressors in crop plants with focus on both intra-generational and transgenerational mechanisms. Perspectives for further research are presented in order to understand the underlying mechanisms of stress priming for the application of priming effects in crop production.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Wang, Xiao","Wollenweber, Bernd","Jiang, Dong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137069"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Abiotic stress","Physiological mechanisms","Priming","Transgenerational"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"abiotic stress priming an effective approach for coping with abiotic stress episodes in crop production","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85137898715","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137069","identifier":[{"id":"85137898715","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0d823224-be74-41f7-afac-ca31a4850570"],"keyword":["abiotic stress","intra-generational","physiological mechanisms","priming","transgenerational"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6E02B842ED01A5E20F58594A40DCF68"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"wangxiaopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bernd","key":"wollenweberberndpau","last":"Wollenweber","locid":"f52f52aa-27ac-43a8-9321-14c192372360","name":"Wollenweber, Bernd","orcid":"0000-0002-7867-4756","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong","key":"jiangdongpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Dong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"F.","key":"liufpedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, F.","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"X.","key":"lixpedh","last":"Li","name":"Li, X.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"P.","key":"hogyppedh","last":"Hogy","name":"Hogy, P.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"D.","key":"jiangdpedh","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, D.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"M.","key":"besticmpedh","last":"Bestic","name":"Bestic, M.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"B.","key":"liubpedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, B.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/b978-0-323-85449-8.00008-7","eisbn":["9780323854498"],"isbn":["9780323854504"],"pages":"295-311","place":"London","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Responses of Crop Plants to Climate Change","title":"Sustainable Crop Productivity and Quality under Climate Change"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137898715"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0d823224-be74-41f7-afac-ca31a4850570"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Abiotic stress priming: an effective approach for coping with abiotic stress episodes in crop production","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-137069","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Psoriasis is a chronic, immune-mediated skin disorder involving hyperproliferation of the keratinocytes in the epidermis. As complex as its pathophysiology, the optimal treatment for psoriasis remains unsatisfactorily addressed. Though systemic administration of biological agents has made an impressive stride in moderate-to-severe psoriasis, a considerable portion of psoriatic conditions were left unresolved, mainly due to adverse effects from systemic drug administration or insufficient drug delivery across a highly packed stratum corneum via topical therapies. Along with the advances in nanotechnologies, the incorporation of nanomaterials as topical drug carriers opens an obvious prospect for the development of antipsoriatic topicals. Hence, this review aims to distinguish the benefits and weaknesses of individual nanostructures when applied as topical antipsoriatics in preclinical psoriatic models. In view of specific features of each nanostructure, we propose that a proper combination of distinctive nanomaterials according to the physicochemical properties of loaded drugs and clinical features of psoriatic patients is becoming a promising option that potentially drives the translation of nanomaterials from bench to bedside with improved transdermal drug delivery and consequently therapeutic effects.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Li, Ning","Qin, Yeping","Dai, Dan","Wang, Pengyu","Shi, Mingfei","Gao, Junwei","Yang, Jinsheng","Xiao, Wei","Song, Ping","Xu, Ruodan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263177"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xu, Ruodan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","Jiangsu Kanion Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd."],"keyword":["Drug delivery","Nanomaterials","Nanotechnology","Psoriasis","Transdermal"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transdermal delivery of therapeutic compounds with nanotechnological approaches in psoriasis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2021.804415","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263177","identifier":[{"id":"85124229938","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35141215","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8819148","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-ea7e1654-3fdc-4460-8e33-4f1819052f3c"],"keyword":["drug delivery","nanomaterials","nanotechnology","psoriasis","transdermal"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C348F8E25C25AEE9E0CE20DBF2C4552"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2021.804415","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of medical sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"jiangsu kanion pharmaceutical co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangsu Kanion Pharmaceutical Co., Ltd.","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yeping","key":"qinpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Yeping","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"daipau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Dan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengyu","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Pengyu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingfei","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Mingfei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Junwei","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Junwei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinsheng","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Jinsheng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Wei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ping","key":"songpau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Ping","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruodan","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"e966d7a9-f7e1-48d2-b7c9-51d8eb2d21ee","name":"Xu, Ruodan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35141215"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fbioe.2021.804415","issn":["22964185"],"journal":"Frontiers in Bioengineering and Biotechnology","paperid":"804415","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Bioengineering and Biotechnology","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124229938"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ea7e1654-3fdc-4460-8e33-4f1819052f3c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Transdermal Delivery of Therapeutic Compounds With Nanotechnological Approaches in Psoriasis","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263177","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The temporal heterogeneity of nitrogen availability in soils is increasing due to agricultural deposition. We here compared the effects of gradually increasing nitrogen deposition rate and its increasing temporal heterogeneity patterns on the functional traits of seedlings of exotic species Rhus typhina and the native species Rhus chinensis. Nitrogen deposition rates of 0, 8, 20 g N m−2 year−1 and constant, single-peak, and double-peak nitrogen were added to simulate deposition rate and temporal heterogeneity. After 60 days of treatment, R. typhina seedlings had several advantageous growth trait values, such as higher total biomass production, but lower phenotypic plasticity than R. chinensis seedlings. R. typhina seedlings also had higher phenotypic integration, measured as the correlation among functional traits. The increased nitrogen deposition rate affected several traits of the two species differently. Thus, while R. chinensis seedlings allocated more biomass to leaves and less to roots with increasing N deposition, R. typhina seedlings had stable biomass allocation among all N treatments. Chlorophyll content, leaf phosphorus concentration, and water use efficiency increased, but the maximum net photosynthetic rate decreased, with N availability in R. chinensis, but not in R. typhina. Temporal heterogeneity had no significant effect on the total biomass of R. typhina and R. chinensis seedlings. Overall, the performance of R. typhina is better than that of R. chinensis seedlings under different nitrogen deposition treatments, which is due to the significantly advantageous trait values and greater phenotypic integration of R. typhina seedlings, whereas R. chinensis seedlings have higher phenotypic plasticity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wang, Qun","Li, Ming Yan","Eller, Franziska","Luo, Yu Jie","Nong, Ying Lan","Xing, Li Jun","Xu, Zhen Wei","Li, Hai Mei","Lu, Hui Cui","Guo, Xiao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-271003"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Xiao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qingdao Agricultural University","Shandong University","Shandong Women’s University","Zhejiang Agriculture and Forestry University"],"keyword":["Nitrogen deposition","Phenotypic integration","Phenotypic plasticity","Temporal heterogeneity","Trait value"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trait value and phenotypic integration contribute to the response of exotic rhus typhina to heterogeneous nitrogen deposition a comparison with native rhus chinensis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134255508","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-271003","identifier":[{"id":"35810896","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85134255508","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f85a7cb2-75ea-4e6d-8e72-c971b0c2745d"],"keyword":["Nitrogen deposition","Phenotypic integration","Phenotypic plasticity","Rhus chinensis","Rhus typhina","Temporal heterogeneity","Trait value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C976CAF7CCA755574E2532E25C7D7DC5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"qingdao agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang agriculture and forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang Agriculture and Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shandong women s university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong Women’s University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qun","key":"wangqunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Qun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ming Yan","key":"limingyanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ming Yan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu Jie","key":"luoyujiepau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Yu Jie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying Lan","key":"nongyinglanpau","last":"Nong","name":"Nong, Ying Lan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li Jun","key":"xinglijunpau","last":"Xing","name":"Xing, Li Jun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhen Wei","key":"xuzhenweipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Zhen Wei","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai Mei","key":"lihaimeipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hai Mei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui Cui","key":"luhuicuipau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Hui Cui","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"guoxiaopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35810896"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.157199","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"157199","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"844"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134255508"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f85a7cb2-75ea-4e6d-8e72-c971b0c2745d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Trait value and phenotypic integration contribute to the response of exotic Rhus typhina to heterogeneous nitrogen deposition : A comparison with native Rhus chinensis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-271003","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Differences by sex in lung cancer incidence and mortality have been reported which cannot be fully explained by sex differences in smoking behavior, implying existence of genetic and molecular basis for sex disparity in lung cancer development. However, the information about sex dimorphism in lung cancer risk is quite limited despite the great success in lung cancer association studies. By adopting a stringent two-stage analysis strategy, we performed a genome-wide gene-sex interaction analysis using genotypes from a lung cancer cohort including ~ 47 000 individuals with European ancestry. Three low-frequency variants (minor allele frequency < 0.05), rs17662871 [odds ratio (OR) = 0.71, P = 4.29×10-8); rs79942605 (OR = 2.17, P = 2.81×10-8) and rs208908 (OR = 0.70, P = 4.54×10-8) were identified with different risk effect of lung cancer between men and women. Further expression quantitative trait loci and functional annotation analysis suggested rs208908 affects lung cancer risk through differential regulation of Coxsackie virus and adenovirus receptor gene expression in lung tissues between men and women. Our study is one of the first studies to provide novel insights about the genetic and molecular basis for sex disparity in lung cancer development.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Li, Yafang","Xiao, Xiangjun","Li, Jianrong","Byun, Jinyoung","Cheng, Chao","Bossé, Yohan","McKay, James","Albanes, Demetrios","Lam, Stephen","Tardon, Adonina","Chen, Chu","Bojesen, Stig E","Landi, Maria T.","Johansson, Mattias","Risch, Angela","Bickeböller, Heike","Wichmann, H. Erich","Christiani, David C.","Rennert, Gad","Arnold, Susanne","Goodman, Gary","Field, John K.","Davies, Michael P.A.","Shete, Sanjay S.","Le Marchand, Loic","Melander, Olle","Brunnström, Hans","Liu, Geoffrey","Hung, Rayjean J.","Andrew, Angeline S.","Kiemeney, Lambertus A.","Shen, Hongbing","Sun, Ryan","Zienolddiny, Shan","Grankvist, Kjell","Johansson, Mikael","Caporaso, Neil","Teare, Dawn M.","Hong, Yun Chul","Lazarus, Philip","Schabath, Matthew B.","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Schwartz, Ann G.","Gorlov, Ivan","Purrington, Kristen","Yang, Ping","Liu, Yanhong","Han, Younghun","Bailey-Wilson, Joan E.","Pinney, Susan M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-435864"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["INTEGRAL-ILCCO lung cancer consortium"],"country":["Austria","Canada","China","France","Germany","Israel","Netherlands","Norway","South Korea","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","Clalit Health Services","Dartmouth College","Department of Health Sciences Research","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Laval University","Lund University","Nanjing Medical University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","Princess Margaret Cancer Center","Radboud University Nijmegen","Seoul National University","Sinai Health System","Swedish Medical Center","Technical University of Munich","Translational Lung Research Center Heidelberg (TLRC-H)","Umeå University","University of British Columbia","University of Cincinnati","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Kentucky","University of Liverpool","University of Newcastle","University of Oviedo","University of Salzburg","University of South Florida","University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Spokane","Wayne State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["D