last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Gang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Tsechoe","key":"dorjipau","last":"Dorji","name":"Dorji, Tsechoe","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Georg","key":"guggenbergerpau","last":"Guggenberger","name":"Guggenberger, Georg","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35690211"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.156542","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"156542","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"838"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131944036"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-630a0dae-9c0a-46a1-8daa-5ddf1910ec60"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The glacial–terrestrial–fluvial pathway : A multiparametrical analysis of spatiotemporal dissolved organic matter variation in three catchments of Lake Nam Co, Tibetan Plateau","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452676","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND. Adoptive cell therapy (ACT) with tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes (TILs) has achieved remarkable clinical efficacy in metastatic cancers such as melanoma and cervical cancer (CC). Here, we explored the safety, feasibility, and preliminary tumor response and performed translational investigations of adjuvant immunotherapy using infusion of autogenous TILs (auto-TILs) following concurrent chemoradiotherapy (CCRT) in patients with CC who had locally advanced disease. METHODS. Twenty-seven patients with CC with stage III-IV disease were recruited in this single-center, phase I study. TILs were isolated from lesions in the uterine cervix and generated under good manufacturing practice (GMP) conditions and then infused after CCRT plus i.m. IL-2 injections. RESULTS. TILs from 20 of the 27 patients were successfully expanded, with a feasibility of 74.1%. Twelve patients received TILs following CCRT. Adverse events (AEs) were primarily attributable to CCRT. Only 1 (8.3%) patient experienced severe toxicity with a grade 3 hypersensitivity reaction after TIL infusion. No autoimmune AEs, such as pneumonitis, hepatitis, or myocarditis, occurred, and there were no treatment-related mortalities. Nine of 12 patients (75.0%) attained a complete response, with a disease control duration of 9-22 months. Translational investigation showed that the transcriptomic characteristics of the infused TIL products and some immune biomarkers in the tumor microenvironment and serum of patients with CC at baseline were correlated with the clinical response. CONCLUSION. TIL-based ACT following CCRT was safe in an academic center setting, with potentially effective responses in patients with locally advanced CC. \"Hot\" inflammatory immune environments were beneficial to the clinical efficacy of TILbased ACT as adjuvant therapy.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Huang, He","Nie, Cai-Ping","Liu, Xiu-feng","Song, Bin","Yue, Jianhui","Xu, Jing-xiao","He, Jia","Li, Kui","Feng, Yan-ling","Wan, Ting","Zheng, Min","Zhang, Yan-Na","Ye, Wei-Jun","Li, Jun-Dong","Li, Yan-Fang","Li, Jun-yun","Cao, Xin-Ping","Liu, Zhi-min","Zhang, Xiao-shi","Liu, Qing","Zhang, Xi","Liu, Ji-Hong","Li, Jiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488896"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Sun Yat-Sen University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phase i study of adjuvant immunotherapy with autologous tumor infiltrating lymphocytes in locally advanced cervical cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI157726","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488896","identifier":[{"id":"35727633","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9337833","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85135219892","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9fb3cd9d-11a8-4b0f-9d8e-5e45d0f1086d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EC8C4384A4D68EB91C50BCB79BD97C3A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/318804510/157726.2_20220726135251_covered_e0fd13ba177f913fd3156f593ead4cfd.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI157726","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"B