"last":"Yao","name":"Yao, Yong-Gang","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 13","first":"Ya-Ping","key":"zhangyapingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ya-Ping","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 14 15","first":"Guojie","key":"zhangguojiepau","last":"Zhang","locid":"f5381bdc-b377-47a3-bdc0-4deccfda761c","name":"Zhang, Guojie","orcid":"0000-0001-6860-1521","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35008130"],"pub":{"doi":"10.24272/j.issn.2095-8137.2022.001","issn":["20958137"],"issue":"2","journal":"Zoological research","pages":"147-149","status":"p","title":"Zoological research","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123459722"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c604ea8b-e0dc-4250-8338-329883bd300b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Initiation of the Primate Genome Project","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-511643","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Indoor positioning data is of high significance to many indoor location-based services whereas it is of low quality due to the limitations of indoor positioning technologies. Thus, our work is focused on cleansing indoor positioning data to enhance its quality significantly. In this paper, we first introduce the data quality issues consisting in indoor positioning data and propose a cleansing framework to handle such issues. Subsequently, we formulate four specific research questions in order to settle related quality issues. In addition, we present promising methodologies and comprehensive evaluation criteria to resolve our proposed research questions.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Li, Xiao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-572933"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-09","place":"Virtual, Paphos, cy","start":"2022-06-06","title":"23rd IEEE International Conference on Mobile Data Management, MDM 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cleansing and analytics of indoor positioning data","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-572933","identifier":[{"id":"85137600838","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-fb8c8ba0-2ad3-4b9b-ab75-237644adbdf6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8CE7E852B605059E10B5AB43803F3293"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Xiao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"8b86b24d-5f2f-42ea-84c1-ce252da514d9","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/mdm55031.2022.00075","eisbn":["9781665451765"],"issn":["15516245"],"pages":"334-336","publisher":"IEEE","series":"Proceedings - IEEE International Conference on Mobile Data Management","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2022 23rd IEEE International Conference on Mobile Data Management, MDM 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137600838"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-fb8c8ba0-2ad3-4b9b-ab75-237644adbdf6"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Cleansing and Analytics of Indoor Positioning Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-572933","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Alcohol intake is thought to be a risk factor for breast cancer, but the causal relationship and carcinogenic mechanisms are not clear. We performed an up-to-date meta-analysis of prospective studies to assess observational association, and then conducted MR analysis to make causal inference based on the genetic predisposition to alcohol consumption (“drinks per week”) and pathological drinking behaviours (“alcohol use disorder” and “problematic alcohol use”), as well as genetically predicted DNA methylation at by alcohol-related CpG sites in blood. We found an observational dose–response association between alcohol intake and breast cancer incidence with an additional risk of 4% for per 10 g/day increase in alcohol consumption. Genetic predisposition to alcohol consumption (“drinks per week”) was not causally associated with breast cancer incidence at the OR of 1.01 (95% CI 0.84, 1.23), but problematic alcohol use (PAU) was linked to a higher breast cancer risk at the OR of 1.76 (95% CI 1.04, 2.99) when conditioning on alcohol consumption. Epigenetic MR analysis identified four CpG sites, cg03260624 near CDC7 gene, cg10816169 near ZNF318 gene, cg03345232 near RIN3 gene, and cg26312998 near RP11-867G23.13 gene, where genetically predicted epigenetic modifications were associated with an increased breast cancer incidence risk. Our findings re-affirmed that alcohol consumption is of high risk for breast cancer incidence even at a very low dose, and the pathogenic effect of alcohol on breast cancer could be due to pathological drinking behaviour and epigenetic modification at several CpG sites, which could be potential intervention targets for breast cancer prevention.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Zhou, Xuan","Yu, Lili","Wang, Lijuan","Xiao, Jiarui","Sun, Jing","Zhou, Yajing","Xu, Xiaolin","Xu, Wanghong","Spiliopoulou, Athina","Timofeeva, Maria","Zhang, Xiaomeng","He, Yazhou","Yang, Haomin","Campbell, Harry","Zhang, Ben","Zhu, Yimin","Theodoratou, Evropi","Li, Xue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-639469"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Xue"],"country":["China","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","College of Information Science and Electronic Engineering, Zhejiang University","Fudan University","Fujian Medical University","Karolinska Institute","Sichuan University","The Key Laboratory of Intelligent Preventive Medicine of Zhejiang Province","The University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Alcohol","Alcohol Drinking epidemiology","Breast Neoplasms epidemiology","Breast cancer","Cell Cycle Proteins genetics","DNA methylation","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Humans","Mendelian Randomization Analysis","Mendelian randomisation","Prospective Studies","Protein Serine Threonine Kinases","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alcohol consumption blood dna methylation and breast cancer a mendelian randomisation study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-022-00886-1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["XL is supported by the Natural Science Fund for Distinguished Young Scholars of Zhejiang Province (LR22H260001). ET is supported by CRUK Career Development Fellowship (C31250/A22804). AS acknowledges support from the Academy of Medical Sciences/the Wellcome Trust/ the Government Department of Business, Energy and Industrial Strategy/the British Heart Foundation/Diabetes UK Springboard Award [SBF006\\1109]."],"id":"S01-000.00-639469","identifier":[{"id":"85132296729","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9329409","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35708873","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e75ed527-b84b-4001-bcac-161395437ef6"],"keyword":["Alcohol","Alcohol Drinking/epidemiology","Breast Neoplasms/epidemiology","Breast cancer","Cell Cycle Proteins/genetics","DNA methylation","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Humans","Mendelian Randomization Analysis","Mendelian randomisation","Prospective Studies","Protein Serine-Threonine Kinases","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-37A217E5046818DE511DD9F3600EAF91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-022-00886-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215954932/s10654_022_00886_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"college of information science and electronic engineering zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"College of Information Science and Electronic Engineering, Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"the key laboratory of intelligent preventive medicine of zhejiang province","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"The Key Laboratory of Intelligent Preventive Medicine of Zhejiang Province","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"fudan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fudan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"the university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark