{"abstract":"Featuring high electrical conductivity and electrochemical activity, transition metal sulfides are promising materials for the positive electrode of hybrid supercapacitors. However, considering their poor cycling life and rate performance, critical challenges remain. In this contribution, we describe hollow NiS2/CoS2@C composites obtained by stepwise etching, annealing, and sulfuration of ZIF-67. Specifically, NiS2/CoS2 particles were dispersed on N/S co-doped carbon nanocages and found to exhibit outstanding stability and rate performance. The unique nanocage structure of N/S co-doped carbon and heterogeneous interfaces of NiS2 and CoS2 can promote both ion transport and electron transfer, enriching the active site for enhanced reactivity. The resulting NiS2/CoS2@C nanocage composites in fact showed considerable electrochemical performance, with a specific capacity of 1373 C g-1 at 1 A g-1. When combined with reduced graphene oxide (RGO)-based negative electrode, the assembled hybrid supercapacitor registered an energy density of 63.3 Wh kg-1 at a power density of 800 W kg-1, retaining exceeding 98% of the initial capacity even after 13,000 cycles.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Li, Shanshan","Yang, Yuan","Hu, Zhibiao","Li, Shuo","Ding, Fei","Xiao, Xinxin","Si, Pengchao","Ulstrup, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339522"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Si, Pengchao","Xiao, Xinxin"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hebei University of Technology","Shandong University"],"keyword":["Electrochemical performance","Hybrid supercapacitors","Transition metal sulfides"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hetero structured nis sub 000000000002 sub cos sub 000000000002 sub nanospheres embedded on n s co doped carbon nanocages with ultra thin nanosheets for hybrid supercapacitors","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electacta.2022.140604","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339522","identifier":[{"id":"85131118040","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-75049893-55b1-4738-9263-1371882f795b"],"keyword":["Electrochemical performance","Hybrid supercapacitors","N/S co-doped carbon nanocages","Transition metal sulfides"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DDF12A657D92A574D7EF0B2F6E4C8E7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electacta.2022.140604","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/278124895/1_s2.0_S0013468622007630_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hebei university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hebei University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shanshan","key":"lishanshanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shanshan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuan","key":"yangyuanpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Yuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhibiao","key":"huzhibiaopau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Zhibiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuo","key":"lishuopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shuo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fei","key":"dingfeipau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Fei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaoxinxinpau","last":"Xiao","locid":"8cd768ff-d2df-4d64-bd7c-0d46854d561c","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengchao","key":"sipengchaopau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Pengchao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"ulstrupjenspau","last":"Ulstrup","locid":"a7bf8f77-fd81-4dce-8592-8c7bec26750b","name":"Ulstrup, Jens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.electacta.2022.140604","issn":["00134686","18733859"],"issn_org":["00134686"],"journal":"Electrochimica Acta","paperid":"140604","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Electrochimica Acta","volume":"424"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131118040"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-75049893-55b1-4738-9263-1371882f795b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Hetero-structured NiS<sub>2</sub>/CoS<sub>2</sub> nanospheres embedded on N/S co-doped carbon nanocages with ultra-thin nanosheets for hybrid supercapacitors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-339522","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Hepatocellular carcinoma has high recurrence rates after surgery; however, there are no approved standard-of-care neoadjuvant or adjuvant therapies. Immunotherapy has been shown to improve survival in advanced hepatocellular carcinoma; we therefore aimed to evaluate the safety and tolerability of perioperative immunotherapy in resectable hepatocellular carcinoma. Methods: In this single-centre, randomised, open-label, phase 2 trial, patients with resectable hepatocellular carcinoma were randomly assigned (1:1) to receive 240 mg of nivolumab intravenously every 2 weeks (for up to three doses before surgery at 6 weeks) followed in the adjuvant phase by 480 mg of nivolumab intravenously every 4 weeks for 2 years, or 240 mg of nivolumab intravenously every 2 weeks (for up to three doses before surgery) plus one dose of 1 mg/kg of ipilimumab intravenously concurrently with the first preoperative dose of nivolumab, followed in the adjuvant phase by 480 mg of nivolumab intravenously every 4 weeks for up to 2 years plus 1 mg/kg of ipilimumab intravenously every 6 weeks for up to four cycles. Patients were randomly assigned to the treatment groups by use of block randomisation with a random block size. The primary endpoint was the safety and tolerability of nivolumab with or without ipilimumab. Secondary endpoints were the proportion of patients with an overall response, time to progression, and progression-free survival. This trial is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT03222076) and is completed. Findings: Between Oct 30, 2017, and Dec 3, 2019, 30 patients were enrolled and 27 were randomly assigned: 13 to nivolumab and 14 to nivolumab plus ipilimumab. Grade 3–4 adverse events were higher with nivolumab plus ipilimumab (six [43%] of 14 patients) than with nivolumab alone (three [23%] of 13). The most common treatment-related adverse events of any grade were increased alanine aminotransferase (three [23%] of 13 patients on nivolumab vs seven [50%] of 14 patients on nivolumab plus ipilimumab) and increased aspartate aminotransferase (three [23%] vs seven [50%]). No patients in either group had their surgery delayed due to grade 3 or worse adverse events. Seven of 27 patients had surgical cancellations, but none was due to treatment-related adverse events. Estimated median progression-free survival was 9·4 months (95% CI 1·47–not estimable [NE]) with nivolumab and 19·53 months (2·33–NE) with nivolumab plus ipilimumab (hazard ratio [HR] 0·99, 95% CI 0·31–2·54); median time to progression was 9·4 months (95% CI 1·47–NE) in the nivolumab group and 19·53 months (2·33–NE) in the nivolumab plus ipilimumab group (HR 0·89, 95% CI 0·31–2·54). In an exploratory analysis, three (23%) of 13 patients had an overall response with nivolumab monotherapy, versus none with nivolumab plus ipilimumab. Three (33%) of nine patients had a major pathological response (ie, ≥70% necrosis in the resected tumour area) with nivolumab monotherapy compared with three (27%) of 11 with nivolumab plus ipilimumab. Interpretation: Perioperative nivolumab alone and nivolumab plus ipilimumab appears to be safe and feasible in patients with resectable hepatocellular carcinoma. Our findings support further studies of immunotherapy in the perioperative setting in hepatocellular carcinoma. Funding: Bristol Myers Squibb and the US National Institutes of Health.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Kaseb, Ahmed Omar","Hasanov, Elshad","Cao, Hop Sanderson Tran","Xiao, Lianchun","Vauthey, Jean Nicolas","Lee, Sunyoung S.","Yavuz, Betul Gok","Mohamed, Yehia I.","Qayyum, Abbas Ali","Jindal, Sonali","Duan, Fei","Basu, Sreyashi","Yadav, Shalini S.","Nicholas, Courtney","Sun, Jing","Singh Raghav, Kanwal Pratap","Rashid, Asif","Carter, Kristen","Chun, Yun Shin","Tzeng, Ching Wei David","Sakamuri, Divya","Xu, Li","Sun, Ryan","Cristini, Vittorio","Beretta, Laura","Yao, James C.","Wolff, Robert A.","Allison, James Patrick","Sharma, Padmanee"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-407407"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Houston Methodist Hospital","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"perioperative nivolumab monotherapy versus nivolumab plus ipilimumab in resectable hepatocellular carcinoma a randomised open label phase 000000000002 trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359087800/1_s2.0_S2468125321004271_am.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-407407","identifier":[{"id":"35065057","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8840977","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85123066537","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-176b7dc6-46f6-4846-aea5-ddd9adf0ebcd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-71EBA577DBC04A3C0A70894845FE1490"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359087800/1_s2.0_S2468125321004271_am.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of texas md anderson cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"houston methodist hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Houston Methodist Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ahmed Omar","key":"kasebahmedomarpau","last":"Kaseb","name":"Kaseb, Ahmed Omar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elshad","key":"hasanovelshadpau","last":"Hasanov","name":"Hasanov, Elshad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hop Sanderson Tran","key":"caohopsandersontranpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Hop Sanderson Tran","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lianchun","key":"xiaolianchunpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Lianchun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jean Nicolas","key":"vautheyjeannicolaspau","last":"Vauthey","name":"Vauthey, Jean Nicolas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sunyoung S.","key":"leesunyoungspau","last":"Lee","name":"Lee, Sunyoung S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Betul Gok","key":"yavuzbetulgokpau","last":"Yavuz","name":"Yavuz, Betul Gok","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yehia I.","key":"mohamedyehiaipau","last":"Mohamed","name":"Mohamed, Yehia I.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Aliya","key":"qayyumabbasalipau","last":"Qayyum","locid":"3e88be55-12b0-4193-bec8-a16adbb85fe3","name":"Qayyum, Abbas Ali","name_org":"Qayyum, Aliya","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sonali","key":"jindalsonalipau","last":"Jindal","name":"Jindal, Sonali","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fei","key":"duanfeipau","last":"Duan","name":"Duan, Fei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sreyashi","key":"basusreyashipau","last":"Basu","name":"Basu, Sreyashi","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shalini S.","key":"yadavshalinispau","last":"Yadav","name":"Yadav, Shalini S.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Courtney","key":"nicholascourtneypau","last":"Nicholas","name":"Nicholas, Courtney","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jing Jing","key":"sunjingpau","last":"Sun","locid":"b4956605-0f72-4e78-be11-d9406afde2e9","name":"Sun, Jing","name_org":"Sun, Jing Jing","orcid":"0000-0003-0103-6809","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kanwal Pratap","key":"singhraghavkanwalpratappau","last":"Singh Raghav","name":"Singh Raghav, Kanwal Pratap","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asif","key":"rashidasifpau","last":"Rashid","name":"Rashid, Asif","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristen","key":"carterkristenpau","last":"Carter","name":"Carter, Kristen","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yun Shin","key":"chunyunshinpau","last":"Chun","name":"Chun, Yun Shin","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ching Wei David","key":"tzengchingweidavidpau","last":"Tzeng","name":"Tzeng, Ching Wei David","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Divya","key":"sakamuridivyapau","last":"Sakamuri","name":"Sakamuri, Divya","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Li","key":"xulipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Li","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ryan","key":"sunryanpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Ryan","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Vittorio","key":"cristinivittoriopau","last":"Cristini","name":"Cristini, Vittorio","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laura","key":"berettalaurapau","last":"Beretta","name":"Beretta, Laura","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"James C.","key":"yaojamescpau","last":"Yao","name":"Yao, James C.","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Robert A.","key":"wolffrobertapau","last":"Wolff","name":"Wolff, Robert A.","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"James Patrick","key":"allisonjamespatrickpau","last":"Allison","name":"Allison, James Patrick","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Padmanee","key":"sharmapadmaneepau","last":"Sharma","name":"Sharma, Padmanee","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35065057"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2468-1253(21)00427-1","issn":["24681253"],"issue":"3","journal":"The Lancet Gastroenterology and Hepatology","pages":"208-218","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Gastroenterology and Hepatology","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-176b7dc6-46f6-4846-aea5-ddd9adf0ebcd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Perioperative nivolumab monotherapy versus nivolumab plus ipilimumab in resectable hepatocellular carcinoma : a randomised, open-label, phase 2 trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-407407","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Salmonella is a leading cause of foodborne illness worldwide and is a common concern in food safety. Salmonella enterica displaying resistance to extended-spectrum cephalosporins (ESCs) and fluoroquinolone (FQs) has been deemed a high-priority pathogen by the World Health Organization. Co-resistance to ESCs and FQs has been reported in S. enterica serovar Thompson (S. Thompson). However, the genetic context of ESCs and FQs resistance genes in S. Thompson lacks sufficient characterization. In this study, we characterized a multi-drug resistant (MDR) S. Thompson isolate recovered from a retail ready-to-eat (RTE) pork product in China. Short- and long-read sequencing (HiSeq and MinION) of the genome identified the presence of blaCMY−2, qnrS1, and qepA8, along with 11 additional acquired antimicrobial resistance genes, residing on a 152,940 bp IncA/C plasmid. Specifically, the blaCMY−2, qnrS1, and qepA8 genes were located in insertion sequences (ISs) and integron mediated mobile genetic structure, sugE-blc-blaCMY−2-ISEc9, IS26-orf6-qnrS1-orf5-ISKpn19, and intl1-qepA8-orf10-IS91-orf1-dfrA12-orf11-aadA2-qacEΔ1-sul1, respectively. Each gene was identified in various bacteria species, indicating their high transfer ability. The plasmid was found to be transferable to Escherichia coli J53 by conjugation and resulted in the acquiring of multiple resistances in the transconjugants. The plasmid is closely related to plasmids from two human S. Thompson strains isolated in different regions and years in China. Moreover, core-genome Multi Locus Sequence Typing (cgMLST) and phylogenetic analysis based on global 1,868 S. Saintpaul isolates showed that the S. Thompson isolate was highly epidemiologically linked to a human isolate in China. Our findings suggest that Chinese RTE pork products are a possible source of human pathogenic ESCs and FQs co-resistant S. Thompson. Furthermore, the results underline the important role of conjugative plasmids in acquiring and transmission of ESCs and FQs resistance in S. Thompson isolates, which need continuous investigation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Lili","Olsen, Rikke Heidemann","Xiao, Jian","Liang, Meidan","Meng, Hecheng","Peng, Shifu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415298"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangzhou Food Inspection Institute","Jiangsu Provincial Center for Disease Control and Prevention","Jinan University","South China University of Technology"],"keyword":["bla","qnrS1","ready to eat pork product"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of extended spectrum cephalosporins and fluoroquinolone resistance of a salmonella enterica serovar thompson isolate from ready to eat pork product in china","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2022.964009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-415298","identifier":[{"id":"36187962","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85139028300","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9521377","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-24aad79a-6e79-4811-82f8-5410e6117bc6"],"keyword":["Salmonella Thompson","bla","qepA8","qnrS1","ready-to-eat pork product"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-01A55070D674D2B029AF37A1DA3EB79B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/323855729/fmicb_13_964009.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2022.964009","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jinan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jinan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"guangzhou food inspection institute","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangzhou Food Inspection Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"jiangsu provincial center for disease control and prevention","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangsu Provincial Center for Disease Control and Prevention","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Lili","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rikke Heidemann","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8bc39fd7-fa38-4eb8-8c84-01b4682efd79","name":"Olsen, Rikke Heidemann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jian","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Meidan","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Meidan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Hecheng","key":"mengpau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Hecheng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Shifu","key":"pengpau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Shifu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36187962"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2022.964009","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"964009","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139028300"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-24aad79a-6e79-4811-82f8-5410e6117bc6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterization of extended-spectrum cephalosporins and fluoroquinolone resistance of a Salmonella enterica serovar Thompson isolate from ready-to-eat pork product in China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415298","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The Earth's redox evolution has been commonly assumed to have played a key role in shaping the evolutionary history of the biosphere. However, whether and how shifts in marine redox conditions are linked to key biotic events – foremost the rise of animals and the ecological expansion of eukaryotic algae in the late Proterozoic oceans – remains heavily debated. Our current picture of global marine redox evolution during this critical interval is incomplete. This is particularly the case for the Tonian Period (∼1.0 to ∼0.717 Ga), when animals may have diverged and when eukaryotic algae began their rise in ecological importance. Here, we present new uranium isotope (δ238U) measurements from Tonian carbonates to fill this outstanding gap. These Tonian carbonates (∼1000–800 Ma) record variable δ238U values, indicating temporal variation in global marine redox through this under-investigated time interval. Arguably the most interesting feature of this new δ238U dataset is an interval of anomalously negative δ238U values (<−1‰) that represent among the most negative stratigraphically continuous values reported to date. These low δ238U values are best explained by prevalent shallow-water anoxia, potentially driven by increases in productivity in a low-O2 Tonian Earth system. We thus provide compelling evidence for extensive shallow marine anoxia just prior to or coincident with Neoproterozoic ecological shifts.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Zhang, Feifei","Stockey, Richard G.","Xiao, Shuhai","Shen, Shu-zhong","Dahl, Tais W.","Wei, Guang-Yi","Cao, Mengchun","Li, Ziheng","Kang, Junyao","Cui, Ying","Anbar, Ariel D.","Planavsky, Noah J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463309"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Arizona State University","China University of Geosciences, Wuhan","Montclair State University","Nanjing University","Stanford University","Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University","Yale University"],"keyword":["Mass balance model","Ocean anoxia","Uranium isotopes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uranium isotope evidence for extensive shallow water anoxia in the early tonian oceans","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-463309","identifier":[{"id":"85125498720","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-74db84f1-aaaa-473c-949b-83e48d690ab6"],"keyword":["Tonian","early Neoproterozoic","mass balance model","ocean anoxia","rise of animals","uranium isotopes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63F04AF30C5C4605CA8A8160AFCB6591"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"virginia polytechnic institute and state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"china university of geosciences wuhan",