l.2022.117437","issn":["0012821X","1385013X"],"issn_org":["0012821X"],"journal":"Earth and Planetary Science Letters","paperid":"117437","status":"p","title":"Earth and Planetary Science Letters","volume":"583"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125498720"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-74db84f1-aaaa-473c-949b-83e48d690ab6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uranium isotope evidence for extensive shallow water anoxia in the early Tonian oceans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463309","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Blood lipids are heritable modifiable causal factors for coronary artery disease. Despite well-described monogenic and polygenic bases of dyslipidemia, limitations remain in discovery of lipid-associated alleles using whole genome sequencing (WGS), partly due to limited sample sizes, ancestral diversity, and interpretation of clinical significance. Among 66,329 ancestrally diverse (56% non-European) participants, we associate 428M variants from deep-coverage WGS with lipid levels; ~400M variants were not assessed in prior lipids genetic analyses. We find multiple lipid-related genes strongly associated with blood lipids through analysis of common and rare coding variants. We discover several associated rare non-coding variants, largely at Mendelian lipid genes. Notably, we observe rare LDLR intronic variants associated with markedly increased LDL-C, similar to rare LDLR exonic variants. In conclusion, we conducted a systematic whole genome scan for blood lipids expanding the alleles linked to lipids for multiple ancestries and characterize a clinically-relevant rare non-coding variant model for lipids.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Selvaraj, Margaret Sunitha","Li, Xihao","Li, Zilin","Pampana, Akhil","Zhang, David Y.","Park, Joseph","Aslibekyan, Stella","Bis, Joshua C.","Brody, Jennifer A.","Cade, Brian E.","Chuang, Lee Ming","Chung, Ren Hua","Curran, Joanne E.","de las Fuentes, Lisa","de Vries, Paul S.","Duggirala, Ravindranath","Freedman, Barry I.","Graff, Mariaelisa","Guo, Xiuqing","Heard-Costa, Nancy","Hidalgo, Bertha","Hwu, Chii Min","Irvin, Marguerite R.","Kelly, Tanika N.","Kral, Brian G.","Lange, Leslie","Li, Xiaohui","Lisa, Martin","Lubitz, Steven A.","Manichaikul, Ani W.","Michael, Preuss","Montasser, May E.","Morrison, Alanna C.","Naseri, Take","O’Connell, Jeffrey R.","Palmer, Nicholette D.","Peyser, Patricia A.","Reupena, Muagututia S.","Smith, Jennifer A.","Sun, Xiao","Taylor, Kent D.","Tracy, Russell P.","Tsai, Michael Y.","Wang, Zhe","Wang, Yuxuan","Loos, Ruth J.F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504421"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["NHLBI Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine (TOPMed) Consortium"],"country":["Samoa","Taiwan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston University","George Washington University","Harvard University","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Johns Hopkins University","Lutia i Puava ae Mapu i Fagalele","Ministry of Health","National Health Research Institutes Taiwan","National Taiwan University","Tulane University","University of Alabama at Birmingham","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus","University of Maryland, Baltimore","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Minnesota Twin Cities","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Pennsylvania","University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University of Texas Rio Grande Valley","University of Vermont","University of Virginia","University of Washington","Veterans General Hospital-Taipei","Wake Forest University","Washington University St. Louis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"whole genome sequence analysis of blood lipid levels in gt 000000000066 000000000000 individuals","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-33510-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-504421","identifier":[{"id":"000866124200006","type":"wos"},{"id":"36220816","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9553944","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139608936","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b9efa3a8-7c99-40c2-8b25-def7