{"abstract":"Topological systems are inherently robust to disorder and continuous perturbations, resulting in dissipation-free edge transport of electrons in quantum solids, or reflectionless guiding of photons and phonons in classical wave systems characterized by topological invariants. Realization of robust, lossless topological insulators in the technologically important terahertz (THz) frequency range has drawn immense attention. In this paper, we propose a Kagome lattice structure that supports topological edge states with valley-dependent transport. Optical topological insulators are subsequently fabricated, in which mirror symmetry is broken and degenerate states are lifted at K(K′) valleys in the band structure. Theoretical and numerical analyses show that four types of edge states can be obtained. The performance of the fabricated topological waveguides is characterized with THz time-domain spectroscopy (TDS). Nearly identical THz wave transmission in the 0.437-0.453-THz range is verified with a straight-line topological waveguide and Z-shaped waveguides with multiple sharp turning corners, which quantitatively illustrate the strong backscattering suppression effects from the nontrivial topology edge states of the structures. Particularly, the THz TDS measurements provide important extra time-domain information about the topological waveguiding mode, which is generally unavailable from previous topological insulator investigations solely replying on power spectrum measurements.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Shen, Yun","Ji, Jie","Li, Hui Chang","Zhang, Le","Yu, Xin","Yan, Shu Bin","Rasmussen, Mattias","Shen, Qian","Madhi, Daena","Zhou, Binbin","Jepsen, Peter Uhd","Deng, Xiao Hua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341774"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Jiliang University","Nanchang University","Zhejiang University of Water Resources and Electric Power"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"realization of photonic topological insulators at terahertz frequencies characterized by time domain spectroscopy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.18.064025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-341774","identifier":[{"id":"85143676746","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7caed306-51fe-4193-9370-ddce0e5070eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-664613A518107C0FA8AFED71105C6089"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/301869721/PhysRevApplied.18.064025_Realization_of_photonic_topological_insulators_at_terahertz_frequencies_characterized_by_time_domain_spectroscopy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.18.064025","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanchang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanchang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Nanomaterials and Devices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"china jiliang university","loc":["China",