{"author_count":8,"contributors":["Chen, Yifan","Li, Chunlong","Mizuno, Yosuke","Shu, Jing","Xue, Xiao","Yuan, Qiang","Zhao, Yue","Zhou, Zihan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-427994"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"birefringence tomography for axion cloud","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2208.05724.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-427994","identifier":[{"id":"85139745172","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3a0c0c5b-03f0-4569-be98-4facd94e1201"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8B76884C524DAEA5955EC455F123E8B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2208.05724.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Theoretical high energy, astroparticle and gravitational physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yifan","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"d2bd98dd-d64a-4a2a-bc7f-7682ef4b7e91","name":"Chen, Yifan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Chunlong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Chunlong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yosuke","key":"mizunopau","last":"Mizuno","name":"Mizuno, Yosuke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jing","key":"shupau","last":"Shu","name":"Shu, Jing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao","key":"xuepau","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Xiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qiang","key":"yuanpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Qiang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yue","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Yue","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zihan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Zihan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1475-7516/2022/09/073","issn":["14757516"],"issue":"09","journal":"Journal of Cosmology and Astroparticle Physics","paperid":"073","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cosmology and Astroparticle Physics","volume":"2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139745172"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3a0c0c5b-03f0-4569-be98-4facd94e1201"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Birefringence tomography for axion cloud","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-427994","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Lorises are a group of globally threatened strepsirrhine primates that exhibit many unusual physiological and behavioral features, including a low metabolic rate, slow movement, and hibernation. Here, we assembled a chromosome-level genome sequence of the pygmy loris (Xanthonycticebus pygmaeus) and resequenced whole genomes from 50 pygmy lorises and 6 Bengal slow lorises (Nycticebus bengalensis). We found that many gene families involved in detoxification have been specifically expanded in the pygmy loris, including the GSTA gene family, with many newly derived copies functioning specifically in the liver. We detected many genes displaying evolutionary convergence between pygmy loris and koala, including PITRM1. Significant decreases in PITRM1 enzymatic activity in these two species may have contributed to their characteristic low rate of metabolism. We also detected many evolutionarily convergent genes and positively selected genes in the pygmy loris that are involved in muscle development. Functional assays demonstrated the decreased ability of one positively selected gene, MYOF, to up-regulate the fast-type muscle fiber, consistent with the lower proportion of fast-twitch muscle fibers in the pygmy loris. The protein product of another positively selected gene in the pygmy loris, PER2, exhibited weaker binding to the key circadian core protein CRY, a finding that may be related to this species’ unusual circadian rhythm. Finally, population genomics analysis revealed that these two extant loris species, which coexist in the same habitat, have exhibited an inverse relationship in terms of their demography over the past 1 million years, implying strong interspecies competition after speciation.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Li, Ming Li","Wang, Sheng","Xu, Penghui","Tian, Hang Yu","Bai, Mixue","Zhang, Ya Ping","Shao, Yong","Xiong, Zi Jun","Qi, Xiao Guang","Cooper, David N.","Zhang, Guojie","Zhu, He Helen","Wu, Dong Dong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-429009"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Kunming Institute of Zoology","Cardiff University","China National GeneBank","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Northwest University China","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Zhengzhou University"],"keyword":["Adaptive evolution","Demographic history"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional genomics analysis reveals the evolutionary adaptation and demographic history of pygmy lorises","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2123030119","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-429009","identifier":[{"id":"36161902","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138661207","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9546566","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-3b98c302-682d-4df4-9058-4900d7574c71"],"keyword":["adaptive evolution","demographic history","slow lorises"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE48FF179AEE212F74F18EAD499989E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2123030119","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/329193254/pnas.2123030119.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhengzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhengzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"cas kunming institute of zoology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Kunming Institute of Zoology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"northwest university china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwest University China","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"cardiff university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Cardiff University","used":1},{"affno":"8","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"cn","key":"china national genebank","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China National GeneBank","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ming Li","key":"liminglipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ming Li","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sheng","key":"wangshengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Sheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Penghui","key":"xupenghuipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Penghui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Hang Yu","key":"tianhangyupau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Hang Yu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mixue","key":"baimixuepau","last":"Bai","name":"Bai, Mixue","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","first":"Ya Ping","key":"z