{"abstract":"Antibiotic resistance genes (ARGs) are emerging environmental contaminants posing a threat to public health. Intensive swine farms are recognized as hotspots for antibiotic resistance genes (ARGs). However, antibiotic resistome and their genetic contexts, hosts, and transferability in Chinese swine farms remain largely unexplored. Here, we used Illumina and Oxford Nanopore metagenomics sequencing to investigate the antibiotic resistome context of 14 distantly located large-scale (10,000 animals per year) commercial swine farms in China. We identified high abundant and diverse ARGs (609,966.8 with 1433 types, belonging to 38 different antibiotic classes) in all samples, including those encoding resistance to clinically critical important antibiotics (such as mcr, tetX, optrA, poxtA, qnr and blaCTX-M). About 75% of the ARGs detected were carried by mobile genetic elements (mainly plasmids), suggesting their high transmission potential into receiving environments. Host-tracking analysis identified Clostridiales, Faecalibacterium prausnitzii and Escherichia coli as the predominant bacterial hosts of mobile ARGs. Notably, genome binning generated 246 high-completeness draft genomes. Genetic context analysis of the multiple resistant (MDR) genes in binned genomes showed the involvement of insertion sequences (ISs), integron and SGI2 genomic island, implying their importance role in promoting the development of MDR bacteria. Overall, these findings substantially expand our current knowledge of mobile antibiotic resistome in Chinese swine farms, and suggest reasonable management of animal wastes in swine farms to reduce the dissemination of antibiotic resistance to the environment.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Lili","Xiao, Yawen","Olsen, Rikke Heidemann","Wang, Chong","Meng, Hecheng","Shi, Lei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453118"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jinan University","Shandong New Hope Liuhe Group Ltd","South China University of Technology"],"keyword":["Illumina sequencing","Nanopore sequencing","Resistome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short and long read metagenomics insight into the genetic contexts and hosts of mobile antibiotic resistome in chinese swine farms","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-453118","identifier":[{"id":"35259381","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85126052677","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-63d10ad5-e53a-4c40-982f-60875b7e6824"],"keyword":["Genetic context","Host-tracking","Illumina sequencing","Nanopore sequencing","Resistome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-985C2FD94D2EABEC791642D5076ECDDE"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jinan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jinan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shandong new hope liuhe group ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong New Hope Liuhe Group Ltd","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Lili","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yawen","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Yawen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rikke Heidemann","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8bc39fd7-fa38-4eb8-8c84-01b4682efd79","name":"Olsen, Rikke Heidemann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Chong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Chong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Hecheng","key":"mengpau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Hecheng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lei","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Lei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35259381"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2022.154352","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"154352","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"827"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126052677"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-63d10ad5-e53a-4c40-982f-60875b7e6824"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Short- and long-read metagenomics insight into the genetic contexts and hosts of mobile antibiotic resistome in Chinese swine farms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453118","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"There have been rare reports about the structure/composition of polymers in blueberry skin and their changes during fermentation for wine production. In this study, the compositional changes occurring in blueberry skin during fermentation were tracked by a combination of cell wall analysis techniques including infra-red spectroscopy, monosaccharide analysis, and comprehensive microarray polymer profiling (CoMPP). The cross-corroborating data revealed that blueberry skin cell wall is particularly rich in xyloglucan. Chemical fractionation analysis indicated that the KOH soluble fraction is a dominant fraction in fermented blueberry skin. Interestingly, the KOH soluble fraction contained abundant epitopes associated with pectin branch chains, indicating tight binding of some enzyme-resistant pectin polymers to hemicellulose. This study provides important implications for the development of effective strategies to extract beneficial substances (such as aromatics, tannins and pigments) from berry tissues during processing.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Nawei","Gao, Yu","Fan, Gang","Zhong, Wu","Chen, Xuanxuan","Guo, Xiao","Hansen, Jeanett","Jørgensen, Bodil","Li, Erhu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-480254"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huazhong Agricultural University","Ningxia University","Wuhan Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["Cell wall","Hemicellulose","Pectin","Polysaccharide","Winemaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"combined high throughput and fractionation approaches reveal changes of polysaccharides in blueberry skin cell walls during fermentation for wine production","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-480254","identifier":[{"id":"000869491100002","type":"wos"},{"id":"36461247","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85139590984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9145c5a4-095e-4929-a08d-18002a7ad57d"],"keyword":["Blueberry skin","Cell wall","Hemicellulose","Pectin","Polysaccharide","Winemaking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C49AF34E518A575B9F8D99F19114F253"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"huazhong agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"ningxia university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ningxia University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"wuhan polytechnic university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan Polytechnic University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nawei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Nawei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yu","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Yu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gang","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Gang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Wu","key":"zhongpau","last":"Zhong","name":"Zhong, Wu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xuanxuan","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xuanxuan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jeanett","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"7f3f1db5-811b-43f4-98e6-ddf304013d1d","name":"Hansen, Jeanett","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Bodil","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ab0f85f4-70e2-443b-bdde-331840596eea","name":"Jørgensen, Bodil","orcid":"0000-0002-0453-1277","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erhu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Erhu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36461247"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.foodres.2022.112027","issn":["09639969","18737145"],"issn_org":["09639969"],"issue":"Part A","journal":"Food Research International","paperid":"112027","status":"p","title":"Food Research International","volume":"162"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139590984"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9145c5a4-095e-4929-a08d-18002a7ad57d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Combined high-throughput and fractionation approaches reveal changes of polysaccharides in blueberry skin cell walls during fermentation for wine production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-480254","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Alcohol consumption is thought to be one of the modifiable risk factors for colorectal cancer (CRC). However, the causality and mechanisms by which alcohol exerts its carcinogenic effect are unclear. We evaluated the association between alcohol consumption and CRC risk by analyzing data from 32 cohort studies and conducted two-sample Mendelian randomization (MR) analysis to examine for casual relationship. To explore the effect of alcohol related DNA methylation on CRC risk, we performed an epigenetic MR analysis with data from an epigenome-wide association study (EWAS). We additionally performed gene-alcohol interaction analysis nested in the UK Biobank to assess effect modification between alcohol consumption and susceptibility genes. We discovered distinct effects of alcohol on CRC incidence and mortality from the meta-analyses, and genetic predisposition to alcohol drinking was causally associated with an increased CRC risk (OR = 1.79, 95% CI: 1.23-2.61) using two-sample MR approaches. In epigenetic MR analysis, two alcohol-related CpG sites (cg05593667 and cg10045354 mapped to COLCA1/COLCA2 gene) were identified causally associated with an increased CRC risk (P < 8.20 × 10−4). Gene-alcohol interaction analysis revealed that carriage of the risk allele of the eQTL (rs3087967) and mQTL (rs11213823) polymorphism of COLCA1/COLCA2 would interact with alcohol consumption to increase CRC risk (PInteraction =.027 and PInteraction =.016). Our study provides comprehensive evidence to elucidate the role of alcohol in CRC and highlights that the pathogenic effect of alcohol on CRC could be partly attributed to DNA methylation by regulating the expression of COLCA1/COLCA2 gene.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Zhou, Xuan","Wang, Lijuan","Xiao, Jiarui","Sun, Jing","Yu, Lili","Zhang, Han","Meng, Xiangrui","Yuan, Shuai","Timofeeva, Maria","Law, Philip J.","Houlston, Richard S.","Ding, Kefeng","Dunlop, Malcolm G.","Theodoratou, Evropi","Li, Xue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-623142"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Xue"],"country":["China","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","College of Information Science and Electronic Engineering, Zhejiang University","Institute for Global Health","Institute of Cancer Research","Karolinska Institute","The University of Edinburgh","Zhengzhou University"],"keyword":["Alcohol","Alcohol Drinking epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Colorectal Neoplasms epidemiology","Colorectal cancer","DNA methylation","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Mendelian Randomization Analysis methods","Mendelian randomization","Neoplasm Proteins genetics","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alcohol consumption dna methylation and colorectal cancer risk results from pooled cohort studies and mendelian randomization analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.33945","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Our study was conducted using CRC summary statistics form 12 previous CRC GWASs and individual data from the UK Biobank (application number 66345). The authors thank all the participants, institutions and their staff for providing data. Xue Li is supported by the Natural Science Fund for Distinguished Young Scholars of Zhejiang Province (LR22H260001). Evropi Theodoratou is supported by a CRUK Career Development Fellowship (C31250/A22804). The work is supported by Programme Grant funding from Cancer Research UK (C348/A12076) and by funding for the infrastructure and staffing of the Edinburgh CRUK Cancer Research Centre. This work is also funded by a grant to Malcolm G. Dunlop as Project Leader with the MRC Human Genetics Unit Centre Grant (U127527198). CRUK Career Development Fellowship, Grant/Award Number: C31250/A22804; Natural Science Fund for Distinguished Young Scholars of Zhejiang Province, Grant/Award Number: LR22H260001; Project Leader with the MRC Human Genetics Unit Centre Grant, Grant/Award Number: U127527198; Edinburgh CRUK Cancer Research Centre; Programme Grant funding from Cancer Research UK, Grant/Award Number: C348/A12076 Funding information"],"id":"S01-000.00-623142","identifier":[{"id":"35102554","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9487984","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85124159178","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ae45dbe8-d04c-4ebc-a751-e1974982e1c9"],"keyword":["Alcohol Drinking/epidemiology","Cohort Studies","Colorectal Neoplasms/epidemiology","DNA methylation","Genome-Wide Association Study","Humans","Mendelian Randomization Analysis/methods","Mendelian randomization","Neoplasm Proteins/genetics","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","alcohol","colorectal cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA4A0E89456F784F46E0FF29401AA258"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/198862680/Zhou_2022_Alcohol_consumption_dna_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.33945","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"college of information science and electronic engineering zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"College of Information Science and Electronic Engineering, Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhengzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhengzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"institute for global health","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute for Global Health","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institute","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Danish Institute for Advanced Study","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Epidemiology, Biostatistics and Biodemography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"the university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"institute of cancer research","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Institute of Cancer Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xuan","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Xuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lijuan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Lijuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiarui","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jiarui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Jing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lili","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Lili","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Han","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Han","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","correspo