{"abstract":"Electroactive biofilms (EABs) play an important role in bioelectrochemical systems due to their abilities to generate electrons and perform extracellular electron transfer (EET). Here, we investigated the effects of quorum sensing (QS) signals on power output, chlortetracycline degradation, and structure of EABs in MFCs treating antibiotic wastewater. The voltage output of MFCs with C4-HSL and PQS increased by 21.57% and 13.73%, respectively, compared with that without QS signals. The chlortetracycline degradation efficiency in closed-circuit MFCs with C4-HSL and PQS increased by 56.53% and 50.04%, respectively, which resulted from the thicker biofilms, higher biomass, and stronger activities. Additionally, QS signals induced the heterogeneous distribution of EPS for a balance between self-protection and EET under environmental pressure. Geobacter prevailed by the addition of QS signals to resist high chlortetracycline concentration. Our results provided a broader understanding on regulating EABs within electrode interface to improve their performance for environmental remediation and clean energy development.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Cheng, Xiao-Long","Xu, Qiang","Sun, Jia-Dong","Li, Chun-Rui","Yang, Qian-Wen","Li, Biao","Zhang, Xue-Ying","Zhou, Jun","Yong, Xiao-Yu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324709"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Yong, Xiao-Yu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing Tech University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quorum sensing signals improve the power performance and chlortetracycline degradation efficiency of mixed culture electroactive biofilms","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2022.104299","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324709","identifier":[{"id":"35573194","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129745771","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9097700","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-43b8943e-9a69-4796-98be-09cd2743db69"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B43BEDD4001D9AA2D5E7379D0676E111"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/276379796/1_s2.0_S2589004222005697_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2022.104299","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing tech university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Tech University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Water Technology & Processes"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Long","key":"chengxiaolongpau","last":"Cheng","name":"Cheng, Xiao-Long","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiang","key":"xuqiangpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Qiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia-Dong","key":"sunjiadongpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Jia-Dong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chun-Rui","key":"lichunruipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Chun-Rui","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian-Wen","key":"yangqianwenpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Qian-Wen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Biao","key":"libiaopau","last":"Li","locid":"906c1985-9a04-443f-9b60-db5831bf520e","name":"Li, Biao","orcid":"0000-0002-7359-3690","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xue-Ying","key":"zhangxueyingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xue-Ying","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun","key":"zhoujunpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Jun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Yu","key":"yongxiaoyupau","last":"Yong","name":"Yong, Xiao-Yu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35573194"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.isci.2022.104299","issn":["25890042"],"issue":"5","journal":"iScience","paperid":"104299","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"iScience","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129745771"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-43b8943e-9a69-4796-98be-09cd2743db69"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Quorum sensing signals improve the power performance and chlortetracycline degradation efficiency of mixed-culture electroactive biofilms","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324709","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The urea oxidization reaction (UOR) is an important anodic reaction in electro-catalytic energy conversion. However, the sluggish reaction kinetics and complex catalyst transformation in electrocatalysis require activity improvement and better mechanistic understanding of the state-of-the-art Ni(OH)2 catalyst. Herein, by utilizing low-temperature argon (Ar) plasma processing, tooth-wheel Ni(OH)2 nanosheets self-supported on Ni foam (Ni(OH)2-Ar) are demonstrated to have improved UOR activity compared to conventional Ni(OH)2. The theoretical assessment confirms that the edge has a smaller cation vacancy formation energy than the basal plane, consequently explaining the structural formation. Operando and quasi-operando methods are employed to investigate the dynamic evolution of the Ni(OH)2 film in UOR. The crucial dehydrogenation products of Ni(OH)5O- intermediates are identified to be stable on the etched edge and explain the enhanced UOR in the low potential region. In addition, the dynamic active sites are monitored to elucidate the reaction mechanism in different potential ranges.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Li, Dan","Zhang, Yuefeng","Zhou, Xiaomin","Huang, Chao","Wen, Ying","Liu, Liangliang","Li, Qingwei","Xu, Yue","Wu, Yuzheng","Ruan, Qingdong","Ma, Yinghe","Xiong, Fangyu","Xiao, Dezhi","Liu, Pei","Wang, Guomin","Mehrjou, Babak","Wang, Bin","Li, Hao","Chen, Rongsheng","Ni, Hongwei","Zeng, Zhiyuan","Chu, Paul K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335571"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Chu, Paul K.","Ni, Hongwei","Zeng, Zhiyuan"],"country":["China","Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City University of Hong Kong","Wuhan University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Active site","Dehydrogenation","Plasma processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamic active sites on plasma engraved ni hydroxide for enhanced electro catalytic urea oxidation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85129534911","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335571","identifier":[{"id":"85129534911","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-67cdec87-be05-4bb7-bebb-da5fe9f6a706"],"keyword":["Active site","Dehydrogenation","Ni hydroxide","Plasma processing","Urea oxidization reaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BE1C048B7DCD487ED2E31CC1FEB65334"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"hk","key":"city university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"City University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"wuhan university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Catalysis Theory Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"lidanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Dan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuefeng","key":"zhangyuefengpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yuefeng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaomin","ke