 Kai","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/en15010389","issn":["19961073"],"issue":"1","journal":"Energies","paperid":"389","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Energies","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122242879"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6e22b879-7c81-4046-b174-59335b58c10f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"OC6 Phase Ia: CFD Simulations of the Free-Decay Motion of the DeepCwind Semisubmersible","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-337488","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Biomass ashes are frequently known for their limiting effects in thermochemical conversion processes. Thus, a comprehensive understanding and prediction of the temperature-depending behavior of the ashes is indispensable for practical applications. In the present study, the flow behavior of low-temperature ash (LTA) and high-temperature ash (HTA) of biomass is investigated in detail and monitored by in situ methods. For this purpose, the mineral matter formation and transformation of both ashes are studied by X-ray diffraction (XRD) and X-ray fluorescence (XRF) analysis. A combination of heating-stage microscope and scanning electron microscope equipped with energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (SEM-EDX) has enabled a systematic identification of the microstructures and observations of LTA and HTA. The results have illustrated an associated release of K and Cl and the formation of new mineral phases in the remaining material during ashing at increased temperature. Both ashes have exhibited flow temperatures below 1100 °C and a rarely observed behavior of higher characteristic temperatures for LTA than for HTA is detected. From the heating-stage microscopy, the ashes have given evidence to a significant formation of slag at the characteristic temperatures and a viscosity-driven behavior at the characteristic points of ash fusion. Based on these results, a conclusion can be drawn regarding the usability of this biomass for high-temperature conversion processes on the industrial scale.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Li, Jiazhu","Wei, Juntao","Reinmöller, Markus","Liang, Chen","Li, Shuangshuang","Xiao, Ruirui","Xu, Jie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349294"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wei, Juntao","Xu, Jie"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing Forestry University","Qingdao Agricultural University","Zaozhuang University"],"keyword":["Ashing temperature","Biomass"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative observation of the flow behavior of low and high temperature ashes of biomass","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134350862","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-349294","identifier":[{"id":"85134350862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-95f9ab25-1c31-4725-b499-924f97e75f22"],"keyword":["Ash fusion test","Ashing temperature","Biomass","Heating-stage microscope","Mineral phase transformation","Thermochemical calculations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B585C0410BCE919C5EE764B7DAAA63D"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"qingdao agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"nanjing forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Mechanical Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"zaozhuang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zaozhuang University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiazhu","key":"lijiazhupau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jiazhu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Juntao","key":"weijuntaopau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Juntao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Markus","key":"reinmöllermarkuspau","last":"Reinmöller","locid":"9fc74702-5e52-4db1-843f-9e9a2708fb6c","name":"Reinmöller, Markus","orcid":"0000-0001-8188-5469","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chen","key":"liangchenpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Chen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuangshuang","key":"lishuangshuangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shuangshuang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruirui","key":"xiaoruiruipau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Ruirui","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"xujiepau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Jie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fuel.2022.125232","issn":["00162361","18737153"],"issn_org":["00162361"],"journal":"Fuel","paperid":"125232","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fuel","volume":"327"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134350862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-95f9ab25-1c31-4725-b499-924f97e75f22"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Comparative observation of the flow behavior of low- and high-temperature ashes of biomass","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-349294","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Wearable chemical sensors have recently received great attention, especially on monitoring ion concentration in sweat. However, challenges still remain, such as the nonnegligible potential deviation of the ion-selective electrode (ISE) based potentiometric sensor after multi-use. Herein, we propose an easily prepared and highly integrated wearable solid contact-ISE (SC-ISE), allowing multiple measurements with repeatable open circuit potential (OCP), which is achieved by applying a positive potential on the working electrode. It’s believed that the positive potential alters the oxidation-reduction state of the conducting polymer with a repeatable standard redox potential. The integrated SC-ISE sensor is fabricated on a printed circuit board (PCB) substrate, eliminating external hardware. Preparation of the sensor electrode adopts a standard route, i.e. employing the electroless nickel immersion gold (ENIG) process for plating gold layers. Dual working electrodes have been designed to measure either sodium or potassium ion. This wearable platform has been validated through on-body tests by monitoring ion levels in the real sweat.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Liu, Huixin","Gu, Zhen","Zhao, Qing","Li, Shuai","Ding, Xi","Xiao, Xinxin","Xiu, Guangli"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-375128"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Xinxin","Xiu, Guangli"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","East China University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Conducting polymer","Electrochemistry","Printed circuit board","Wearable sensor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"printed circuit board integrated wearable ion selective electrode with potential treatment for highly repeatable sweat monitoring","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/263885399/1_s2.0_S0925400521016701_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-375128","identifier":[{"id":"85121576447","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ebd22c1f-fffb-4f06-be5e-39311f5d8e70"],"keyword":["Conducting polymer","Electrochemistry","Printed circuit board","Solid contact ion-selective electrodes","Wearable sensor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-894D1E38000484EE96ED7A244B51BEF7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/263885399/1_s2.0_S0925400521016701_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"east china university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huixin","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Huixin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhen","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Zhen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qing","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Qing","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuai","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shuai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xi","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Xi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"8cd768ff-d2df-4d64-bd7c-0d46854d561c","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guangli","key":"xiupau","last":"Xiu","name":"Xiu, Guangli","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.snb.2021.131102","issn":["09254005","18733077"],"issn_org":["09254005"],"journal":"Sensors and Actuators B: Chemical","paperid":"131102","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Sensors and Actuators B: Chemical","volume":"355"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121576447"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ebd22c1f-fffb-4f06-be5e-39311f5d8e70"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Printed Circuit Board Integrated Wearable Ion-Selective Electrode with Potential Treatment for Highly Repeatable Sweat Monitoring","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-375128","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"To identify new susceptibility loci to lung cancer among diverse populations, we performed cross-ancestry genome-wide association studies in European, East Asian and African populations and discovered five loci that have not been previously reported. We replicated 26 signals and identified 10 new lead associations from previously reported loci. Rare-variant associations tended to be specific to populations, but even common-variant associations influencing smoking behavior, such as those with CHRNA5 and CYP2A6, showed population specificity. Fine-mapping and expression quantitative trait locus colocalization nominated several candidate variants and susceptibility genes such as IRF4 and FUBP1. DNA damage assays of prioritized genes in lung fibroblasts indicated that a subset of these genes, including the pleiotropic gene IRF4, potentially exert effects by promoting endogenous DNA damage.","author_count":85,"contributors":["Byun, Jinyoung","Han, Younghun","Li, Yafang","Xia, Jun","Long, Erping","Choi, Jiyeon","Xiao, Xiangjun","Zhu, Meng","Zhou, Wen","Sun, Ryan","Bossé, Yohan","Song, Zhuoyi","Schwartz, Ann","Lusk, Christine","Rafnar, Thorunn","Stefansson, Kari","Zhang, Tongwu","Zhao, Wei","Pettit, Rowland W.","Liu, Yanhong","Li, Xihao","Zhou, Hufeng","Walsh, Kyle M.","Gorlov, Ivan","Gorlova, Olga","Zhu, Dakai","Rosenberg, Susan M.","Pinney, Susan","Bailey-Wilson, Joan E.","Mandal, Diptasri","de Andrade, Mariza","Gaba, Colette","Willey, James C.","You, Ming","Anderson, Marshall","Wiencke, John K.","Albanes, Demetrius","Lam, Stephan","Tardon, Adonina","Chen, Chu","Goodman, Gary","Bojesen, Stig E","Brenner, Hermann","Landi, Maria Teresa","Chanock, Stephen J.","Johansson, Mattias","Muley, Thomas","Risch, Angela","Wichmann, H. Erich","Bickeböller, Heike","Christiani, David C.","Rennert, Gad","Arnold, Susanne","Field, John K.","Shete, Sanjay","Le Marchand, Loic","Melander, Olle","Brunnstrom, Hans","Liu, Geoffrey","Andrew, Angeline S.","Kiemeney, Lambertus A.","Shen, Hongbing","Zienolddiny, Shanbeh","Grankvist, Kjell","Johansson, Mikael","Caporaso, Neil","Cox, Angela","Hong, Yun Chul","Yuan, Jian Min","Lazarus, Philip","Schabath, Matthew B.","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Patel, Alpa","Lan, Qing","Rothman, Nathaniel","Taylor, Fiona","Kachuri, Linda","Witte, John S.","Sakoda, Lori C.","Spitz, Margaret","Brennan, Paul","Lin, Xihong","McKay, James","Hung, Rayjean J.","Amos, Christopher I."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472991"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada","China","France","Germany","Iceland","Israel","Netherlands","Norway","South Korea","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","American Cancer Society","Baylor College of Medicine","British Columbia Cancer Agency","Cancer Cluster Salzburg","Clalit Health Services","Dartmouth College","Duke University","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center","German Center for Lung Research","Harvard University","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Houston Methodist Hospital","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Kaiser Permanente","Laval University","Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center","Lund University","Mayo Clinic College of Medicine and Science","Nanjing Medical University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","Princess Margaret Cancer Center","Radboud University Nijmegen","Seoul National University College of Medicine","Sinai Health System","Stanford University","Swedish Medical Center","Umeå University","University of California San Francisco","University of Cincinnati","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Kentucky","University of Liverpool","University of Oviedo","University 