":"pau"},{"affno":"22","first":"James","key":"mckayjamespau","last":"McKay","name":"McKay, James","rank":83,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"48 49","first":"Rayjean J.","key":"hungrayjeanjpau","last":"Hung","name":"Hung, Rayjean J.","rank":84,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher I.","key":"amoschristopheripau","last":"Amos","name":"Amos, Christopher I.","rank":85,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35915169"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41588-022-01115-x","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"8","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"1167-1177","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135272569"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-84eba12b-9079-49c7-9785-61451a6eeda3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cross-ancestry genome-wide meta-analysis of 61,047 cases and 947,237 controls identifies new susceptibility loci contributing to lung cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472991","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Australia experienced multi-year drought and record high temperatures, and massive forest fires occurred across the southeast in 2019 and early 2020. In the fire-affected forest areas, understory and often tree canopies were burned, and in-situ observations in late 2020 reported rapid vegetation recovery, including grasses, shrubs, and tree canopies from burned-but-not-dead eucalyptus trees. Considering the strong fire resilience and resistance of eucalyptus trees and above-average rainfall in 2020, we assessed how much and how quickly vegetation structure and biomass changed from loss to post-fire and drought recovery in 2020 for all forest areas in Australia. Here, we analyzed space-borne optical, thermal, and microwave images to assess changes in the structure and function of vegetation using four vegetation indices (VIs), leaf area index (LAI), solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF), gross primary production (GPP), and aboveground biomass (AGB). We found that all eight variables show large losses in 2019, driven by fires and climate (drought and high temperature), but large gains in 2020, resulting from the high resilience of most trees to fire and rapid growth of understory vegetation under wet condition in 2020. In 2019, the forest area has an AGB loss of 0.20 Pg C, which is ~15% of the pre-fire AGB. Attribution analyses showed that both fire and climate (prior and co-occurring severe drought and record high temperatures) are responsible for the AGB loss in 2019, approximately 0.09 Pg C (fire) and 0.11 Pg C (climate), respectively. In 2020, the forest area has a total AGB gain of 0.26 Pg C, composed of 0.22 Pg C from fire-affected forest area and 0.04 Pg C from fire-unaffected forest area. Fire-adapted Eucalyptus forests and above-average annual precipitation in 2020 brought by a moderate La Niña drove the recovery of vegetation cover, productivity, and AGB. The results from this study shows the potential of multiple sensors for monitoring and assessing the impacts of fire and climate on the forest areas in Australia and their post-fire recovery.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Qin, Yuanwei","Xiao, Xiangming","Wigneron, Jean-Pierre","Ciais, Philippe","Canadell, Josep G.","Brandt, Martin","Li, Xiaojun","Fan, Lei","Wu, Xiaocui","Tang, Hao","Dubayah, Ralph","Doughty, Russell","Crowell, Sean","Zheng, Bo","Moore, Berrien"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493075"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","China","France","Singapore","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CSIRO","California Institute of Technology","INRAE","National University of Singapore","Paris-Saclay University","Southwest University","Tsinghua University","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Maryland, College Park","University of Oklahoma"],"keyword":["Carbon","Climate change","Fire","Forest","Remote sensing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"large loss and rapid recovery of vegetation cover and aboveground biomass over forest areas in australia during 000000002019 000000002020","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357504803/1_s2.0_S0034425722002012_am.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-493075","identifier":[{"id":"85130893785","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a6d6b6a4-f83c-43ab-b6a8-0ac60a31b06c"],"keyword":["Carbon","Climate change","Fire","Forest","Forest recovery","Remote sensing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59C325A87D5310A901B02B35AAB9AA67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357504803/1_s2.0_S0034425722002012_am.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"inrae","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRAE","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"paris saclay university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Saclay University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"csiro","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"CSIRO","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"southwest university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"university of illinois at urbana champaign","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"National University of Singapore","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"us","key":"university of maryland college park","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Maryland, College Park","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"california institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"California Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yuanwei","key":"qinpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Yuanwei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiangming","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xiangming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jean-Pierre","key":"wigneronpau","last":"Wigneron","name":"Wigneron, Jean-Pierre","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Philippe","key":"ciaispau","last":"Ciais","name":"Ciais, Philippe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Josep G.","key":"canadellpau","last":"Canadell","name":"Canadell, Josep G.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Martin","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"ff0528eb-4f80-444b-a7ad-2d2307f7bdc9","name":"Brandt, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-1239","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xiaojun","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaojun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Lei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Lei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Xiaocui","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xiaocui","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Hao","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Hao","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Ralph","key":"dubayahpau","last":"Dubayah","name":"Dubayah, Ralph","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Russell","key":"doughtypau","last":"Doughty","name":"Doughty, Russell","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sean","key":"crowellpau","last":"Crowell","name":"Crowell, Sean","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Bo","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Bo","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Berrien","key":"moorepau","last":"Moore","name":"Moore, Berrien","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rse.2022.113087","issn":["00344257"],"journal":"Remote Sensing of Environment","paperid":"113087","status":"p","title":"Remote Sensing of Environment","volume":"278"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130893785"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a6d6b6a4-f83c-43ab-b6a8-0ac60a31b06c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Large loss and rapid recovery of vegetation cover and aboveground biomass over forest areas in Australia during 2019–2020","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493075","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Although genome-wide association studies have been conducted to investigate genetic variation of lung tumorigenesis, little is known about gene-gene (G × G) interactions that may influence the risk of non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC). Methods: Leveraging a total of 445,221 European-descent participants from the International Lung Cancer Consortium OncoArray project, Transdisciplinary Research in Cancer of the Lung and UK Biobank, we performed a large-scale genome-wide G × G interaction study on European NSCLC risk by a series of analyses. First, we used BiForce to evaluate and rank more than 58 billion G × G interactions from 340,958 single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs). Then, the top interactions were further tested by demographically adjusted logistic regression models. Finally, we used the selected interactions to build lung cancer screening models of NSCLC, separately, for never and ever smokers. Results: With the Bonferroni correction, we identified eight statistically significant pairs of SNPs, which predominantly appeared in the 6p21.32 and 5p15.33 regions (e.g., rs521828C6orf10 and rs204999PRRT1, ORinteraction = 1.17, p = 6.57 × 10−13; rs3135369BTNL2 and rs2858859HLA-DQA1, ORinteraction = 1.17, p = 2.43 × 10−13; rs2858859HLA-DQA1 and rs9275572HLA-DQA2, ORinteraction = 1.15, p = 2.84 × 10−13; rs2853668TERT and rs62329694CLPTM1L, ORinteraction = 0.73, p = 2.70 × 10−13). Notably, even with much genetic heterogeneity across ethnicities, three pairs of SNPs in the 6p21.32 region identified from the European-ancestry population remained significant among an Asian population from the Nanjing Medical University Global Screening Array project (rs521828C6orf10 and rs204999PRRT1, ORinteraction = 1.13, p = 0.008; rs3135369BTNL2 and rs2858859HLA-DQA1, ORinteraction = 1.11, p = 5.23 × 10−4; rs3135369BTNL2 and rs9271300HLA-DQA1, ORinteraction = 0.89, p = 0.006). The interaction-empowered polygenetic risk score that integrated classical polygenetic risk score and G × G information score was remarkable in lung cancer risk stratification. Conclusions: Important G × G interactions were identified and enriched in the 5p15.33 and 6p21.32 regions, which may enhance lung cancer screening models.","author_count":51,"contributors":["Zhang, Ruyang","Shen, Sipeng","Wei, Yongyue","Zhu, Ying","Li, Yi","Chen, Jiajin","Guan, Jinxing","Pan, Zoucheng","Wang, Yuzhuo","Zhu, Meng","Xie, Junxing","Xiao, Xiangjun","Zhu, Dakai","Li, Yafang","Albanes, Demetrios","Landi, Maria Teresa","Caporaso, Neil E.","Lam, Stephen","Tardon, Adonina","Chen, Chu","Bojesen, Stig E","Johansson, Mattias","Risch, Angela","Bickeböller, Heike","Wichmann, H. Erich","Rennert, Gadi","Arnold, Susanne","Brennan, Paul","McKay, James D.","Field, John K.","Shete, Sanjay S.","Le Marchand, Loic","Liu, Geoffrey","Andrew, Angeline S.","Kiemeney, Lambertus A.","Zienolddiny-Narui, Shan","Behndig, Annelie","Johansson, Mikael","Cox, Angela","Lazarus, Philip","Schabath, Matthew B.","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Dai, Juncheng","Ma, Hongxia","Zhao, Yang","Hu, Zhibin","Hung, Rayjean J.","Amos, Christopher I.","Shen, Hongbing","Chen, Feng","Christiani, David C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-509451"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada","China","France","Germany","Israel","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","Clalit Health Services","Dartmouth College","Harvard University","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Nanjing Medical University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","Radboud University Nijmegen","Umeå University","University of British Columbia","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Kentucky","University of Liverpool","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of Oviedo","University of Salzburg","University of Sheffield","University of South Florida","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","University of Washington","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Spokane"],"keyword":["Cancer risk","GWAS","Gene gene interaction","Lung cancer","Single nucleotide polymorphism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a large scale genome wide gene gene interaction study of lung cancer susceptibility in europeans with a trans ethnic validation in asians","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtho.2022.04.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-509451","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9512697","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35500836","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85130893494","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c25544bd-1e8d-42ac-b5c3-beba6f4c629f"],"keyword":["Cancer risk","GWAS","Gene-gene interaction","Genetic screening model","Lung cancer","Single nucleotide polymorphism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-068EC0A6DECDED1081FCD1675548BDDF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/325381627/1_s2.0_S1556086422002155_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtho.2022.04.011","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nan