"first":"Zhihao","key":"wangzhihaopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Zhihao","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Runzhe","key":"jiangrunzhepau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Runzhe","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fang","key":"wangfangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Fang","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Man Lung","key":"yiumanlungpau","last":"Yiu","name":"Yiu, Man Lung","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Huan","key":"lihuanpau","last":"Li","locid":"56e132ed-e5b3-4abd-951b-790c458b3131","name":"Li, Huan","orcid":"0000-0003-0084-1662","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingji","key":"hanmingjipau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Mingji","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"liqianpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qian","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhenghai","key":"luozhenghaipau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Zhenghai","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3542929.3563503","eisbn":["9781450394147"],"pages":"158-172","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"SoCC 2022 - Proceedings of the 13th Symposium on Cloud Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143254107"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1e55156f-ed8a-45a5-b16b-44f181aaa82c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"GHive : Accelerating Analytical Query Processing in Apache Hive via CPU-GPU Heterogeneous Computing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-667079","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Renewable -based microgrid (MG) is recognized as an eco-friendly solution in the development of renewable energy (RE). Moreover, the MG energy management with high RE penetration faces complicate uncertainties due to the inaccuracy of predictions. Besides, the growing participation of electric vehicles (EVs) makes the traditional model-based methods even more infeasible. Considering uncertainties associated with RE, EVs, and electricity price, a model-free deep reinforcement learning (DRL), namely twin delayed deep deterministic policy gradient (TD3), is employed to develop an optimized control strategy to minimize operating costs and satisfy charging expectations. The energy management problem is first formulated as a Markov decision process. Then, TD3 solely relies on the limited observation to find the optimal continuous control strategy. The proposed method flexibly adjusts the operating and charging strategies of components according to RE output and electricity price. Its real-time optimized performance on three consecutive days along with electricity price is evaluated, indicating its practical potential for future application. Additionally, comparison results demonstrate that the proposed method reduces the total costs up to 15.27% and 4.24%, respectively, compared to traditional optimization and other DRL methods, which illustrates the superiority of the TD3 method on optimizing total costs of the considered MG.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zhang, Bin","Hu, Weihao","Xu, Xiao","Li, Tao","Zhang, Zhenyuan","Chen, Zhe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-667618"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Hu, Weihao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sichuan University","State Grid Corporation of China","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Deep reinforcement learning","Energy management","Microgrid","Neural network","Renewable energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physical model free intelligent energy management for a grid connected hybrid wind microturbine pv ev energy system via deep reinforcement learning approach","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85139731966&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-667618","identifier":[{"id":"85139731966","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d72a0a98-ec54-4aea-a6fc-7415bef0b561"],"keyword":["Deep reinforcement learning","Energy management","Microgrid","Neural network","Renewable energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C39E4DBB5A24C74778340128078F6933"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems and Microgrids"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"state grid corporation of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Grid Corporation of China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bin","key":"zhangbinpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"07ec7f49-3284-4217-8f38-4b06307fb789","name":"Zhang, Bin","orcid":"0000-0002-9237-8144","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Weihao","key":"huweihaopau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Weihao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"xuxiaopau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tao","key":"litaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Tao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhenyuan","key":"zhangzhenyuanpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhenyuan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"chenzhepau","last":"Chen","locid":"d823b80a-ad7f-4339-b75a-8dee8403f02a","name":"Chen, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0002-2919-4481","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.renene.2022.09.125","issn":["09601481","18790682"],"issn_org":["09601481"],"journal":"Renewable Energy","pages":"433-448","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Renewable Energy","volume":"200"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139731966"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d72a0a98-ec54-4aea-a6fc-7415bef0b561"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Physical-model-free intelligent energy management for a grid-connected hybrid wind-microturbine-PV-EV energy system via deep reinforcement learning approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-667618","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The COVID-19 pandemic has caused over 6 million deaths since 2020. To contain the spread of the virus, social distancing is one of the most simple yet effective approaches. Motivated by this, in this paper we study the problem of continuous social distance monitoring (SDM) in indoor space, in which we can monitor and predict the pairwise distances between moving objects (people) in a building in real time. SDM can also serve as the fundamental service for downstream applications, e.g., a mobile alert application that prevents its users from potential close contact with others. To facilitate the monitoring process, we propose a framework that takes the current and future uncertain locations of the objects into account, and finds the object pairs that are close to each other in a near future. We develop efficient algorithms to update the result when object locations update. We carry out experiments on both real and synthetic datasets. The results verify the efficiency and effectiveness of our proposed framework and algorithms.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Chan, Harry Kai Ho","Li, Huan","Li, Xiao","Lu, Hua"],"cuid":["S02-097.78-009536"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-09","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2022-09-05","title":"48th International Conference on Very Large Data Bases, VLDB 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"continuous social distance monitoring in indoor space","src":["aau","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85142491824&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Independent Research Fund Denmark (No. 8022-00366B). Hua Lu is the corresponding author."],"id":"S02-097.78-009536","identifier":[{"id":"85142491824","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85140967067","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c6974dae-3e87-4bc3-a483-05469b756994","ruc-180e729f-aeae-46ff-8989-f898f7cee818"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-77A93FC37AAC5D0C253DCA01C0F41075"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data Engineering, Science and Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Database and Web Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Harry Kai Ho","key":"chanharrykaihopau","last":"Chan","locid":"bc17f697-b629-4e85-a6b2-3be9a73599eb","name":"Chan, Harry Kai Ho","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Huan","key":"lihuanpau","last":"Li","locid":"56e132ed-e5b3-4abd-951b-790c458b3131","name":"Li, Huan","orcid":"0000-0003-0084-1662","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Xiao","key":"lixiaopau","last":"Li","locid":"8b86b24d-5f2f-42ea-84c1-ce252da514d9","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hua","key":"luhuapau","last":"Lu","locid":"ae6c8b81-94a6-4f10-b1b8-a8a1022c3746","name":"Lu, Hua","orcid":"0000-0003-1199-6678","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.14778/3523210.3523217","issn":["21508097"],"issue":"7","journal":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","pages":"1390-1402","publisher":"Very Large Data Base Endowment Inc.","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140967067","2-s2.0-85142491824"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c6974dae-3e87-4bc3-a483-05469b756994","ruc-180e729f-aeae-46ff-8989-f898f7cee818"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Continuous Social Distance Monitoring in Indoor Space","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.78-009536","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Nonoptimal gestational durations could be associated with neurodevelopmental disabilities, yet evidence regarding finer classification of gestational age and rates of multiple major neuropsychiatric disorders beyond childhood is limited.To comprehensively evaluate associations between 6 gestational age groups and rates of 9 major types and 8 subtypes of childhood and adult-onset neuropsychiatric disorders.This cohort study evaluated data from a nationwide register of singleton births in Denmark from January 1, 1978, to December 31, 2016. Data analyses were conducted from October 1, 2019, through November 15, 2020.Gestational age subgroups were classified according to data from the Danish Medical Birth Register: very preterm (20-31 completed weeks), moderately preterm (32-33 completed weeks), late preterm (34-36 completed weeks), early term (37-38 completed weeks), term (39-40 completed weeks, reference), and late or postterm (41-45 completed weeks).Neuropsychiatric diagnostic records (International Statistical Classification of Diseases and Related Health Problems, Tenth Revision codes F00-F99) were ascertained from the Danish Psychiatric Central Register up to August 10, 2017. Poisson regression was used to estimate the incidence rate ratio (IRR) and 95\\ adjusting for selected sociodemographic factors.Of all 2 327 639 singleton births studied (1 194 925 male newborns [51.3\\), 22 647 (1.0\\ were born very preterm, 19 801 (0.9\\ were born moderately preterm, 99 488 (4.3\\ were born late preterm, 388 416 (16.7\\ were born early term, 1 198 605 (51.5\\ were born at term, and 598 682 (25.7\\ were born late or postterm. A gradient of decreasing IRRs was found from very preterm to late preterm for having any or each of the 9 neuropsychiatric disorders (eg, very preterm: IRR, 1.49 [95\\ 1.43-1.55]; moderately preterm: IRR, 1.23 [95\\ 1.18-1.28]; late preterm: IRR, 1.17 [95\\ 1.14-1.19] for any disorders) compared with term births. Individuals born early term had 7\\IRR, 1.07 [95\\ 1.06-1.08]) for any neuropsychiatric diagnosis and a 31\\IRR, 1.31 [95\\ 1.25-1.37]) compared with those born at term. The late or postterm group had lower IRRs for most disorders, except pervasive developmental disorders, for which the rate was higher for postterm births compared with term births (IRR, 1.06 [95\\ 1.03-1.09]).Higher incidences of all major neuropsychiatric disorders were observed across the spectrum of preterm births. Early term and late or postterm births might not share a homogeneous low risk with individuals born at term. These findings suggest that interventions that address perinatal factors associated with nonoptimal gestation might reduce long-term neuropsychiatric risks in the population.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Xia, Yuntian","Xiao, Jingyuan","Yu, Yongfu","Tseng, Wan-Ling","Lebowitz, Eli","DeWan, Andrew Thomas","Pedersen, Lars Henning","Olsen, Jørn","Li, Jiong","Liew, Zeyan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-146873"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Liew, Zeyan"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fudan University","Yale University"],"keyword":["Autism spectrum disorders","Epidemiology","Outcomes","POSTTERM BIRTH","Preeclampsia","Pregnancy","Preterm birth","Risk Factors","Stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rates of neuropsychiatric disorders and gestational age at birth in a danish population","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2021.14913","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-146873","identifier":[{"id":"34185070","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000669052200003","type":"wos"},{"id":"85108873828","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8243234","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-1e9fd967-0e4c-418b-b3d1-8aa900b551e0"],"keyword":["AUTISM SPECTRUM DISORDERS","EPIDEMIOLOGY","NEURODEVELOPMENTAL CONSEQUENCES","OUTCOMES","POSTTERM BIRTH","PREECLAMPSIA","PREGNANCY","PRETERM BIRTH","RISK-FACTORS","STRESS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0A55B1B8DC03DE433418F4019FAE0BC0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2021.14913","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"yale university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yale University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"fudan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fudan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuntian","key":"xiapau","last":"Xia","name":"Xia, Yuntian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingyuan","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jingyuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongfu","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","locid":"06be533f-163e-454d-bd55-9219a4f5cafa","name":"Yu, Yongfu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wan-Ling","key":"tsengpau","last":"Tseng","name":"Tseng, Wan-Ling","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eli","key":"lebowitzpau","last":"Lebowitz","name":"Lebowitz, Eli","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew Thomas","key":"dewanpau","last":"DeWan","name":"DeWan, Andrew Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Henning","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"2057ad48-88eb-439f-87ab-11512c937236","name":"Pedersen, Lars Henning","orcid":"0000-0001-6726-1991","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørn","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"48e09bb0-9b9d-40c8-ab2c-ff256ae11f0f","name":"Olsen, Jørn","orcid":"0000-0001-7462-5140","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"304b9c99-9102-4963-8342-05aae67a5685","name":"Li, Jiong","orcid":"0000-0003-1125-026X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zeyan","key":"liewpau","last":"Liew","locid":"b8824aad-9513-449c-9f80-a99fe58b78d1","name":"Liew, Zeyan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34185070"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2021.14913","issn":["25743805"],"issue":"6","journal":"JAMA network open","paperid":"e2114913","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA network open","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108873828"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1e9fd967-0e4c-418b-b3d1-8aa900b551e0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Rates of Neuropsychiatric Disorders and Gestational Age at Birth in a Danish Population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-146873","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"To achieve the goals of the post-2020 global biodiversity framework, we must identify representative targets that effectively protect biodiversity and can be implemented at a national level. We developed a framework to identify synergies between biodiversity and carbon across the Asian region and proposed a stepwise approach based on scalable priorities at regional, biome, and national levels that can complement potential Convention on Biological Diversity targets of protecting 30% land in the post-2020 global biodiversity framework. Our targets show that 30% of Asian land could effectively protect over 70% of all assessed species relative to only 11% now (based on analysis of 8932 terrestrial vertebrates), in addition to 2.3 to 3.6 hundred billion metric tons of carbon. Funding mechanisms are needed to ensure such targets to support biodiversity-carbon mutually beneficial solutions at the national level while reflecting broader priorities, especially in hyperdiverse countries where priorities exceed 30% of land.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Zhu, Li","Hughes, Alice C.","Zhao, Xiao Qian","Zhou, Li Jing","Ma, Ke Ping","Shen, Xiao Li","Li, Sheng","Liu, Ming Zhang","Xu, Wubing","Watson, James E.M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-214507"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Ma, Ke Ping"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Botany","CAS - Xishuangbanna Tropical Botanical Garden","Peking University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Queensland","Wildlife Conservation Society"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regional scalable priorities for national biodiversity and carbon conservation planning in asia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.abe4261","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-214507","identifier":[{"id":"34446433","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85113594338","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8388611","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-9572b356-5825-4c6b-9048-77ed174374e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-916AD207E03DD3D2F053BE78DA2AB767"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.abe4261","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas institute of botany","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Institute of Botany","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"cas xishuangbanna tropical botanical garden","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Xishuangbanna Tropical Botanical Garden","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"peking university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Peking University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Center for Biodiversity Dynamics in a Changing World","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Ecoinformatics and Biodiversity","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"au","key":"university of queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Queensland","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"wildlife conservation society","name":"Wildlife Conservation Society","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Li","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alice C.","key":"hughespau","last":"Hughes","name":"Hughes, Alice C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Qian","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Xiao Qian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Li Jing","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Li Jing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke Ping","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Ke Ping","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Li","key":"shenpau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Xiao Li","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheng","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Sheng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ming Zhang","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Ming Zhang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Wu Bing","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"eaa77a53-fbdc-49a3-9877-fd8a9bc51751","name":"Xu, Wubing","name_org":"Xu, Wu Bing","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"James E.M.","key":"watsonpau","last":"Watson","name":"Watson, James E.M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34446433"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1126/sciadv.abe4261","issn":["23752548"],"issue":"35","journal":"Science Advances","paperid":"eabe4261","publisher":"American Association for the Advancement of Science","status":"p","title":"Science Advances","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113594338"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9572b356-5825-4c6b-9048-77ed174374e1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Regional scalable priorities for national biodiversity and carbon conservation planning in Asia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-214507","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Transition metal phosphides are promising oxygen evolution reaction (OER) catalysts due to their earth-abundant and cost-effective features. Here, nanostructured CoP nanoparticles locked in hollow nitrogen doped carbon frameworks (CoP@HNC) were successfully designed and characterized for their morphology, composition, and electrochemistry. In a typical low-temperature phosphorization process, the Co species in carbonized poly-dopamine (PDA) coated ZIF-67 are converted to either hollow CoP or small-sized solid CoP nanoparticles governed by the nanoscale Kirkendall effect. The PDA layers derived nitrogen-doped carbon components feature a hollow polyhedral structure, with CoP nanoparticles imbedded in the shell. CoP@HNC demonstrates a low overpotential of 327 mV for 10 mA cm-2 and a good operational stability (72 h) for alkaline OER. The HNC encapsulation affords the low electronic resistance between CoP nanoparticles, as well as the mechanical and chemical stability of composites by preventing the aggregation of CoP nanoparticles during the OER process.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Huang, Wei","Tang, Jing","Diao, Fangyuan","Li, Shuo","Sun, Hongyu","Xiao, Xinxin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347220"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Huang, Wei","Xiao, Xinxin"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hunan University","Northeastern University at Qinhuangdao","Shandong University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cop nanoparticles fabricated through the nanoscale kirkendall effect immobilized in 000000000003d hollow carbon frameworks for oxygen evolution reaction","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/257105598/post_printed_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-347220","identifier":[{"id":"85115161478","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000692002500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-8efc6f49-45ba-4cc9-accd-2cf64d67a83d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7EC70B22C2252B62B8AC7A112D03EECC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/257105598/post_printed_version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"hunan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hunan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"northeastern university at qinhuangdao","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeastern University at Qinhuangdao","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","locid":"0c8bd1b5-159c-49e8-a215-7d67eee49f64","name":"Huang, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Jing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fangyuan","key":"diaopau","last":"Diao","locid":"4a203f26-fea5-4f05-a71d-d66409b2a9ab","name":"Diao, Fangyuan","orcid":"0000-0002-0993-9589","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuo","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shuo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Hongyu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"8cd768ff-d2df-4d64-bd7c-0d46854d561c","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1149/1945-7111/ac2090","issn":["00134651","19457111"],"issn_org":["00134651"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of The Electrochemical Society","paperid":"094501","publisher":"The Electrochemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of The Electrochemical Society","title_org":"Journal of the Electrochemical Society","volume":"168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115161478"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8efc6f49-45ba-4cc9-accd-2cf64d67a83d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"CoP Nanoparticles Fabricated Through the Nanoscale Kirkendall Effect Immobilized in 3D Hollow Carbon Frameworks for Oxygen Evolution Reaction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347220","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Soil fauna takes an active part in accelerating turnover of nutrients in terrestrial ecosystems. Anaerobic ammonium oxidation (anammox) has been widely characterized, however, whether anammox is active in earthworm gut and the effect of earthworm on anammox in soil remain unknown. In this study, the activity, abundance and community of anammox bacteria in earthworm guts and soils from microcosms were determined using a N-15-tracing technique, quantitative PCR, and anammox bacterial 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing. Results showed that anammox rates in guts ranged between 5.81 and 14.19 nmol N g(-1) dw gut content h(-1), which were significantly (P <0.01) higher than that in their surrounding soils during 30 day incubation. On the contrary, abundances of hzsB genes encoding subunit B hydrazine synthase in guts were significantly (P <0.05) lower than those in their surrounding soils. Anammox rates, denitrification N-2 production rates and hzsB genes in soils with earthworms were significantly (P <0.05) lower than those in control soils. Anammox bacterial compositions differed significantly (P <0.05) between gut and soil, and earthworm altered anammox bacterial communities in soils. Brocadia, Kuenenia and abundant unclassified anammox bacteria were detected in collected soils and gut contents, in which Brocadia was only detected in guts. These results suggested that microbes in earthworm gut increase, but present of earthworm reduces anammox and denitrification associated N loss by altering the anammox bacterial community compositions in soils. (C) 2020 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Li, Hu","Yang, Xiao-Ru","Wang, Juan","Zhou, Guo-Wei","Zhang, Yu-Sen","Lassen, Simon Bo","Zhu, Yong-Guan","Su, Jian-Qiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425849"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Agricultural soil","Anammox","Denitrification","Denitrifying bacteria","Gut microbiota","Microbial biomass","Nitrification","Nitrogen cycle","Nitrogen loss","Organic matter","Soil fauna","Temperature"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"earthworm gut an overlooked niche for anaerobic ammonium oxidation in agricultural soil","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-425849","identifier":[{"id":"000588243900067","type":"wos"},{"id":"32889284","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090052492","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3687e7f7-127d-4691-8cfe-5693dc9c4b2b"],"keyword":["Agricultural soil","Anammox","DENITRIFICATION","DENITRIFYING BACTERIA","Gut microbiota","IN-SITU DETECTION","MICROBIAL BIOMASS","NITRIFICATION","NITROGEN LOSS","Nitrogen cycle","ORGANIC-MATTER","OXIDIZING BACTERIA","Soil fauna","TEMPERATURE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0DC6A3E5318CA66F841D054F977E5CC2"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Microbial Ecology and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Hu","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao-Ru","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao-Ru","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juan","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Juan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guo-Wei","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Guo-Wei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yu-Sen","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yu-Sen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Simon Bo","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"7550f1f0-7813-4a66-8524-1287b55f402a","name":"Lassen, Simon Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-9781-1939","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yong-Guan","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yong-Guan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian-Qiang","key":"supau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Jian-Qiang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32889284"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2020.141874","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","paperid":"141874","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"752"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090052492"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3687e7f7-127d-4691-8cfe-5693dc9c4b2b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Earthworm gut : An overlooked niche for anaerobic ammonium oxidation in agricultural soil","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-425849","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"High-quality and comprehensive reference gene catalogs are essential for metagenomic research. The rather low diversity of samples used to construct existing catalogs of the mouse gut metagenome limits the numbers of identified genes in existing catalogs. We therefore established an expanded catalog of genes in the mouse gut metagenome (EMGC) containing >5.8 million genes by integrating 88 newly sequenced samples, 86 mouse gut-related bacterial genomes, and 3 existing gene catalogs. EMGC increases the number of nonredundant genes by more than 1 million genes compared to the so-far most extensive catalog. More than 60% of the genes in EMGC were assigned to Bacteria, with 54.20% being assigned to a phylum and 35.33% to a genus, while 30.39% were annotated at the KEGG orthology level. Nine hundred two metagenomic species (MGS) assigned to 122 taxa are identified based on the EMGC. The EMGC-based analysis of samples from groups of mice originating from different animal providers, housing laboratories, and genetic strains substantiated that diet is a major contributor to differences in composition and functional potential of the gut microbiota irrespective of differences in environment and genetic background. We envisage that EMGC will serve as a valuable reference data set for future metagenomic studies in mice.IMPORTANCE We established an expanded gene catalog of the mouse gut metagenome not only to increase the sample size compared to that in existing catalogs but also to provide a more comprehensive reference data set of the mouse gut microbiome for bioinformatic analysis. The expanded gene catalog comprises more than 5.8 million unique genes, as well as a wide range of taxonomic and functional information. Particularly, the analysis of metagenomic species with the expanded gene catalog reveals a great novelty of mouse gut-inhabiting microbial species. We envisage that the expanded gene catalog of the mouse gut metagenome will serve as a valuable bioinformatic resource for future gut metagenomic studies in mice.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Zhu, Jiahui","Ren, Huahui","Zhong, Huanzi","Li, Xiaoping","Zou, Yuanqiang","Han, Mo","Li, Minli","Madsen, Lise","Kristiansen, Karsten","Xiao, Liang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-449286"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Southeast University, Nanjing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an expanded gene catalog of mouse gut metagenomes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mSphere.01119-20","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-449286","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8544893","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33627510","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85102098208","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5d44947a-006e-4944-8336-7f8125630ae1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B8509CAD9F94505816BBFEB3905F9C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/260547066/An_Expanded_Gene_Catalog_of_Mouse_Gut_Metagenomes.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mSphere.01119-20","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southeast university nanjing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southeast University, Nanjing","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jiahui","key":"zhujiahuipau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Jiahui","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Huahui","key":"renhuahuipau","last":"Ren","locid":"d4e1d52c-5265-493f-a471-e26fd515d72f","name":"Ren, Huahui","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Huanzi","key":"zhonghuanzipau","last":"Zhong","locid":"00f8ce53-c1cd-4045-a1f2-216320dac529","name":"Zhong, Huanzi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Xiaoping","key":"lixiaopingpau","last":"Li","locid":"52a5b694-e829-4a6b-9b3c-7b51ce894f48","name":"Li, Xiaoping","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Yuanqiang","key":"zouyuanqiangpau","last":"Zou","locid":"ab60b640-70f1-45fe-a394-f8f7b35f4eee","name":"Zou, Yuanqiang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Mo","key":"hanmopau","last":"Han","locid":"40fd89c1-9808-423f-9021-ab3911a46e33","name":"Han, Mo","orcid":"0000-0002-4404-297X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Minli","key":"liminlipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Minli","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Lise","key":"madsenlisepau","last":"Madsen","locid":"194bda7c-3b62-451f-b9b3-6742361fe601","name":"Madsen, Lise","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenkarstenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"941041b1-1b8f-4be5-9a65-5e98f662c07e","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","orcid":"0000-0002-6024-0917","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Liang","key":"xiaoliangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Liang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33627510"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/msphere.01119-20","issn":["23795042"],"issue":"1","journal":"mSphere","paperid":"e-01119-20","status":"p","title":"mSphere","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102098208"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5d44947a-006e-4944-8336-7f8125630ae1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Expanded Gene Catalog of Mouse Gut Metagenomes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-449286","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Genome-wide association studies (GWASs) have discovered 20 risk loci in the human genome where germline variants associate with risk of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) in populations of European ancestry. Here, we fine-mapped one such locus on chr16q23.1 (rs72802365, p = 2.51 × 10−17, OR = 1.36, 95% CI = 1.31–1.40) and identified colocalization (PP = 0.87) with aberrant exon 5–7 CTRB2 splicing in pancreatic tissues (pGTEx = 1.40 × 10−69, βGTEx = 1.99; pLTG = 1.02 × 10−30, βLTG = 1.99). Imputation of a 584 bp structural variant overlapping exon 6 of CTRB2 into the GWAS datasets resulted in a highly significant association with pancreatic cancer risk (p = 2.83 × 10−16, OR = 1.36, 95% CI = 1.31–1.42), indicating that it may underlie this signal. Exon skipping attributable to the deletion (risk) allele introduces a premature stop codon in exon 7 of CTRB2, yielding a truncated chymotrypsinogen B2 protein that lacks chymotrypsin activity, is poorly secreted, and accumulates intracellularly in the endoplasmic reticulum (ER). We propose that intracellular accumulation of a nonfunctional chymotrypsinogen B2 protein leads to ER stress and pancreatic inflammation, which may explain the increased pancreatic cancer risk in carriers of CTRB2 exon 6 deletion alleles.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Jermusyk, Ashley","Zhong, Jun","Connelly, Katelyn E.","Gordon, Naomi","Perera, Sumeth","Abdolalizadeh, Ehssan","Zhang, Tongwu","O'Brien, Aidan","Hoskins, Jason W.","Collins, Irene","Eiser, Daina","Yuan, Chen","Albanes, Demetrius","Arslan, Alan A.","Gurrea, Aurelio Barricarte","Beane-Freeman, Laura","Bracci, Paige M.","Bueno-de-Mesquita, Bas","Buring, Julie","Canzian, Federico","Gallinger, Stephen","Gaziano, J. Michael","Giles, Graham G.","Goodman, Phyllis J.","Johansson, Mattias","Kooperberg, Charles","LeMarchand, Loic","Malats, Nuria","Neale, Rachel E.","Panico, Salvatore","Peters, Ulrike","Real, Francisco X.","Shu, Xiao Ou","Sund, Malin","Thornquist, Marc","Tj