{"abstract":"The thermal stability of hexagonal boron nitride (h-BN) plays a crucial role in stabilizing the braking performance of friction pairs (i.e., brake-pad/disc) in high-speed trains. In this study, h-BN modified copper metal matrix composites (Cu-MMCs) were fabricated via powder metallurgy, and their tribological behavior and mechanism upon pairing with C/C–SiC were investigated. Results show that as the h-BN content increased, the wear mechanism of the Cu-MMCs switched from abrasive to severe fatigue, followed by switching from mild oxidation to adhesive abrasion. Additionally, Cu-MMCs containing 2 wt% h-BN exhibited a high, stable coefficient of friction (COF) during repeated high-speed braking cycles together with a smoothed braking process at high braking speeds.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Chen, Fu","Li, Zhuan","Zou, Ling Fang","Ma, Wen Jie","Li, Jin Wei","Chen, Zhuo","Niu, Zi Bo","Liu, Pengfei","Xiao, Peng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-072507"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Zhuan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central South University","Inner Mongolia First Machinery Group Co., Ltd."],"keyword":["Metal matrix composites","Tribological behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tribological behavior and mechanism of h bn modified copper metal matrix composites paired with c c sic","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85089747377&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grant No. 51575536), Natural Science Foundation of Hunan Province (Grant No. 2020JJ2682), Graduate Research and Innovation Project of Central South University (Grant No. 1053320190038), and the State Key Laboratory of Powder Metallurgy for their financial support. The authors would like to thank the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grant No. 51575536 ), Natural Science Foundation of Hunan Province (Grant No. 2020JJ2682 ), Graduate Research and Innovation Project of Central South University (Grant No. 1053320190038 ), and the State Key Laboratory of Powder Metallurgy for their financial support."],"id":"S01-000.00-072507","identifier":[{"id":"85089747377","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-4d7c3e79-4326-4102-a7dc-fca2b7e9a224"],"keyword":["Metal matrix composites","Solid lubricant","Tribological behavior","Wear mechanism map"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77D546B4F2F72304A51B253EE6EE54AC"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"central south university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Central South University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"inner mongolia first machinery group co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Inner Mongolia First Machinery Group Co., Ltd.","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Disordered Materials","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fu","key":"chenfupau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Fu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhuan","key":"lizhuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ling Fang","key":"zoulingfangpau","last":"Zou","name":"Zou, Ling Fang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen Jie","key":"mawenjiepau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Wen Jie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin Wei","key":"lijinweipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jin Wei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhuo","key":"chenzhuopau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhuo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zi Bo","key":"niuzibopau","last":"Niu","name":"Niu, Zi Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peng Fei","key":"liupengfeipau","last":"Liu","locid":"670a1205-2565-4aaf-9a34-a0471fd58659","name":"Liu, Pengfei","name_org":"Liu, Peng Fei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng","key":"xiaopengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Peng","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.triboint.2020.106561","issn":["0301679X","18792464"],"issn_org":["0301679X"],"journal":"Tribology International","paperid":"106561","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Tribology International","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089747377"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4d7c3e79-4326-4102-a7dc-fca2b7e9a224"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Tribological behavior and mechanism of h-BN modified copper metal matrix composites paired with C/C–SiC","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-072507","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Net ecosystem gas exchange (NEE), a balance between gross ecosystem primary productivity (GPP) and ecosystem respiration (ER), is an important indicator of terrestrial ecosystem CO2 sink or source. Increasing frequency in droughts during different periods of the growing season may affect terrestrial ecosystem carbon (C) balance. However, detecting how drought timing controls ecosystem C processes is insufficiently explored because it is a challenge to accurately monitor and forecast drought dynamics. In a 5-year (2015–2019) precipitation manipulation experiment in a temperate steppe in northern China, we imposed a 60% decrease in precipitation in the early (April–June, DEP) and late (July–September, DLP) growing seasons in plots under rainout shelters to simulate drought occurrence timing. The responses of GPP, ER and NEE to DEP and DLP were examined to determine how the timing of decreased precipitation affects CO2 fluxes. Both DEP and DLP reduced GPP and ER. Decreased precipitation in the late growing season reduced NEE due to a greater decline in GPP than ER. In contrast, the lack of an effect of DEP on NEE can be attributed to a proportional decline in GPP and ER. Reduced normalized difference vegetation index (NDVI) and GPP induced by decreased precipitation explained the decline in GPP and ER respectively. Drought in the late growing season weakened the ecosystem C sink. The result indicates a low resistance in net C uptake to DLP. However, we did not find evidence that previous precipitation decreases resulted in a lower overall rate of ecosystem C exchange, indicating a high resilience in C processes in this semi-arid grassland. Synthesis and applications. Our study provides solid evidence that drought in the late growing season weakens ecosystem C sink in the semi-arid grassland. The findings suggest that management practices aimed at enhancing water availability during the late growing season should be preferred for increasing C sequestration.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Yang, Zhongling","Wei, Yueyue","Fu, Guangya","Xiao, Rui","Chen, Ji","Zhang, Yaojun","Wang, Dong","Li, Junyong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-156261"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Junyong","Wang, Dong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Henan University"],"keyword":["Balance","CO2 exchange","Carbon sink","Climate change","DIOXIDE EXCHANGE","Plant phenology","Soil respiration","Temperature","Variability","Water"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"decreased precipitation in the late growing season weakens an ecosystem carbon sink in a semi arid grassland","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85114116768","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-156261","identifier":[{"id":"85114116768","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000692264800001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-2f198cc4-a890-447f-9195-ae9bd11cfbfe"],"keyword":["BALANCE","CO2 EXCHANGE","DIOXIDE EXCHANGE","NET ECOSYSTEM","PLANT PHENOLOGY","SOIL RESPIRATION","TEMPERATURE","VARIABILITY","WATER","carbon processes","carbon sink","climate change","decreased precipitation","drought timing","photosynthetic substrate","plant community cover","semi-arid steppe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F4AFEBD14A26C87EDE28365B0C35DC94"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"henan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Henan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, CBIO - Centre for Circular Bioeconomy, Foulum"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongling","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Zhongling","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yueyue","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Yueyue","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guangya","key":"fupau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Guangya","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Rui","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ji","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"05f23b9e-16c0-478d-840b-18a8d914c393","name":"Chen, Ji","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaojun","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yaojun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Dong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Junyong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Junyong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1365-2664.13942","issn":["00218901","13652664"],"issn_org":["00218901"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Applied Ecology","pages":"2101-2112","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Ecology","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114116768"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2f198cc4-a890-447f-9195-ae9bd11cfbfe"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Decreased precipitation in the late growing season weakens an ecosystem carbon sink in a semi-arid grassland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-156261","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The COVID-19 pandemic has increased negative emotions and decreased positive emotions globally. Left unchecked, these emotional changes might have a wide array of adverse impacts. To reduce negative emotions and increase positive emotions, we tested the effectiveness of reappraisal, an emotion-regulation strategy that modifies how one thinks about a situation. Participants from 87 countries and regions (n = 21,644) were randomly assigned to one of two brief reappraisal interventions (reconstrual or repurposing) or one of two control conditions (active or passive). Results revealed that both reappraisal interventions (vesus both control conditions) consistently reduced negative emotions and increased positive emotions across different measures. Reconstrual and repurposing interventions had similar effects. Importantly, planned exploratory analyses indicated that reappraisal interventions did not reduce intentions to practice preventive health behaviours. The findings demonstrate the viability of creating scalable, low-cost interventions for use around the world. PROTOCOL REGISTRATION: The stage 1 protocol for this Registered Report was accepted in principle on 12 May 2020. The protocol, as accepted by the journal, can be found at https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.4878591.v1.","author_count":456,"contributors":["Wang, Ke","Goldenberg, Amit","Dorison, Charles A.","Miller, Jeremy K.","Uusberg, Andero","Lerner, Jennifer S.","Gross, James J.","Agesin, Bamikole Bamikole","Bernardo, Márcia","Campos, Olatz","Eudave, Luis","Grzech, Karolina","Ozery, Daphna Hausman","Jackson, Emily A.","Garcia, Elkin Oswaldo Luis","Drexler, Shira Meir","Jurković, Anita Penić","Rana, Kafeel","Wilson, John Paul","Antoniadi, Maria","Desai, Kermeka","Gialitaki, Zoi","Kushnir, Elizaveta","Nadif, Khaoula","Bravo, Olalla Niño","Nauman, Rafia","Oosterlinck, Marlies","Pantazi, Myrto","Pilecka, Natalia","Szabelska, Anna","van Steenkiste, I. M.M.","Filip, Katarzyna","Bozdoc, Andreea Ioan