{"abstract":"Owing to their numerous nutritional and bioactive functions, phospholipids (PLs), which are major components of biological membranes in all living organisms, have been widely applied as nutraceuticals, food supplements, and cosmetic ingredients. To date, PLs are extracted solely from soybean or egg yolk, despite the diverse market demands and high cost, owing to a tedious and inefficient manufacturing process. A microbial-based manufacturing process, specifically phospholipase D (PLD)-based biocatalysis and biotransformation process for PLs, has the potential to address several challenges associated with the soybean- or egg yolk-based supply chain. However, poor enzyme properties and inefficient microbial expression systems for PLD limit their wide industrial dissemination. Therefore, sourcing new enzyme variants with improved properties and developing advanced PLD expression systems are important. In the present review, we systematically summarize recent achievements and trends in the discovery, their structural properties, catalytic mechanisms, expression strategies for enhancing PLD production, and its multiple applications in the context of PLs. This review is expected to assist researchers to understand current advances in this field and provide insights for further molecular engineering efforts toward PLD-mediated bioprocessing.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zhang, Peng","Gong, Jin-Song","Qin, Jiufu","Li, Hui","Hou, Hai-Juan","Zhang, Xiao-Mei","Xu, Zheng-Hong","Shi, Jin-Song"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365906"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Gong, Jin-Song"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangnan University"],"keyword":["Biomanufacturing","Enzyme structure","Heterologous expression","Molecular engineering","Phospholipase D","Phospholipids"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phospholipids pls know how exploring and exploiting phospholipase d for its industrial dissemination","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85106294132","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365906","identifier":[{"id":"33985392","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85106294132","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cd79b907-3fba-4f11-a12f-d5196b845cde"],"keyword":["Biomanufacturing","Enzyme structure","Genome and metagenome mining","Heterologous expression","Molecular engineering","Phospholipase D","Phospholipids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1BB214DA77D6B769B4C7F8C7570C9AC3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng","key":"zhangpengpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Peng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin-Song","key":"gongjinsongpau","last":"Gong","name":"Gong, Jin-Song","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jiufu","key":"qinjiufupau","last":"Qin","locid":"a583e453-db66-4875-a71a-eb7e71f7e504","name":"Qin, Jiufu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"lihuipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hui","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai-Juan","key":"houhaijuanpau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Hai-Juan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Mei","key":"zhangxiaomeipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao-Mei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng-Hong","key":"xuzhenghongpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Zheng-Hong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin-Song","key":"shijinsongpau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Jin-Song","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33985392"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/07388551.2021.1921690","issn":["07388551","15497801"],"issn_org":["07388551"],"issue":"8","journal":"Critical Reviews in Biotechnology","pages":"1257-1278","publisher":"Taylor & Francis Inc.","status":"p","title":"Critical Reviews in Biotechnology","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106294132"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cd79b907-3fba-4f11-a12f-d5196b845cde"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Phospholipids (PLs) know-how: exploring and exploiting phospholipase D for its industrial dissemination","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365906","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Surplus active power will be accumulated in the DC link of permanent magnetic synchronous generator (PMSG) based wind turbine generator (WTG) system during the grid faults, thus resulting in DC link overvoltage and trip-off of WTGs. This paper reviews comprehensively the superconducting-type FRT strategy (SFRTT) based on superconducting magnetic energy storage system (SMES), superconducting fault current limiter (SFCL) and unified power quality conditioner (UPQC) for PMSG based WTG, aiming at introducing the basic principle and characteristics of various SFRTTs. Moreover, combined use of SFCL and SMES (SFCL-MES), together with the cost-effective method that cooperates modified WTG control strategies and superconducting devices, are introduced for performing better FRT enhancement. The comparison study concludes that the cost-effective based SFRTTs show the best comprehensive performance. This paper will be beneficial to promote the application of superconducting technologies, and be useful to the study in the field of grid integration of wind power.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zheng, Zixuan","Xie, Qi","Huang, Chunjun","Xiao, Xianyong","Li, Changsong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-369128"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sichuan University"],"keyword":["Coordinated control","Fault ride through","PMSG","SFCL","SMEs","UPQC"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"superconducting technology based fault ride through strategy for pmsg based wind turbine generator a comprehensive review","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85112607839","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-369128","identifier":[{"id":"85112607839","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000698708000012","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-d809937a-3196-470a-a4c8-eeff36d36ad1"],"keyword":["Coordinated control","Fault ride through","PMSG","SFCL","SMES","UPQC"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80EA83F70E7DB037CAD778DFA06B6AC4"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Electric Power and Energy, Distributed Energy Resources","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zixuan","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Zixuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qi","key":"xiepau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Qi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chunjun","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","locid":"4422fc32-e44d-4b2c-a0bb-be4fc40078c4","name":"Huang, Chunjun","orcid":"0000-0003-4340-5887","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianyong","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xianyong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Changsong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Changsong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tasc.2021.3101767","issn":["10518223","15582515"],"issn_org":["10518223"],"issue":"8","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Applied Superconductivity","paperid":"5403106","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Applied Superconductivity","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112607839"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d809937a-3196-470a-a4c8-eeff36d36ad1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Superconducting Technology Based Fault Ride through Strategy for PMSG-Based Wind Turbine Generator: A Comprehensive Review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-369128","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) has caused a global pandemic of Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). However, the microbial composition of the respiratory tract and other infected tissues as well as their possible pathogenic contributions to varying degrees of disease severity in COVID-19 patients remain unclear. Between 27 January and 26 February 2020, serial clinical specimens (sputum, nasal and throat swab, anal swab and feces) were collected from a cohort of hospitalized COVID-19 patients, including 8 mildly and 15 severely ill patients in Guangdong province, China. Total RNA was extracted and ultra-deep metatranscriptomic sequencing was performed in combination with laboratory diagnostic assays. We identified distinct signatures of microbial dysbiosis among severely ill COVID-19 patients on broad spectrum antimicrobial therapy. Co-detection of other human respiratory viruses (including human alphaherpesvirus 1, rhinovirus B, and human orthopneumovirus) was demonstrated in 30.8% (4/13) of the severely ill patients, but not in any of the mildly affected patients. Notably, the predominant respiratory microbial taxa of severely ill patients were Burkholderia cepacia complex (BCC), Staphylococcus epidermidis, or Mycoplasma spp. (including M. hominis and M. orale). The presence of the former two bacterial taxa was also confirmed by clinical cultures of respiratory specimens (expectorated sputum or nasal secretions) in 23.1% (3/13) of the severe cases. Finally, a time-dependent, secondary infection of B. cenocepacia with expressions of multiple virulence genes was demonstrated in one severely ill patient, which might accelerate his disease deterioration and death occurring one month after ICU admission. Our findings point to SARS-CoV-2-related microbial dysbiosis and various antibiotic-resistant respiratory microbes/pathogens in hospitalized COVID-19 patients in relation to disease severity. Detection and tracking strategies are needed to prevent the spread of antimicrobial resistance, improve the treatment regimen and clinical outcomes of hospitalized, severely ill COVID-19 patients.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Zhong, Huanzi","Wang, Yanqun","Shi, Zhun","Zhang, Lu","Ren, Huahui","He, Weiqun","Zhang, Zhaoyong","Zhu, Airu","Zhao, Jingxian","Xiao, Fei","Yang, Fangming","Liang, Tianzhu","Ye, Feng","Zhong, Bei","Ruan, Shicong","Gan, Mian","Zhu, Jiahui","Li, Fang","Li, Fuqiang","Wang, Daxi","Li, Jiandong","Ren, Peidi","Zhu, Shida","Yang, Huanming","Wang, Jian","Kristiansen, Karsten","Tun, Hein Min","Chen, Weijun","Zhong, Nanshan","Xu, Xun","Li, Yi-min","Li, Junhua","Zhao, Jincun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-403575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of respiratory microbial dysbiosis in hospitalized covid 000000000019 patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41421-021-00257-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-403575","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8043102","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33850111","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85104312574","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-11218c63-84e8-4ebe-b613-cd24f40c65d4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-53AC780D83144F5DED41EBC6192A816C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/261218982/Characterization_of_respiratory_microbial_dysbiosis_in_hospitalized_COVID_19_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41421-021-00257-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Huanzi","key":"zhonghuanzipau","last":"Zhong","locid":"00f8ce53-c1cd-4045-a1f2-216320dac529","name":"Zhong, Huanzi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yanqun","key":"wangyanqunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yanqun","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Zhun","key":"shizhunpau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Zhun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lu","key":"zhanglupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Lu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Huahui","key":"renhuahuipau","last":"Ren","locid":"d4e1d52c-5265-493f-a471-e26fd515d72f","name":"Ren, Huahui","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Weiqun","key":"heweiqunpau","last":"He","name":"He, Weiqun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhaoyong","key":"zhangzhaoyongpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhaoyong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Airu","key":"zhuairupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Airu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jingxian","key":"zhaojingxianpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Jingxian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fei","key":"xiaofeipau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Fei","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Fangming","key":"yangfangmingpau","last":"Yang","name":"