{"abstract":"Knowledge of sedimentary organic carbon (OC) in hadal trenches, the deepest ocean realm, is rudimentary. Here, we conducted a comprehensive analysis of total OC (TOC), stable and radio‐carbon isotopes (δ13C and Δ14C), and biomarkers (e.g., n‐alkanes, n‐alkanols and n‐fatty acids) in 12 sediment cores collected from hadal (trench axis) and non‐hadal (abyssal plains and slopes) settings of the Kermadec Trench (Southwestern Pacific) and Atacama Trench (Southeastern Pacific) regions. Our results show that the TOC in the Atacama Trench region (0.86% ± 0.69%) is significantly higher than that of the Kermadec Trench region (0.29% ± 0.08%), likely related to different surface primary productivity. In both trench regions, the hadal sites are generally characterized by more negative δ13C, higher TOC/TN ratio, and similar or higher abundance ratio of terrigenous/marine biomarkers as compared to the non‐hadal sites, suggesting the selective preservation of terrigenous biogenic/fossil OC at the hadal trench axis. The linear increase in 14C age with sediment depth in non‐hadal cores reflects steady depositional conditions, whereas seven out of eight hadal sediment cores show 14C age reversals presumably due to occasional mass‐transport deposits. Our results suggest (1) a strong heterogeneity in sedimentary OC characteristics between trenches and within each trench and (2) relatively high accumulation rates of terrigenous OC in both the Kermadec Trench (0.35 ± 0.04 g m−2 yr−1) and the Atacama Trench (1.4 ± 0.5 g m−2 yr−1). Thus, hadal trenches appear to represent an important environment for terrigenous carbon deposition in the deep ocean.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Xu, Yunping","Li, Xinxin","Luo, Min","Xiao, Wenjie","Fang, Jiasong","Rashid, Harunur","Peng, Yongbo","Li, Wenpeng","Wenzhöfer, Frank","Rowden, Ashley A.","Glud, Ronnie N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-582429"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Xinxin","Xu, Yunping"],"country":["China","Germany","Japan","New Zealand"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute","All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","Nanjing University","National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research","Qingdao National Laboratory for Marine Science and Technology","Shanghai Ocean University","Southern University of Science and Technology","Tokyo University of Marine Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distribution source and burial of sedimentary organic carbon in kermadec and atacama trenches","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182239239/2020JG006189.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-582429","identifier":[{"id":"85106917233","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-2042ac3e-dc02-473e-9b23-65c0989b344f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B4A829EF8B4F107DD93759D70728D155"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/182239239/2020JG006189.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai ocean university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Ocean University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"southern university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"qingdao national laboratory for marine science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao National Laboratory for Marine Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"nanjing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Danish Institute for Advanced Study","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, HADAL","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Nordcee"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"alfred wegener institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Alfred Wegener Institute","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for marine microbiology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Marine Microbiology","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"nz","key":"national institute of water and atmospheric research","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"National Institute of Water and Atmospheric Research","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"jp","key":"tokyo university of marine science and technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Tokyo University of Marine Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yunping","key":"xuyunpingpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Yunping","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinxin","key":"lixinxinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xinxin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"luominpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Min","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenjie","key":"xiaowenjiepau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Wenjie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiasong","key":"fangjiasongpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Jiasong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harunur","key":"rashidharunurpau","last":"Rashid","name":"Rashid, Harunur","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongbo","key":"pengyongbopau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Yongbo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenpeng","key":"liwenpengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wenpeng","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"wenzhöferfrankpau","last":"Wenzhöfer","locid":"afbd49b8-649d-42f1-9db9-210ceb2e2594","name":"Wenzhöfer, Frank","orcid":"0000-0002-4621-0586","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Ashley A.","key":"rowdenashleyapau","last":"Rowden","name":"Rowden, Ashley A.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Ronnie N.","key":"gludronnienpau","last":"Glud","locid":"aa184a3b-a696-4a69-a7de-66a3eea542cf","name":"Glud, Ronnie N.","orcid":"0000-0002-7069-893X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1029/2020jg006189","issn":["21562202","21698953"],"issn_org":["21698953"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Geophysical Research: Biogeosciences","paperid":"e2020JG006189","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Journal of Geophysical Research: Biogeosciences","volume":"126"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106917233"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2042ac3e-dc02-473e-9b23-65c0989b344f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Distribution, Source, and Burial of Sedimentary Organic Carbon in Kermadec and Atacama Trenches","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-582429","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Upon sustained loading, colloidal gels tend to feature delayed viscoplastic creep deformations. However, the relationship, if any, between the structure and creep dynamics of gels remains elusive. Here, based on accelerated molecular dynamics simulations and the recently developed softness approach (i.e., classification-based machine learning), we reveal that the propensity of a gel to exhibit long-time creep is encoded in its static, unloaded structure. By taking the example of a calcium–silicate–hydrate gel (the binding phase of concrete), we extract a local, non-intuitive structural descriptor (a revised version of the “softness” metric proposed by the pioneering work from Cubuk et al.) that is strongly correlated with the dynamics of the particles. Notably, the macroscopic creep rate exhibits an exponential dependence on the average softness. We find that creep results in a decrease in softness in the gel structure, which, in turn, explains the gradual decay of the creep rate over time. Finally, we demonstrate that the softness metric is strongly correlated with the average energy barrier that is accessible to the particles.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Liu, Han","Xiao, Siqi","Tang, Longwen","Bao, Enigma","Li, Emily","Yang, Caroline","Zhao, Zhangji","Sant, Gaurav","Smedskjær, Morten Mattrup","Guo, Lijie","Bauchy, Mathieu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069437"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bauchy, Mathieu"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing General Research Institute of Mining and Metallurgy","Tongji University","University of California at Los Angeles"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting the early stage creep dynamics of gels from their static structure by machine learning","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-069437","identifier":[{"id":"85103688405","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-42ff0f20-97cf-4859-ac89-3b27ecd8333f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A958A6AE79346DD941D83F6B294B73C0"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of california at los angeles","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Los Angeles","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"tongji university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tongji University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Disordered Materials","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Oxide Glass Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"beijing general research institute of mining and metallurgy","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing General Research Institute of Mining and Metallurgy","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Han","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Han","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siqi","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Siqi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Longwen","key":"tangpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Longwen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Enigma","key":"baopau","last":"Bao","name":"Bao, Enigma","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emily","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Emily","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Caroline","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhangji","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Zhangji","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gaurav","key":"santpau","last":"Sant","name":"Sant, Gaurav","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Mattrup","key":"smedskjærpau","last":"Smedskjær","locid":"5ad9c406-9754-4399-870b-9bed06076ebe","name":"Smedskjær, Morten Mattrup","orcid":"0000-0003-0476-2021","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lijie","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Lijie","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathieu","key":"bauchypau","last":"Bauchy","name":"Bauchy, Mathieu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.actamat.2021.116817","issn":["13596454"],"journal":"Acta Materialia","paperid":"116817","publisher":"Acta Materialia Inc","status":"p","title":"Acta Materialia","volume":"210"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103688405"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-42ff0f20-97cf-4859-ac89-3b27ecd8333f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Predicting the early-stage creep dynamics of gels from their static structure by machine learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069437","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The interface between metal catalyst and support plays a critical role in heterogeneous catalysis. An epitaxial interface is generally considered to be rigid, and tuning its intrinsic microstructure with atomic precision during catalytic reactions is challenging. Using aberration-corrected environmental transmission electron microscopy, we studied the interface between gold (Au) and a titanium dioxide (TiO2) support. Direct atomic-scale observations showed an unexpected dependence of the atomic structure of the Au-TiO2 interface with the epitaxial rotation of gold nanoparticles on a TiO2surface during carbon monoxide (CO) oxidation. Taking advantage of the reversible and controllable rotation, we achieved in situ manipulation of the active Au-TiO2 interface by changing gas and temperature. This result suggests that real-time design of the catalytic interface in operating conditions may be possible.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Yuan, Wentao","Zhu, Beien","Fang, Ke","Li, Xiao Yan","Hansen, Thomas Willum","Ou, Yang","Yang, Hangsheng","Wagner, Jakob Birkedal","Gao, Yi","Wang, Yong","Zhang, Ze"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-330819"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Yong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Shanghai Advanced Research Institute","Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in situ manipulation of the active au tio sub 000000000002 sub interface with atomic precision during co oxidation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258507060/Manuscript_20201122_author_copy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-330819","identifier":[{"id":"85100485375","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33510028","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-584f5815-1f06-4256-9efd-e2475ce9e94d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9C0A7CC73E098AFF7AF285F5E40912BC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258507060/Manuscript_20201122_author_copy.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Nanostructured Graphene","Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization","Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization, Nanocharacterization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"cas shanghai advanced research institute","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Shanghai Advanced Research Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wentao","key":"yuanpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Wentao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Beien","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Beien","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"fangpau","last":"Fang","name":"Fang, Ke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Yan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Yan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas W.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"7ae02872-2172-403d-8859-1d8a33665d2c","name":"Hansen, Thomas Willum","name_org":"Hansen, Thomas W.","orcid":"0000-0002-1861-3054","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yang","key":"oupau","last":"Ou","name":"Ou, Yang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hangsheng","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Hangsheng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob B.","key":"wagnerpau","last":"Wagner","locid":"18f73542-3752-4043-a7b2-391ee78ba1eb","name":"Wagner, Jakob Birkedal","name_org":"Wagner, Jakob B.","orcid":"0000-0002-2945-0190","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Yi","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yong","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ze","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ze","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33510028"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1126/science.abe3558","issn":["00368075","10959203"],"issn_org":["00368075"],"issue":"6528","journal":"Science","paperid":"abe3558","publisher":"American Association for the Advancement of Science","status":"p","title":"Science","volume":"371"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100485375"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-584f5815-1f06-4256-9efd-e2475ce9e94d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"In situ manipulation of the active Au-TiO<sub>2 </sub>interface with atomic precision during CO oxidation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-330819","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Transition metal phosphides are emerging as promising anode materials of sodium ion batteries (SIBs) due to their high performance in terms of capacity and operational stability. Highly isolated CoP nanoparticles encapsulated in 3D hollow nitrogen-doped carbon networks (CoP/HNC composite) are designed via polymerization of poly-dopamine (PDA) on ZIF-67 and the subsequent in-situ phosphorization. Ultrafine CoP nanoparticles (10 ± 2 nm) are decorated in nitrogen-doped carbon polyhedral shells in a porous 3D hollow architecture. Benefiting from the unique construction, the CoP/HNC electrode delivers a high reversible long cycle-life capacity of 223 mA h g−1 for sodium storage at 500 mA g−1 after 700 cycles. DFT simulations indicate that Na atoms strongly bound to CoP surfaces, and significantly concentrate near CoP surfaces, beneficial for the Na atoms storage in this composite material. These results suggest the CoP/HNC composite can be a promising anode material for SIBs. Besides, the designed strategy of CoP/HNC composite could be applied to fabricate other metal phosphides for electrochemical storage devices.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Huang, Wei","Shangguan, Huihui","Zheng, Xiaowen","Engelbrekt, Christian","Yang, Yuan","Li, Shuo","Mølhave, Kristian","Xiao, Xinxin","Lin, Xiaohang","Ci, Lijie","Si, Pengchao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334907"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Lin, Xiaohang","Si, Pengchao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shandong University"],"keyword":["COP","Hollow structure","ZIF 67"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"three dimensional hollow nitrogen doped carbon shells enclosed monodisperse cop nanoparticles for long cycle life sodium storage","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256265110/berat_1_s2.0_S001346862101402X_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334907","identifier":[{"id":"85114990623","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-65b28676-b608-4644-9321-21551c3fbf1f"],"keyword":["CoP","Hollow structure","PDA derived carbon","Sodium storage","ZIF-67"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F957543EFF3B318C615D662744089AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/256265110/berat_1_s2.0_S001346862101402X_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Wei","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","locid":"0c8bd1b5-159c-49e8-a215-7d67eee49f64","name":"Huang, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Huihui","key":"shangguanpau","last":"Shangguan","name":"Shangguan, Huihui","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaowen","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Xiaowen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"engelbrektpau","last":"Engelbrekt","locid":"a1b586e6-3d4b-4ebc-9037-259adc94bc5a","name":"Engelbrekt, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3679-3666","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuan","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Yuan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuo","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shuo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"mølhavepau","last":"Mølhave","locid":"745c31cd-5de7-4dd8-909e-d0f5de0fed5c","name":"Mølhave, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-6493-2750","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"8cd768ff-d2df-4d64-bd7c-0d46854d561c","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaohang","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Xiaohang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lijie","key":"cipau","last":"Ci","name":"Ci, Lijie","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengchao","key":"sipau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Pengchao","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.electacta.2021.139112","issn":["00134686","18733859"],"issn_org":["00134686"],"journal":"Electrochimica Acta","paperid":"139112","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Electrochimica Acta","volume":"395"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114990623"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-65b28676-b608-4644-9321-21551c3fbf1f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Three-dimensional hollow nitrogen-doped carbon shells enclosed monodisperse CoP nanoparticles for long cycle-life sodium storage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334907","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Metal doping has been demonstrated to be an effective strategy to modulate photocatalytic properties. However, it is very challenging to achieve tunable electronic structures and controllable morphologies with more active sites only via metal doping. Herein, Zr doped CaTiO3 photocatalysts with enhanced photocatalytic activities toward the hydrogen evolution was prepared by one-step mild hydrothermal reaction. We revealed that zirconium doping would regulate the surface structures of CaTiO3 from smooth surface to characteristic nanosteps structures. This nanosteps structure with more exposed active sites accompanied by higher exposed surface area, oxygen vacancies and reduction ability, effectively promote the separation of photo-induced carriers, thus resulting in increased photocatalytic properties. This work provides a guideline for surface structures and electronic structures modification simultaneously to design powerful photocatalysts only by metal doping.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gao, Qiang","Meng, Jie","Yang, Ya","Lin, Qingyun","Lu, Yangfan","Wei, Xiao","Li, Jixue","Han, Gaorong","Zhang, Ze"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352084"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Ze"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Science and Technology of China","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"zirconium doping in calcium titanate perovskite oxides with surface nanostep structure for promoting photocatalytic hydrogen evolution","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85097331059","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352084","identifier":[{"id":"85097331059","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9f433e27-3d49-4834-988f-1bd5da22170e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2F0C85D88EBD8D51AB24ABEDE35D4C60"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology of China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiang","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Qiang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jie","key":"mengpau","last":"Meng","locid":"2ffb0f5d-8ce8-4b1b-a8ea-f89e50095f6b","name":"Meng, Jie","orcid":"0000-0002-3813-5221","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ya","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Ya","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qingyun","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Qingyun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yangfan","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Yangfan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","name":"Wei, Xiao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jixue","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name"