hytopathological Society","status":"p","title":"Phytopathology","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118612459"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d5cb50d9-5f9c-4f8a-becf-b6435bd9d418"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Phylogenomic Analysis of a 55.1-kb 19-Gene Dataset Resolves a Monophyletic Fusarium that Includes the Fusarium solani Species Complex","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-368448","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"To explore pesticide uptake from soil into a growing potato, a moving-boundary dynamic model is proposed on the basis of the radical diffusion process of a chemical to a sphere. This model, which considers the logistic growth of the potato tuber, describes two hypothetical processes of chemical diffusion within a growing tuber. The model was tested in an illustrative case study for an application of chlorpyrifos. Results indicate that the distribution of chlorpyrifos concentrations along the potato radius is significantly affected by the tuber development. In comparison of our results to results from a classic model using a fixed boundary, the proposed dynamic model yields a quick and big jump for both the average concentration and bioconcentration factor (BCF) of chlorpyrifos in the potato as a result of the sigmoid expansion boundary. Overall, the dynamic model predicts that chlorpyrifos BCFs in the potato at harvest are higher than those using the classical model. In comparison of model results to measured uptake of chlorpyrifos into potato at harvest, the dynamic model shows better performance than the classical model. Our results provide a new perspective on pesticide uptake into potatoes and inform human health risk assessment for pesticides applied at different tuber growth stages.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Xiao, Shenglan","Gong, Yishu","Li, Zijian","Fantke, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373290"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Zijian"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","Sun Yat-Sen University"],"keyword":["Diffusion process","Logistic growth","Soil pollution","Uptake model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving pesticide uptake modeling into potatoes considering tuber growth dynamics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jafc.1c00151","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-373290","identifier":[{"id":"85103614992","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000636687300006","type":"wos"},{"id":"33729792","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-e5eb4311-7325-4806-877d-5c97d58176d1"],"keyword":["Crop contamniations","Diffusion process","Logistic growth","Soil pollution","Uptake model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB5CF36BCE644513B2679FCB7F96714B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jafc.1c00151","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/246653855/acs.jafc.1c00151.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Sustainability","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Sustainability, Society and Economics, Quantitative Sustainability Assessment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shenglan","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Shenglan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yishu","key":"gongpau","last":"Gong","name":"Gong, Yishu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zijian","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zijian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"fantkepau","last":"Fantke","locid":"5ba443c7-8e07-4435-9946-883e7f5f1ff7","name":"Fantke, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7148-6982","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33729792"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jafc.1c00151","issn":["00218561","15205118"],"issn_org":["00218561"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","pages":"3607-3616","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103614992"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e5eb4311-7325-4806-877d-5c97d58176d1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improving Pesticide Uptake Modeling into Potatoes: Considering Tuber Growth Dynamics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373290","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Efficient CO2 capture and separation, such as from natural gas, biogas, and landfill gas, is highly desirable to maximize the use of energy and alleviate carbon emission and greenhouse effect. A novel approach of charge/strain-regulated gas capture and separation has been proposed to offer the advantages of reversibility and controllable kinetics. We demonstrated the highly controllable CO2 capture and separation from CO2/CH4 on porous g-C9N7 nanosheets with varying charge densities and strains using molecular dynamics (MD) simulations and first-principle density function theory (DFT) calculations. The remarkable CO2 permeance up to 5.94 × 107 GPU can be achieved by charge engineering, such as through the strategies of electrochemical methods. A tunable CO2 separation performance was exhibited under the condition of tensile strain. The permeance of CO2 was found to increase with increasing the applied tensile strain, and the maximum permeance was 3.61 × 107 GPU with 7.5% strained g-C9N7 membrane. More interestingly, a promising approach for combining a charged state with the strain engineering was explored to investigate the synergistic effect. Under conditions of 1 e- negative charge and 3% tensile strain on g-C9N7 membrane, the CO2 permeance reached 3.18 × 107 GPU, which was 9 times higher than only with adding 1 e-, and 8 times higher than only applying 3% strain. Additionally, the temperature effect indicated that the g-C9N7 membrane can be served as an excellent candidate for CO2/CH4 separation at ambient conditions. These results provide useful guidance for developing advanced materials with highly controllable CO2 capture and separation properties.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Liu, Zilong","Li, Xue","He, Wenhao","Zhao, Ge","Yang, Yanning","Liu, Xinlei","Zhang, Xiao","Li, Xiaofang","Zhang, Suian","Sun, Weichao","Lu, Guiwu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-404496"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China National Petroleum Corporation","China University of Petroleum (East China)","China University of Petroleum - Beijing","State Key Laboratory of Coal and Coalbed Methane Co-production","Tianjin University"],"keyword":["Charge regulation","Membrane","Permeance","Strain engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synergistic effect of charge and strain engineering on porous g c sub 000000000009 sub n sub 000000000007 sub nanosheets for highly controllable co sub 000000000002 sub capture and separation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-404496","identifier":[{"id":"85119433899","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1294d66c-e914-4040-a786-b51a41375436"],"keyword":["CO capture and separation","Charge regulation","Membrane","Permeance","Strain engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DCB74F604C711D791643C65ABB2ED466"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Support"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"china university of petroleum beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Petroleum - Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"china national petroleum corporation","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China National Petroleum Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"tianjin university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"china university of petroleum","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Petroleum (East China)","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"state key laboratory of coal and coalbed methane co production","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Key Laboratory of Coal and Coalbed Methane Co-production","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Zilong","key":"liuzilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zilong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xue","key":"lixuepau","last":"Li","locid":"d0062fe5-e25b-4406-9330-18e20f9a4792","name":"Li, Xue","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Wenhao","key":"hewenhaopau","last":"He","name":"He, Wenhao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ge","key":"zhaogepau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Ge","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Yanning","key":"yangyanningpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Yanning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Xinlei","key":"liuxinleipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xinlei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Xiao","key":"zhangxiaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Xiaofang","key":"lixiaofangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaofang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 6","first":"Suian","key":"zhangsuianpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Suian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Weichao","key":"sunweichaopau","last":"Sun","locid":"728793c2-52fc-4c6d-b1be-14dc08be63b6","name":"Sun, Weichao","orcid":"0000-0002-8597-7501","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Guiwu","key":"luguiwupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Guiwu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.seppur.2021.120135","issn":["13835866","18733794"],"issn_org":["13835866"],"issue":"Part B","journal":"Separation and Purification Technology","paperid":"120135","status":"p","title":"Separation and Purification Technology","volume":"282"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119433899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1294d66c-e914-4040-a786-b51a41375436"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Synergistic effect of charge and strain engineering on porous g-C<sub>9</sub>N<sub>7</sub> nanosheets for highly controllable CO<sub>2</sub> capture and separation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-404496","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Conjunctive transfer of antibiotic resistance genes (ARGs) among bacteria driven by plasmids facilitated the evolution and spread of antibiotic resistance. Heavy metal exposure accelerated the plasmid-mediated conjunctive transfer of ARGs. Nanomaterials are well-known adsorbents for heavy metals removal, with the capability of combatting resistant bacteria/facilitating conjunctive transfer of ARGs. However, co-effect of heavy metals and nanomaterials on plasmid-mediated conjunctive transfer of ARGs was still unknown. In this study, we investigated the effect of the simultaneous exposure of Cd2+ and nano Fe2O3 on conjugative transfer of plasmid RP4 from Pseudomonas putida KT2442 to water microbial community. The permeability of bacterial cell membranes, antioxidant enzyme activities and conjugation gene expression were also investigated. The results suggested that the combination of Cd2+ and high concentration nano Fe2O3 (10 mg/L and 100 mg/L) significantly increased conjugative transfer frequencies of RP4 plasmid (p < 0.05). The most transconjugants were detected in the treatment of co-exposure to Cd2+ and nano Fe2O3, the majority of which were identified to be human pathogens. The mechanisms of the exacerbated conjugative transfer of ARGs were involved in the enhancement of cell membrane permeability, antioxidant enzyme activities, and mRNA expression levels of the conjugation genes by the co-effect of Cd2+ and nano Fe2O3. This study confirmed that the simultaneous exposure to Cd2+and nano Fe2O3 exerted a synergetic co-effect on plasmid-mediated conjunctive transfer of ARGs, emphasizing that the co-effect of nanomaterials and heavy metals should be prudently evaluated when combating antibiotic resistance.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pu, Qiang","Fan, Xiao Ting","Sun, An Qi","Pan, Ting","Li, Hu","Lassen, Simon Bo","An, Xin Li","Su, Jian Qiang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408666"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Fujian Normal University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Horizontal gene transfer","Microbial community","Nanomaterials","Plasmid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co effect of cadmium and iron oxide nanoparticles on plasmid mediated conjugative transfer of antibiotic resistance genes incl corrigendum","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2021.106453","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-408666","identifier":[{"id":"000641974400012","type":"wos"},{"id":"85105002727","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33798824","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1978017b-04c7-436b-b293-e1db5f5f1451"],"keyword":["Conjugative transfer","Horizontal gene transfer","Microbial community","Nanomaterials","Plasmid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-904598D90D4138DF22031EE0DB71EEB3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/262847604/1_s2.0_S0160412021000787_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.envint.2021.106453","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chines