","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xiangming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jean-pierre","key":"wigneronpau","last":"Wigneron","name":"Wigneron, Jean-pierre","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Philippe","key":"ciaispau","last":"Ciais","name":"Ciais, Philippe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","locid":"ff0528eb-4f80-444b-a7ad-2d2307f7bdc9","name":"Brandt, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-9531-1239","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lei","key":"fanpau","last":"Fan","name":"Fan, Lei","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiaojun","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaojun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sean","key":"crowellpau","last":"Crowell","name":"Crowell, Sean","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiaocui","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xiaocui","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Russell","key":"doughtypau","last":"Doughty","name":"Doughty, Russell","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yao","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fang","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Fang","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephen","key":"sitchpau","last":"Sitch","name":"Sitch, Stephen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Berrien","key":"moorepau","last":"Moore","name":"Moore, Berrien","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41558-021-01026-5","issn":["1758678X","17586798"],"issn_org":["1758678X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Nature Climate Change","pages":"442-448","status":"p","title":"Nature Climate Change","title_org":"Nature climate change","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105132848"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-678b232d-0fa9-4ec4-8a61-99f16df07461"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Carbon loss from forest degradation exceeds that from deforestation in the Brazilian Amazon","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455263","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Climate warming has significantly advanced plant spring phenology in temperate and boreal biomes in the northern hemisphere. However, the response of subtropical forest phenology to climate change remains largely unclear. This study aimed to determine the spatiotemporal patterns of spring photosynthetic phenology in subtropical forests in China over the period 2002-2017 and explore its underlying mechanism in response to the changes of different climate variables. We applied four methods to extract the start of the photosynthetic period (SOP) from a solar–induced chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF) data set during the period 2002 to 2017, and determined correlations between SOP and environmental factors using partial correlation analyses. Overall, the SOP was advanced by 6.8 days. Furthermore, we found that the SIF-based SOP is highly correlated with the flux data–based photosynthetic onset dates, demonstrating that SIF can be a useful index in characterizing the photosynthetic phenology in subtropical forests. Interestingly, based on partial correlation analysation temperature dominated the SOP in the northern subtropical forest, but the importance of precipitation increased with decreasing latitudes, and the primary climatic control of SOP in southern monsoon evergreen forests is precipitation. These results suggested that the predicted increase in temperature and shift in precipitation regimes under ongoing climate change might potentially largely affect the photosynthetic phenology, and thus affect the carbon and water cycles in subtropical forests.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Li, Xinxi","Fu, Yongshuo H.","Chen, Shouzhi","Xiao, Jingfeng","Yin, Guodong","Li, Xing","Zhang, Xuan","Geng, Xiaojun","Wu, Zhaofei","Zhou, Xuancheng","Tang, Jing","Hao, Fanghua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-484009"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","China","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Normal University","Lund University","University of Antwerp","University of New Hampshire"],"keyword":["Climate change","Precipitation","Subtropical forest"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increasing importance of precipitation in spring phenology with decreasing latitudes in subtropical forest area in china","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-484009","identifier":[{"id":"85104488778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9789cb37-b4ce-40af-89c0-0efd1fd60d4f"],"keyword":["Climate change","Latitudinal shift","Photosynthetic phenology","Precipitation","SIF","Subtropical forest"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-44C7E6AF6C24514EF969803C04374223"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"university of antwerp","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Antwerp","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of new hampshire","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of New Hampshire","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xinxi","key":"lixinxipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xinxi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Yongshuo H.","key":"fuyongshuohpau","last":"Fu","name":"Fu, Yongshuo H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shouzhi","key":"chenshouzhipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Shouzhi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jingfeng","key":"xiaojingfengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jingfeng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guodong","key":"yinguodongpau","last":"Yin","name":"Yin, Guodong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Xing","key":"lixingpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xuan","key":"zhangxuanpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xuan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaojun","key":"gengxiaojunpau","last":"Geng","name":"Geng, Xiaojun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhaofei","key":"wuzhaofeipau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Zhaofei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xuancheng","key":"zhouxuanchengpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Xuancheng","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Jing","key":"tangjingpau","last":"Tang","locid":"fc4649e9-70de-4576-b7a5-40b50d51c509","name":"Tang, Jing","orcid":"0000-0001-7961-8214","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fanghua","key":"haofanghuapau","last":"Hao","name":"Hao, Fanghua","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.agrformet.2021.108427","issn":["01681923","18732240"],"issn_org":["01681923"],"journal":"Agricultural and Forest Meteorology","paperid":"108427","status":"p","title":"Agricultural and Forest Meteorology","volume":"304-305"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104488778"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9789cb37-b4ce-40af-89c0-0efd1fd60d4f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Increasing importance of precipitation in spring phenology with decreasing latitudes in subtropical forest area in China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-484009","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Germline variation and smoking are independently associated with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC). We conducted genome-wide smoking interaction analysis of PDAC using genotype data from four previous genome-wide association studies in individuals of European ancestry (7,937 cases and 11,774 controls). Examination of expression quantitative trait loci data from the Genotype-Tissue Expression Project followed by colocalization analysis was conducted to determine whether there was support for common SNP(s) underlying the observed associations. Statistical tests were two sided and P < 5 similar to 10(-8) was considered statistically significant. Genome-wide significant evidence of qualitative interaction was identified on chr2q21.3 in intron 5 of the transmembrane protein 163 (TMEM163) and upstream of the cyclin T2 (CCNT2). The most significant SNP using the Empirical Bayes method, in this region that included 45 significantly associated SNPs, was rs1818613 [per allele OR in never smokers 0.87, 95% confidence interval (CI), 0.82-0.93; former smokers 1.00, 95% CI, 0.91-1.07; current smokers 1.25, 95% CI 1.12-1.40, P-interaction = 3.08 x 10(-9)). Examination of the Genotype-Tissue Expression Project data demonstrated an expression quantitative trait locus in this region for TMEM163 and CCNT2 in several tissue types. Colocalization analysis supported a shared SNP, rs842357, in high linkage disequilibrium with rs1818613 (r(2) = 0. 94) driving both the observed interaction and the expression quantitative trait loci signals. Future studies are needed to confirm and understand the differential biologic mechanisms by smoking status that contribute to our PDAC findings. Significance: This large genome-wide interaction study identifies a susceptibility locus on 2q21.3 that significantly modified PDAC risk by smoking status, providing insight into smoking-associated PDAC, with implications for prevention.","author_count":77,"contributors":["Mocci, Evelina","Kundu, Prosenjit","Wheeler, William","Arslan, Alan A.","Beane-Freeman, Laura E.","Bracci, Paige M.","Brennan, Paul","Canzian, Federico","Du, Mengmeng","Gallinger, Steven","Giles, Graham G.","Goodman, Phyllis J.","Kooperberg, Charles","Le Marchand, Loic","Neale, Rachel E.","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Visvanathan, Kala","White, Emily","Zheng, Wei","Albanes, Demetrius","Andreotti, Gabriella","Babic, Ana","Bamlet, William R.","Berndt, Sonja","Blackford, Amanda L.","Bueno-de-Mesquita, Bas","Buring, Julie E.","Campa, Daniele","Chanock, Stephen J.","Childs, Erica J.","Duell, Eric J.","Fuchs, Charles S.","Gaziano, J. Michael","Giovannucci, Edward L.","Goggins, Michael G.","Hartge, Patricia","Hassan, Manal M.","Holly, Elizabeth A.","Hoover, Robert N.","Hung, Rayjean J.","Kurtz, Robert C.","Lee, I-Min","Malats, Nuria","Milne, Roger L.","Ng, Kimmie","Oberg, Ann L.","Panico, Salvatore","Peters, Ulrike","Porta, Miquel","Rabe, Kari G.","Riboli, Elio","Rothman, Nathaniel","Scelo, Ghislaine","Sesso, Howard D.","Silverman, Debra T.","Stevens, Victoria L.","Strobel, Oliver","Thompson, Ian M.","Tjønneland, Anne","Trichopoulou, Antonia","Van den Eeden, Stephen K.","Wactawski-Wende, Jean","Wentzensen, Nicolas","Wilkens, Lynne R.","Yu, Herbert","Yuan, Fangcheng","Zeleniuch-Jacquotte, Anne","Amundadottir, Laufey T.","Li, Donghui","Jacobs, Eric J.","Petersen, Gloria M.","Wolpin, Brian M.","Risch, Harvey A.","Kraft, Peter","Chatterjee, Nilanjan","Klein, Alison P.","Stolzenberg-Solomon, Rachael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-544085"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Malaysia","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amer Canc Soc, American Cancer Society, Behav & Epidemiol Res Grp","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","Boston Vet Affairs Healthcare Syst","Buffalo State College, State University of New York","CHRISTUS Santa Rosa Hosp Med Ctr","Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Imperial College London","Informat Management Serv Inc, Information Management Services, Inc.","International Agency for Research on Cancer (WHO-IARC), Lyon","Johns Hopkins University","Kaiser Permanente Northern Calif, Kaiser Permanente, Div Res","Mayo Clin, Mayo Clinic, Dept Hlth Sci Res, Coll Med","Mem Sloan Kettering Canc Ctr, Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center, Dept Epidemiol & Biostat","Mem Sloan Kettering Canc Ctr, Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center, Gastroenterol Hepatol & Nutr Serv","Monash University","National Institutes of Health","National and Kapodistrian University of Athens","New York University","QIMR Berghofer Med Res Inst, QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute, Dept Populat Hlth","Smilow Canc Hosp","Spanish Natl Canc Res Ctr, Spanish National Cancer Research Centre, Genet & Mol Epidemiol Grp","Univ Malaya, Universiti Malaya, Fac Med, Dept Social & Prevent Med","University of California San Francisco","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Naples Federico II","University of Pisa","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","Vanderbilt University","Yale University"],"keyword":["Anterior cingulate cortex","Cigarette smoking","GWAS","Genome wide association","Linkage","Metaanalysis","Protein","Susceptibility loci","TRENDS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"smoking modifies pancreatic cancer risk loci on 000000000002q000000000021 000000000003","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft