"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhenghui","key":"luozhenghuipau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Zhenghui","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Huiliang","key":"sunhuiliangpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Huiliang","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Lintao","key":"houlintaopau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Lintao","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Weiguo","key":"zhuweiguopau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Weiguo","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinhui","key":"luxinhuipau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Xinhui","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Feng","key":"gaofengpau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Feng","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen","key":"moonsellenpau","last":"Moons","name":"Moons, Ellen","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 10","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Donghong","key":"yudonghongpau","last":"Yu","locid":"9bf68567-02d0-41e9-a849-c0c03bbdfb9d","name":"Yu, Donghong","orcid":"0000-0002-3035-5035","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"He","key":"yanhepau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, He","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 11","corresponding":null,"first":"Ergang","key":"wangergangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ergang","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11426-021-1020-7","issn":["16747291","18691870"],"issn_org":["16747291"],"issue":"8","journal":"Science China Chemistry","pages":"1380-1388","publisher":"Science China Press","status":"p","title":"Science China Chemistry","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85112386404"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-11140217-2ec4-4c4e-9e5f-9ed1179d53ea"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"High-performance all-polymer solar cells enabled by a novel low bandgap non-fully conjugated polymer acceptor","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-055037","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: High incidence of asymptomatic venous thromboembolism (VTE) has been observed in severe COVID-19 patients, but the characteristics of symptomatic VTE in general COVID-19 patients have not been described. OBJECTIVES: To comprehensively explore the prevalence and reliable risk prediction for VTE in COVID-19 patients. METHODS/RESULTS: This retrospective study enrolled all COVID-19 patients with a subsequent VTE in 16 centers in China from January 1 to March 31, 2020. A total of 2779 patients were confirmed with COVID-19. In comparison with 23,434 non-COVID-19 medical inpatients, the ORs for developing symptomatic VTE in severe and non-severe hospitalized COVID-19 patients were 5.94 (95%CI 3.91 to 10.09) and 2.79 (95%CI 1.43 to 5.60), respectively. When 104 VTE cases and 208 Non-VTE cases were compared, pulmonary embolism cases had a higher rate for in-hospital death (OR 6.74, 95%CI 2.18 to 20.81). VTE developed at a median of 21 days (IQR 13.25 to 31) since onset. Independent factors for VTE were advancing age, cancer, longer interval from symptom onset to admission, lower fibrinogen and higher D-dimer on admission, and D-dimer increment (DI) ≥ 1.5 fold; of these, DI ≥ 1.5 fold had the most significant association (OR 14.18, 95%CI 6.25-32.18, P = 2.23 × 10-10 ). A novel model consisting of simple 3 coagulation variables (fibrinogen and D-dimer levels on admission, and DI ≥ 1.5 fold) showed good prediction for symptomatic VTE (AUC 0.865, 95%CI 0.822 to 0.907, sensitivity 0.930, specificity 0.710). CONCLUSIONS: There is an excess risk of VTE in hospitalized COVID-19 patients. The novel model can help early identification of patients who are at high risk for VTE.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Li, Jun-Ying","Wang, Hong-Fei","Yin, Ping","Li, Di","Wang, Di-Le","Peng, Peng","Wang, Wei-Hua","Wang, Lan","Yuan, Xiao-Wei","Xie, Jin-Yuan","Zhou, Fan","Xiong, Nian","Shao, Feng","Wang, Chun-Xiu","Tong, Xiang","Ye, Hao","Wan, Wen-Jun","Liu, Ben-De","Li, Wen-Zhu","Li, Qian","Tang, Liang V","Hu, Yu","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-067255"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["Thrombo-COVID-19 Collaborative"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Blood Center of Wuhan City","Central Hospital Of Wuhan","First People's Hospital of Jiangxia District","First People's Hospital of Jingmen","First People's Hospital of Tianmen City","Huang Gang Central Hospital","Huazhong University of Science and Technology","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","People's Hospital of Dongxihu District","People's Hospital of Honghu","People's Hospital of Jingshan","University of Liverpool","Wuhan Pulmonary Hospital","Xishui County People's Hospital","Yangtze University"],"keyword":["Covid 19","SARS CoV 2","Thrombosis","Venous thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical characteristics and risk factors for symptomatic venous thromboembolism in hospitalized covid 000000000019 patients a multicenter retrospective study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/404297303/Li_et_al._2021_Accepted_Article.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-067255","identifier":[{"id":"33534149","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85101664100","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3b5ac1cc-4017-41ea-99dd-208036b2b2c7"],"keyword":["COVID-19","D-dimer increment","SARS-CoV-2","thrombosis","venous thromboembolism"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBFAA9E40CA3F8FAE080A7BAD67FE306"],"oa_link":[{"acces