,"rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Hamid","key":"sarlakpau","last":"Sarlak","locid":"3daada7f-ac98-4ed9-9dad-600021965492","name":"Sarlak, Hamid","orcid":"0000-0003-4326-2695","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Edward","key":"ransleypau","last":"Ransley","name":"Ransley, Edward","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Scott","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, Scott","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Martyn","key":"hannpau","last":"Hann","name":"Hann, Martyn","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"netzbandpau","last":"Netzband","name":"Netzband, Stefan","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Malwin","key":"wermbterpau","last":"Wermbter","name":"Wermbter, Malwin","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"Beatriz","key":"méndezlópezpau","last":"Méndez López","name":"Méndez López, Beatriz","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.oceaneng.2021.110026","issn":["00298018","18735258"],"issn_org":["00298018"],"journal":"Ocean Engineering","paperid":"110026","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Ocean Engineering","volume":"241"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117226547"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4818eb24-0116-4823-9654-99e5c3f10d6a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"OC6 Phase Ib: Validation of the CFD predictions of difference-frequency wave excitation on a FOWT semisubmersible","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-326020","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The natural surge and pitch frequencies of semisubmersible offshore wind platforms are typically designed to be below the wave frequencies to avoid direct excitation. However, surge or pitch resonance can be excited by the nonlinear low-frequency loads generated by irregular incident waves. Second-order potential-flow models with added Morison drag have been found to underpredict this low-frequency excitation and response. As part of the OC6 project1, the authors performed computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulations to enable a better understanding of the low-frequency loads and the limitations of lower-fidelity models. The focus of this paper is to set up a computationally cost-effective CFD simulation of a fixed semisubmersible platform to investigate nonlinear differencefrequency loads and establish the corresponding uncertainty in the results. Because of the high computing cost, CFD simulations of irregular waves can be challenging. Instead, simulations were performed with bichromatic waves having a shorter repeat period. A preliminary comparison with quadratic transfer functions from second-order potential-flow theory shows that CFD models consistently predict higher nonlinear wave loads at the difference frequency, likely because of flow separation and viscous drag not accounted for in potential-flow theory.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Wang, Lu","Robertson, Amy","Jonkman, Jason","Yu, Yi-Hsiang","Koop, Arjen","Nadal, Adrià Borràs","Li, Haoran","Shi, Wei","Pinguet, Romain","Zhou, Yang","Xiao, Qing","Kumar, Rupesh","Sarlak, Hamid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331074"],"event":{"end":"2021-02-17","place":"Online event","start":"2021-02-16","title":"ASME 2021 3rd International Offshore Wind Technical Conference","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Netherlands","Norway","South Korea","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dalian University of Technology","IFP Énergies nouvelles","Maritime Research Institute Netherlands","National Renewable Energy Laboratory","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Principle Power, Inc.","University of Strathclyde","University of Ulsan"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of nonlinear difference frequency wave excitation on a semisubmersible offshore wind platform with bichromatic wave cfd simulations","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85099207391","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331074","identifier":[{"id":"85099207391","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-592b7553-b215-4ecd-ab17-ba3083124afb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83DB6671454DEF1113496380B1A329E8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"national renewable energy laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Renewable Energy Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"maritime research institute netherlands","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Maritime Research Institute Netherlands","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"ifp énergies nouvelles","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"IFP Énergies nouvelles","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"dalian university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Dalian Un