{"abstract":"The Indo-Pacific humpback dolphin (Sousa chinensis) is a small inshore species of odontocete cetacean listed as Vulnerable on the IUCN Red List. Here, we report on the evolution of S. chinensis chromosomes from its cetruminant ancestor and elucidate the evolutionary history and population genetics of two neighboring S. chinensis populations. We found that breakpoints in ancestral chromosomes leading to S. chinensis could have affected the function of genes related to kidney filtration, body development, and immunity. Resequencing of individuals from two neighboring populations in the northwestern South China Sea, Leizhou Bay and Sanniang Bay, revealed genetic differentiation, low diversity, and small contemporary effective population sizes. Demographic analyses showed a marked decrease in the population size of the two investigated populations over the last ~4,000 years, possibly related to climatic oscillations. This study implies a high risk of extinction and strong conservation requirement for the Indo-Pacific humpback dolphin.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Zhang, Peijun","Zhao, Yong","Li, Chang","Lin, Mingli","Dong, Lijun","Zhang, Rui","Liu, Mingzhong","Li, Kuan","Zhang, He","Liu, Xiaochuan","Zhang, Yaolei","Yuan, Yuan","Liu, Huan","Seim, Inge","Sun, Shuai","Du, Xiao","Chang, Yue","Li, Feida","Liu, Shanshan","Lee, Simon Ming-Yuen","Wang, Kun","Wang, Ding","Wang, Xianyan","McGowen, Michael R.","Jefferson, Thomas A.","Olsen, Morten Tange","Stiller, Josefin","Zhang, Guojie","Xu, Xun","Yang, Huanming","Fan, Guangyi","Liu, Xin","Li, Songhai"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-037733"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Fan, Guangyi"],"country":["Australia","China","Hong Kong","Macao","Singapore","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","BGI Group","China National GeneBank","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Clymene Enterprises","Hong Kong Baptist University","Huazhong Agricultural University","Ministry of Land and Resources P.R.C.","Ministry of Natural Resources","Nanjing Normal University","National University of Singapore","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","Qingdao National Laboratory for Marine Science and Technology","Queensland University of Technology","Smithsonian Institution","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Macau","Xi'an Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["Evolutionary biology","Genetics","Genomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an indo pacific humpback dolphin genome reveals insights into chromosome evolution and the demography of a vulnerable species","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2020.101640","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-037733","identifier":[{"id":"85092632069","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33103078","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7569330","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-e64ee754-21bb-46cb-b06a-21f49da1a862","ku-1fc6be25-eddc-4b5d-bf98-a088cc9e0946"],"keyword":["Evolutionary Biology","Genetics","Genomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C11E156DFB35EFDEC5ACFF146B0FB812"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250864782/An_Indo_Pacific_Humpback_Dolphin_Genome_Reveals_Insights_into_Chromosome_Evolution_and_the_Demography_of_a_Vulnerable_Species.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.202