{"abstract":"An improved understanding of the origin of the electrocatalytic activity is of importance to the rational design of highly efficient electrocatalysts for the hydrogen evolution reaction. Here, an ambipolar single-crystal tungsten diselenide (WSe2) semiconductor is employed as a model system where the conductance and carrier of WSe2 can be individually tuned by external electric fields. The field-tuned electrochemical microcell is fabricated based on the single-crystal WSe2 and the catalytic activity of the WSe2 microcell is measured versus the external electric field. Results show that WSe2 with electrons serving as the dominant carrier yields much higher activity than WSe2 with holes serving as the dominant carrier even both systems exhibit similar conductance. The catalytic activity enhancement can be characterized by the Tafel slope decrease from 138 to 104 mV per decade, while the electron area concentration increases from 0.64 × 1012 to 1.72 × 1012 cm−2. To further understand the underlying mechanism, the Gibbs free energy and charge distribution for adsorbed hydrogen on WSe2 versus the area charge concentration is systematically computed, which is in line with experiments. This comprehensive study not only sheds light on the mechanism underlying the electrocatalysis processes, but also offers a strategy to achieve higher electrocatalytic activity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Wang, Zegao","Wu, Hong Hui","Li, Qiang","Besenbacher, Flemming","Li, Yanrong","Zeng, Xiao Cheng","Dong, Mingdong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-187095"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zeng, Xiao Cheng"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shandong University","Sichuan University","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","University of Nebraska-Lincoln","University of Science and Technology Beijing"],"keyword":["Density function theory","FIELD","Hydrogen evolution","MoS2","Nanosheets","SITES","Transistors","model catalysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reversing interfacial catalysis of ambipolar wse sub 000000000002 sub single crystal","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.201901382","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-187095","identifier":[{"id":"000500653100001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85076104767","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32042552","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7001631","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-651c9076-2796-433b-94f6-9911cfbefdaf"],"keyword":["FIELD","MOS2","NANOSHEETS","SITES","TRANSISTORS","ambipolar carrier","density function theory","electrochemical microcells","hydrogen evolution","model catalysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE99C2CC50D26E467860FD767A3CB9F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.201901382","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of nebraska lincoln","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Nebraska-Lincoln","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology Beijing","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zegao","key":"wangzegaopau","last":"Wang","locid":"2f191f69-88c1-4291-8610-6d3b85bbc312","name":"Wang, Zegao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong Hui","key":"wuhonghuipau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Hong Hui","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiang","key":"liqiangpau","last":"Li","locid":"f5d17801-6cfb-4c75-8f63-7bdb69eb130c","name":"Li, Qiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"besenbacherflemmingpau","last":"Besenbacher","locid":"0aa89800-dd75-4f15-a575-c419dda7a69f","name":"Besenbacher, Flemming","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanrong","key":"liyanrongpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yanrong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Cheng","key":"zengxiaochengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Xiao Cheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mingdong","key":"dongmingdongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32042552"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/advs.201901382","issn":["21983844"],"issue":"3","journal":"Advanced Science","paperid":"1901382","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Advanced Science","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076104767"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-651c9076-2796-433b-94f6-9911cfbefdaf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reversing Interfacial Catalysis of Ambipolar WSe<sub>2</sub> Single Crystal","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-187095","year":"2020","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Tamarix chinensis is a dominant species in both the Yellow River Delta Natural Reserve and Changyi National Marine Specific Protection Area, Laizhou Bay, China, and plays an important role in wetland ecosystems. We investigated the relationship between T. chinensis and environmental factors, and the influences of T. chinensis on understory plants. We selected four T. chinensis communities with different hydrologic conditions and salinities in the Yellow River Delta Natural Reserve and the Changyi National Marine Specific Protection Area. The results showed that the growth of T. chinensis was negatively correlated with soil salinity. Generally no fertile island effects or salt island effects of T. chinensis on herbaceous plant communities were found in the coastal area of Laizhou Bay, China. In areas with high salinity, T. chinensis provided nursery effects for understory herbaceous species, increasing species diversity and enhancing plant growth. In low-salinity environments, T. chinensis appeared to restrain the growth of understory plants. This study observed different influences of T. chinensis on herbaceous species between the Yellow River Delta Natural Reserve and Changyi National Marine Specific Protection Area, providing scientific basis and theoretical foundation for investigating plant distribution and ecological community succession in Laizhou Bay, China.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Zhou, Dayou","Guo, Weihua","Li, Mingyan","Eller, Franziska","Zhang, Cheyu","Wu, Pan","Yi, Shijie","Yang, Shuren","Du, Ning","Yu, Xiaona","Guo, Xiao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259667"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Xiao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qingdao Agricultural University","Shandong University"],"keyword":["Biodiversity","Laizhou Bay","Salinity","Yellow River Delta"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no fertile island effects or salt island effects of i tamarix chinensis i on understory herbaceous communities were found in the coastal area of laizhou bay china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85087137789","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-259667","identifier":[{"id":"85087137789","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000552427800002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-e442e27b-0456-4c4e-a1e5-42a45b25cdfb"],"keyword":["Biodiversity","Laizhou Bay","Nursery effects","Salinity","Tamarix chinensis","Yellow River Delta"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E817B539125318EE822F47183F0E081"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"qingdao agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dayou","key":"zhoudayoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Dayou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Weihua","key":"guoweihuapau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Weihua","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingyan","key":"limingyanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Mingyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cheyu","key":"zhangcheyupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Cheyu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pan","key":"wupanpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Pan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shijie","key":"yishijiepau","last":"Yi","name":"Yi, Shijie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuren","key":"yangshurenpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Shuren","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"duningpau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Ning","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaona","key":"yuxiaonapau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Xiaona","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"guoxiaopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13157-020-01316-2","issn":["02775212","19436246"],"issn_org":["02775212"],"issue":"6","journal":"Wetlands","pages":"2679-2689","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media BV","publisher_org":"Springer Science and Business Media B.V.","status":"p","title":"Wetlands","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087137789"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e442e27b-0456-4c4e-a1e5-42a45b25cdfb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"No fertile island effects or salt island effects of <i>Tamarix chinensis </i>on understory herbaceous communities were found in the coastal area of Laizhou Bay, China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-259667","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Cardiovascular development critical genes are key determinants in cardiovascular diseases. We hypothesize that SNPs in these genes may play critical roles in the development of hypertension. Therefore, we enrolled 516 paired hypertension patients and controls in a total of 2,742 subjects in a cross-sectional population study by the propensity score matching (PSM) method. Twenty-one SNPs from 5 cardiovascular developmental related genes were detected by the improved multiplex ligase detection reaction (iMLDR) method. Conditioned logistic regression under three different genetic models, namely, additive model, dominant model, and recessive model, was performed. The odds ratio (ORs) and 95% confidence intervals (95% CIs) were used to estimate the associations of SNPs with hypertension. We found that the distribution of genotypes at rs833061, rs3025010, and rs699947 within the VEGFA gene and the distribution of alleles at rs3025010 in hypertension subjects were different from those in controls. Both rs833061 and rs3025010 were associated with hypertension in crude models, but only rs3025010 remains associated with hypertension after adjusting with confounding factors in the additive model and the dominant model. We also found that hypertension subjects with C/T and C/C genotypes at rs3025010 had lower SBP and DBP levels. In addition, rs3025010 could interact with rs6784267 within the CCM3 gene in the association. In conclusion, our findings suggest that rs3025010 may play a role in the pathogenesis of hypertension, which may be a potential target for individualized prevention and treatment of hypertension.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Zhao, Zhiqiang","Gong, Chunmei","Gao, Yanfang","Liu, Xiaoli","Wu, Sai","Zhao, Heping","Wang, Xiaohui","Liu, Huaixiang","Xiao, Chen","Liu, Jieyi","Li, Jiong","He, Yun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-261765"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["He, Yun"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Gannan Medical College","Sun Yat-Sen University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between single nucleotide polymorphisms in cardiovascular developmental critical genes and hypertension a propensity score matching analysis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2020/9185697","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-261765","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7106934","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32257424","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85082764486","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e80f5c06-bd24-4ecb-801a-fceb62567caa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48528F09CAAF6AADA5CD7E6FFB71CC18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2020/9185697","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"gannan medical college","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Gannan Medical College","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"na