"first":"Wim","key":"timenswimpau","last":"Timens","name":"Timens, Wim","rank":104,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"55 56","first":"María Soler","key":"artigasmaríasolerpau","last":"Artigas","name":"Artigas, María Soler","rank":105,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"57","first":"Sanjay","key":"shetesanjaypau","last":"Shete","name":"Shete, Sanjay","rank":106,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"58","first":"Hermann","key":"brennerhermannpau","last":"Brenner","name":"Brenner, Hermann","rank":107,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Stephen","key":"chanockstephenpau","last":"Chanock","name":"Chanock, Stephen","rank":108,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"Paul","key":"brennanpaulpau","last":"Brennan","name":"Brennan, Paul","rank":109,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","first":"James D.","key":"mckayjamesdpau","last":"McKay","name":"McKay, James D.","rank":110,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 59","first":"Christopher I.","key":"amoschristopheripau","last":"Amos","name":"Amos, Christopher I.","rank":111,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32393777"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-020-15905-6","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"2220","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084474621"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-634346e4-5dcb-4714-b8d3-7a16a737bf8a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protein-altering germline mutations implicate novel genes related to lung cancer development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452821","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Non-obstructive azoospermia (NOA) is the most severe form of male infertility. However, the etiology of NOA is largely unknown, resulting in a lack of clinical treatments. Here, we performed a comparative genome-wide profiling of DNA methylation and identified SOX30 as the most notably hyper-methylated gene at promoter in testicular tissues from NOA patients. This hyper-methylation at promoter of SOX30 directly causes its silencing of expression in NOA. The reduced levels of SOX30 expression are correlated with severity of NOA disease. Deletion of Sox30 in mice uniquely impairs testis development and spermatogenesis with complete absence of spermatozoa in testes leading to male infertility, but does not influence ovary development and female fertility. The pathology and testicular size of Sox30 null mice highly simulate those of NOA patients. Re-expression of Sox30 in Sox30 null mice at adult age reverses the pathological damage of testis and restores the spermatogenesis. The re-presented spermatozoa after re-expression of Sox30 in Sox30 null mice have the ability to start a pregnancy. Moreover, the male offspring of Sox30 re-expression Sox30 null mice still can father children, and these male offspring and their children can live normally more than 1 year without significant difference of physical appearance compared with wild-type mice. In summary, methylated inactivation of SOX30 uniquely impairs spermatogenesis, probably causing NOA disease, and re-expression of SOX30 can successfully restore the spermatogenesis and actual fertility. This study advances our understanding of the pathogenesis of NOA, offering a promising therapy target for NOA disease.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Han, Fei","Jiang, Xiao","Li, Zhi ming","Zhuang, Xuan","Zhang, Xi","Ouyang, Wei ming","Liu, Wen bin","Mao, Cheng yi","Chen, Qing","Huang, Chuan shu","Gao, Fei","Cui, Zhi hong","Ao, Lin","Li, Yan feng","Cao, Jia","Liu, Jin yi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-517073"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Male infertility","Methylation","Non obstructive azoospermia","Spermatogenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epigenetic inactivation of sox000000000030 is associated with male infertility and offers a therapy target for non obstructive azoospermia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtn.2019.10.038","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-517073","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6926170","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85076053801","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31835093","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-cef0ab89-6045-42c0-aa20-7f5a17717e2d"],"keyword":["male infertility","methylation","non-obstructive azoospermia","spermatogenesis","therapy target"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B144D7F759A6017650B156D12A7D66DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.omtn.2019.10.038","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/234208621/1_s2.0_S216225311930349X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Comparative Pediatrics and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Fei","key":"hanfeipau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Fei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao","key":"jiangxiaopau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Xiao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhi ming","key":"lizhimingpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhi ming","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xuan","key":"zhuangxuanpau","last":"Zhuang","name":"Zhuang, Xuan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xi","key":"zhangxipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wei ming","key":"ouyangweimingpau","last":"Ouyang","name":"Ouyang, Wei ming","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wen bin","key":"liuwenbinpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Wen bin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cheng yi","key":"maochengyipau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Cheng yi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qing","key":"chenqingpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Qing","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chuan shu","key":"huangchuanshupau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Chuan shu","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fei","key":"gaofeipau","last":"Gao","locid":"70b6cfb5-ec35-418f-8f24-520bb5696a8d","name":"Gao, Fei","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhi hong","key":"cuizhihongpau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Zhi hong","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lin","key":"aolinpau","last":"Ao","name":"Ao, Lin","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yan feng","key":"liyanfengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yan feng","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jia","key":"caojiapau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Jia","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jin yi","key":"liujinyipau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jin yi","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31835093"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.omtn.2019.10.038","issn":["21622531"],"journal":"Molecular Therapy - Nucleic Acids","pages":"72-83","status":"p","title":"Molecular Therapy - Nucleic Acids","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076053801"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cef0ab89-6045-42c0-aa20-7f5a17717e2d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Epigenetic Inactivation of SOX30 Is Associated with Male Infertility and Offers a Therapy Target for Non-obstructive Azoospermia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-517073","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We investigated the role of PRMT5 in MPN pathogenesis and aimed to elucidate key PRMT5 targets contributing to MPN maintenance. PRMT5 is overexpressed in primary MPN cells and PRMT5 inhibition potently reduced MPN cell proliferation ex vivo. PRMT5 inhibition was efficacious at reversing elevated hematocrit, leukocytosis and splenomegaly in a model of JAK2V617F+ polycythemia vera (PV) and leukocyte and platelet counts, hepatosplenomegaly and fibrosis in the MPLW515L model of myelofibrosis (MF). Dual targeting of JAK and PRMT5 was superior to JAK or PRMT5 inhibitor monotherapy, further decreasing elevated counts and extramedullary hematopoiesis in vivo. PRMT5 inhibition reduced expression of E2F targets and altered the methylation status of E2F1 leading to attenuated DNA damage repair, cell cycle arrest and increased apoptosis. Our data link PRMT5 to E2F1 regulatory function and MPN cell survival and provide a strong mechanistic rationale for clinical trials of PRMT5 inhibitors in MPN.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Pastore, Friederike","Bhagwat, Neha","Pastore, Alessandro","Radzisheuskaya, Aliaksandra","Karzai, Abdul","Krishnan, Aishwarya","Li, Bing","Bowman, Robert L","Xiao, Wenbin","Viny, Aaron D","Zouak, Anouar","Park, Young C","Cordner, Keith B","Braunstein, Stephanie","Maag, Jesper L V","Grego, Alexander","Mehta, Jaanvi","Wang, Min","Lin, Hong","Durham, Benjamin H","Koche, Richard P","Rampal, Raajit K","Helin, Kristian","Scherle, Peggy","Vaddi, Kris","Levine, Ross L"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-524711"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Forest Research, Northern Research Station","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Human Oncology and Pathogenesis Program"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prmt000000000005 inhibition modulates e000000000002f000000000001 methylation and gene regulatory networks leading to therapeutic efficacy in jak000000000002v000000000617f mutant mpn","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7642059/pdf/nihms-1613154.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-524711","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7642059","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85089385706","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32669286","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-dbce1534-6822-4572-9f0c-d23314b37a5b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9BC3000E29EBC3FAB1E5A0CA32CC5824"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7642059/pdf/nihms-1613154.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Human Oncology and Pathogenesis Program"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"memorial sloan kettering cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["De