:"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085961865"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cb3a4de4-bdd0-49cb-9fdb-48e8f6b4b9dc","au-0614156b-a2c0-4741-8d9d-246492a23d0e","ku-65e1ef68-98b7-4f78-b688-37925d743acd","sdu-566c67c1-87eb-413a-9d2e-5d75456e53ec"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cohort Profile : The Copenhagen Child Cohort Study (CCC2000)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-098.64-009748","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: This paper aims to attempt to explore the influence of network position on innovation performance, specifically for companies from a less-developed area in China. Design/methodology/approach: The paper uses a social network analysis method based on the data of high and new tech companies from Jiangxi province, China. It relies on Ucinet 6.212 software for data processing. Findings: The present work, on the one hand, reveals that a high and new tech company from Jiangxi province tends to achieve better innovation performances if it is in the central position of its social network. On the other hand, it indicates that the same type of company from the same area does not always accomplish better innovation performance, even it possesses more structural holes. Originality/value: The conclusions of this paper suggest that a high and new tech company from a less-developed area in China should build up its position closer to the center when constructing a social network. Meanwhile, the company should also exert more effort into managing its networks, as only building structural holes offers little help with operations besides showing that it has a broad social network.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Min","Xiao, F.","Cheng, Yang","Xie, B.","Liu, C.","Xu, B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053463"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangxi University of Finance and Economics"],"keyword":["Innovation performance","Network position","Social network"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the relationship between network position and innovation performance evidence from a social network analysis of high and new tech companies from a less developed area in china","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85075935359&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053463","identifier":[{"id":"85075935359","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0bb8b2eb-2b63-468f-ae56-785a922a0096"],"keyword":["High and new tech companies","Innovation performance","Jiangxi province","Network position","Social network"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C89C6E4F8DC11427060A0B1BC37BA8A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangxi university of finance and economics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangxi University of Finance and Economics","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Sustainable Operations and Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Min","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yang","key":"chengpau","last":"Cheng","locid":"879b5c5d-06e0-4733-a85b-3ad6e8a340c2","name":"Cheng, Yang","orcid":"0000-0002-3082-4890","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"xiepau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, B.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/cms-10-2018-0717","issn":["1750614X","17506158"],"issn_org":["1750614X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Chinese Management Studies","pages":"93-111","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing Limited","status":"p","title":"Chinese Management Studies","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075935359"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0bb8b2eb-2b63-468f-ae56-785a922a0096"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Exploring the relationship between network position and innovation performance : Evidence from a social network analysis of high and new tech companies from a less-developed area in China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053463","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"High frequency (HF) ac linked converter functions well to interface between buses with different voltage types. Using a three-phase-to-single-phase matrix converter, a single-phase cyclo converter, and a HF transformer, we can compose a HF ac linked converter to interface between three-phase ac grids and single-phase ac or dc distributed generations (DGs). In this paper, a novel space vector modulation (SVM) method is proposed for such kind of converter. The proposed SVM method converts the mains three-phase ac voltage to a HF ac voltage at the primary side of transformer, and then unfolds the HF ac voltage to a single-phase ac or dc voltage at the secondary side of transformer. Without need to compute separate switching signals for the primary and secondary converters and then coordinate their operations elaborately, the proposed SVM method can be easily implemented by incorporating the HF chopping into the SVM of traditional indirect matrix converter. Therefore, no complicated duty cycle computation or elaborate switching states combination is required. Simulation and hardware-in-loop implementation demonstrate the validity of the proposed method.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liu, Yushan","He, Jie","Ge, Baoming","Li, Xiao","Xue, Yaosuo","Blaabjerg, Frede"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065193"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beihang University","Oak Ridge National Laboratory","Texas A&M University"],"keyword":["Distributed generations","Matrix converter","Space vector modulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a simple space vector modulation of high frequency ac linked three phase to single phase dc converter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.2978886","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-065193","identifier":[{"id":"85083197051","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3431078b-fad4-4841-a6d9-7d6362c7c895"],"keyword":["High-frequency ac","distributed generations","matrix converter","space vector modulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51CC004234399D8F037BF1BC993C0E67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.2978886","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/406319139/09026877.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beihang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beihang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"texas a m university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Texas A&M University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"oak ridge national laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Oak Ridge National Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yushan","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yushan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Jie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Baoming","key":"gepau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Baoming","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yaosuo","key":"xuepau","last":"Xue","name":"Xue, Yaosuo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Frede","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"22b09e36-1f7b-4d33-90bf-918730e1d09a","name":"Blaabjerg, Frede","orcid":"0000-0001-8311-7412","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2020.2978886","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","pages":"59278-59289","paperid":"9026877","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083197051"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3431078b-fad4-4841-a6d9-7d6362c7c895"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Simple Space Vector Modulation of High-Frequency AC Linked Three-Phase-to-Single-Phase/DC Converter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065193","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Obtaining both high open-circuit voltage (Voc) and short-circuit current density (Jsc) has been a major challenge for efficient all-polymer solar cells (all-PSCs). Herein, we developed a polymer acceptor PF5-Y5 with excellent optical absorption capability (onset extending to ∼880 nm and maximum absorption coefficient exceeding 105 cm-1 in a film), high electron mobility (3.18 × 10-3 cm2 V-1 s-1) and high LUMO level (-3.84 eV) to address such a challenge. As a result, the PBDB-T:PF5-Y5-based all-PSCs achieved a high power conversion efficiency of up to 14.45% with both a high Voc (0.946 V) and a high Jsc (20.65 mA cm-2), due to the high and broad absorption coverage, small energy loss (0.57 eV) and efficient charge separation and transport in the device, which are among the best values in the all-PSC field. In addition, the all-PSC shows a ∼15% improvement in PCE compared to its counterpart small molecule acceptor (Y5)-based device. Our results suggest that PF5-Y5 is a very promising polymer acceptor candidate for applications in efficient all-PSCs. This journal is","author_count":19,"contributors":["Fan, Qunping","An, Qiaoshi","Lin, Yuanbao","Xia, Yuxin","Li, Qian","Zhang, Ming","Su, Wenyan","Peng, Wenhong","Zhang, Chunfeng","Liu, Feng","Hou, Lintao","Zhu, Weiguo","Yu, Donghong","Xiao, Min","Moons, Ellen","Zhang, Fujun","Anthopoulos, Thomas D.","Inganäs, Olle","Wang, Ergang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-102397"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Ergang"],"country":["China","Saudi Arabia","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing Institute of Technology","Beijing Jiaotong University","Chalmers University of Technology","Changzhou University","Jinan University","Karlstad University","King Abdullah University of Science and Technology","Linköping University","Nanjing University","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Sino-Danish Center for Education and Research","Zhengzhou University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"over 000000000014 efficiency all polymer solar cells enabled by a low bandgap polymer acceptor with low energy loss and efficient charge separation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d0ee01828g","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the Swedish Research Council (2015-04853, 2016-06146, 2019-04683), the Swedish Research Council Formas, and the Wallenberg Foundation (2017.0186, 2016.0059) for financial support. D. Y. is thankful for the financial support from Innovation fund Denmark (INKA project) and Sino-Danish Centre for Education and Research (SDC). Y. L. and T. D. A. acknowledge support from the King Abdullah University of Science and Technology (KAUST) and Office of Sponsored Research (OSR) under Award No: OSR-2018-CARF/CCF-3079. W. S. is thankful for the project funded by Jinan University Postdoctoral Science Foundation, China Postdoctoral Science Foundation (2020M673054), and National Natural Science Foundation of China (22005121). Q. A. is thankful for the project funded by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (61805009)."],"id":"S01-000.00-102397","identifier":[{"id":"85098322481","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b43c5f05-97cb-4620-ae4b-5c849b6dfc6b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-36020F2967F788A296C0BB48FEDF1AE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/d0ee01828g","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.