u","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Yanhong","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32405021"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-020-2243-7","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7807","journal":"Nature","pages":"159-163","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"581"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084625937"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6bd0cd6b-ec96-41ff-b0d9-baf94c9ac4f2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Spin squeezing of 10<sup>11</sup> atoms by prediction and retrodiction measurements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-190839","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Strict medication guidance and lifestyle interventions to manage blood pressure (BP) in hypertensive patients are typically difficult to follow. Objective: To evaluate the 1-year effectiveness of lifestyle and drug intervention in the management of rural hypertensive patients. Design: Randomized community intervention trial. Participants: The control group comprised 967 patients who received standard antihypertensive drug intervention therapy from two communities, whereas the intervention group comprised 1945 patients who received antihypertensive drug and lifestyle intervention therapies from four communities in rural China. Main Measures: Data on lifestyle behaviors and BP measurements at baseline and 1-year follow-up were collected. A difference-in-difference logistic regression model was used to assess the effect of the intervention. Key Results: BP control after the 1-year intervention was better than that at baseline in both groups. The within-group change in BP control of 59.3% in the intervention group was much higher than the 25.2% change in the control group (P < 0.001). Along with the duration of the follow-up period, systolic and diastolic BP decreased rapidly in the early stages and then gradually after 6 months in the intervention group (P < 0.001). In the intervention group, drug therapy adherence was increased by 39.5% (from 48.1% at 1 month to 87.6% at 1 year) (P < 0.001), more in women (45.6%) than in men (31.2%; P < 0.001). The net effect of the lifestyle intervention improved the rate of BP control by 56.1% (70.8% for men and 44.7% for women). For all physiological and biochemical factors, such as body mass index, waist circumference, lipid metabolism, and glucose control, improvements were more significant in the behavioral intervention group than those in the control group (all P < 0.001). Conclusion: The addition of lifestyle intervention by physicians or nurses helps control BP effectively and lowers BP better than usual care with antihypertensive drug therapy alone.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Xiao, Jing","Ren, Wen Long","Liang, Yuan Yuan","Shen, Huan","Gao, Yue Xia","Chu, Min Jie","Li, Zhou","Wang, Xiao Jian","Zhang, Zuo Feng","Zhuang, Xun","Yu, Yongfu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-231475"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zhuang, Xun"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nantong University","University of California at Los Angeles"],"keyword":["Effectiveness","Hypertension","Lifestyle intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness of lifestyle and drug intervention on hypertensive patients a randomized community intervention trial in rural china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85092150669","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-231475","identifier":[{"id":"85092150669","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33021715","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7728841","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-b303ba34-ef5e-4a59-ad17-97a8bd6c4bea"],"keyword":["blood pressure control rate","effectiveness","hypertension","lifestyle intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0EA073DE72AE49E40DC285818366FB55"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nantong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nantong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at los angeles","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Los Angeles","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen Long","key":"renpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Wen Long","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuan Yuan","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Yuan Yuan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Huan","key":"shenpau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Huan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yue Xia","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Yue Xia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Min Jie","key":"chupau","last":"Chu","name":"Chu, Min Jie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhou","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhou","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Jian","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao Jian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zuo Feng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zuo Feng","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xun","key":"zhuangpau","last":"Zhuang","name":"Zhuang, Xun","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong Fu","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","locid":"06be533f-163e-454d-bd55-9219a4f5cafa","name":"Yu, Yongfu","name_org":"Yu, Yong Fu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33021715"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11606-019-05601-7","issn":["08848734","15251497"],"issn_org":["08848734"],"issue":"12","journal":"Journal of General Internal Medicine","pages":"3449-3457","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of General Internal Medicine","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092150669"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b303ba34-ef5e-4a59-ad17-97a8bd6c4bea"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effectiveness of Lifestyle and Drug Intervention on Hypertensive Patients : a Randomized Community Intervention Trial in Rural China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-231475","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Estuaries are dynamic and selective environments that provide frequent opportunities for the turnover of Phragmites australis populations. We studied Phragmites genetic diversity patterns in three of the major deltas of China, viz. the Yellow River, the Yangtze and the Liaohe, in relation to Phragmites global phylogeography and soil salinity. We found that two distantly related P. australis haplotypes, each with intercontinental distribution, co-occur in these deltas in China. One is European Phragmites (Haplotype O) and is related to P. japonicus; the other (Haplotype P) has its range in East Asia and Australia and is related to the Asian tropical species P. karka. The two haplotypes have differing salt tolerance, with Haplotype O in areas with the highest salinity and Haplotype P in areas with the lowest. Introgressed hybrids of Haplotype P with P. karka, and F1 hybrids with Haplotype O, have higher salt tolerance than Haplotype P. Phylogenetic diversity appears as the factor that better explains population structure and salinity tolerance in these estuaries. Future research may explain whether the two P. australis haplotypes evolved in East Asia, and East Asia is a center of Phragmites diversity, or are introduced and a threat to P. japonicus and P. karka.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lambertini, Carla","Guo, Wen Yong","Ye, Siyuan","Eller, Franziska","Guo, Xiao","Li, Xiu-Zhen","Sorrell, Brian Keith","Speranza, Maria","Brix, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","East China Normal University","Qingdao Institute of Marine Geology","University of Bologna"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phylogenetic diversity shapes salt tolerance in i phragmites australis i estuarine populations in east china","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-74727-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239159","identifier":[{"id":"85092786744","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7572363","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33077795","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c079bf68-6c09-4915-93d1-5f2fdc1300cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EFE95B93B8C1D0B49D3F7EDF982150F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-74727-0","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"qingdao institute of marine geology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Institute of Marine Geology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"east china normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China Normal University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carla","key":"lambertinicarlapau","last":"Lambertini","locid":"539cdc5f-a62e-4b9d-bd32-6316a6003286","name":"Lambertini, Carla","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen-Yong","key":"guowenyongpau","last":"Guo","locid":"0061a6f4-1828-4e8d-899f-759e877791a6","name":"Guo, Wen Yong","name_org":"Guo, Wen-Yong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyuan","key":"yesiyuanpau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Siyuan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"guoxiaopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiu-Zhen","key":"lixiuzhenpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiu-Zhen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian K","key":"sorrellbriankeithpau","last":"Sorrell","locid":"40386ff0-c1da-4809-8d85-2a247fb590f6","name":"Sorrell, Brian Keith","name_org":"Sorrell, Brian K","orcid":"0000-0002-2460-8438","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"speranzamariapau","last":"Speranza","name":"Speranza, Maria","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"brixhanspau","last":"Brix","locid":"4068bdb4-1c13-432c-b420-3991683780b5","name":"Brix, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-2771-2983","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33077795"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-020-74727-0","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"17645","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092786744"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c079bf68-6c09-4915-93d1-5f2fdc1300cb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Phylogenetic diversity shapes salt tolerance in <i>Phragmites australis </i>estuarine populations in East China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239159","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Integrated optics provides a versatile platform for quantum information processing and transceiving with photons1–8. The implementation of quantum protocols requires the capability to generate multiple high-quality single photons and process photons with multiple high-fidelity operators9–11. However, previous experimental demonstrations were faced by major challenges in realizing sufficiently high-quality multi-photon sources and multi-qubit operators in a single integrated system4–8, and fully chip-based implementations of multi-qubit quantum tasks remain a significant challenge1–3. Here, we report the demonstration of chip-to-chip quantum teleportation and genuine multipartite entanglement, the core functionalities in quantum technologies, on silicon-photonic circuitry. Four single photons with high purity and indistinguishablity are produced in an array of microresonator sources, without requiring any spectral filtering. Up to four qubits are processed in a reprogrammable linear-optic quantum circuit that facilitates Bell projection and fusion operation. The generation, processing, transceiving and measurement of multi-photon multi-qubit states are all achieved in micrometre-scale silicon chips, fabricated by the complementary metal–oxide–semiconductor process. Our work lays the groundwork for large-scale integrated photonic quantum technologies for communications and computations.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Llewellyn, Daniel","Ding, Yunhong","Faruque, Imad I.","Paesani, Stefano","Bacco, Davide","Santagati, Raffaele","Qian, Yan Jun","Li, Yan","Xiao, Yun Feng","Huber, Marcus","Malik, Mehul","Sinclair, Gary F.","Zhou, Xiaoqi","Rottwitt, Karsten","O’Brien, Jeremy L.","Rarity, John G.","Gong, Qihuang","Oxenløwe, Leif Katsuo","Wang, Jianwei","Thompson, Mark G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356441"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Jianwei"],"country":["Australia","Austria","China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Austrian Academy of Sciences","Beijing Academy of Quantum Information Sciences","Heriot-Watt University","Peking University","Sun Yat-Sen University","University of Bristol","University of Western Australia"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chip to chip quantum teleportation and multi photon entanglement in silicon","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/208913063/s41567_020_0840_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank G.J. Mendoza and D. Bonneau for useful discussions. We thank W.A. Murray, M. Loutit, E. Johnston, J.W. Silverstone and L. Kling for experimental assistance. We acknowledge support from the National Key R&D Program of China (2019YFA0308700, 2018YFB1107205), the Natural Science Foundation of China (nos 61975001, 61590933, 11527901 and 11825402), Beijing Natural Science Foundation (Z190005), Beijing Academy of Quantum Information Sciences (Y18G21) and Key R&D Program of Guangdong Province (2018B030329001). Y.D. acknowledges support from Denmark SPOC (DNRF123), Villum Fonden, QUANPIC (00025298). I.I.F. acknowledges support from the FP7 Marie Curie Initial Training Network PICQUE (608062). M.H. acknowledges support from the Austrian Science Fund (FWF) through the START project (Y879-N27) and the joint Czech–Austrian project MultiQUEST (I 3053-N27, GF17-33780L). M.M. acknowledges support from the Engineering and Physical Sciences Research Council (EPSRC; EP/P024114/1) and the QuantERA ERA-NET co-fund (FWF Project I3773-N36). K.R. acknowledges support from QuantERA. J.L.O. acknowledges a Royal Society Wolfson Merit Award and a Royal Academy of Engineering Chair in Emerging Technologies. M.G.T. acknowledges support from a European Research Council (ERC) starter grant (ERC-2014-STG 640079) and an EPSRC Early Career Fellowship (EP/K033085/1)."],"id":"S01-000.00-356441","identifier":[{"id":"85077059438","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ada6d0b2-0e64-4f31-99ca-99b1c2097faf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1EA2B522219015B93E161C012390A2AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/208913060/1911.07839.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/208913063/s41567_020_0840_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Centre of Excellence for Silicon Photonics for Optical Communications","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Nanophotonic Devices","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Ultra-fast Optical Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"peking university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Peking University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"beijing academy of quantum information sciences","loc":["China","A