{"abstract":"Importance: Advanced parental age has been associated with autism spectrum disorders (ASDs) in children. However, little is known about the association between grandparental age at the time of birth of the parent and the risk of ASD in the grandchildren. Objective: To estimate the associations between parental and grandparental age and ASD risk in children. Design, Setting, and Participants: This population-based, multigenerational cohort study used data from Danish national health registries. A parental age cohort was constructed to evaluate the association between parental age and ASD in 1 476 783 singleton children born from 1990 to 2013, and a multigenerational cohort was also constructed including 362 438 fathers and 458 234 mothers born from 1973 to 1990 for whom information on grandparental age was available. Data analyses were conducted from November 1, 2018, through February 7, 2020. Exposures: Parental age at childbirth and grandparental age at the time of the birth of the parent. Main Outcomes and Measures: Diagnoses of ASD in children were obtained from the Danish Psychiatric Central Register (1994-2017). Logistic regression analysis was used to estimate the associations between parental or grandparental age and ASD in children. Results: Of the 1 476 783 children born from 1990 to 2013, 758 066 (51.3%) were male, and 27 616 (1.9%) had ASD (20 467 [74.1%] were male). Advanced paternal or maternal age over 30 years was monotonically associated with increased ASD risk, with odds ratios (ORs) of 1.56 (95% CI, 1.45-1.68) for maternal age 40 years and older and 1.57 (95% CI, 1.39-1.78) for paternal age 50 years and older, compared with parents aged 25 to 29 years. In the multigenerational cohort, 9364 grandchildren (1.7%) had ASD. This study found U-shaped associations, in that ASD risk was higher among grandchildren of younger (≤19 years) maternal grandmothers (OR, 1.68; 95% CI, 1.52-1.85), younger maternal grandfathers (OR, 1.50; 95% CI, 1.26-1.78), and younger paternal grandmothers (OR, 1.18; 95% CI, 1.04-1.34), and older (≥40 years) paternal grandmothers (OR, 1.40; 95% CI, 1.03-1.90) compared with the grandchildren of grandparents who were aged 25 to 29 years at the time of giving birth to the parents. Conclusions and Relevance: These findings corroborate previous studies suggesting that advanced parental age is independently associated with increased ASD risk in children. This study also found that children with young maternal grandparents and children with young and old paternal grandparents had elevated ASD risk. Possible transmission of ASD risk across generations should be considered in etiological research on ASD.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Gao, Yu","Yu, Yongfu","Xiao, Jingyuan","Luo, Jiajun","Zhang, Yawei","Tian, Ying","Zhang, Jun","Olsen, Jørn","Li, Jiong","Liew, Zeyan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-198465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Yale University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of grandparental and parental age at childbirth with autism spectrum disorder in children","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85083404815","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-198465","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7160691","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85083404815","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32293683","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-78e444c7-6a59-49d9-b483-0fd9ef3d67d3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77ECBA44F09A578516E1D47E9313A26C"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"yale university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yale University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"gaoyupau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Yu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongfu","key":"yuyongfupau","last":"Yu","locid":"06be533f-163e-454d-bd55-9219a4f5cafa","name":"Yu, Yongfu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingyuan","key":"xiaojingyuanpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Jingyuan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiajun","key":"luojiajunpau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Jiajun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yawei","key":"zhangyaweipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yawei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ying","key":"tianyingpau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Ying","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun","key":"zhangjunpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørn","key":"olsenjørnpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"48e09bb0-9b9d-40c8-ab2c-ff256ae11f0f","name":"Olsen, Jørn","orcid":"0000-0001-7462-5140","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiong","key":"lijiongpau","last":"Li","locid":"304b9c99-9102-4963-8342-05aae67a5685","name":"Li, Jiong","orcid":"0000-0003-1125-026X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Zeyan","key":"liewzeyanpau","last":"Liew","name":"Liew, Zeyan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32293683"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2020.2868","issn":["25743805"],"issue":"4","journal":"JAMA network open","paperid":"e202868","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA network open","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083404815"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-78e444c7-6a59-49d9-b483-0fd9ef3d67d3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Association of Grandparental and Parental Age at Childbirth With Autism Spectrum Disorder in Children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-198465","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Transition-metal carbides have been proven to be efficient catalysts for the hydrogen evolution reaction (HER); however, their application as a bifunctional electrocatalyst towards the HER and oxygen evolution reaction (OER) altogether remains a significant challenge. Herein, we report unique heterostructures comprising cobalt-doped molybdenum-carbide (Co-Mo2C) nanorods encapsulated in nitrogen-doped graphitic carbon shell (NGCS) through one-step pyrolysis of a Co-adenine-MoO3 hybrid. The as-synthesized Co-Mo2C@NGCS heterostructures could be directly used as a catalyst for overall water splitting. Low overpotentials of 161 and 360 mV are needed for the HER and OER to reach 10 mA cm-2, and the corresponding Tafel slopes are just 60 and 54 mV dec-1, respectively. Theoretical simulations implied that the synergistic effects between the cobalt heteroatoms, NGCS and Mo2C resulted in the enhanced catalytic performance. Our work not only provides a facile method to construct hybrid electrocatalysts with inexpensive metals, but also gives new insights into the mechanism of the HER and OER in alkaline media.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jiang, Anning","Zhang, Wei","Wang, Zegao","Nidamanuri, Naga Pradeep","Li, Qiang","Zeng, Xiao Cheng","Dong, Mingdong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244503"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Qiang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing University of Chemical Technology","Shandong University","Sichuan University"],"keyword":["Active sites","Catalysts","Efficient","Electrocatalysts","Hydrogen evolution","Molybdenum carbide","Nanoparticles","Oxygen","TOTAL ENERGY CALCULATIONS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"direct synthesis of bifunctional nanorods from a co adenine moo sub 000000000003 sub hybrid for overall water splitting","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85079382673","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244503","identifier":[{"id":"85079382673","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000513242900015","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-c9a00c87-5571-4fa2-adb9-4a673dbbac44"],"keyword":["ACTIVE-SITES","CATALYSTS","EFFICIENT","ELECTROCATALYSTS","HYDROGEN-EVOLUTION","MOLYBDENUM-CARBIDE","N-DOPED CARBON","NANOPARTICLES","OXYGEN","TOTAL-ENERGY CALCULATIONS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D5A91D01B11D26937FB9B67B8BAF266B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"beijing university of chemical technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing University of Chemical Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anning","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Anning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Zegao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"2f191f69-88c1-4291-8610-6d3b85bbc312","name":"Wang, Zegao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Naga Pradeep","key":"nidamanuripau","last":"Nidamanuri","name":"Nidamanuri, Naga Pradeep","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Qiang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Cheng","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Xiao Cheng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mingdong","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c9qm00626e","issn":["20521537"],"issue":"2","journal":"Materials Chemistry Frontiers","pages":"546-554","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Materials Chemistry Frontiers","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079382673"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c9a00c87-5571-4fa2-adb9-4a673dbbac44"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Direct synthesis of bifunctional nanorods from a Co-adenine-MoO<sub>3</sub> hybrid for overall water splitting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244503","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The access of rhizobia to legume host is a prerequisite for nodulation. Rhizobia are poorly motile in soil, while filamentous fungi are known to grow extensively across soil pores. Since root exudates-driven bacterial chemotaxis cannot explain rhizobial long-distance dispersal, mycelia could constitute ideal dispersal networks to help rhizobial enrichment in the legume rhizosphere from bulk soil. Thus, we hypothesized that mycelia networks act as vectors that enable contact between rhizobia and legume and influence subsequent nodulation. By developing a soil microcosm system, we found that a facultatively biotrophic fungus, Phomopsis liquidambaris, helps rhizobial migration from bulk soil to the peanut (Arachis hypogaea) rhizosphere and, hence, triggers peanut–rhizobium nodulation but not seen in the absence of mycelia. Assays of dispersal modes suggested that cell proliferation and motility mediated rhizobial dispersal along mycelia, and fungal exudates might contribute to this process. Furthermore, transcriptomic analysis indicated that genes associated with the cell division, chemosensory system, flagellum biosynthesis, and motility were regulated by Ph. liquidambaris, thus accounting for the detected rhizobial dispersal along hyphae. Our results indicate that rhizobia use mycelia as dispersal networks that migrate to legume rhizosphere and trigger nodulation. This work highlights the importance of mycelial network-based bacterial dispersal in legume–rhizobium symbiosis.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhang, Wei","Li, Xiao Gang","Sun, Kai","Tang, Meng Jun","Xu, Fang Ji","Zhang, Ming","Dai, Chuan Chao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340435"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Dai, Chuan Chao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nanjing Forestry University","Nanjing Normal University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mycelial network mediated rhizobial dispersal enhances legume nodulation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/221988595/ISME_Journal_14_10151029.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340435","identifier":[{"id":"85078120544","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000509036400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7082348","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31974462","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-782dff0b-8ddc-46cd-8e38-1075d5791daa"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0A143D65C30F441CC2667D8088F85647"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/221988595/ISME_Journal_14_10151029.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"nanjing normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"nanjing forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology, Nanomaterials and Nanobiosensors"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"zhangweipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Wei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Gang","key":"lixiaogangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Gang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai","key":"sunkaipau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Kai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Meng Jun","key":"tangmengjunpau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Meng Jun","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fang Ji","key":"xufangjipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Fang Ji","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ming","key":"zhangmingpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"f10de10d-99d4-4fb0-bf06-929dc5a1040c","name":"Zhang, Ming","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuan Chao","key":"daichuanchaopau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Chuan Chao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31974462"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41396-020-0587-5","issn":["17517362","17517370"],"issn_org":["17517362"],"journal":"ISME Journal","pages":"1015-1029","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"ISME Journal","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078120544"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-782dff0b-8ddc-46cd-8e38-1075d5791daa"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Mycelial network-mediated rhizobial dispersal enhances legume nodulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340435","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Supporting materials are often employed to enhance the stability of iron oxides oxygen carriers, but the reactivity is compromised for the dilution of the active phase. Here, we report several iron oxides supported by ionic conducting gadolinium-doped cerium oxides (GDC) for efficient chemical looping hydrogen production. The results show that GDC support can simultaneously improve redox stability and activity. Specifically, the produced Fe2O3/Gd0.3Ce0.7O3−δ exhibits a high hydrogen production rate of ~0.71 mmol·g−1·min−1 and hydrogen yield of ~10 mmol·g−1 with negligible decay through 20 redox cycle. When using methane as the reducing agent, Fe2O3/Gd0.3Ce0.7O3−δ shows high methane conversion of 75.67% and much lower carbon deposition than Fe2O3. The high performance is attributed to the improved oxide ion-conductivity through the oxygen carrier, which is further verified as the ability of the GDC support to accelerate the oxygen diffusion in the bulk. The explored support effects in this work can be extended to design oxygen carrier materials with both high activity and stability.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Zeng, Dewang","Kang, Fengwen","Qiu, Yu","Cui, Dongxu","Li, Min","Ma, Li","Zhang, Shuai","Xiao, Rui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357983"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Rui"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Southeast University, Nanjing"],"keyword":["Chemical looping","Hydrogen production","Oxygen carrier","Support effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"iron oxides with gadolinium doped cerium oxides as active supports for chemical looping hydrogen production","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/220188043/2020_CEJ_Iron_oxides_with_gadolinium_doped_cerium_oxides_as_active_supports_for_chemical_looping_hydrogen_production_for_lab.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors gratefully acknowledge National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grant No. 51906041 ), the Natural Science Foundation of Jiangsu province (Grant NO. BK20190360 ) and the National Science Foundation for Distinguished Young Scholars of China (Grant No. 51525601 )."],"id":"S01-000.00-357983","identifier":[{"id":"85084229463","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b2c115e9-307d-441d-bd0a-c0a3d4a63007"],"keyword":["Chemical looping","Hydrogen production","Oxygen carrier","Support effects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE5D8F54F573B9CBC7096D44CD139493"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/220188043/2020_CEJ_Iron_oxides_with_gadolinium_doped_cerium_oxides_as_active_supports_for_chemical_looping_hydrogen_production_for_lab.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"southeast university nanjing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southeast University, Nanjing","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Structured Electromagnetic Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dewang","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Dewang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fengwen","key":"kangpau","last":"Kang","locid":"672468bd-14cc-41f5-9328-1cb50a819f46","name":"Kang, Fengwen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"qiupau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, Yu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongxu","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Dongxu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Min","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Li","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuai","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Shuai","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rui","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Rui","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cej.2020.125153","issn":["13858947","18733212"],"issn_org":["13858947"],"journal":"Chemical Engineering Journal","paperid":"125153","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Chemical Engineering Journal","volume":"396"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084229463"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b2c115e9-307d-441d-bd0a-c0a3d4a63007"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Iron oxides with gadolinium-doped cerium oxides as active supports for chemical looping hydrogen production","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357983","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"With the aim to enhance the system reliability and reduce the system cost of induction motor drives, the speed-sensorless control, implemented by various speed estimation schemes, is demanded. The speed estimation provided by the second-order generalized integrator-frequency-locked loop (SOGI-FLL) is emerging as a promising method for speed-sensorless control. However, most of the existing SOGI-FLL schemes may undergo performance degradation during frequency ramps. Additionally, the SOGI-FLL scheme has an insufficient capability to reject disturbances, e.g., DC offsets. To address these issues, a speed estimation scheme based on an improved SOGI-FLL scheme for speed-sensorless control of induction motor drives is proposed. In this scheme, a new FLL is utilized as the speed estimator, which achieves accurate estimation with frequency ramps. Specifically, by employing a second-order SOGI-based flux observer, acceptable robustness of the proposed estimation scheme against DC offsets is obtained. Simulations are performed to investigate the performance of the proposed speed estimation scheme and a comparison with the conventional SOGI-FLL scheme is made.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wang, Huimin","Yang, Yongheng","Zuo, Yun","Li, Songtao","Hu, Xiao","Ge, Xinglai"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-115335"],"event":{"acronym":"IES","end":"2020-10-21","place":"Virtual, Singapore, sg","start":"2020-10-18","title":"46th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society, IECON 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Southwest Jiaotong University"],"keyword":["DC offsets","Induction motor drives","speed estimation scheme"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a speed estimation scheme based on an improved sogi fll for speed sensorless control of induction motor drives","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85097758929&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-115335","identifier":[{"id":"85097758929","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e08974b1-aece-4185-b67c-952bdee6b1e1"],"keyword":["DC offsets","improved second-order generalized integrator frequency-locked loop (SOGI-FLL)","induction motor drives","second-order second-order generalized integrator-based observer","speed estimation scheme"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-75B9A71568B22372692BD6BEE9FCE00B"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"southwest jiaotong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwest Jiaotong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Huimin","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"ba1b3aa8-2a9a-4012-81d4-fe6741b9c4e0","name":"Wang, Huimin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yongheng","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","locid":"d4e88c1b-191c-43c1-90e4-13e51951780e","name":"Yang, Yongheng","orcid":"0000-0002-1488-4762","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yun","key":"zuopau","last":"Zuo","name":"Zuo, Yun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Songtao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Songtao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Xiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinglai","key":"gepau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Xinglai","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iecon43393.2020.9255253","eisbn":["9781728154145"],"isbn":["9781728154152"],"issn":["1553572X"],"pages":"852-857","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Proceedings of the Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","status":"p","subtitle":"46th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","title":"Proceedings - IECON 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097758929"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e08974b1-aece-4185-b67c-952bdee6b1e1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A Speed Estimation Scheme Based on An Improved SOGI-FLL for Speed-Sensorless Control of Induction Motor Drives","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115335","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this work, temperature characteristics during hydrate formation were investigated in the cyclopentane-methane system using large-scale equipment with bubbling. The volume in each experiment was increased by a factor of 80 compared with previous work. A group of scaled-up experiments, under the optimal condition based on experiments in the smaller crystallizer, was carried out to verify the scale-up potential of hydrate-based thermal fluid production process. Another group of scaled-up experiments were performed with different variables (volume ratio of cyclopentane to water, gas/liquid ratio and pressure) to figure out the initial hydrate formation interface and optimize the temperature of the thermal fluid. Experimental results illustrate that hydrate-based thermal fluid production process can be scaled up by a factor of 80, however, the temperature of the thermal fluid needs to be optimized by adjusting variables accordingly. Moreover, the liquid cyclopentane/water interface more than the gas/liquid interface affects hydrate formation and hydrate accumulation. In particular, the hydrate formation interface initially occurs on the water side near the liquid cyclopentane/water interface. A large amount of hydrate accumulates in the bulk liquid cyclopentane phase, forming new hydrate formation interfaces. Thermal fluid with a specific temperature range can be produced based on the heat released and conducted from the hydrate formation interfaces.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cai, Jing","Lv, Tao","Zhang, Yu","von Solms, Nicolas","Xu, Chun Gang","Chen, Zhao Yang","Li, Xiao Sen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305886"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Xiao Sen"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Cyclopentane","Heat","Temperature characteristics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"studies on temperature characteristics and initial formation interface during cyclopentane methane hydrate formation in large scale equipment with bubbling","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/216127688/manuscript_Jing_Cai_nvs_edit_02072019.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Key Program of National Natural Science Foundation of China ( 51736009 ), Special Project for Marine Economy Development of Guangdong Province ( GDME-2018d002 ), National Science Fund for International S&T Cooperation Program of China ( 2015DFA61790 ), Science and Technology Apparatus Development Program of the Chinese Academy of Sciences ( YZ201619 ), Frontier Sciences Key Research Program of the Chinese Academy of Sciences ( QYZDJ-SSW-JSC033 ) and China Scholarship Council ( CSC201804910598 )."],"id":"S01-000.00-305886","identifier":[{"id":"85075740974","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0447a1f9-7e6e-4a80-a3bc-94508ca6438e"],"keyword":["Cyclopentane","Heat","Hydrate formation interface","Temperature characteristics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B2DCCFC839428C56117FA4CBDE6F36E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/216127688/manuscript_Jing_Cai_nvs_edit_02072019.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jing","key":"caipau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Jing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tao","key":"lvpau","last":"Lv","name":"Lv, Tao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicolas","key":"vonsolmspau","last":"von Solms","locid":"8ae12603-c1ee-4bf7-8893-337b5b940cfb","name":"von Solms, Nicolas","orcid":"0000-0002-5007-8987","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chun Gang","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Chun Gang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhao Yang","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhao Yang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Sen","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Sen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apenergy.2019.114076","issn":["03062619","18729118"],"issn_org":["03062619"],"journal":"Applied Energy","paperid":"114076","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Energy","volume":"258"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075740974"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0447a1f9-7e6e-4a80-a3bc-94508ca6438e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Studies on temperature characteristics and initial formation interface during cyclopentane-methane hydrate formation in large-scale equipment with bubbling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305886","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Microbial fuel cell as a sustainable microbial-electrochemical reactor can harvest bio-power from wastewater by the oxidation of electro-active bacteria on the anode, while its power output is greatly relying on the oxygen reduction reaction performance of the cathode electro-catalysts. Here, the dahlia flower-like nickel-based composites have been synthesized through a hydrothermal reaction, and was used as an efficient oxygen reduction reaction catalyst in a single chamber microbial fuel cell. The physical characterization of surface structure suggests the composites have successfully prepared. The MFC with Ni-melamine cathode can achieve obviously higher power density of 378.08 mW m−2 than those of Ni-urea cathode (244.02 mW m−2) and Ni-dicyandiamide cathode (201.67 mW m−2). A series of electrochemical characterization suggests that Ni-melamine electrode possesses larger electrochemical active surface area, lower charge transfer resistance, and higher oxygen reduction performance than those of Ni-urea electrode and Ni-dicyandiamide electrode. The electrochemical measurements have also demonstrated that nickel-melamine composites can be involved in oxygen reduction reaction via a four-electron route due to the high-efficient electrocatalytic activity. In addition, the maximum power density of nickel-based composites is obviously increased with an increase of catalysts coating amounts. When the loading amounts are 4 mg cm−2, the power density for nickel-based composites is improved to 1421.4 mW m−2, which is 1.68 times higher than that of Pt/C due to the introduction of oxygen vacancies and nitrogen element. Thus, nickel-based composite is an effective and promising catalyst material for microbial fuel cell to substitute Pt/C for oxygen reduction reaction application.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Li, Meng","Li, Yan Wen","Yu, Xiao Long","Xiang, Lei","Zhao, Hai Ming","Yan, Jian Fang","Feng, Nai Xian","Xu, Mingyi","Cai, Quan Ying","Mo, Ce Hui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327044"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Mo, Ce Hui"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Guangdong University of Petrochemical Technology","Jinan University"],"keyword":["Microbial fuel cells","Stability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhancing bioelectricity generation of bio electrochemical reactors using porous nickel based composite as effective oxygen reduction catalyst","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235973833/Enhancing_bioelectricity_generation_of_bio_electrochemical_reactors_using_porous_nickel_based_composite_as_effective_oxygen_reduction_catalyst.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We gratefully thank the financial support from Project Funded by China Postdoctoral Science Foundation ( 2019M663382 ), Science and Technology Project of Guangzhou City ( 201704020074 ), NSFC-Guangdong Joint Fund ( U1501233 ), Research Team Project of the Natural Science Foundation of Guangdong Province ( 2016A030312009 ), and the Program of the Guangdong Science and Technology Department ( 2017B020238002 )."],"id":"S01-000.00-327044","identifier":[{"id":"85091111268","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4b9c8887-9075-4b41-9b84-95c72afd12dd"],"keyword":["Microbial fuel cells","Nickel-based composites","Oxygen reduction performance","Stability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-90594A0DDA716650D32595B2CB2C895F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235973833/Enhancing_bioelectricity_generation_of_bio_electrochemical_reactors_using_porous_nickel_based_composite_as_effective_oxygen_reduction_catalyst.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jinan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jinan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"guangdong university of petrochemical technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Guangdong University of Petrochemical Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Residual Resource Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Meng","key":"limengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Meng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan Wen","key":"liyanwenpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yan Wen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Long","key":"yuxiaolongpau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Xiao Long","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lei","key":"xiangleipau","last":"Xiang","name":"Xiang, Lei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai Ming","key":"zhaohaimingpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Hai Ming","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian Fang","key":"yanjianfangpau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Jian Fang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nai Xian","key":"fengnaixianpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Nai Xian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingyi","key":"xumingyipau","last":"Xu","locid":"0cf0b39e-632d-4d3d-9ebe-a5853bfc8757","name":"Xu, Mingyi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Quan Ying","key":"caiquanyingpau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Quan Ying","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ce Hui","key":"mocehuipau","last":"Mo","name":"Mo, Ce Hui","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jclepro.2020.124137","issn":["09596526"],"journal":"Journal of Cleaner Production","paperid":"124137","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cleaner Production","title_org":"Journal of cleaner production","volume":"277"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091111268"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4b9c8887-9075-4b41-9b84-95c72afd12dd"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Enhancing bioelectricity generation of bio-electrochemical reactors using porous nickel-based composite as effective oxygen reduction catalyst","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327044","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Floating wind turbines are designed to survive 50-year-extreme environmental conditions during their 20-year service life, as specified by International Electrotechnical Commission (IEC) standards. For a tension-leg platform (TLP)-type floating wind turbine, extreme wave loads can induce significant high-frequency resonant and transient responses, e.g. springing and ringing, which greatly amplify the structural responses of the floating wind turbines. This study aims to predict the springing-induced extreme responses of the WindStar TLP system by using FAST__(Fatigue, Aerodynamics, Structures, and Turbulence), a fully coupled simulation tool. The hydrodynamic loads considered include both first- and second-order wave-excitation loads. Different simulation sizes are compared. Different extreme-value prediction methods are applied and the results are compared. Both the peak-over-threshold (POT) and block maxima method (BMM) are applied to extract local maxima, which are then fitted using a threeparameter Weibull distribution. The average conditional exceedance rate (ACER) method and the Gumbel method are applied and compared with the above method.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Xie, Si-Hong","Zhao, Yong-Sheng","He, Yan-Ping","Shao, Yanlin","Han, Zhao-Long","Huang, Chao","Gu, Xiao-Li"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356750"],"event":{"end":"2020-10-16","place":"Shanghai, cn","start":"2020-10-11","title":"30th International Ocean and Polar Engineering Conference (ISOPE 2020)","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Floating wind turbine","Tension leg platform"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prediction of springing induced extreme responses of a tlp type floating wind turbine","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090907826","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356750","identifier":[{"id":"85090907826","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-aea3af5a-9f85-4e4a-b270-e1393c4c5c0c"],"keyword":["Extreme theory","Floating wind turbine","Springing response","Tension-leg platform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2FB10A4281437AD43C999DD02B3D6B9C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Si-Hong","key":"xiepau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Si-Hong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong-Sheng","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Yong-Sheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan-Ping","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Yan-Ping","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan-Lin","key":"shaopau","last":"Shao","locid":"bf399627-8602-43b6-8175-a0fc3c3d9d82","name":"Shao, Yanlin","name_org":"Shao, Yan-Lin","orcid":"0000-0002-9080-8438","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhao-Long","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Zhao-Long","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chao","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Chao","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Li","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Xiao-Li","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781880653845"],"issn":["10986189"],"pages":"423-431","publisher":"International Society of Offshore and Polar Engineers","series":"Proceedings of the International Offshore and Polar Engineering Conference","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Thirtieth (2020) International Ocean and Polar Engineering Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090907826"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-aea3af5a-9f85-4e4a-b270-e1393c4c5c0c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Prediction of Springing-induced Extreme Responses of a TLP-Type Floating Wind Turbine","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356750","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Resonant and transient responses of a tension leg platform (TLP)-type floating offshore wind turbine can be excited by high-frequency wave forces. This paper investigates the damaging effect of second-order wave forces on structural fatigue in the WindStar TLP system. Dynamic responses in the time domain are analyzed using the program FAST. To explore the mechanisms of different combinations of wind and wave loads inducing damage, five scenarios are considered: wind only, first-order wave only, second-order wave only, joint wind and first-order wave, and joint wind and second-order wave. The results show the dominant effect of second-order waves in tower structural fatigue damage. Additionally, wind and wave coupling becomes stronger under second-order wave loads. 1. INTRODUCTION A trend in wind farm development is the shifting of turbines from land to offshore deep water, where conditions are better for wind-energy generation. In addition to being plentiful, wind on the ocean is more stable with lower turbulence than that on land. The development of offshore wind turbines therefore represents a strong contribution to clean and renewable electricity generation as well as eliminating the negative visual and acoustic impacts of turbines. With increasing water depth, the economic feasibility of traditional fixed turbines, supported by such as jacket-based and gravity-based structures, dramatically decreases. Therefore, several concepts of floating offshore wind turbine (FOWT) have been proposed. Three representative types, categorized by the method of attaining static stability, are spar-type, semi-submersible type, and tension-leg-platform (TLP) type (Robertson and Jonkman 2011). The TLP type uses a vertically tensioned mooring system. The natural periods of heave, pitch, and roll are restricted to between 3–5 s, while those of surge, sway, and yaw are >20 s, all different to waveenergy frequencies. This ensures that a TLP-type FOWT has small wavefrequency responses, providing a stable foundation for the wind turbine (Suzuki et al. 2011). However, in realistic sea conditions, the resonant and transient responses (springing and ringing) of TLP-type FOWTs can be excited by high-frequency wave forces, especially during storms (Zou 1998). Severe sea states have more wave energy at higher and lower frequency ranges than calmer seas due to nonlinear wave effects (Xu et al. 2019). These high-frequency responses can undoubtedly induce greater structural fatigue damage and thus reduce the safety of a TLP-type FOWT.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Liu, Jia-Rong","Zhao, Yong-Sheng","He, Yan-Ping","Shao, Yanlin","Mao, Weng-Gang","Han, Zhao-Long","Gu, Xiao-Li","Chao-Huang, _"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-371981"],"event":{"end":"2020-10-16","place":"Shanghai, cn","start":"2020-10-11","title":"30th International Ocean and Polar Engineering Conference (ISOPE 2020)","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","Shanghai Jiao Tong University"],"keyword":["Fatigue damage","Floating wind turbine","Second order wave force"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of second order wave force on fatigue damage assessment of a tlp type floating wind turbine","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090912320","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-371981","identifier":[{"id":"85090912320","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e172fe86-9035-41c5-9192-da0563534fed"],"keyword":["Fatigue damage","Floating wind turbine","Second-order wave force","TLP platform"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-37F0CA082ADA6C31FFBB8ABC78504107"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia-Rong","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jia-Rong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong-Sheng","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Yong-Sheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan-Ping","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Yan-Ping","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan-Lin","key":"shaopau","last":"Shao","locid":"bf399627-8602-43b6-8175-a0fc3c3d9d82","name":"Shao, Yanlin","name_org":"Shao, Yan-Lin","orcid":"0000-0002-9080-8438","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Weng-Gang","key":"maopau","last":"Mao","name":"Mao, Weng-Gang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhao-Long","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Zhao-Long","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Li","key":"gupau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Xiao-Li","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"_","key":"chaohuangpau","last":"Chao-Huang","name":"Chao-Huang, _","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781880653845"],"issn":["10986189"],"pages":"415-422","publisher":"International Society of Offshore and Polar Engineers","series":"Proceedings of the International Offshore and Polar Engineering Conference","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Thirtieth (2020) International Ocean and Polar Engineering Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090912320"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e172fe86-9035-41c5-9192-da0563534fed"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Effects of Second-order Wave Force on Fatigue Damage Assessment of a TLP-type Floating Wind Turbine","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-371981","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Although 20 pancreatic cancer susceptibility loci have been identified through genome-wide association studies in individuals of European ancestry, much of its heritability remains unexplained and the genes responsible largely unknown. Methods: To discover novel pancreatic cancer risk loci and possible causal genes, we performed a pancreatic cancer transcriptome-wide association study in Europeans using three approaches: FUSION, MetaXcan, and Summary-MulTiXcan. We integrated genome-wide association studies summary statistics from 9040 pancreatic cancer cases and 12 496 controls, with gene expression prediction models built using transcriptome data from histologically normal pancreatic tissue samples (NCI Laboratory of Translational Genomics [n = 95] and Genotype-Tissue Expression v7 [n = 174] datasets) and data from 48 different tissues (Genotype-Tissue Expression v7, n = 74-421 samples). Results: We identified 25 genes whose genetically predicted expression was statistically significantly associated with pancreatic cancer risk (false discovery rate <.05), including 14 candidate genes at 11 novel loci (1p36.12: CELA3B; 9q31.1: SMC2, SMC2-AS1; 10q23.31: RP11-80H5.9; 12q13.13: SMUG1; 14q32.33: BTBD6; 15q23: HEXA; 15q26.1: RCCD1; 17q12: PNMT, CDK12, PGAP3; 17q22: SUPT4H1; 18q11.22: RP11-888D10.3; and 19p13.11: PGPEPI) and 11 at six known risk loci (5p15.33: TERT, CLPTMIL, ZDHHCIIB; 7p14.1: INHBA; 9q34.2: ABO; 13q12.2: PDX1; 13q22.1: KLF5; and 16q23.1: WDR59, CFDP1, BCAR1, TMEM170A). The association for 12 of these genes (CELA3B, SMC2, and PNMT at novel risk loci and TERT, CLPTMIL, INHBA, ABO, PDX1, KLF5, WDR59, CFDP1, and BCAR1 at known loci) remained statistically significant after Bonferroni correction. Conclusions: By integrating gene expression and genotype data, we identified novel pancreatic cancer risk loci and candidate functional genes that warrant further investigation.","author_count":95,"contributors":["Zhong, Jun","Jermusyk, Ashley","Wu, Lang","Hoskins, Jason W.","Collins, Irene","Mocci, Evelina","Zhang, Mingfeng","Song, Lei","Chung, Charles C.","Zhang, Tongwu","Xiao, Wenming","Albanes, Demetrius","Andreotti, Gabriella","Arslan, Alan A.","Babic, Ana","Bamlet, William R.","Beane-Freeman, Laura","Berndt, Sonja","Borgida, Ayelet","Bracci, Paige M.","Brais, Lauren","Brennan, Paul","Bueno-de-Mesquita, Bas","Buring, Julie","Canzian, Federico","Childs, Erica J.","Cotterchio, Michelle","Du, Mengmeng","Duell, Eric J.","Fuchs, Charles","Gallinger, Steven","Gaziano, J. Michael","Giles, Graham G.","Giovannucci, Edward","Goggins, Michael","Goodman, Gary E.","Goodman, Phyllis J.","Haiman, Christopher","Hartge, Patricia","Hasan, Manal","Helzlsouer, Kathy J.","Holly, Elizabeth A.","Klein, Eric A.","Kogevinas, Manolis","Kurtz, Robert J.","LeMarchand, Loic","Malats, Nuria","Mannisto, Satu","Milne, Roger","Neale, Rachel E.","Ng, Kimmie","Obazee, Ofure","Oberg, Ann L.","Orlow, Irene","Patel, Alpa","Peters, Ulrike","Porta, Miquel","Rothman, Nathaniel","Scelo, Ghislaine","Sesso, Howard D.","Severi, Gianluca","Sieri, Sabina","Silverman, Debra","Sund, Malin","Tjønneland, Anne","Thornquist, Mark D.","Tobias, Geoffrey S.","Trichopoulou, Antonia","Van den Eeden, Stephen K.","Visvanathan, Kala","Wactawski-Wende, Jean","Wentzensen, Nicolas","White, Emily","Yu, Herbert","Yuan, Chen","Zeleniuch-Jacquotte, Anne","Hoover, Robert","Brown, Kevin","Kooperberg, Charles","Risch, Harvey A.","Jacobs, Eric J.","Li, Donghui","Yu, Kai","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Chanock, Stephen J.","Wolpin, Brian M.","Stolzenberg-Solomon, Rachael Z.","Chatterjee, Nilanjan","Klein, Alison P.","Smith, Jill P.","Kraft, Peter","Shi, Jianxin","Petersen, Gloria M.","Zheng, Wei","Amundadottir, Laufey T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-406191"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Finland","Fra