"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Transcriptome-Wide Association Study Identifies Novel Candidate Susceptibility Genes for Pancreatic Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-406191","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Heterotrimeric G proteins are molecular switches in GPCR signaling pathways and regulate a plethora of physiological and pathological processes. GPCRs are efficient drug targets, and more than 30% of the drugs in use target them. However, selectively targeting an individual GPCR may be undesirable in various multifactorial diseases in which multiple receptors are involved. In addition, abnormal activation or expression of G proteins is frequently associated with diseases. Furthermore, G proteins harboring mutations often result in malignant diseases. Thus, targeting G proteins instead of GPCRs might provide alternative approaches for combating these diseases. In this review, we discuss the biochemistry of heterotrimeric G proteins, describe the G protein-associated diseases, and summarize the currently known modulators that can regulate the activities of G proteins. The outlook for targeting G proteins to treat diverse diseases is also included in this manuscript.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Jian","Ge, Yang","Huang, Jun-Xiang","Strømgaard, Kristian","Zhang, Xiaolei","Xiong, Xiao-Feng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-409995"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sun Yat-Sen University"],"keyword":["COUPLED RECEPTORS","Heart failure"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"heterotrimeric g proteins as therapeutic targets in drug discovery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-409995","identifier":[{"id":"000585210700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85077686714","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31841625","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1bc4a516-d87b-4833-9f95-f6c38d6e2d37"],"keyword":["BETA-GAMMA-SUBUNITS","BRONCHIAL SMOOTH-MUSCLE","COUPLED RECEPTORS","G-ALPHA-Q","HEART-FAILURE","HUMAN THYROTROPIN RECEPTOR","LONG-LASTING HYPERALGESIA","PASTEURELLA-MULTOCIDA TOXIN","PHOSPHOLIPASE-C-BETA","PROTEASE-ACTIVATED RECEPTOR-1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C48ED7BBFB14F29F1204E48B45FD57E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Biopharmaceuticals"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jian","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yang","key":"gepau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Yang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jun-Xiang","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jun-Xiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kristian","key":"stromgaardpau","last":"Stromgaard","locid":"78f1a438-9c1e-4795-bf55-b266b5d2cde4","name":"Strømgaard, Kristian","name_org":"Stromgaard, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2206-4737","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaolei","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiaolei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao-Feng","key":"xiongpau","last":"Xiong","name":"Xiong, Xiao-Feng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31841625"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.9b01452","issn":["00222623","15204804"],"issn_org":["00222623"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Medicinal Chemistry","pages":"5013-5030","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medicinal Chemistry","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077686714"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1bc4a516-d87b-4833-9f95-f6c38d6e2d37"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Heterotrimeric G Proteins as Therapeutic Targets in Drug Discovery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-409995","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Retinal (C20) and the C25 and C30 homologues were compared as radical scavengers together with their C22, C27, and C32 homologues linked with daidzein through a B′3 (isoflavonoid) to oxo-carbon (aldehyde) covalent bond. Oxidation potential in acetonitrile determined by cyclic voltammetry and ionization potential calculated by density functional theory for the aldehydes and dyads (conjugates), of which the two longer are new, decreased linearly with the wavenumber for absorption maximum. The logarithm of the second-order rate constant for scavenging of the ABTS•+ increased linearly with decreasing oxidation potential suggesting that longer conjugation in the antioxidant increases the rate of electron transfer. A similar linear free energy relationship was found for the rate of scavenging DPPH•, including daidzein, which may indicate involvement of hydrogen atom transfer from an isoflavonoid phenol. Prediction of radical scavenging efficiency from visible absorption spectra was demonstrated with the perspective of rational design of bifunctional amphiphilic antioxidants.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jiang, Yang-Lin","Chen, Bai-Ling","Yan, Xiao-Kun","Xu, Yi","Zhao, Chen-Chen","Chen, Zi-Li","Wang, Peng","Zhang, Jian-Ping","Skibsted, Leif Horsfelt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-456152"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conjugation length dependence of free radical scavenging efficiency of retinal and retinylisoflavonoid homologues","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsomega.0c00925","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-456152","identifier":[{"id":"32566842","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85086270819","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7301560","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-6902bac5-ca8f-4544-8e4a-a9cb6825733b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-36D522F2FD0E81C5D69291C56526B759"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsomega.0c00925","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/244279505/Conjugation_Length_Dependence_of_Free_Radical_Scavenging_Efficiency_of_Retinal_and_Retinylisoflavonoid_Homologues.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Ingredient and Dairy Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Yang-Lin","key":"jiangyanglinpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Yang-Lin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bai-Ling","key":"chenbailingpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Bai-Ling","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao-Kun","key":"yanxiaokunpau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Xiao-Kun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yi","key":"xuyipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Yi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Chen-Chen","key":"zhaochenchenpau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Chen-Chen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zi-Li","key":"chenzilipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zi-Li","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peng","key":"wangpengpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Peng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian-Ping","key":"zhangjianpingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jian-Ping","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leif H.","key":"skibstedleifhorsfeltpau","last":"Skibsted","locid":"c8bd9975-50bb-4e25-8dd3-a3738a78ec9b","name":"Skibsted, Leif Horsfelt","name_org":"Skibsted, Leif H.","orcid":"0000-0003-1734-5016","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32566842"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsomega.0c00925","issn":["24701343"],"issue":"23","journal":"ACS Omega","pages":"13770-13776","status":"p","title":"ACS Omega","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086270819"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6902bac5-ca8f-4544-8e4a-a9cb6825733b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Conjugation Length Dependence of Free Radical Scavenging Efficiency of Retinal and Retinylisoflavonoid Homologues","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-456152","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The purpose of the study was to examine 5-year changes in eyes with optic disc drusen at baseline on optical coherence tomography (OCT) scans and the relation of incident drusen to hyperreflective prelaminar lines. METHODS: The study included children who presented at baseline, when participants were aged 11-12 years, and again 5 years later. Grading for optic disc drusen was made in all. Grading for prelaminar lines was made in all children at follow-up and in eyes with optic disc drusen at baseline. Analyses included associations with scleral canal diameter at baseline in all children with optic disc drusen and a nested control group of 115 children without optic disc drusen. Data are reported as the number of children having at least one drusen or at least one hyperreflective line per person. RESULTS: The analysis included 724 children who attended both rounds of the study. Of these, 11 (1.5%) had optic disc drusen at baseline. Five additional children had developed optic disc drusen at follow-up, whereas optic disc drusen had disappeared in none, so that 16 (2.2%) children had optic disc drusen in one or both eyes at follow-up. Children with optic disc drusen at the 5-year follow-up had had a mean scleral canal diameter of 1,364 µm (interquartile range [IQR] 81 µm), compared with 1,457 µm (IQR 197) µm in 115 nested controls without optic disc drusen (P < 0.001). Optic disc drusen at follow-up were associated with more hypermetropic refraction. All children who had optic disc drusen at follow-up also had prelaminar hyperreflective lines. In addition, such lines were found at follow-up in 24 of the remaining 708 children without optic disc drusen (P < 0.001). Prelaminar hyperreflective lines with or without optic disc drusen were associated with a narrower scleral canal (diameter 1,364 µm, IQR 119 µm) compared with absence of prelaminar lines (1,486 µm, IQR 206 µm; P < 0.0001). CONCLUSION: This study provides the first evidence from a prospective study that small optic discs and prelaminar hyperreflective lines on OCT are risk factors for the development of optic disc drusen. The association between prelaminar hyperreflective lines, hypermetropia, and a narrow scleral canal supports that a crowded disc is an essential predisposing factor for the development of optic disc drusen.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Malmqvist, Lasse","Li, Xiao Qiang","Hansen, Mathias H.","Thomsen, Alexander K.","Skovgaard, Anne Mette","Olsen, Else Marie","Larsen, Michael","Munch, Inger Christine","Hamann, Steffen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-040477"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Ukendt"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"progression over 000000000005 years of prelaminar hyperreflective lines to optic disc drusen in the copenhagen child cohort 000000002000 eye study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85087074295","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-040477","identifier":[{"id":"32108119","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85087074295","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-173fe96a-db4b-47cb-b1a2-c260456ccc60","sdu-3dff4ed6-9c20-4ac4-8353-3e3e6bb0749c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AD7DFE5B41C13B15B8CF76589AC65182"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Ukendt"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Health and Social Context"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lasse","key":"malmqvistpau","last":"Malmqvist","name":"Malmqvist, Lasse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Xiao Q.","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"06b00c50-ba17-4187-b5f0-fdec382d5ffa","name":"Li, Xiao Qiang","name_org":"Li, Xiao Q.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias H.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Mathias H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alexander K.","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Alexander K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Anne M.","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"f1e6d144-f7de-4477-a60c-3046ccb9ca8d","name":"Skovgaard, Anne Mette","name_org":"Skovgaard, Anne M.","orcid":"0000-0002-8793-8303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Else M.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"9be69922-e68e-4556-9b40-34a82fc88a15","name":"Olsen, Else Marie","name_org":"Olsen, Else M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1a555c4a-f5eb-40fe-8f79-6442177ac676","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger C.","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","name_org":"Munch, Inger C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Steffen","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","locid":"4e7d48fd-1aa8-4703-94ec-8ae85794b7d7","name":"Hamann, Steffen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32108119"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/wno.0000000000000911","issn":["10708022","15365166"],"issn_org":["10708022"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Neuro-Ophthalmology","pages":"315-321","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neuro-Ophthalmology","title_org":"Journal of neuro-ophthalmology : the official journal of the North American Neuro-Ophthalmology Society","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087074295"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-173fe96a-db4b-47cb-b1a2-c260456ccc60","sdu-3dff4ed6-9c20-4ac4-8353-3e3e6bb0749c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Progression Over 5 Years of Prelaminar Hyperreflective Lines to Optic Disc Drusen in the Copenhagen Child Cohort 2000 Eye Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-040477","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Myopic eyes are longer than nonmyopic eyes and have thinner choroids. The purpose of present study was to investigate whether a thinner subfoveal choroid at 11 years of age predicted axial eye elongation and myopia during adolescence. Methods: Longitudinal, population-based observational study. Axial length was measured using an interferometric device and choroidal thickness was measured by spectral-domain optical coherence tomography. Myopia was defined as non-cycloplegic subjective spherical equivalent refraction ≤-0.50 diopters. Results: Right eyes of 714 children (317 boys) were examined at age (median (IQR)) 11.5 (0.6) years and 16.6 (0.3) years during which axial length (median (IQR)) increased by 243 (202) μm in eyes without myopia (n = 630) at baseline compared with 454 (549) μm in eyes with myopia (n = 84) at baseline, p < 0.0001. A thicker baseline subfoveal choroid was associated with increased five-year axial elongation after adjustment for baseline axial length in nonmyopic eyes (β = 27 μm/100 μm, 95%CI 6 to 48, p = 0.011) but not in myopic eyes (p = 0.34). Subfoveal choroidal thickness at 11 years of age did not predict incident myopia at 16 years of age (p = 0.11). Longer baseline axial length was associated with greater five-year axial elongation in both myopic (β = 196 μm/mm, 95%CI 127 to 265, p < 0.0001) and nonmyopic eyes (β = 28 μm/mm, 95%CI 7 to 49, p = 0.0085) and the odds for incident myopia increased with 1.57 (95%CI 1.18 to 2.09, p = 0.0020) per mm longer axial length at baseline. Conclusion: A thin subfoveal choroid at age 11 years did not predict axial eye elongation and incident myopia from age 11 to 16 years. A longer eye at age 11 years was associated with greater subsequent axial eye elongation and with increased risk of incident myopia at age 16 years.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt","Kessel, Line","Li, Xiao Qiang","Skovgaard, Anne Mette","Larsen, Michael","Munch, Inger Christine"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-044353"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt"],"keyword":["Axial length","CCC2000","Children","Choroidal thickness","Cohort study","Incident myopia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"axial length change and its relationship with baseline choroidal thickness a five year longitudinal study in danish adolescents the ccc000000002000 eye study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12886-020-01427-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-044353","identifier":[{"id":"85083477238","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7161004","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32295547","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8f84dacc-a4de-47c7-b439-8e62047e8d16","sdu-adab4303-c19d-468c-ba8d-4501bdce3f27"],"keyword":["Axial length","CCC2000","Children","Choroidal thickness","Cohort study","Incident myopia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-66E8C53CE2F7A30965F74CD2C348D573"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/243013179/Axial_length_change_and_its_relationship_with_baseline_choroidal_thickness.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/169276037/s12886_020_01427_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12886-020-01427-8","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Health and Social Context"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias Hvidtfelt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6664e645-b606-45cf-9176-f713f0a120b9","name":"Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"06b00c50-ba17-4187-b5f0-fdec382d5ffa","name":"Li, Xiao Qiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Mette","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"16faee51-f101-47f9-8757-c611e52d7381","name":"Skovgaard, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8793-8303","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1a555c4a-f5eb-40fe-8f79-6442177ac676","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32295547"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12886-020-01427-8","issn":["14712415"],"journal":"BMC Ophthalmology","paperid":"152","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Ophthalmology","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083477238"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8f84dacc-a4de-47c7-b439-8e62047e8d16","sdu-adab4303-c19d-468c-ba8d-4501bdce3f27"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Axial length change and its relationship with baseline choroidal thickness-a five-year longitudinal study in Danish adolescents : The CCC2000 eye study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-044353","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In-situ mullite toughened 3Y-TZP ceramics (Mullite/3Y-TZP ceramics) with different content of mullite were prepared by gel-casting combined with pressureless sintering to study effects of the content of mullite on their microstructure and tribological properties. The results indicated that the mullite uniformly distributed in the zirconia matrix had a complete columnar structure and a moderate content in S2 (the sample containing 4 mol% mullite), and the smooth surface caused by low porosity combined with the good mechanical properties significantly reduced the coefficient of friction and wear rate of S2. A high proportion of irregular mullite destroyed the overall structure of S3-S5 (the samples containing 6, 8 and 10 mol% mullite, respectively), combined with high porosity not only reduced the mechanical properties of them, but also led to an increment in surface roughness, which significantly lowered the wear resistance of the material. Studies of worn surfaces showed that micro-cutting was present in every sample, but the degree of micro-cutting and adhesive wear in S2 were minimal due to its good structure and properties. However, the micro-cutting and adhesive wear of S3-S5 were exacerbated.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Huang, Yan qi","Li, Zhuan","Liu, Peng fei","Huang, Tian xing","Li, Yang","Xiao, Peng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-051862"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Zhuan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central South University","State Key Laboratory of Powder Metallurgy"],"keyword":["Microstructure","Tribological properties","Wear rate"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tribological properties of mullite 000000000003y tzp ceramics with different content of mullite fabricated by gel casting","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/316026150/Tribological_properties_of_Mullite_3Y_TZP_ceramics_with_di_2019_Applied_Surf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank the National Natural Science Foundation of China (Grant No. 51575536 ) and the State Key Laboratory of Powder Metallurgy for their financial support."],"id":"S01-000.00-051862","identifier":[{"id":"85059855611","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-064f7fe2-0d49-45c1-9928-eab77b34b75a"],"keyword":["Microstructure","Mullite/3Y-TZP ceramics","Tribological properties","Wear mechanisms","Wear rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-227A6D3D5082F3AA2C4AEE13817C07A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/316026150/Tribological_properties_of_Mullite_3Y_TZP_ceramics_with_di_2019_Applied_Surf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"central south university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Central South University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"state key laboratory of powder metallurgy","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Key Laboratory of Powder Metallurgy","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan qi","key":"huangyanqipau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Yan qi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhuan","key":"lizhuanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng fei","key":"liupengfeipau","last":"Liu","locid":"85955ab7-64d4-4e44-9dfe-6af8393dc206","name":"Liu, Peng fei","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tian xing","key":"huangtianxingpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Tian xing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Yang","key":"liyangpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peng","key":"xiaopengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Peng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apsusc.2018.12.291","issn":["01694332","18735584"],"issn_org":["01694332"],"journal":"Applied Surface Science","pages":"232-241","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Surface Science","volume":"476"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059855611"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-064f7fe2-0d49-45c1-9928-eab77b34b75a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Tribological properties of Mullite/3Y-TZP ceramics with different content of mullite fabricated by gel-casting","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-051862","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The wind resource is comparatively abundant and the installed capacity of wind power in some areas has increased rapidly in recent years, but the phenomenon of the curtailment of wind power under high penetration is still serious. Power-to-gas (P2G) can be used as a large-scale storage device to store the excess wind power. In this paper, an optimal planning strategy for integrated electricity and natural gas system by means of particle swarm optimization (PSO) is proposed, the P2G devices are added in this hybrid system. The goal of this strategy is to optimize the sizing of P2G plant based on return on investment (ROI) index. The results show that the optimal sizing of P2G plant is 92.43 MW which can reduce about 70% excess wind power, and the ROI is 16.45 years.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hu, Kaige","Li, Jian","Xu, Xiao","Hu, Weihao","Huang, Qi","Xu, Shuwen","Xu, Dechao","Chen, Zhe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-112734"],"event":{"acronym":"ISGT ASIA","end":"2019-05-24","place":"Chengdu, China","start":"2019-05-21","title":"2019 IEEE Innovative Smart Grid Technologies - Asia (ISGT Asia)","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Electric Power Research Institute","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Hydrogen","Investment","Natural gas","Pipelines","Planning","Wind power generation","Wind turbines"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized planning of p000000000002g plant in integrated electricity and natural gas system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8881808/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-112734","identifier":[{"id":"85074923016","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d7bd1cc6-3637-40e4-890e-1912319d7e28"],"keyword":["Hydrogen","Investment","Natural gas","Pipelines","Planning","Wind power generation","Wind turbines"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D0C23A1DBD3EAC1178FD5210B904000"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"china electric power research institute","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Electric Power Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaige","key":"hukaigepau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Kaige","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"lijianpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"xuxiaopau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Weihao","key":"huweihaopau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Weihao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qi","key":"huangqipau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Qi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuwen","key":"xushuwenpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Shuwen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dechao","key":"xudechaopau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Dechao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"chenzhepau","last":"Chen","locid":"d823b80a-ad7f-4339-b75a-8dee8403f02a","name":"Chen, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0002-2919-4481","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/isgt-asia.2019.8881808","isbn":["9781728135212"],"issn":["23788534"],"pages":"1984-1989","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Innovative Smart Grid Technologies - Asia (ISGT Asia), IEEE","status":"p","title":"2019 IEEE Innovative Smart Grid Technologies - Asia (ISGT Asia)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074923016"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d7bd1cc6-3637-40e4-890e-1912319d7e28"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Optimized Planning of P2G Plant in Integrated Electricity and Natural Gas System","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-112734","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, with the increase in energy resource penetration into power systems, more technical requirements regarding the frequency control capability of renewable energy have become required. Plug-in electrical vehicles (PEVs) have become increasingly commercialized, and vehicle-to-grid technology has received extensive attention. This paper proposes a novel frequency control strategy for EVs to participate in the primary and secondary frequency regulations of microgrids. Virtual inertia and virtual damping are introduced using a virtual synchronous generator through AC/DC control. Thus, the charging/discharging device has the characteristics of inertia and damping, which are similar to those of a synchronous generator. According to the droop characteristic of an EV’s charging frequency, the designed auxiliary frequency regulation method can be used to calculate the power adjustment to change the reference value of the EV’s charging/discharging power, allowing the EV to participate in the frequency regulation of a microgrid. The models and connected microgrid were established using MATLAB/Simulink software, and the proposed control strategy was tested. The proposed frequency control strategy can provide virtual inertia, damping, and frequency support; improve the dynamic stability; and realize an effective frequency regulation when the microgrid works in an independent operational mode.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Li, Pengfei","Hu, Weihao","Xu, Xiao","Huang, Qi","Liu, Zhou","Chen, Zhe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-117482"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Hu, Weihao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Electric vehicle","Microgrid","Primary frequency control","Secondary frequency control","Virtual synchronous generator"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a frequency control strategy of electric vehicles in microgrid using virtual synchronous generator control","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-117482","identifier":[{"id":"85074399537","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e7ebcfef-0a23-45a8-a417-7cbb02327763"],"keyword":["Charging and discharging","Electric vehicle","Microgrid","Primary frequency control","Secondary frequency control","Virtual synchronous generator"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F945FC8ECB6A15EE6435ADC1A2C7D9A4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengfei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"530f9cc9-f0e9-4a9d-88cc-11ee47c2a6ef","name":"Li, Pengfei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Weihao","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Weihao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qi","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Qi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhou","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"7eef9354-5956-42e8-9004-a978884796ef","name":"Liu, Zhou","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"d823b80a-ad7f-4339-b75a-8dee8403f02a","name":"Chen, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0002-2919-4481","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.energy.2019.116389","issn":["03605442","18736785"],"issn_org":["03605442"],"journal":"Energy","paperid":"116389","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Energy","volume":"189"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074399537"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e7ebcfef-0a23-45a8-a417-7cbb02327763"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A frequency control strategy of electric vehicles in microgrid using virtual synchronous generator control","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-117482","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Phosphatidylserine is widely used in food, health, chemical and pharmaceutical industries. The phospholipase D-mediated green synthesis of phosphatidylserine has attracted substantial attention in recent years. In this study, the phospholipase D was heterologously expressed in Bacillus subtilis, Pichia pastoris, and Corynebacterium glutamicum, respectively. The highest activity of phospholipase D was observed in C. glutamicum, which was 0.25 U/mL higher than these in B. subtilis (0.14 U/mL) and P. pastoris (0.22 U/mL). System engineering of three potential factors, including (1) signal peptides, (2) ribosome binding site, and (3) promoters, was attempted to improve the expression level of phospholipase D in C. glutamicum. The maximum phospholipase D activity reached 1.9 U/mL, which was 7.6-fold higher than that of the initial level. The enzyme displayed favorable transphosphatidylation activity and it could efficiently catalyze the substrates l-serine and soybean lecithin for synthesis of phosphatidylserine after optimizing the conversion reactions in detail. Under the optimum conditions (trichloromethane/enzyme solution 4:2, 8 mg/mL soybean lecithin, 40 mg/mL l-serine, and 15 mM CaCl 2 , with shaking under 40 °C for 10 h), the reaction process showed 48.6% of conversion rate and 1.94 g/L of accumulated phosphatidylserine concentration. The results highlight the use of heterologous expression, system engineering, and process optimization strategies to adapt a promising phospholipase D for efficient phosphatidylserine production in synthetic application.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hou, Hai Juan","Gong, Jin Song","Dong, Yu Xiu","Qin, Jiufu","Li, Heng","Li, Hui","Lu, Zhen Ming","Zhang, Xiao Mei","Xu, Zheng Hong","Shi, Jin Song"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-348541"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jiangnan University"],"keyword":["Heterologous expression","Phosphatidylserine","Phospholipase D","System engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phospholipase d engineering for improving the biocatalytic synthesis of phosphatidylserine","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85064464484","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-348541","identifier":[{"id":"30989410","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85064464484","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9351c5a1-64c5-4225-8985-097c0b72f47e"],"keyword":["Heterologous expression","Phosphatidylserine","Phospholipase D","System engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D519389B27071DB4D39704A98B02D96D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"jiangnan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jiangnan University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability","Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability, Yeast Cell Factories"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai Juan","key":"houhaijuanpau","last":"Hou","name":"Hou, Hai Juan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin Song","key":"gongjinsongpau","last":"Gong","name":"Gong, Jin Song","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu Xiu","key":"dongyuxiupau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Yu Xiu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiufu","key":"qinjiufupau","last":"Qin","locid":"a583e453-db66-4875-a71a-eb7e71f7e504","name":"Qin, Jiufu","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heng","key":"lihengpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Heng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hui","key":"lihuipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Hui","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhen Ming","key":"luzhenmingpau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Zhen Ming","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Mei","key":"zhangxiaomeipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao Mei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng Hong","key":"xuzhenghongpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Zheng Hong","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin Song","key":"shijinsongpau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Jin Song","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30989410"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00449-019-02116-7","issn":["16157591","16157605"],"issn_org":["16157591"],"issue":"7","journal":"Bioprocess and Biosystems Engineering","pages":"1185-1194","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Bioprocess and Biosystems Engineering","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064464484"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9351c5a1-64c5-4225-8985-097c0b72f47e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Phospholipase D engineering for improving the biocatalytic synthesis of phosphatidylserine","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-348541","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Floor heating (FH) system is a widely-used thermally active building system, which can take advantage of building thermal mass to shift energy demands to off-peak hours. Its ability of effective utilization of low-temperature energy resources also helps to increase energy efficiency and reduce greenhouse gas emissions. However, control of FH systems remains a challenge due to the large thermal inertia of the pipe-embedded concrete floor. In the context of smart grids, the control issue becomes more complicated because the dynamic electricity prices need to be taken into consideration to achieve economic benefits and encourage demand response participation. In this study, an advanced optimal control method, i.e., model predictive control (MPC), is developed for FH systems, which can simultaneously consider all the influential variables including weather conditions, occupancy and dynamic electricity prices. Considering the on-line computational efficiency, a control-oriented dynamic thermal model for a room integrated with FH system is developed and represented in a stochastic state-space form. An economic MPC controller, formulated as a mixed integer linear programming problem, is designed for FH systems. A TRNSYS-MATLAB co-simulation testbed is developed to test and compare different control methods under various operating conditions in terms of energy consumption, thermal comfort and operating costs. Test results show that, compared to the conventional on-off controller, the MPC controller is able to use building thermal mass to optimally shift energy consumption to low-price periods, improve thermal comfort at the beginning of occupancy, reduce energy demand during peak periods, and save electricity costs for residential end-users. The weather conditions and electricity prices have influences on the start-up time and duration of preheating, energy flexibility potential and electricity cost savings of FH systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hu, Maomao","Xiao, Fu","Jørgensen, John Bagterp","Li, Rongling"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352212"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Fu"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hong Kong Polytechnic University"],"keyword":["Demand response","Energy flexibility","Floor heating","Model predictive control","RC model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"price responsive model predictive control of floor heating systems for demand response using building thermal mass","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/198803833/Accepted_manuscript_MPC_Nordhavn_apartment.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The research work presented in this paper is financially supported by a research grant (G-YBTB) in the Hong Kong Polytechnic University (PolyU) and the Strategic Focus Area (SFA) Scheme (1-BBW7) of Research Institute for Sustainable Urban Development (RISUD) in PolyU. Furthermore, the presented work partially receives the support of the CITIES project, the SCA project, and the EnergyLab Nordhavn project in Denmark. All the supports are gratefully acknowledged."],"id":"S01-000.00-352212","identifier":[{"id":"85062463077","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9fa76c02-11e8-4b7d-9336-431b6b20d855"],"keyword":["Demand response","Dynamic electricity prices","Energy flexibility","Floor heating","Model predictive control","RC model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-46457D51C621E13F70B8F28997806431"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/198803833/Accepted_manuscript_MPC_Nordhavn_apartment.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"hk","key":"hong kong polytechnic university","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Hong Kong Polytechnic University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Energy Resources Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Scientific Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maomao","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Maomao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fu","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Fu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Bagterp","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"d2bc6de4-a5c6-43f7-8712-606bd02a88e9","name":"Jørgensen, John Bagterp","orcid":"0000-0001-9799-2808","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rongling","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"3abaa1f5-4a6f-4b8c-93a4-96d52a5beef9","name":"Li, Rongling","orcid":"0000-0002-3654-8014","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2019.02.107","issn":["13594311"],"journal":"Applied Thermal Engineering","pages":"316-329","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Applied Thermal Engineering","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062463077"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9fa76c02-11e8-4b7d-9336-431b6b20d855"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Price-responsive model predictive control of floor heating systems for demand response using building thermal mass","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352212","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Unlike rare earth (RE) (e.g., Eu2+) and non-RE (e.g., Mn2+) doped tunable solid solutions that frequently suffer from the visible re-absorption issue, the Bi3+ ion features the remarkable advantages of a strong UV excitation intensity and an excitation tail of less than 430 nm, giving Bi3+ a strong potential to solve the re-absorption issue for future lighting technology. Herein, we report a type of zircon-type ScVxP1-xO4:Bi3+ (0 ≤ x ≤ 1) emission-tunable solid solution that has a strong UV excitation intensity yet no significant light absorption. We reveal that gradual substitution of larger V ions for smaller P ions, which means expansion of the lattice cell, can shift the excitation edge from 295 to 385 nm, the excitation tail from 340 to 425 nm and emission position from 455 to 641 nm, without causing a large change to the Stokes shift. This spectral shifting is found to be a consequence of the complex dependence of the intra-ion and charge-transfer related transitions of Bi3+ with the crystal structure. Owing to the remarkable excitation-triggered multi-emission properties, we then discover that the ScVxP1-xO4:Bi3+ solid solution can serve as a type of potential material for anti-counterfeiting and information protection applications. This work can provide design insights into discovering more RE and non-RE doped tunable solid solutions in the future, through modulation of the secondary cations in the isostructural crystals.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kang, Fengwen","Sun, Guohuan","Boutinaud, Philippe","Gao, Fei","Wang, Zhenhu","Lu, Jian","Li, Yang Yang","Xiao, Sanshui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-363373"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kang, Fengwen"],"country":["China","France","Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","City University of Hong Kong","Hunan University","Institut de Chimie de Clermont-Ferrand"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tuning the bi sup 000000000003 sup photoemission color over the entire visible region by manipulating secondary cations modulation in the scv sub x sub p sub 000000000001 x sub o sub 000000000004 sub bi sup 000000000003 sup 000000000000 x 000000000001 solid solution","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196506794/Final_manuscript_TC_ART_03_2019_001385.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-363373","identifier":[{"id":"85070765545","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c4d64875-df04-43c1-ac88-d0e66765f57d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11624D4081D37D8813EA3B3F6B43345E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196506794/Final_manuscript_TC_ART_03_2019_001385.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Structured Electromagnetic Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of medical sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","coun