{"abstract":"We propose a terahertz broadband absorber composed by silicon strips with continuous graphene on top of a metal mirror. The simulation results show that under the combined effect of the Fabry–Perot resonance and the dipole mode oscillation excited in the silicon strip array interacting with graphene, this structure can achieve an ultra-wide absorption band from 0.73 to 1.95 THz with absorbance of 90%. By changing the size of the silicon strips or the Fermi level of graphene, the working band of the absorber can be tuned.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhai, Zhaocheng","Zhang, Le","Li, Xiangjun","Xiao, Sanshui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380883"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Le"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Jiliang University"],"keyword":["Broadband absorber","Multilayer graphene","Terahertz wave"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tunable terahertz broadband absorber based on a composite structure of graphene multilayer and silicon strip array","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196506301/_OPTICS_23456_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380883","identifier":[{"id":"85053826741","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fee875ef-3785-4277-8bc2-cf6f7ac182e9"],"keyword":["Broadband absorber","Multilayer graphene","Terahertz wave","Tunable absorber"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2EDC272DA9DC7E86B832D298B50902A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196506301/_OPTICS_23456_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china jiliang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Jiliang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Structured Electromagnetic Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhaocheng","key":"zhaipau","last":"Zhai","name":"Zhai, Zhaocheng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Le","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Le","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiangjun","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiangjun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanshui","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"c516dded-c5eb-40a6-b2dd-37be55b893c8","name":"Xiao, Sanshui","orcid":"0000-0001-6529-5047","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.optcom.2018.09.017","issn":["00304018","18730310"],"issn_org":["00304018"],"journal":"Optics Communications","pages":"199-202","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Optics Communications","volume":"431"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85053826741"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fee875ef-3785-4277-8bc2-cf6f7ac182e9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tunable terahertz broadband absorber based on a composite structure of graphene multilayer and silicon strip array","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380883","year":"2019","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To examine retinal blood flow at arteriovenous crossings using spectral-domain optical coherence tomography (SD-OCT). METHODS: Retrospective observational case series of 11 arteriovenous crossings in 10 eyes examined by SD-OCT and fluorescein angiography on suspicion of manifest or imminent branch retinal vein occlusion. RESULTS: Fluorescein angiographic evidence of turbulence was seen at 5 of 11 arteriovenous crossings, whereas laminar angiographic flow was intact at the crossing and downstream thereof at the remaining 6 crossings. On SD-OCT, chaotic reflectivity patterns were seen at the point of crossing and downstream thereof in all 5 cases with angiographic turbulence, whereas an intravascular trilayer SD-OCT pattern consistent with laminar flow was seen throughout the examined course of the vein in the eyes with laminar angiographic flow. CONCLUSION: We examined retinal blood flow at and near arteriovenous crossings and found that SD-OCT may rival fluorescein angiography in the ability to demonstrate turbulent venous blood flow.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Willerslev, Anne","Li, Xiao Qiang","Munch, Inger Christine","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395949"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Female","Fluorescein Angiography methods","Fundus Oculi","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Regional Blood Flow physiology","Retina pathology","Retinal Artery pathology","Retinal Vein Occlusion diagnosis","Retinal Vein pathology","Retrospective Studies","Tomography Optical Coherence methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relation between fluorescein angiographic and spectral domain optical coherence tomography findings of blood flow turbulence at arteriovenous crossings in the retina","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-395949","identifier":[{"id":"28134740","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85058757011","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-042ccdfd-3289-4d0c-bb42-e91a3d9f84c5"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Female","Fluorescein Angiography/methods","Fundus Oculi","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Regional Blood Flow/physiology","Retina/pathology","Retinal Artery/pathology","Retinal Vein Occlusion/diagnosis","Retinal Vein/pathology","Retrospective Studies","Tomography, Optical Coherence/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-20168B92BC5C3E6B7328448B181F1F5B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"willerslevpau","last":"Willerslev","name":"Willerslev, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Qiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28134740"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/icb.0000000000000534","issn":["19351089","19371578"],"issn_org":["19351089"],"issue":"1","journal":"Retinal Cases & Brief Reports","pages":"61-66","status":"p","title":"Retinal Cases & Brief Reports","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058757011"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-042ccdfd-3289-4d0c-bb42-e91a3d9f84c5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RELATION BETWEEN FLUORESCEIN ANGIOGRAPHIC AND SPECTRAL-DOMAIN OPTICAL COHERENCE TOMOGRAPHY FINDINGS OF BLOOD FLOW TURBULENCE AT ARTERIOVENOUS CROSSINGS IN THE RETINA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395949","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Both short and long sleep are associated with an adverse lipid profile, likely through different biological pathways. To elucidate the biology of sleep-associated adverse lipid profile, we conduct multi-ancestry genome-wide sleep-SNP interaction analyses on three lipid traits (HDL-c, LDL-c and triglycerides). In the total study sample (discovery + replication) of 126,926 individuals from 5 different ancestry groups, when considering either long or short total sleep time interactions in joint analyses, we identify 49 previously unreported lipid loci, and 10 additional previously unreported lipid loci in a restricted sample of European-ancestry cohorts. In addition, we identify new gene-sleep interactions for known lipid loci such as LPL and PCSK9. The previously unreported lipid loci have a modest explained variance in lipid levels: most notable, gene-short-sleep interactions explain 4.25% of the variance in triglyceride level. Collectively, these findings contribute to our understanding of the biological mechanisms involved in sleep-associated adverse lipid profiles.","author_count":148,"contributors":["Noordam, Raymond","Bos, Maxime M","Wang, Heming","Winkler, Thomas W","Bentley, Amy R","Kilpeläinen, Tuomas O","de Vries, Paul S","Sung, Yun Ju","Schwander, Karen","Cade, Brian E","Manning, Alisa","Aschard, Hugues","Brown, Michael R","Chen, Han","Franceschini, Nora","Musani, Solomon K","Richard, Melissa","Vojinovic, Dina","Aslibekyan, Stella","Bartz, Traci M","de Las Fuentes, Lisa","Feitosa, Mary","Horimoto, Andrea R","Ilkov, Marjan","Kho, Minjung","Kraja, Aldi","Li, Changwei","Lim, Elise","Liu, Yongmei","Mook-Kanamori, Dennis O","Rankinen, Tuomo","Tajuddin, Salman M","van der Spek, Ashley","Wang, Zhe","Marten, Jonathan","Laville, Vincent","Alver, Maris","Evangelou, Evangelos","Graff, Maria E","He, Meian","Kühnel, Brigitte","Lyytikäinen, Leo-Pekka","Marques-Vidal, Pedro","Nolte, Ilja M","Palmer, Nicholette D","Rauramaa, Rainer","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Snieder, Harold","Weiss, Stefan","Wen, Wanqing","Yanek, Lisa R","Adolfo, Correa","Ballantyne, Christie","Bielak, Larry","Biermasz, Nienke R","Boerwinkle, Eric","Dimou, Niki","Eiriksdottir, Gudny","Gao, Chuan","Gharib, Sina A","Gottlieb, Daniel J","Haba-Rubio, José","Harris, Tamara B","Heikkinen, Sami","Heinzer, Raphaël","Hixson, James E","Homuth, Georg","Ikram, M Arfan","Komulainen, Pirjo","Krieger, Jose E","Lee, Jiwon","Liu, Jingmin","Lohman, Kurt K","Luik, Annemarie I","Mägi, Reedik","Martin, Lisa W","Meitinger, Thomas","Metspalu, Andres","Milaneschi, Yuri","Nalls, Mike A","O'Connell, Jeff","Peters, Annette","Peyser, Patricia","Raitakari, Olli T","Reiner, Alex P","Rensen, Patrick C N","Rice, Treva K","Rich, Stephen S","Roenneberg, Till","Rotter, Jerome I","Schreiner, Pamela J","Shikany, James","Sidney, Stephen S","Sims, Mario","Sitlani, Colleen M","Sofer, Tamar","Strauch, Konstantin","Swertz, Morris A","Taylor, Kent D","Uitterlinden, André G","van Duijn, Cornelia M","Völzke, Henry","Waldenberger, Melanie","Wallance, Robert B","van Dijk, Ko Willems","Yu, Caizheng","Zonderman, Alan B","Becker, Diane M","Elliott, Paul","Esko, Tõnu","Gieger, Christian","Grabe, Hans J","Lakka, Timo A","Lehtimäki, Terho","North, Kari E","Penninx, Brenda W J H","Vollenweider, Peter","Wagenknecht, Lynne E","Wu, Tangchun","Xiang, Yong-Bing","Zheng, Wei","Arnett, Donna K","Bouchard, Claude","Evans, Michele K","Gudnason, Vilmundur","Kardia, Sharon","Kelly, Tanika N","Kritchevsky, Stephen B","Loos, Ruth J F","Pereira, Alexandre C","Province, Mike","Psaty, Bruce M","Rotimi, Charles","Zhu, Xiaofeng","Amin, Najaf","Cupples, L Adrienne","Fornage, Myriam","Fox, Ervin F","Guo, Xiuqing","Gauderman, W James","Rice, Kenneth","Kooperberg, Charles","Munroe, Patricia B","Liu, Ching-Ti","Morrison, Alanna C","Rao, Dabeeru C","van Heemst, Diana","Redline, Susan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Americ