sities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f997cd11-7067-407e-b370-4e586b567eb5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Viral integration drives multifocal HCC during the occult HBV infection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542404","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE. We describe changes in choroidal thickness from age 11 to 16 years and its association with ocular biometrics and body development. METHOD. In this longitudinal, population-based observational study, choroidal thickness was measured subfoveally and 1- and 3-mm temporal thereof using enhanced depth imaging spectral domain optical coherence tomography. Analyses were stratified by sex and adjusted for age and the time of day that the scan was performed. RESULTS. The study included 687 participants (304 boys). Median (interquartile range [IQR]) age was 11.5 (0.6) years at baseline and 16.6 (0.3) years at follow-up. Mean increase in choroidal thickness was 33, 27, and 11 lm at the three respective locations. The subfoveal choroid thickened less in eyes whose axial length increased more (boys, b ¼ 85 lm/mm; 95% confidence interval [CI], 104 to 66, P < 0.0001; girls, b ¼ 105 lm/mm; 95% CI, 121 to 89, P < 0.0001) and in eyes with a more negative refractive development (boys, 11 lm/diopters [D]; 95% CI, 4.0 to 18, P ¼ 0.0022; girls, 22 lm/D; 95% CI, 16 to 27, P < 0.0001). Subfoveal choroidal thickness increased less in girls who underwent early puberty (Tanner stage 4 vs. 1; 39 lm’ 95% CI, 72 to 5.9, P ¼ 0.021) and who had a longer baseline axial length (b ¼ 8.6 lm/mm; 95% CI, 15 to 2.7, P ¼ 0.0043), and more in girls who grew taller (b ¼ 0.9 lm/cm; 95% CI, 0.1 to 1.7, P ¼ 0.026). CONCLUSIONS. The choroid increased in thickness from age 11 to 16 years. The increase was greater in girls with later sexual maturation and smaller in eyes that added more axial length and had a relatively negative refractive development. Keywords: choroidal thickness changes, longitudinal study, cohort study, axial eye growth","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt","Li, Xiao Qiang","Larsen, Michael","Olsen, Else Marie","Skovgaard, Anne Mette","Kessel, Line","Munch, Inger Christine"],"cuid":["S02-099.36-039819"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt"],"keyword":["Axial eye growth","Choroidal thickness changes","Cohort study","Longitudinal study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"five year change in choroidal thickness in relation to body development and axial eye elongation the ccc000000002000 eye study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.19-26807","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.36-039819","identifier":[{"id":"85072581182","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000488842600003","type":"wos"},{"id":"31546258","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-046780fd-718e-43fd-9c1d-73943bb52e34","sdu-5df5a801-638b-42c4-a924-87cf8ad49198"],"keyword":["axial eye growth","choroidal thickness changes","cohort study","longitudinal study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DCD98110A903DF9352951155AFD62B8E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/159958769/Open_Access_version","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.19-26807","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/228958062/Five_Year_Change_in_Choroidal_Thickness_in_Relation_to_Body_Development_and_Axial_Eye_Elongation.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Danish Stem Cell Center, Developmental biology - endoderm and pancreas development Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mathias Hvidtfelt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Mathias Hvidtfelt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Qiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1a555c4a-f5eb-40fe-8f79-6442177ac676","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Else Marie","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"9be69922-e68e-4556-9b40-34a82fc88a15","name":"Olsen, Else Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Mette","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"16faee51-f101-47f9-8757-c611e52d7381","name":"Skovgaard, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8793-8303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31546258"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1167/iovs.19-26807","issn":["01460404","02730189"],"issn_org":["15525783"],"issue":"12","journal":"Investigative Ophthalmology & Visual Science","pages":"3930-3936","status":"p","title":"Investigative Ophthalmology & Visual Science","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85072581182"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-046780fd-718e-43fd-9c1d-73943bb52e34","sdu-5df5a801-638b-42c4-a924-87cf8ad49198"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Five-Year Change in Choroidal Thickness in Relation to Body Development and Axial Eye Elongation : The CCC2000 Eye Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.36-039819","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background: The gut microbiota plays important roles in modulating host metabolism. Previous studies have demonstrated differences in the gut microbiome of T2D and prediabetic individuals compared to healthy individuals, with distinct disease-related microbial profiles being reported in groups of different age and ethnicity. However, confounding factors such as anti-diabetic medication hamper identification of the gut microbial changes in disease development. Method: We used a combination of in-depth metagenomics and metaproteomics analyses of faecal samples from treatment-naïve type 2 diabetic (TN-T2D, n = 77), pre-diabetic (Pre-DM, n = 80), and normal glucose tolerant (NGT, n = 97) individuals to investigate compositional and functional changes of the gut microbiota and the faecal content of microbial and host proteins in Pre-DM and treatment-naïve T2D individuals to elucidate possible host-microbial interplays characterizing different disease stages. Findings: We observed distinct differences characterizing the gut microbiota of these three groups and validated several key features in an independent TN-T2D cohort. We also demonstrated that the content of several human antimicrobial peptides and pancreatic enzymes differed in faecal samples between three groups. Interpretation: Our findings suggest a complex, disease stage-dependent interplay between the gut microbiota and the host and point to the value of metaproteomics to gain further insight into interplays between the gut microbiota and the host. Fund: The study was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (No. 31601073), the National Key Research and Development Program of China (No. 2017YFC0909703) and the Shenzhen Municipal Government of China (No. JCYJ20170817145809215). The funders had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Zhong, Huanzi","Ren, Huahui","Lu, Yan","Fang, Chao","Hou, Guixue","Yang, Ziyi","Chen, Bing","Yang, Fangming","Zhao, Yue","Shi, Zhun","Zhou, Baojin","Wu, Jiegen","Zou, Hua","Zi, Jin","Chen, Jiayu","Bao, Xiao","Hu, Yihe","Gao, Yan","Zhang, Jun","Xu, Xun","Hou, Yong","Yang, Huanming","Wang, Jian","Liu, Siqi","Jia, Huijue","Madsen, Lise","Brix, Susanne","Kristiansen, Karsten","Liu, Fang","Li, Junhua"],"cuid":["S02-099.81-036368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Kristiansen, Karsten"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","BGI Group","Suzhou Centre for Disease Control and Prevention"],"keyword":["Metagenomics","Metaproteomics","Prediabetes","Treatment naïve type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distinct gut metagenomics and metaproteomics signatures in prediabetics and treatment naïve type 000000000002 diabetics","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ebiom.2019.08.048","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.81-036368","identifier":[{"id":"31492563","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85071606525","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6796533","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-a60d40d8-b53f-4a9f-b64c-6348a2050e5f","ku-b061a50d-f386-4491-8f2a-186ceca9ba78"],"keyword":["Metagenomics","Metaproteomics","Prediabetes","Treatment-naïve type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D5BD713468A7BB2829900FC6A8536DDB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195988157/1_s2.0_S2352396419305729_main.pdf","version":"Published