sponding":null,"first":"Junhua","key":"lijunhuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Junhua","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31492563"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ebiom.2019.08.048","issn":["23523964"],"journal":"EBioMedicine","pages":"373-383","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"EBioMedicine","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071606525"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a60d40d8-b53f-4a9f-b64c-6348a2050e5f","ku-b061a50d-f386-4491-8f2a-186ceca9ba78"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Distinct gut metagenomics and metaproteomics signatures in prediabetics and treatment-naïve type 2 diabetics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.81-036368","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) harbors somatic hypermutation (SHM) in the immunoglobulin heavy chain and light chain variable region genes, IGHV and IGK/LV. Recent studies have revealed that IGV SHM creates neoantigens that activate T-cell responses against B-cell lymphoma. METHODS: To determine the clinical relevance of IGV SHM in DLBCL treated with standard immunochemotherapy, we performed next-generation sequencing of the immunoglobulin variable regions and complementarity determining region 3 (CDR3) for 378 patients with de novo DLBCL. The prognostic effects of IGV SHM and ongoing SHM or intra-clonal heterogeneity were analyzed in the training (192 patients), validation (186 patients), and overall DLBCL cohorts. To gain mechanistic insight, we analyzed the predicted IG-derived neoantigens' immunogenicity potential, determined by the major histocompatibility complex-binding affinity and the frequency-of-occurrence of T cell-exposed motifs (TCEMs) in a TCEM repertoire derived from human proteome, microbiome, and pathogen databases. Furthermore, IGV SHM was correlated with molecular characteristics of DLBCL and PD-1/L1 expression in the tumor microenvironment assessed by fluorescent multiplex immunohistochemistry. RESULTS: SHM was commonly found in IGHV and less frequently in IGK/LV. High levels of clonal IGHV SHM (SHMhigh) were associated with prolonged overall survival in DLBCL patients, particularly those without BCL2 or MYC translocation. In contrast, long heavy chain CDR3 length, the presence of IGHV ongoing SHM in DLBCL, and high clonal IGK/LV SHM in germinal center B-cell-like (GCB)-DLBCL were associated with poor prognosis. These prognostic effects were significant in both the training and validation sets. By prediction, the SHMhigh groups harbored more potentially immune-stimulatory neoantigens with high binding affinity and rare TCEMs. PD-1/L1 expression in CD8+ T cells was significantly lower in IGHV SHMhigh than in SHMlow patients with activated B-cell-like DLBCL, whereas PD-1 expression in CD4+ T cells and PD-L1 expression in natural killer cells were higher in IGK/LV SHMhigh than in SHMlow patients with GCB-DLBCL. PD-L1/L2 (9p24.1) amplification was associated with high IGHV SHM and ongoing SHM. CONCLUSIONS: These results show for the first time that IGV SHMhigh and ongoing SHM have prognostic effects in DLBCL and potential implications for PD-1/PD-L1 blockade and neoantigen-based immunotherapies.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Xu-Monette, Zijun Y","Li, Jianyong","Xia, Yi","Crossley, Beryl","Bremel, Robert D","Miao, Yi","Xiao, Min","Snyder, Thomas","Manyam, Ganiraju C","Tan, Xiaohong","Zhang, Hongwei","Visco, Carlo","Tzankov, Alexandar","Dybkær, Karen","Bhagat, Govind","Tam, Wayne","You, Hua","Hsi, Eric D","van Krieken, J Han","Huh, Jooryung","Ponzoni, Maurilio","Ferreri, Andrés J M","Møller, Michael B","Piris, Miguel A","Winter, Jane N","Medeiros, Jeffrey T","Xu, Bing","Li, Yong","Kirsch, Ilan","Young, Ken H"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011798"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Young, Ken H."],"country":["China","Italy","Netherlands","South Korea","Spain","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["Adaptive Biotechnologies","Affiliated Cancer Hospital of Guangzhou Medical University","All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","Cardiology","Cleveland Clinic Foundation","Columbia University Medical Center","Duke University Medical Center","Northwestern University","Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine","Pediatric Orthopaedic Unit IRCCS Ospedale San Raffaele","Radboud University Medical Center","San Bortolo Hospital Of Vicenza","University Hospital Basel","University Hospital of Basel","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Ulsan","Weill Cornell Medicine","Xiamen University","ioGenetics LLC"],"keyword":["9p 24","BCL2","DLBCL","HLA","Immunoglobulin","MHC","NGS","Neoantigen","PD 1","SHM"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Department of Pathology, San Bortolo Hospital, Vicenza 36100, Italy."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immunoglobulin somatic hypermutation has clinical impact in dlbcl and potential implications for immune checkpoint blockade and neoantigen based immunotherapies","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40425-019-0730-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011798","identifier":[{"id":"31640780","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6806565","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85073741760","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f6e96dbe-266f-4dcb-98f0-c97dedbe7e58","sdu-8334961e-48d4-4403-910c-17b678f18d05"],"keyword":["9p.24","BCL2","DLBCL","HLA","Immunoglobulin","MHC","NGS","Neoantigen","PD-1","SHM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F5B3FBE4BFEAA949370F231845F78DB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/313244720/Xu_Monette_et_al_2019_Immunoglobulin_somatic_hypermutation_has_clinical_impact_in_DLBCL_and_potential_implications_for_immune_checkpoint_blockade.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40425-019-0730-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/161191775/s40425_019_0730_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub