I-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f6e96dbe-266f-4dcb-98f0-c97dedbe7e58","sdu-8334961e-48d4-4403-910c-17b678f18d05"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Immunoglobulin somatic hypermutation has clinical impact in DLBCL and potential implications for immune checkpoint blockade and neoantigen-based immunotherapies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011798","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To assess the prevalence and associations of small hard drusen in a child cohort. Methods: Cross-sectional study of 11- to 12-year-old Danish children from the population-based Copenhagen Child Cohort 2000 Eye Study. Fovea-centered, 45° color images of both eyes were graded for macular drusen (within one optic-disc-rim-to-fovea distance of the foveal center) and for extramacular drusen. Analyses tested for associations between drusen and anthropometric measures including choroidal thickness. Results: Gradable fundus images from both eyes were available for 1333 children (640 boys, 693 girls) with a mean (SD) age of 11.7 (0.40) years. One or more small hard macular drusen (diameter <63 μm) were present in 82 (6.2%) right eyes and 82 (6.2%) left eyes and in 147 (11.0%) subjects. Four children (0.30%) had 20 or more small hard macular drusen in one or both eyes. Extramacular small hard drusen were present in 10.7% of children, and 19% of children had such drusen anywhere. The odds for having one or more small hard macular drusen increased with subfoveal choroidal thickness with an odds ratio of 1.15 (95% confidence interval, 1.03-1.28; P = 0.013) per 50-μm thicker choroid, adjusted for age and sex. The association with choroidal thickness was also present for extramacular drusen. Conclusions: Having one or more small hard macular drusen was common in 11- to 12-year old children and it was associated with a thicker subfoveal choroid. Few children had many small hard drusen. There is no apparent clinical impact of small hard drusen in childhood.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Munch, Inger Christine","Li, Xiao Qiang","Ahmad, Shaista Sumbal Mulk","Olsen, Else Marie","Skovgaard, Anne Mette","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-047530"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["CCC2000","Children","Choroid","Cohort study","Optic coherence tomography","Population based","Small hard drusen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"small hard macular drusen and associations in 000000000011 to 000000000012 year old children in the copenhagen child cohort 000000002000 eye study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.18-25877","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-047530","identifier":[{"id":"000466757300019","type":"wos"},{"id":"85064318991","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30947335","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f863f9d6-4b0c-4237-97eb-2596599c131f","sdu-cb6d5d63-4ece-4550-b089-61b0f1a8dd58"],"keyword":["CCC2000","children","choroid","cohort study","optic coherence tomography","population-based","small hard drusen"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C402D923B89872CE7A8FAE358FB6E139"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/149799610/Small_Hard_Macular_Drusen_and_Associations_in_11_to_12_Year_Old_Children_in_the_Copenhagen_Child_Cohort_2000_Eye_Study.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.18-25877","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/218435303/Small_Hard_Macular_Drusen_and_Associations_in_11_to_12_Year_Old_Children_in_the_Copenhagen_Child_Cohort_2000_Eye_Study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Qiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shaista Sumbal Mulk","key":"ahmadpau","last":"Ahmad","locid":"8f6d8e81-bfa7-40e6-9b23-8f9d330febfa","name":"Ahmad, Shaista Sumbal Mulk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Else Marie","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"9be69922-e68e-4556-9b40-34a82fc88a15","name":"Olsen, Else Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Anne Mette","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"f1e6d144-f7de-4477-a60c-3046ccb9ca8d","name":"Skovgaard, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8793-8303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30947335"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1167/iovs.18-25877","issn":["01460404","02730189"],"issn_org":["15525783"],"issue":"5","journal":"Investigative Ophthalmology & Visual Science","pages":"1454-1460","status":"p","title":"Investigative Ophthalmology & Visual Science","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064318991"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f863f9d6-4b0c-4237-97eb-2596599c131f","sdu-cb6d5d63-4ece-4550-b089-61b0f1a8dd58"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Small Hard Macular Drusen and Associations in 11-to 12-Year-Old Children in the Copenhagen Child Cohort 2000 Eye Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-047530","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"MicroRNAs (miRNAs) are a type of small non-coding RNAs that participate in diverse cellular processes including microbial invasion and immune defense. In a previous study, we identified a large amount of Japanese flounder (Paralichthys olivaceus) miRNAs responsive to megalocytivirus infection. In the present study, we examined the function of one of these miRNAs, pol-miR-194a, in association with the infectivity of Edwardsiella tarda, an intracellular bacterial pathogen to many fish species including flounder. We found that pol-miR-194a was induced in expression to a significant extent in the spleen, liver, and gill of Japanese flounder infected by E. tarda. Transfection of flounder cells with pol-miR-194a mimic significantly enhanced the intracellular replication of E. tarda. pol-miR-194a was able to interact specifically with the 3′UTR of IRF7 in a negative manner, resulting in inhibition of IRF7 expression. Consistently, pol-miR-194a significantly blocked the promoter activity of type Ⅰ interferon. Taken together, these results indicate that pol-miR-194a plays an important role in the regulation of flounder immune response as well as microbial infection, and that pol-miR-194a probably serves as a target for E. tarda to manipulate and escape host immune defense.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Guan, Xiao lu","Zhang, Bao cun","Sun, Li"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-144690"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Sun, Li"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Laboratory for Marine Mineral Resources, Qingdao National Laboratory for Marine Science and Technology","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Immune escape","Paralichthys olivaceus","Type I interferon","miRNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pol mir 000000000194a of japanese flounder i paralichthys olivaceus i suppresses type i interferon response and facilitates i edwardsiella tarda i infection","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85060053919","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-144690","identifier":[{"id":"30641186","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85060053919","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-1abfcd6d-4d52-4fe0-a914-f6747eaef872"],"keyword":["Edwardsiella tarda","Immune escape","Paralichthys olivaceus","Type I interferon","miRNA"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4F53D43A003B7201198364F6D72A9804"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"laboratory for marine mineral resources qingdao national laboratory for marine science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Laboratory for Marine Mineral Resources, Qingdao National Laboratory for Marine Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao lu","key":"guanpau","last":"Guan","name":"Guan, Xiao lu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bao cun","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95fd8297-24a7-4477-b204-aba9e29edfa7","name":"Zhang, Bao cun","orcid":"0000-0001-6104-0848","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Li","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30641186"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fsi.2019.01.017","issn":["10504648","10959947"],"issn_org":["10504648"],"journal":"Fish and Shellfish Immunology","pages":"220-225","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Fish and Shellfish Immunology","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060053919"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1abfcd6d-4d52-4fe0-a914-f6747eaef872"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"pol-miR-194a of Japanese flounder (<i>Paralichthys olivaceus) </i>suppresses type I interferon response and facilitates <i>Edwardsiella tarda </i>infection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-144690","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Global paddy soil is the primary source of methane, a potent greenhouse gas. It is therefore highly important to understand the carbon cycling in paddy soil. Microbial reduction of iron, which is widely found in paddy soil, is likely coupled with the oxidation of dissolved organic matter (DOM) and suppresses methanogenesis. However, little is known about the biotransformation of small molecular DOM accumulated under flooded conditions and the effect of iron reduction on the biotransformation pathway. Here, we carried out anaerobic incubation experiments using field-collected samples amended with ferrihydrite and different short-chain fatty acids. Our results showed that less than 20% of short-chain fatty acids were mineralized and released to the atmosphere. Using Fourier transform ion cyclotron resonance mass spectrometry, we further found that a large number of recalcitrant molecules were produced during microbial consumption of these short-chain fatty acids. Moreover, the biotransformation efficiency of short-chain fatty acids decreased with the increasing length of carbon chains. Ferrihydrite addition promoted microbial assimilation of short-chain fatty acids as well as enhanced the activation and biotransformation of indigenous stable carbon in the soil replenished with formate. This study demonstrates the significance of ferrihydrite in the biotransformation of labile DOM and promotes a more comprehensive understanding of the coupling of iron reduction and carbon cycling in paddy soils.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Xu, Jian-Xin","Li, Xiao-Ming","Sun, Guo-Xin","Cui, Li","Ding, Long-Jun","He, Chen","Li, Li-Guan","Shi, Quan","Smets, Barth F.","Zhu, Yong-Guan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325744"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhu, Yong-Guan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China University of Petroleum","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fate of labile organic carbon in paddy soil is regulated by microbial ferric iron reduction","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85071066566","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-325744","identifier":[{"id":"85071066566","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31269402","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-4733de31-b788-437b-8977-4184f1f5d641"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FCD8BA3E9989D0B5D918C1844F55F72C"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"china university of petroleum","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China University of Petroleum","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian-Xin","key":"xujianxinpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Jian-Xin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Ming","key":"lixiaomingpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao-Ming","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Guo-Xin","key":"sunguoxinpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Guo-Xin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"cuilipau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Li","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Long-Jun","key":"dinglongjunpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Long-Jun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chen","key":"hechenpau","last":"He","name":"He, Chen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Li-Guan","key":"liliguanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Li-Guan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Quan","key":"shiquanpau","last":"Shi","name":"Shi, Quan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barth F.","key":"smetsbarthfpau","last":"Smets","locid":"915b38db-4460-4b17-b74c-e5cc7581d03f","name":"Smets, Barth F.","orcid":"0000-0003-4119-6292","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong-Guan","key":"zhuyongguanpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Yong-Guan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31269402"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.est.9b01323","issn":["0013936X","15205851"],"issn_org":["0013936X"],"issue":"15","journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","pages":"8633-8542","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science & Technology","title_org":"Environmental Science and Technology","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071066566"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4733de31-b788-437b-8977-4184f1f5d641"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fate of Labile Organic Carbon in Paddy Soil Is Regulated by Microbial Ferric Iron Reduction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-325744","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this White Paper we present the potential of the Enhanced X-ray Timing and Polarimetry (eXTP) mission for determining the nature of dense matter; neutron star cores host an extreme density regime which cannot be replicated in a terrestrial laboratory. The tightest statistical constraints on the dense matter equation of state will come from pulse profile modelling of accretion-powered pulsars, burst oscillation sources, and rotation-powered pulsars. Additional constraints will derive from spin measurements, burst spectra, and properties of the accretion flows in the vicinity of the neutron star. Under development by an international Consortium led by the Institute of High Energy Physics of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, the eXTP mission is expected to be launched in the mid 2020s.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Watts, Anna L.","Yu, Wen Fei","Poutanen, Juri","Zhang, Shu","Bhattacharyya, Sudip","Bogdanov, Slavko","Ji, Long","Patruno, Alessandro","Riley, Thomas E.","Bakala, Pavel","Baykal, Altan","Bernardini, Federico","Bombaci, Ignazio","Brown, Edward","Cavecchi, Yuri","Chakrabarty, Deepto","Chenevez, J.","Degenaar, Nathalie","Del Santo, Melania","Di Salvo, Tiziana","Doroshenko, Victor","Falanga, Maurizio","Ferdman, Robert D.","Feroci, Marco","Gambino, Angelo F.","Ge, Ming Yu","Greif, Svenja K.","Guillot, Sebastien","Gungor, Can","Hartmann, Dieter H.","Hebeler, Kai","Heger, Alexander","Homan, Jeroen","Iaria, Rosario","Zand, Jean in’t","Kargaltsev, Oleg","Kurkela, Aleksi","Lai, Xiao Yu","Li, Ang","Li, Xiang Dong","Li, Zhao Sheng","Linares, Manuel","Lu, Fang Jun","Mahmoodifar, Simin","Méndez, Mariano","Coleman Miller, M.","Morsink, Sharon","Nättilä, Joonas","Possenti, Andrea","Xu, Yu Peng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357465"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","N