:"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hannah","key":"zuckermanhannahpau","last":"Zuckerman","name":"Zuckerman, Hannah","rank":1577,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ran","key":"lyuranpau","last":"Lyu","name":"Lyu, Ran","rank":1578,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wayne","key":"pullanwaynepau","last":"Pullan","name":"Pullan, Wayne","rank":1579,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33326193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/database/baz085","issn":["17580463"],"journal":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","pages":"1-67","paperid":"085","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","title_org":"Database","volume":"2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082592913"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-88b053a3-63ab-4380-ab20-90a54b540224","au-6bf5b1c8-6cc1-4ee4-b711-48f478a90279","ku-291608f7-132f-41ac-94ae-fe9aa192baf0","sdu-a9479d7b-e13c-4f9b-8edd-dd71403513e8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Large expert-curated database for benchmarking document similarity detection in biomedical literature search","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-087.05-006608","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Renewable energy is widely used as a clean energy in the world, yet the intermittent of the power generation from renewable energy power plants, resulting in poor quality of power supply. However, the hybrid energy system and some energy storage devices can be installed to mitigate the power fluctuation, to achieve power smoothing and maximize the profit, a double-objective optimization model of hybrid system integrated with micro-hydro power (MHP), photovoltaic (PV), and pumped hydro storage (PHS) is established in this study. The day-ahead optimized operation strategy of the PHS based-on hour-level data of seven days is obtained, which aims to maximize the similarity value (SIM) between the power generation curve and load profile, and the economic revenue (ER) of the PHS. Optimized schedule is obtained by means of chance-constrained programming (CCP) and modified multi-objective particle swarm optimization (MOPSO). The performance of the model is evaluated by using the meteorological, the historical MHP power generation and the load data obtained in Xiaojin County, Sichuan province, China. The simulation results reveal that the best trade-off value between SIM and ER can be obtained on the Pareto front with comprehensive consideration of the system operation strategy and target. Furthermore, the generation/load similarity can be increased 7.89% under the participating of the PHS.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Li, Tao","Hu, Weihao","Xu, Xiao","Huang, Qi","Chen, Gang","Han, Xiaoyan","Chen, Zhe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-089055"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chengdu University","State Grid Sichuan Electric Power Company","University of Electronic Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Economics","Energy storage","Hybrid power systems","Power generation","Renewable energy sources","Reservoirs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimized operation of hybrid system integrated with mhp pv and phs considering generation load similarity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2019.2932851","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-089055","identifier":[{"id":"85071135009","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-85ef336f-602d-40b4-b54d-a8b1955c814c"],"keyword":["Economics","Energy storage","Hybrid power systems","Power generation","Renewable energy sources","Reservoirs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67014127A782D715AAF3528583072393"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2019.2932851","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"university of electronic science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Electronic Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chengdu university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chengdu University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"state grid sichuan electric power company","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Grid Sichuan Electric Power Company","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tao","key":"litaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Tao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Weihao","key":"huweihaopau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Weihao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"xuxiaopau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qi","key":"huangqipau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Qi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gang","key":"chengangpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Gang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoyan","key":"hanxiaoyanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Xiaoyan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"chenzhepau","last":"Chen","locid":"d823b80a-ad7f-4339-b75a-8dee8403f02a","name":"Chen, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0002-2919-4481","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/access.2019.2932851","issn":["21693536"],"journal":"IEEE Access","pages":"107793-107804","paperid":"8786116","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Access","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071135009"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-85ef336f-602d-40b4-b54d-a8b1955c814c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Optimized Operation of Hybrid System Integrated With MHP, PV and PHS Considering Generation/Load Similarity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-089055","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Microorganisms in wastewater treatment plants (WWTPs) are essential for water purification to protect public and environmental health. However, the diversity of microorganisms and the factors that control it are poorly understood. Using a systematic global-sampling effort, we analysed the 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequences from ~1,200 activated sludge samples taken from 269 WWTPs in 23 countries on 6 continents. Our analyses revealed that the global activated sludge bacterial communities contain ~1 billion bacterial phylotypes with a Poisson lognormal diversity distribution. Despite this high diversity, activated sludge has a small, global core bacterial community (n = 28 operational taxonomic units) that is strongly linked to activated sludge performance. Meta-analyses with global datasets associate the activated sludge microbiomes most closely to freshwater populations. In contrast to macroorganism diversity, activated sludge bacterial communities show no latitudinal gradient. Furthermore, their spatial turnover is scale-dependent and appears to be largely driven by stochastic processes (dispersal and drift), although deterministic factors (temperature and organic input) are also important. Our findings enhance our mechanistic understanding of the global diversity and biogeography of activated sludge bacterial communities within a theoretical ecology framework and have important implications for microbial ecology and wastewater treatment processes.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Wu, Linwei","Ning, Daliang","Zhang, Bing","Li, Yong","Zhang, Ping","Shan, Xiaoyu","Zhang, Qiuting","Brown, Mathew","Li, Zhenxin","Van Nostrand, Joy D.","Ling, Fangqiong","Xiao, Naijia","Zhang, Ya","Vierheilig, Julia","Wells, George F.","Yang, Yunfeng","Deng, Ye","Tu, Qichau","Wang, Aijie","Zhang, Tong","He, Zhili","Keller, Jurg","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Alvarez, Pedro J. J.","Criddle, Craig S.","Wagner, Michael","Tiedje, James M.","He, Qiang","Curtis, Thomas P.","Stahl, David A","Alvarez-Cohen, Lisa","Rittmann, Bruce E.","Wen, Xianghua","Zhou, Jizhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-100841"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["Global Water Microbiome Consortium"],"country":["Australia","Austria","China","Hong Kong","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Arizona State University","CAS - Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Harbin Institute of Technology","Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory","Michigan State University","Newcastle University","Northeastern University China","Northwestern University","Rice University","Shandong University","Southwest University","Stanford University","Sun Yat-Sen University","Swiss Federal Institute of Aquatic Science and Technology","The University of Hong Kong","Tsinghua University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","University of Oklahoma","University of Queensland","University of Tennessee","University of Vienna","University of Washington","Washington University St. Louis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"global diversity and biogeography of bacterial communities in wastewater treatment plants","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/335043255/186595.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-100841","identifier":[{"id":"85065757739","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-af00aaec-ef75-44d0-83c8-dd119384a694"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5F41BDADFCB56476DFE6ACBA61A0A586"],"oa_link":[{"access