{"abstract":"The modelling and adaptive sliding-mode control of a high-order buck-boost converter is presented. The converter gives a high voltage gain and presents low current stress on its circuit components. The full-order model of the converter is derived by using a combination of the averaged state-space modeling approach and a duty ratio constraint deriving method. An adaptive sliding-mode controller for this converter is then proposed in which the adaptive law calculates the estimated load conductance to generate the required sliding surface. The stability analysis of the adaptive sliding-mode controlled system is performed. In addition, experimental results comparing the performance of the proposed adaptive sliding-mode controller with that of an existing robust sliding-mode controller are provided to present the advantages.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dong, Chaoyu","Jiang, Wentao","Xiao, Qian","Li, Xiangke","Jin, Yu","Dragicevic, Tomislav"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-078426"],"event":{"acronym":"IES","end":"2019-10-17","place":"Lisbon, Portugal","start":"2019-10-14","title":"IECON 2019 - 45th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South"],"country":["China","Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harbin Institute of Technology","Nanyang Technological University","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","Tianjin University"],"keyword":["Adaptation models","Capacitors","DC DC power converters","Integrated circuit modeling","Load modeling","Stress","Switches"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Key Laboratory of Smart Grid of Ministry of Education"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling analysis and adaptive sliding mode control of a high order buck boost dc dc converter","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8927665/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-078426","identifier":[{"id":"85084123092","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-61d13cb9-d097-4dcb-a19e-f402aa4223a5"],"keyword":["Adaptation models","Capacitors","DC-DC power converters","Integrated circuit modeling","Load modeling","Stress","Switches"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3EFDA279A2483F2ACEBA7C2E215C108A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tianjin university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"nanyang technological university","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Nanyang Technological University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Key Laboratory of Smart Grid of Ministry of Education"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"northwestern polytechnical university xian","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"harbin institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Harbin Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Power Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chaoyu","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Chaoyu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wentao","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Wentao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Qian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiangke","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiangke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"jinpau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Yu","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomislav","key":"dragičevićpau","last":"Dragičević","locid":"224cc3a8-56cb-42cf-a124-1fed779085e1","name":"Dragicevic, Tomislav","name_org":"Dragičević, Tomislav","orcid":"0000-0003-4755-2024","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iecon.2019.8927665","isbn":["9781728148793"],"issn":["1553572X"],"pages":"1844-1849","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"Proceedings of the Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","status":"p","title":"IECON 2019 - 45th Annual Conference of the IEEE Industrial Electronics Society","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084123092"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-61d13cb9-d097-4dcb-a19e-f402aa4223a5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Modeling, Analysis, and Adaptive Sliding-Mode Control of a High-Order Buck/Boost DC-DC Converter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-078426","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Octahedral PtNi/C catalysts have demonstrated superior catalytic performance in oxygen reduction reaction (ORR) over commercial Pt/C with rotating disk electrode (RDE). However, it is not trivial to translate such promising results to real-world membrane-electrode assembly (MEA). In this work, we have synthesized octahedral PtNi/C catalysts using poly(diallyldimethylammonium chloride) (PDDA) as a capping agent and investigated their performance from RDE to MEA. In RDE, mass activity and specific activity of the optimized octahedral PtNi/C catalyst for oxygen reduction reaction (ORR) are nearly 19 and 28 times high of the state-of-the-art commercial Pt/C, respectively. At MEA level, the octahedral PtNi/C catalyst exhibits excellent power generation performance and durability paired with commercial Pt/C anode. Its cell voltage at 1,000 mA·cm −2 reaches 0.712 V, and maximum power density is 881.6 mW·cm −2 and its performance attenuation is also less, around 11.8% and 7% under galvanostatic condition of 1,000 mA·cm −2 for 100 h. Such results are investiaged by thermodynamic analysis and fundametal performance modeling, which indicate the single cell performance can be further improved by reducing the size of PtNi/C catalyst agglomerates. Such encouraging results have demonstrated the feasibility to convey the superior performance of octahedral PtNi/C from RDE to MEA. [Figure not available: see fulltext.].","author_count":8,"contributors":["Li, Bing","Wang, Jue","Gao, Xin","Qin, Congwei","Yang, Daijun","Lv, Hong","Xiao, Qiangfeng","Zhang, Cunman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-085795"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tongji University"],"keyword":["Durability","Oxygen reduction reaction ORR","Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell PEMFC"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high performance octahedral ptni c catalysts investigated from rotating disk electrode to membrane electrode assembly","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85055291715&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-085795","identifier":[{"id":"85055291715","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7af3af33-5fa7-41f4-9ac1-b2e4255d2a90"],"keyword":["Durability","Membrane electrode assembly (MEA)","Octahedral PtNi/C","Oxygen Reduction reaction (ORR)","Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cell (PEMFC)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A4F7409826D4F86CCA76BD499666A86A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tongji university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tongji University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Thermal Energy Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bing","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jue","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jue","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xin","key":"gaopau","last":"Gao","locid":"0c7cc98f-3f75-4d7a-baac-8833cfc63ab5","name":"Gao, Xin","orcid":"0000-0001-6011-0859","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Congwei","key":"qinpau","last":"Qin","name":"Qin, Congwei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daijun","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Daijun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong","key":"lvpau","last":"Lv","name":"Lv, Hong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiangfeng","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Qiangfeng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cunman","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Cunman","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12274-018-2211-9","issn":["19980000","19980124"],"issn_org":["19980124"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nano Research","pages":"281-287","publisher":"Tsinghua University Press","status":"p","title":"Nano Research","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055291715"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7af3af33-5fa7-41f4-9ac1-b2e4255d2a90"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"High performance octahedral PtNi/C catalysts investigated from rotating disk electrode to membrane electrode assembly","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-085795","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Improving biodegradation of pharmaceuticals during wastewater treatment is critical to control the release of emerging micropollutants to natural waters. In this study, biodegradation of six model pharmaceuticals was investigated at different initial concentrations in two discrete activated sludge systems, and moreover, the correlation was explored between the biodegradation rate and key molecular properties of the contaminants. First, the biodegradation rates of the pharmaceuticals were measured fitting a pseudo first−order kinetic model to the experimental kinetic data. The degradation rate constants (k bio ) were found to negatively correlate to the initial concentration of the chemicals, indicating an inhibitory effect on the microorganisms by the pharmaceuticals. Further examinations of the rate data against the key molecular properties of the pharmaceuticals revealed, for the first time, that the electrophilicity index (ω), a measure of electrophilic power, served as a better indicator of the biodegradability and predictive parameter for the k bio than the conventional log K OW (a measure of hydrophobicity) in the two discrete aerobic activated sludge systems. However, the correlation strength (goodness‒of‒fit) between ω and k bio deteriorated when the reactor turned from aerobic to anoxic and anaerobic conditions, suggesting that electron transfer from pharmaceutical molecules to enzymes was inhibited when dissolved oxygen was deficit or absent. Our results show that ω can potentially serve as a straightforward and robust indicator for predicting the biodegradability of pharmaceutical in conventional activated sludge processes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Wei, Zongsu","Li, Wei","Zhao, Dongye","Seo, Youngwoo","Spinney, Richard","Dionysiou, Dionysios D.","Wang, Yong","Zeng, Weizhi","Xiao, Ruiyang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-184901"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Xiao, Ruiyang"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Central South University","Chinese National Engineering Research Center for Control & Treatment of Heavy Metal Pollution","Ohio State University","University of Cincinnati","University of Science and Technology Beijing","University of Toledo"],"keyword":["Activated sludge","Biodegradation","Hydrophobicity","Pharmaceutical"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"electrophilicity index as a critical indicator for the biodegradation of the pharmaceuticals in aerobic activated sludge processes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85065903712","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-184901","identifier":[{"id":"85065903712","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31129377","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-6154dc9b-8ddc-440d-86b2-46d6f5234035"],"keyword":["Activated sludge","Biodegradation","Electrophilicity index","Emerging micropollutants","Hydrophobicity","Pharmaceutical"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C98990933CBB9E694932959C12747CE0"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Biological and Chemical Engineering, Hangøvej"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"central south university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Central South University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"chinese national engineering research center for control treatment of heavy metal pollution","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese National Engineering Research Center for Control & Treatment of Heavy Metal Pollution","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of toledo","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toledo","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"ohio state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ohio State University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"university of cincinnati","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Cincinnati","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology beijing","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology Beijing","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zongsu","key":"weipau","last":"Wei","locid":"e187efc6-abcf-468f-92b6-f27824e33e91","name":"Wei, Zongsu","orcid":"0000-0001-8747-2251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Wei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dongye","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"ef6bc8f8-e602-432a-a65b-a5f32d2d1dbf","name":"Zhao, Dongye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Youngwoo","key":"seopau","last":"Seo","name":"Seo, Youngwoo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"spinneypau","last":"Spinney","name":"Spinney, Richard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Dionysios D.","key":"dionysioupau","last":"Dionysiou","name":"Dionysiou, Dionysios D.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Yong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yong","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Weizhi","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Weizhi","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruiyang","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Ruiyang","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31129377"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.watres.2019.05.057","issn":["00431354","18792448"],"issn_org":["00431354"],"journal":"Water Research","pages":"10-17","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Water Research","volume":"160"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065903712"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6154dc9b-8ddc-440d-86b2-46d6f5234035"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Electrophilicity index as a critical indicator for the biodegradation of the pharmaceuticals in aerobic activated sludge processes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-184901","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Influenza is a persistent threat to human health and there is a continuing requirement for updating anti-influenza strategies. Initiated by observations of different endoplasmic reticulum (ER) responses of host to seasonal H1N1 and highly pathogenic avian influenza (HPAI) A H5N1 infections, we identified an alternative antiviral role of tauroursodeoxycholic acid (TUDCA), a clinically available ER stress inhibitor, both in vitro and in vivo. Rather than modulating ER stress in host cells, TUDCA abolished the proton conductivity of viral M2 by disrupting its oligomeric states, which induces inefficient viral infection. We also showed that M2 penetrated cells, whose intracellular uptake depended on its proton channel activity, an effect observed in both TUDCA and M2 inhibitor amantadine. The identification and application of TUDCA as an inhibitor of M2 proton channel will expand our understanding of IAV biology and complement current anti-IAV arsenals.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Li, Ning","Zhang, Yanxu","Wu, Shuangxiu","Xu, Ruodan","Li, Zhiqing","Zhu, Jindong","Wang, Hongliang","Li, Xiao","Tian, Mingyao","Lu, Huijun","Jin, Ningyi","Jiang, Chengyu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-217571"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Jin, Ningyi"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["Academy of Military Medical Science China","All Global Affiliations","Tsinghua University"],"keyword":["Acute Lung Injury","Bile salts","Cell penetrating peptide","Cholesterol","DRUG","ER stress","Entry","Influenza","M2 proton channel","Mechanism","Protein","Virus entry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tauroursodeoxycholic acid tudca inhibits influenza a viral infection by disrupting viral proton channel m000000000002","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7104969/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-217571","identifier":[{"id":"85060093032","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000460873100007","type":"wos"},{"id":"32288967","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7104969","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-9ad8d879-6341-42da-9ff5-d3829fad6e52"],"keyword":["ACUTE LUNG INJURY","BILE-SALTS","CHOLESTEROL","Cell-penetrating peptide","DRUG","ENTRY","ER STRESS","Influenza","M-2 ION-CHANNEL","M2 proton channel","MECHANISM","Oligomerization inhibitor","PROTEIN","TUDCA","VIRUS M2","Virus entry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D0455D65AEB85889B11FFE8C77B24052"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7104969/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-MBG, iNANO-huset","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Nanofiber Technology and Cellular Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"academy of military medical science china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Academy of Military Medical Science China","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"liningpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yanxu","key":"zhangyanxupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yanxu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuangxiu","key":"wushuangxiupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Shuangxiu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ruodan","key":"xuruodanpau","last":"Xu","locid":"e966d7a9-f7e1-48d2-b7c9-51d8eb2d21ee","name":"Xu, Ruodan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhiqing","key":"lizhiqingpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhiqing","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jindong","key":"zhujindongpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Jindong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongliang","key":"wanghongliangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hongliang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"lixiaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingyao","key":"tianmingyaopau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Mingyao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Huijun","key":"luhuijunpau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Huijun","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ningyi","key":"jinningyipau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Ningyi","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chengyu","key":"jiangchengyupau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Chengyu","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32288967"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scib.2018.08.013","issn":["20959273","20959281"],"issn_org":["20959273"],"issue":"3","journal":"Science Bulletin","pages":"180-188","publisher":"Science Press","status":"p","title":"Science Bulletin","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060093032"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9ad8d879-6341-42da-9ff5-d3829fad6e52"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Tauroursodeoxycholic acid (TUDCA) inhibits influenza A viral infection by disrupting viral proton channel M2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-217571","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Recent studies have described several new species within the section Compressa of the genus Chaetoceros. To explore the diversity in the section, further studies were conducted based on monoclonal strains established from Chinese warm waters. A combination of molecular and morphological data showed the presence of a new species, Chaetoceros brevispinosus, within the section. Morphologically, C. brevispinosus is characterised mainly by the morphology of the resting spore. The primary valve is convex with numerous short spines, whereas the secondary valve has a more centrally placed vault with less developed spines and ridges. Chaetoceros brevispinosus constitutes a distinct lineage on the LSU and SSU phylogenetic trees, and forms a sister taxon to C. contortus cf. var. contortus. In the phylogenetic analyses, C. contortus var. ornatus formed a distinct lineage and did not form a sister clade to C. contortus cf. var. contortus. Nine and six different base pairs, as well as a genetic distance of 0.012 and 0.008, separated C. contortus var. ornatus and two clades of C. contortus cf. var. contortus. Morphological differences, based on vegetative cells and resting spores, are still uncertain as the morphology of C. contortus var. contortus needs to be examined based on material from the type locality. Chaetoceros contortus var. ornatus makes up the sister taxon to C. bifurcates on the LSU tree. Hence, we propose that C. contortus var. ornatus be raised to species level as C. ornatus stat. nov.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Xu, Xiao Jing","Lundholm, Nina","Chen, Zuo Yi","Li, Yang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-436224"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hebei Geological Prospecting Bureau","South China Normal University"],"keyword":["Chinese warm waters","Diversity","Morphology","Phylogeny","Resting spore"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"revisiting section compressa of chaetoceros bacillariophyceae with descriptions of c brevispinosus sp nov and c ornatus comb nov","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-436224","identifier":[{"id":"85070985640","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-47a7c8b5-4216-4ab7-8033-771e366c5784"],"keyword":["Chaetoceros brevispinosus","Chaetoceros ornatus","Chinese warm waters","Diversity","Morphology","Phylogeny","Resting spore"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C280F7481306158BE30E1D1890C6629"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"south china normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"hebei geological prospecting bureau","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hebei Geological Prospecting Bureau","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Jing","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xiao Jing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nina","key":"lundholmpau","last":"Lundholm","locid":"8a8a8b45-8d40-4f5f-b3e2-ad8b18835107","name":"Lundholm, Nina","orcid":"0000-0002-2035-1997","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Zuo Yi","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zuo Yi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00318884.2019.1641370","issn":["00318884","23302968"],"issn_org":["00318884"],"issue":"6","journal":"Phycologia","pages":"614-627","status":"p","title":"Phycologia","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070985640"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-47a7c8b5-4216-4ab7-8033-771e366c5784"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Revisiting section Compressa of Chaetoceros (Bacillariophyceae), with descriptions of C. brevispinosus sp. nov. and C. ornatus comb. nov.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-436224","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Many Large-scale image databases such as ImageNet have significantly advanced image classification and other visual recognition tasks. However much of these datasets are constructed only for single-label and coarse object-level classification. For real-world applications, multiple labels and fine-grained categories are often needed, yet very few such datasets exist publicly, especially those of large-scale and high quality. In this work, we contribute to the community a new dataset called iMaterialist Fashion Attribute (iFashion-Attribute) to address this problem in the fashion domain. The dataset is constructed from over one million fashion images with a label space that includes 8 groups of 228 fine-grained attributes in total. Each image is annotated by experts with multiple, high-quality fashion attributes. The result is the first known million-scale multi-label and fine-grained image dataset. We conduct extensive experiments and provide baseline results with modern deep Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs). Additionally, we demonstrate models pre-trained on iFashion-Attribute achieve superior transfer learning performance on fashion related tasks compared with pre-training from ImageNet or other fashion datasets.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Guo, Sheng","Huang, Weilin","Zhang, Xiao","Srikhanta, Prasanna","Cui, Yin","Li, Yuan","Adam, Hartwig","Scott, Matthew R.","Belongie, Serge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-451126"],"event":{"end":"2019-10-28","place":"Seoul, kr","start":"2019-10-27","title":"17th IEEE/CVF International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop, ICCVW 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Alphabet Inc.","Cornell University","Malong Technologies Co., Ltd."],"keyword":["Fine grained","Large scale","Multi label classification"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Wish"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the imaterialist fashion attribute dataset","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-451126","identifier":[{"id":"85082461588","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6064bab3-6b98-46c1-9d36-274beb0c26ba"],"keyword":["Fine grained","IFashion attribute","Large scale","Multi label classification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8951EDD9A23242F6B99CAF5166D8AACA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"malong technologies co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Malong Technologies Co., Ltd.","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Wish"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Developmental Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"alphabet inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Alphabet Inc.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sheng","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Sheng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Weilin","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Weilin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Prasanna","key":"srikhantapau","last":"Srikhanta","name":"Srikhanta, Prasanna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Yin","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Yin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Yuan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"d316351b-6850-40d8-a032-7ea894203e37","name":"Li, Yuan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Hartwig","key":"adampau","last":"Adam","name":"Adam, Hartwig","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthew R.","key":"scottpau","last":"Scott","name":"Scott, Matthew R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Serge","key":"belongiepau","last":"Belongie","name":"Belongie, Serge","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iccvw.2019.00377","journal":"Proceedings - 2019 International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop, ICCVW","pages":"3113-3116","status":"p","title":"Proceedings - 2019 International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop, ICCVW","title_org":"Proceedings - 2019 International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop, ICCVW 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6064bab3-6b98-46c1-9d36-274beb0c26ba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The imaterialist fashion attribute dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-451126","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Fledelius, Hans C.","Jacobsen, Nina","Li, Xiao Q.","Goldschmidt, Ernst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-510888"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Age","High myopia","Visual field"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the longitudinal danish high myopia study cohort 000000001948 at age 000000000066 years visual ability is only occasionally affected by visual field defects","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-510888","identifier":[{"id":"85054339302","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000456872000009","type":"wos"},{"id":"30284371","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c4d03424-754a-4126-9b00-f0f211fbe6c7"],"keyword":["age","high myopia","kinetic goldmann perimetry","optos fundus evaluation","population derived data","visual field"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0012681EC7CBF2E32A158056E6C8F4E3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Ophthalmology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Hans C.","key":"fledeliuspau","last":"Fledelius","name":"Fledelius, Hans C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"cce99f14-7329-4dd1-b2fa-c85c4a46d0ad","name":"Jacobsen, Nina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao Q.","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Q.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ernst","key":"goldschmidtpau","last":"Goldschmidt","name":"Goldschmidt, Ernst","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30284371"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.13820","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"36-43","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"97"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054339302"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c4d03424-754a-4126-9b00-f0f211fbe6c7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Longitudinal Danish High Myopia Study, Cohort 1948 : at age 66 years visual ability is only occasionally affected by visual field defects","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510888","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PD-1/L1 and CTLA-4 blockade immunotherapies have been approved for 13 types of cancers and are being studied in diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL), the most common aggressive B-cell lymphoma. However, whether both PD-1 and CTLA-4 checkpoints are active and clinically significant in DLBCL is unknown. Whether PD-1 ligands expressed by tumor cells or by the microenvironment of DLBCL are critical for the PD-1 immune checkpoint is unclear. We performed immunophenotypic profiling for 405 patients with de novo DLBCL using a MultiOmyx immunofluorescence platform and simultaneously quantitated expression/coexpression of 13 immune markers to identify prognostic determinants. In both training and validation cohorts, results demonstrated a central role of the tumor immune microenvironment, and when its functionality was impaired by deficiency in tumor-infiltrating T cells and/or natural killer cells, high PD-1 expression (but not CTLA-4) on CD8+ T cells, or PD-L1 expression on T cells and macrophages, patients had significantly poorer survival after rituximab–CHOP (cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin, vincristine, and prednisone) immunochemotherapy. In contrast, tumor-cell PD-L2 expression was associated with superior survival, as well as PD-L1+CD20+ cells proximal (indicates interaction) to PD-1+CD8+ T cells in patients with low PD-1+ percentage of CD8+ T cells. Gene-expression profiling results suggested the reversibility of T-cell exhaustion in PD-1+/PD-L1+ patients with unfavorable prognosis and implication of LILRA/B, IDO1, CHI3L1, and SOD2 upregulation in the microenvironment dysfunction with PD-L1 expression. This study comprehensively characterized the DLBCL immune landscape, deciphered the differential roles of various checkpoint components in rituximab–CHOP resistance in DLBCL patients, and suggests targets for PD-1/PD-L1 blockade and combination immunotherapies.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Xu-Monette, Ziju Y.","Xiao, Min","Au, Qingyan","Padmanabhan, Raghav","Xu, Bing","Hoe, Nicholas","Rodríguez-Perales, Sandra","Torres-Ruiz, Raul","Manyam, Ganiraju C.","Visco, Carlo","Miao, Yi","Tan, Xiaohong","Zhang, Hongwei","Tzankov, Alexandar","Wang, Jing","Dybkær, Karen","Tam, Wayne","You, Hua","Bhagat, Govind","Hsi, Eric D.","Ponzoni, Maurilio","Ferreri, Andrés J.M.","Møller, Michael B.","Piris, Miguel A.","van Krieken, J. Han","Winter, Jane N.","Westin, Jason R.","Pham, Lan V.","Medeiros, L. Jeffrey","Rassidakis, George Z.","Li, Yong","Freeman, Gordon J.","Young, Ken H."],"cuid":["S02-086.71-008065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Case Western Reserve University","Cleveland Clinic","Columbia University Medical Center","Dana–Farber Cancer Institute","Guangzhou Medical University","Karolinska Institute","Marqués de Valdecilla University Hospital","NeoGenomics Laboratories","NewYork-Presbyterian Hospital","Northwestern University Feinberg School of Medicine","Radboud University Medical Center","San Bortolo Hospital Of Vicenza","San Raffaele Scientific Institute","Spanish National Cancer Research Centre","The First Affiliated Hospital of Xiamen University","The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston","University Hospital of Basel","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","Weill Cornell Medicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immune profiling and quantitative analysis decipher the clinical role of immune checkpoint expression in the tumor immun