{"abstract":"This commentary on Lapoujade (Human Arenas, 1, 1–9, 2018) elaborates the author’s ideas from a new angle. It reviews the “liquid” and “gaseous” society at the level of capital and technology and also tries to analyze the origin of the problems of modern society from a philosophic perspective: abstract individuals caused by the subjectification of self-consciousness and abstract labor. By analyzing and discussing the relationship between ideology and the realistic world, the difference between abstract individuals and realistic individuals and the historical construction of human essence, the possibility of philosophy as an international healing resource, is explored.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Xu, Shuangshuang","Li, Xiao Wen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-097446"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xu, Shuangshuang"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","East China Normal University","School of Psychology and Cognitive Science"],"keyword":["Capitalism","Historicity","Ideology","Metaphysics","Modernity"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"becoming becomings historically a commentary on lapoujade s article","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85075703607&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Shuang-Shuang Xu is supported by the China Scholarship Council for a 3-year study at the Aalborg University."],"id":"S01-000.00-097446","identifier":[{"id":"85075703607","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a3881832-b980-4c9c-a2bc-f9261263ce15"],"keyword":["Capitalism","Historicity","Human essence","Ideology","Metaphysics","Modernity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BBB0FAFAD46FBDC46857F42E2947E48C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Qualitative Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"school of psychology and cognitive science","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"School of Psychology and Cognitive Science","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"east china normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China Normal University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuang Shuang","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","locid":"95299298-09f9-45b0-8cf4-a0d5f114760d","name":"Xu, Shuangshuang","name_org":"Xu, Shuang Shuang","orcid":"0000-0002-3830-542X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Wen","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Wen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s42087-018-0042-6","issn":["25225790","25225804"],"issn_org":["25225790"],"issue":"4","journal":"Human Arenas","pages":"366-372","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Human Arenas","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075703607"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a3881832-b980-4c9c-a2bc-f9261263ce15"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Becoming Becomings Historically : a Commentary on Lapoujade’s Article","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-097446","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The palaeoenvironmental reconstruction of central Tibet is key to understanding the uplift history of the Tibetan Plateau, which had a profound influence on Cenozoic global climate and biotic change. Here we report an amber layer from the lower part of the Dingqing Formation (late Oligocene) in Lunpola of central Tibet, which is the first record of amber from Tibet. Herein we find that Lunpola amber is derived from dipterocarp trees, as determined by gas chromatography-mass spectrometry, which are restricted to and dominant in Asian rainforest nowadays. This amber forest represents the northernmost dipterocarp forest and is consistent with the hypothesis of out-of-India dispersal of Asian dipterocarps. The Lunpola amber most probably was derived from the lower part of the Niubao Formation (early–middle Eocene) and suggests a tropical/subtropical wet forest was present in central Tibet at least before the late Oligocene (probably early–middle Eocene).","author_count":12,"contributors":["Wang, He","Dutta, Suryendu","Kelly, Richard S.","Rudra, Arka","Li, Sha","Zhang, Qing Qing","Zhang, Qian Qi","Wu, Yi Xiao","Cao, Mei Zhen","Wang, Bo","Li, Jian","Zhang, Hai Chun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-227745"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Li, Jian"],"country":["China","India","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay","Shandong University of Science and Technology","University of Bristol","University of Science and Technology of China"],"keyword":["Oligocene","Palynology","Rainforest"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"amber fossils reveal the early cenozoic dipterocarp rainforest in central tibet","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055085523","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-227745","identifier":[{"id":"85055085523","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ac9ad8c7-fabf-4278-8251-915d38ce12dc"],"keyword":["Oligocene","Ostrocods","Palynology","Rainforest","Tibet amber"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9C81570A27B10DBE7FCB5001ABF50D69"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"university of science and technology of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Science and Technology of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"in","key":"indian institute of technology bombay","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"shandong university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"He","key":"wanghepau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, He","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Suryendu","key":"duttasuryendupau","last":"Dutta","name":"Dutta, Suryendu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard S.","key":"kellyrichardspau","last":"Kelly","name":"Kelly, Richard S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arka","key":"rudraarkapau","last":"Rudra","locid":"74f10f00-45db-42c5-8256-e4a412d8779a","name":"Rudra, Arka","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sha","key":"lishapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Sha","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qing Qing","key":"zhangqingqingpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Qing Qing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qian Qi","key":"zhangqianqipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Qian Qi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi Xiao","key":"wuyixiaopau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Yi Xiao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mei Zhen","key":"caomeizhenpau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Mei Zhen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"wangbopau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Bo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian Guo","key":"lijianpau","last":"Li","locid":"2aaa3f80-114a-4e01-81ef-b8d3a526100c","name":"Li, Jian","name_org":"Li, Jian Guo","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai Chun","key":"zhanghaichunpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Hai Chun","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.palwor.2018.09.006","issn":["1871174X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Palaeoworld","pages":"506-513","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Palaeoworld","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ac9ad8c7-fabf-4278-8251-915d38ce12dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Amber fossils reveal the Early Cenozoic dipterocarp rainforest in central Tibet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-227745","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The differences in artificial and natural selection have been some of the factors contributing to phenotypic diversity between Chinese and western pigs. Here, 830 individuals from western and Chinese pig breeds were genotyped using the reduced-representation genotyping method. First, we identified the selection signatures for different pig breeds. By comparing Chinese pigs and western pigs along the first principal component, the growth gene IGF1R; the immune genes IL1R1, IL1RL1, DUSP10, RAC3 and SWAP70; the meat quality-related gene SNORA50 and the olfactory gene OR1F1 were identified as candidate differentiated targets. Further, along a principal component separating Pudong White pigs from others, a potential causal gene for coat colour (EDNRB) was discovered. In addition, the divergent signatures evaluated by F st within Chinese pig breeds found genes associated with the phenotypic features of coat colour, meat quality and feed efficiency among these indigenous pigs. Second, admixture and genomic introgression analysis were performed. Shan pigs have introgressed genes from Berkshire, Yorkshire and Hongdenglong pigs. The results of introgression mapping showed that this introgression conferred adaption to the local environment and coat colour of Chinese pigs and the superior productivity of western pigs.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Zhang, Zhe","Xiao, Qian","Zhang, Qianqian","Sun, Hao","Chen, Jiu cheng","Li, Zheng cao","Xue, Ming","Ma, Pei pei","Yang, Hong jie","Xu, Ning ying","Wang, Qi-shan","Pan, Yu chun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-399748"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Station of Animal Husbandry","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Shanghai Key Laboratory of Veterinary Biotechnology","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1