,"key":"yingsunpau","last":"Ying Sun","name":"Ying Sun, Zhi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00170-017-1494-4","issn":["02683768","14333015"],"issn_org":["02683768"],"issue":"9-12","journal":"International Journal of Advanced Manufacturing Technology","pages":"3905-3918","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Advanced Manufacturing Technology","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039840631"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-52ba3a50-837d-44c7-adde-38687f2a2d99"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Rigid-flexible coupling forming process for aluminum alloy automobile body panels","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-074080","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Two-dimensional (2D) van der Waals (vdW) materials with strong in-plane chemical bonds and weak interaction in the out-of-plane direction have been acknowledged as a basic building block for designing dimensional materials in 0D, 1D, 2D and 3D forms. Compared to the explosive research on 2D vdW materials, quasi-one-dimensional (quasi-1D) vdW materials have received rare attention, despite the fact that they also present rich physics in electronics and engineering implications. Herein, quasi-1D MoS2 nanoscrolls are directly fabricated from CVD-grown 2D triangular MoS2 sheets. The formation, stability and electronic properties of quasi-1D MoS2 nanoscrolls are studied experimentally and theoretically. The formation of a nanoscroll always starts from the edge of a triangular MoS2 sheet along its armchair orientation. The electronic properties of MoS2 nanoscrolls are systemically studied with optical spectroscopy and electrical transport together with density-functional theory (DFT) calculations. Surprisingly, the carrier mobility and contact properties of MoS2 nanoscroll based field effect transistors (FETs) are distinct from that of 2D MoS2 sheets. The transition from a 2D semiconductor MoS2 sheet to a 1D metallic MoS2 nanoscroll is successfully achieved. It is expected that this method of fabricating MoS2 nanoscrolls will attract wide interest for 1D transition metal dichalcogenides with novel physical and chemical properties.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wang, Zegao","Wu, Hong Hui","Li, Qiang","Besenbacher, Flemming","Zeng, Xiao Cheng","Dong, Mingdong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-222538"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Zeng, Xiao Cheng"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shandong University","Sichuan University","University of Nebraska-Lincoln"],"keyword":["Carbon nanoscrolls","Fabrication","GROWTH","Heterostructures","Hydrogen evolution","Large area","MONOLAYER MOS2","Mobility","Quantum dots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self scrolling mos sub 000000000002 sub metallic wires","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85054439056","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-222538","identifier":[{"id":"000450820400007","type":"wos"},{"id":"30255900","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85054439056","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a39e0b14-64b8-4325-b6f4-d5dd18293479"],"keyword":["CARBON NANOSCROLLS","FABRICATION","GROWTH","HETEROSTRUCTURES","HYDROGEN EVOLUTION","LARGE-AREA","MOBILITY","MONOLAYER MOS2","QUANTUM DOTS","SCHOTTKY BARRIERS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-190FD78592AF99B0561A5919A735B0AF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center, Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center - INANO-Fysik, iNANO-huset"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of nebraska lincoln","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Nebraska-Lincoln","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zegao","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"2f191f69-88c1-4291-8610-6d3b85bbc312","name":"Wang, Zegao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong Hui","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Hong Hui","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"f5d17801-6cfb-4c75-8f63-7bdb69eb130c","name":"Li, Qiang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Flemming","key":"besenbacherpau","last":"Besenbacher","locid":"0aa89800-dd75-4f15-a575-c419dda7a69f","name":"Besenbacher, Flemming","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Cheng","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Xiao Cheng","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mingdong","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30255900"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c8nr04611e","issn":["20403364","20403372"],"issn_org":["20403364"],"issue":"38","journal":"Nanoscale","pages":"18178-18185","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Nanoscale","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054439056"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a39e0b14-64b8-4325-b6f4-d5dd18293479"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Self-scrolling MoS<sub>2</sub> metallic wires","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-222538","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Due to excess nutrient loading, loss of submersed macrophytes is a worldwide phenomenon in shallow lakes. Phosphorus is known to contribute significantly to macrophyte recession, but the role of nitrogen has received increasing attention. Our understanding of how high nitrogen concentrations affect the growth of submersed macrophytes, particularly under natural conditions, is still limited. In this study, we conducted experiments with canopy-forming Potamogeton crispus in 10 ponds subjected to substantial differences in nitrogen loading (five targeted total nitrogen concentrations: control, 2, 10, 20, and 100 mg L -1) and compared the results with those of our earlier published experiments with rosette-forming Vallisneria natans performed 1 year before. Canopy-forming P. crispus was more tolerant than rosette-forming V. natans to exposure to high NH 4 concentrations. This is probably because canopy-forming species reach the water surface where there is sufficient light for production of carbohydrates, thereby allowing the plants to partly overcome high NH 4 stress. Both the canopy-forming P. crispus and the rosette-forming V. natans showed clear declining trends with increasing chlorophyll a in the water. Accordingly, shading by phytoplankton might be of key importance for the decline in submersed macrophytes in this experiment. Both experiments revealed free amino acids (FAA) to be a useful indicator of physiological stress by high ammonium but is not a reliable indicator of macrophyte growth.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Yu, Qing","Wang, Hong-Zhu","Xu, Chi","Yan, Li","Ma, Shuo Nan","Liang, Xiao-Min","Jeppesen, Erik","Wang, Hai Jun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-257958"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CAS - Institute of Hydrobiology","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Nanjing University","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Ammonium","Growth form","Periphyton","Phosphorus","Phytoplankton","Submersed macrophytes","Whole ecosystem experiment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"higher tolerance of canopy forming potamogeton crispus than rosette forming vallisneria natans to high nitrogen concentration as evidenced from experiments in 000000000010 ponds with contrasting nitrogen levels","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2018.01845","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-257958","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6300520","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85058784195","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30619414","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-e14a4f74-7c85-4852-815b-9d844016f5e9"],"keyword":["Ammonium","Growth form","Periphyton","Phosphorus","Phytoplankton","Submersed macrophytes","Whole-ecosystem experiment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6304EE8B6B8EB25ED35A7BFB873A99E1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/139721713/fpls_09_01845.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2018.01845","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"cas institute of hydrobiology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"CAS - Institute of Hydrobiology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"nanjing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Nanjing University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Center, ECOS Water","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Lake Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Qing","key":"yuqingpau","last":"Yu","name":"Yu, Qing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong-Zhu","key":"wanghongzhupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hong-Zhu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chi","key":"xuchipau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Chi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"yanlipau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Li","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuo Nan","key":"mashuonanpau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Shuo Nan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Min","key":"liangxiaominpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Xiao-Min","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hai Jun","key":"wanghaijunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hai Jun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30619414"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fpls.2018.01845","issn":["1664462X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Plant Science","paperid":"1845","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Plant 