{"abstract":"Pangenome analyses facilitate the interpretation of genetic diversity and evolutionary history of a taxon. However, there is an urgent and unmet need to develop new tools for advanced pangenome construction and visualization, especially for metagenomic data. Here, we present an integrated pipeline, named MetaPGN, for construction and graphical visualization of pangenome networks from either microbial genomes or metagenomes. Given either isolated genomes or metagenomic assemblies coupled with a reference genome of the targeted taxon, MetaPGN generates a pangenome in a topological network, consisting of genes (nodes) and gene-gene genomic adjacencies (edges) of which biological information can be easily updated and retrieved. MetaPGN also includes a self-developed Cytoscape plugin for layout of and interaction with the resulting pangenome network, providing an intuitive and interactive interface for full exploration of genetic diversity. We demonstrate the utility of MetaPGN by constructing Escherichia coli pangenome networks from five E. coli pathogenic strains and 760 human gut microbiomes,revealing extensive genetic diversity of E. coli within both isolates and gut microbial populations. With the ability to extract and visualize gene contents and gene-gene physical adjacencies of a specific taxon from large-scale metagenomic data, MetaPGN provides advantages in expanding pangenome analysis to uncultured microbial taxa.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Peng, Ye","Tang, Shanmei","Wang, Dan","Zhong, Huanzi","Jia, Huijue","Cai, Xianghang","Zhang, Zhaoxi","Xiao, Minfeng","Yang, Huanming","Wang, Jian","Kristiansen, Karsten","Xu, Xun","Li, Junhua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-532212"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metapgn a pipeline for construction and graphical visualization of annotated pangenome networks","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/gigascience/giy121","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-532212","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6251982","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30277499","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85057146860","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e8605592-5ff5-4b43-9704-98aad302c81c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B2B74A785E83C7E9C46BCE78FBFF0F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209801069/MetaPGN.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/gigascience/giy121","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ye","key":"pengyepau","last":"Peng","name":"Peng, Ye","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shanmei","key":"tangshanmeipau","last":"Tang","name":"Tang, Shanmei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dan","key":"wangdanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Dan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Huanzi","key":"zhonghuanzipau","last":"Zhong","locid":"00f8ce53-c1cd-4045-a1f2-216320dac529","name":"Zhong, Huanzi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Huijue","key":"jiahuijuepau","last":"Jia","name":"Jia, Huijue","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xianghang","key":"caixianghangpau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Xianghang","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhaoxi","key":"zhangzhaoxipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhaoxi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Minfeng","key":"xiaominfengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Minfeng","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Huanming","key":"yanghuanmingpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Huanming","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jian","key":"wangjianpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenkarstenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"941041b1-1b8f-4be5-9a65-5e98f662c07e","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","orcid":"0000-0002-6024-0917","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xun","key":"xuxunpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Xun","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Junhua","key":"lijunhuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Junhua","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30277499"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/gigascience/giy121","issn":["2047217X"],"issue":"11","journal":"GigaScience","pages":"1-11","paperid":"giy121","status":"p","title":"GigaScience","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057146860"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e8605592-5ff5-4b43-9704-98aad302c81c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MetaPGN : a pipeline for construction and graphical visualization of annotated pangenome networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532212","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Inbreeding, which has several causes including genetic drift, population bottlenecks, mating of close relatives and selection, can leave tracts of runs of homozygosity (ROH) along genomes. Recently, decreasing performance on reproductive traits, which might have resulted from inbreeding, has been observed in Chinese pigs. In this study, 830 individuals from Western and Chinese pig breeds were genotyped using the reduced-representation sequencing method. After imputation and quality control, 60 850 high-confidence SNPs were retained for ROH detection. A simulation was performed to explore the reliability of ROH detection with imputed data. Different ROH-related variables were compared between imputed and non-missing genotypes used in ROH detection. Furthermore, ROH islands were evaluated and annotated to find genes influenced by inbreeding in these pigs. The simulation results showed that imputed data with 0.7 as the average missing genotype rate and three heterozygotes allowed in a sliding window have comparable ROH detected compared with data with no missing genotypes. Compared with Western pig breeds, Chinese pigs had more autosomes covered by ROH longer than 5 Mb, indicating higher inbreeding in Chinese pigs in recent times. Genes related to reproduction, immunity, meat quality and adaptability in Chinese pigs and several genes related to growth speed and immunity in Western pigs were observed in short ROH islands. The reproduction-related gene PRM1 was found to be located in the most frequent long ROH island in Chinese pigs, which might explain the decreasing fertility in Chinese pig breeds.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Zhang, Zhe","Zhang, Qianqian","Xiao, Qian","Sun, Hao","Gao, Hongding","Yang, Yumei","Chen, Jiucheng","Li, Zhengcao","Xue, Ming","Ma, Peipei","Yang, Hongjie","Xu, Ningying","Wang, Qishan","Pan, Yuchun"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023310"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Qishan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Station of Animal Husbandry","Shanghai Jiao Tong University","Shanghai Key Laboratory of Veterinary Biotechnology","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["Chinese indigenous pigs","Imputation","Inbreeding","ROH islands","Selection sweep"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"distribution of runs of homozygosity in chinese and western pig breeds evaluated by reduced representation sequencing data","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85054908781","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-023310","identifier":[{"id":"85054908781","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30324759","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-91bdb620-6711-4b04-a31b-5eb16a3fae13","ku-41c2d292-bcb0-4bf2-9b2f-e16459dfd9d4"],"keyword":["Chinese indigenous pigs","ROH islands","imputation","inbreeding","selection sweep"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B7C72E9296E33AB29685DC357E3851F8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"shanghai jiao tong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Jiao Tong University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shang