{"abstract":"Background: Reduced representation bisulfite sequencing (RRBS) has been widely used to profile genome-scale DNA methylation in mammalian genomes. However, the applications and technical performances of RRBS with different fragment sizes have not been systematically reported in pigs, which serve as one of the important biomedical models for humans. The aims of this study were to evaluate capacities of RRBS libraries with different fragment sizes to characterize the porcine genome.  Results: We found that the MspI-digested segments between 40 and 220 bp harbored a high distribution peak at 74 bp, which were highly overlapped with the repetitive elements and might reduce the unique mapping alignment. The RRBS library of 110-220 bp fragment size had the highest unique mapping alignment and the lowest multiple alignment. The cost-effectiveness of the 40-110 bp, 110-220 bp and 40-220 bp fragment sizes might decrease when the dataset size was more than 70, 50 and 110 million reads for these three fragment sizes, respectively. Given a 50-million dataset size, the average sequencing depth of the detected CpG sites in the 110-220 bp fragment size appeared to be deeper than in the 40-110 bp and 40-220 bp fragment sizes, and these detected CpG sties differently located in gene- and CpG island-related regions.  Conclusions: In this study, our results demonstrated that selections of fragment sizes could affect the numbers and sequencing depth of detected CpG sites as well as the cost-efficiency. No single solution of RRBS is optimal in all circumstances for investigating genome-scale DNA methylation. This work provides the useful knowledge on designing and executing RRBS for investigating the genome-wide DNA methylation in tissues from pigs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Yuan, Xiao Long","Zhang, Zhe","Pan, Rong Yang","Gao, Ning","Deng, Xi","Li, Bin","Zhang, Hao","Sangild, Per Torp","Li, Jia Qi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-529998"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","South China Agricultural University","University of Göttingen"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","Pigs","RRBS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"performances of different fragment sizes for reduced representation bisulfite sequencing in pigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12575-017-0054-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-529998","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5463379","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85020286851","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28596713","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e4baebc7-e5b4-4d0a-857d-ffefd5e8c45a"],"keyword":["DNA methylation","Different fragment sizes","Pigs","RRBS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7FF72B3EA4F253398B17AF3FA9C7AD1E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/184390564/s12575_017_0054_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12575-017-0054-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"south china agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of göttingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Göttingen","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Comparative Pediatrics and Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiao Long","key":"yuanxiaolongpau","last":"Yuan","name":"Yuan, Xiao Long","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zhe","key":"zhangzhepau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Zhe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rong Yang","key":"panrongyangpau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Rong Yang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ning","key":"gaoningpau","last":"Gao","name":"Gao, Ning","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xi","key":"dengxipau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, Xi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bin","key":"libinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Bin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hao","key":"zhanghaopau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Hao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Per Torp","key":"sangildpertorppau","last":"Sangild","locid":"d0225a7f-ad88-418d-8660-bff37f7358d9","name":"Sangild, Per Torp","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jia Qi","key":"lijiaqipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jia Qi","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28596713"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12575-017-0054-5","issn":["14809222"],"issue":"1","journal":"Biological Procedures Online","paperid":"5","status":"p","title":"Biological Procedures Online","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020286851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e4baebc7-e5b4-4d0a-857d-ffefd5e8c45a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Performances of Different Fragment Sizes for Reduced Representation Bisulfite Sequencing in Pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-529998","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Both maternal smoking during pregnancy and low birth weight have been implicated in impaired development of the retina. Objective: To investigate the associations of maternal smoking during pregnancy and low birth weight with retinal nerve fiber layer (RNFL) thickness in preadolescent children. Design, Setting, Participants: The Copenhagen Child Cohort 2000 Eye Study is a prospective, population-based, birth cohort study that included all children (n = 6090) born in 2000 in Copenhagen, Denmark. Maternal smoking data were collected through parental interviews. Birth weight, pregnancy, and medical history data were obtained from the Danish Medical Birth Registry. As a follow-up, the study performed eye examinations on 1406 of these children from May 1, 2011, to October 31, 2012, when the children were aged 11 or 12 years. The participants were predominantly (1296 [92.4%]) of European descent. Study data were analyzed from June 1, 2016, to October 1, 2016. Main Outcomes and Measures: Peripapillary RNFL thickness measured using optical coherence tomography at the 11- or 12-year examination. Results: Of the 1406 children in the study, 1323 were included in the analysis (mean [SD] age was 11.7 [0.4] years; 633 [47.8%] were boys and 690 [52.2%] were girls). The mean (SD) RNFL thickness was 104 (9.6) μm. In 227 children whose mothers had smoked during pregnancy, the peripapillary RNFL was 5.7 μm (95% CI, 4.3-7.1 μm; P < .001) thinner than in children whose mothers had not smoked after correction for age, sex, birth weight, height, body weight, Tanner stage of pubertal development, axial length, and spherical equivalent refractive error. In low-birth-weight children (<2500 g), the RNFL was 3.5 μm (95% CI, 0.6-6.3 μm; P = .02) thinner than in normal-birth-weight children after adjustment for all variables. Conclusions and Relevance: Exposure to maternal smoking during uterine life and low birth weight were independently associated with having a thinner RNFL at age 11 or 12 years. These observations support previous findings that intrauterine and perinatal factors can have long-lasting effects on the retina and the optic nerve. The results of this study add evidence to existing recommendations to avoid smoking during pregnancy and support measures that promote maternal and fetal health.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ashina, Håkan","Li, Xiao Qiang","Olsen, Else Marie","Skovgaard, Anne Mette","Larsen, Michael","Munch, Inger Christine"],"cuid":["S02-090.74-040211"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ashina, Håkan"],"keyword":["Birth Weight","Child","Denmark","Female","Humans","Infant Low Birth Weight","Journal Article","Male","Maternal Behavior","Nerve Fibers","Nerve Fibers pathology","Optic Disk","Optic Disk pathology","Pregnancy","Prenatal Exposure Delayed Effects","Prenatal Exposure Delayed Effects diagnosis","Prospective Studies","Retinal Diseases","Retinal Diseases diagnosis","Retinal Ganglion Cells","Retinal Ganglion Cells pathology","Risk Factors","Smoking","Smoking adverse effects","Tomography Optical Coherence","Tomography Optical Coherence methods","Visual Acuity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of maternal smoking during pregnancy and birth weight with retinal nerve fiber layer thickness in children aged 000000000011 or 000000000012 years the copenhagen child cohort 000000002000 eye study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85017620512","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.74-040211","identifier":[{"id":"85017620512","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28253396","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0fb85b5a-e6a6-4dc2-b720-411d2f413a08","sdu-6d7d4a3b-3337-415c-8efa-b028081a64c1"],"keyword":["Birth Weight","Child","Denmark","Female","Humans","Infant, Low Birth Weight","Journal Article","Male","Maternal Behavior","Nerve Fibers","Nerve Fibers/pathology","Optic Disk","Optic Disk/pathology","Pregnancy","Prenatal Exposure Delayed Effects","Prenatal Exposure Delayed Effects/diagnosis","Prospective Studies","Retinal Diseases","Retinal Diseases/diagnosis","Retinal Ganglion Cells","Retinal Ganglion Cells/pathology","Risk Factors","Smoking","Smoking/adverse effects","Tomography, Optical Coherence","Tomography, Optical Coherence/methods","Visual Acuity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-676087E995ECB1135C59636DAB79A026"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Child and Adolescent Psychiatry","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3n