83-699X","rank":228,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29083408"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ng.3977","issn":["10614036","15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"12","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"1758-1766","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85035766416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Novo Nordisk","Other Research","Private Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9bad0704-7167-4bb8-b6d3-c81ad12b01fa","ku-a29cce0e-a320-4332-9145-5842de53c720","sdu-aaa3d9ee-231d-4eff-b237-f95089f9d2f7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exome-wide association study of plasma lipids in &gt;300,000 individuals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-092.64-024013","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"1.1 nm tungsten disulfide/poly(3,4-ethylenedioxythiophene) (PEDOT) was successfully electrodeposited on the surface of dealloyed nanoporous gold (NPG) surface to form uniform nanocomposites and offers an excellent electrocatalysis for the electrochemical dihydrogen evolution reaction (HER) in acidic media. The approach is straight forward and does not require any expensive equipment or intensive energy. The morphology and composition of the nanocomposites were structurally mapped by high-resolution transmission electron microscopy (HRTEM), X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS) and Fourier transform infrared spectrometry (FTIR). The roles of both the NPG substrate and PEDOT in the observed enhanced HER activity compared to planar Au-electrode surfaces and pure single-component WS 2 have been deconvoluted experimentally. PEDOT itself is inert for the HER, but was found to improve significantly the conductivity and operating stability of the WS 2 catalyst. The prepared nanocomposites reach the best in 2D WS 2 catalyst family, exhibiting excellent electrochemical catalytic activity for the HER. The optimal electrode showed an onset potential of −164 mV vs. reversible hydrogen electrode (RHE), an apparent exchange current density as high as 0.04 mA cm −2 , and a very low Tafel slope of 53 mV dec −1 . These catalysts are promising electrocatalysts for generation a large amount of H 2 from water.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Xiao, Xinxin","Engelbrekt, Christian","Zhang, Minwei","Li, Zheshen","Ulstrup, Jens","Zhang, Jingdong","Si, Pengchao"],"cuid":["S03-099.20-724372"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Zhang, Jingdong"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Key Laboratory for Liquid-Solid Structural Evolution and Processing of Materials","Shandong University"],"keyword":["ACTIVE EDGE SITES","Electrocatalysis","Electrocatalyst","Electrocatalysts","Hybrid","Hydrogen evolution reaction","Molybdenum sulfide","Nanoporous gold","PEDOT","Performance","Reduced graphene oxide","Tungsten disulfide","WS2 NANOSHEETS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a straight forward approach to electrodeposit tungsten disulfide poly 000000000003 000000000004 ethylenedioxythiophene composites onto nanoporous gold for the hydrogen evolution reaction","src":["aau","au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apsusc.2017.03.130","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Financial support from National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC No. 51301096), Shandong Provincial Natural Science Foundation (ZR2013EMQ012) and the Fundamental Research Funds of Shandong University (No. 2014JC017) to P. S., and from the Lundbeck Foundation (R141-2013-13273) to J. Z. is greatly appreciated."],"id":"S03-099.20-724372","identifier":[{"id":"000401201500036","type":"wos"},{"id":"85015904765","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e0e91065-aa16-456d-93a7-3299cf7f66da","au-1c65abdc-a20c-4687-b37e-debe2ee81553","dtu-0e75fb81-df2e-4c4f-857f-7b0c8207a9ab"],"keyword":["ACTIVE EDGE SITES","ELECTROCATALYST","ENHANCED CATALYTIC-ACTIVITIES","Electrocatalysis","Electrocatalysts","HYBRID","Hydrogen evolution reaction","MOLYBDENUM SULFIDE","MOS2 FILMS","Nanoporous gold","PEDOT","PERFORMANCE","REDUCED GRAPHENE OXIDE","Tungsten disulfide","WS2 NANOSHEETS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-D0D8C9A23E7AC89CD6F596E85420B0AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apsusc.2017.03.130","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"key laboratory for liquid solid structural evolution and processing of materials","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Key Laboratory for Liquid-Solid Structural Evolution and Processing of Materials","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, NanoChemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Organic Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy, Department of Physics and Astronomy - Centre for Storage Ring Facilities (ISA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaoxinxinpau","last":"Xiao","locid":"fd69114c-9434-44ba-b01b-e9ecb3831cae","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"engelbrektchristianpau","last":"Engelbrekt","locid":"a1b586e6-3d4b-4ebc-9037-259adc94bc5a","name":"Engelbrekt, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3679-3666","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Minwei","key":"zhangminweipau","last":"Zhang","locid":"5ef56fa7-35c7-4c87-a634-99be40d0966f","name":"Zhang, Minwei","orcid":"0000-0001-5588-6169","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheshen","key":"lizheshenpau","last":"Li","locid":"063ebd9e-41f2-4dcc-a04f-3d893fbccb86","name":"Li, Zheshen","orcid":"0000-0002-8381-1620","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"ulstrupjenspau","last":"Ulstrup","locid":"a7bf8f77-fd81-4dce-8592-8c7bec26750b","name":"Ulstrup, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jingdong","key":"zhangjingdongpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"4ad653c4-dedf-4da4-9808-9d4be7846db0","name":"Zhang, Jingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-0889-7057","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengchao","key":"sipengchaopau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Pengchao","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apsusc.2017.03.130","issn":["01694332","18735584"],"issn_org":["01694332"],"journal":"Applied Surface Science","pages":"308-314","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Applied Surface Science","volume":"410"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015904765"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e0e91065-aa16-456d-93a7-3299cf7f66da","au-1c65abdc-a20c-4687-b37e-debe2ee81553","dtu-0e75fb81-df2e-4c4f-857f-7b0c8207a9ab"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A straight forward approach to electrodeposit tungsten disulfide/poly(3,4-ethylenedioxythiophene) composites onto nanoporous gold for the hydrogen evolution reaction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.20-724372","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"A number of studies have revealed ammonia to be toxic to aquatic organisms; however, little is known about its effects under natural conditions. To elucidate the role of ammonia, we conducted 96-h acute toxicity tests as well as a whole-ecosystem chronic toxicity test for one year in ten 600-m 2 ponds. Three common cyprinids, silver carp Hypophthalmichthys molitrix Val. (H.m.), bighead carp Aristichthys nobilis Richardson (A.n.), and gibel carp Carassius auratus gibelio Bloch (C.g.), were used as test organisms. The 96-h LC 50 values of un-ionized ammonia (NH 3) for H.m., A.n., and C.g. were 0.35, 0.33, and 0.73 mg L − 1, respectively. In the ponds, annual mean NH 3 ranged between 0.01 and 0.54 mg L − 1, with 4 ponds having a NH 3 higher than the LC 50 of A.n. (lowest LC 50 in this study). No fish were found dead in the high-nitrogen ponds, but marked histological changes were found in livers and gills. Despite these changes, the specific growth rate of H.m. and A.n. increased significantly with NH 3. Our pond results suggest that fish might be more tolerant to high ammonia concentrations in natural aquatic ecosystems than under laboratory conditions. Our finding from field experiments thus suggests that the existing regulatory limits for reactive nitrogen (NH 3) established from lab toxicity tests might be somewhat too high at the ecosystem conditions. Field-scale chronic toxicity tests covering full life histories of fish and other aquatic organisms are therefore encouraged in order to optimize determination of the effects of ammonia in natural environments.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wang, Haijun","Xiao, Xu-Cheng","Wang, Hong-Zhu","Li, Yan","Liang, Xiao-Min","Feng, Wei-Song","Shao, Jian-Chun","Rybicki, Marcus","Jungmann, Dirk","Jeppesen, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-272942"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ammonia","Whole ecosystem experiment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of high ammonia concentrations on three cyprinid fish acute and whole ecosystem chronic tests","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85018357678","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-272942","identifier":[{"id":"28458207","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85018357678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fbb76ff6-5008-4018-b234-01718744cf58"],"keyword":["Acute test","Ammonia","Chronic test","Cyprinid fish","Whole-ecosystem experiment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-472574429B22B6881D1B3E8E81CF79F4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Center, ECOS Water","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Lake Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Haijun","key":"wanghaijunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Haijun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xu-Cheng","key":"xiaoxuchengpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xu-Cheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong-Zhu","key":"wanghongzhupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hong-Zhu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"liyanpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Min","key":"liangxiaominpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Xiao-Min","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei-Song","key":"fengweisongpau","last":"Feng","name":"Feng, Wei-Song","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian-Chun","key":"shaojianchunpau","last":"Shao","name":"Shao, Jian-Chun","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"rybickimarcuspau","last":"Rybicki","name":"Rybicki, Marcus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dirk","key":"jungmanndirkpau","last":"Jungmann","name":"Jungmann, Dirk","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik","key":"jeppesenerikpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"22bb5d6e-a9ae-4f70-81da-df1c57e71163","name":"Jeppesen, Erik","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28458207"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2017.04.070","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","pages":"900-909","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"598"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018357678"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fbb76ff6-5008-4018-b234-01718744cf58"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects of high ammonia concentrations on three cyprinid fish : Acute and whole-ecosystem chronic tests","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-272942","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"On 2017 August 17, the gravitational-wave event GW170817 was observed by the Advanced LIGO and Virgo detectors, and the gamma-ray burst (GRB) GRB 170817A was observed independently by the Fermi Gamma-ray Burst Monitor, and the Anti-Coincidence Shield for the Spectrometer for the International Gamma-Ray Astrophysics Laboratory. The probability of the near-simultaneous temporal and spatial observation of GRB 170817A and GW170817 occurring by chance is 5.0 x 10-8. We therefore confirm binary neutron star mergers as a progenitor of short GRBs. The association of GW170817 and GRB 170817A provides new insight into fundamental physics and the origin of short GRBs. We use the observed time delay of (+1.74± 0.05)s between GRB 170817A and GW170817 to: (i) constrain the difference between the speed of gravity and the speed of light to be between -3x10-15 and +7x 10-16 times the speed of light, (ii) place new bounds on the violation of Lorentz invariance, (iii) present a new test of the equivalence principle by constraining the Shapiro delay between gravitational and electromagnetic radiation. We also use the time delay to constrain the size and bulk Lorentz factor of the region emitting the gamma-rays. GRB 170817A is the closest short GRB with a known distance, but is between 2 and 6 orders of magnitude less energetic than other bursts with measured redshift. A new generation of gamma-ray detectors, and subthreshold searches in existing detectors, will be essential to detect similar short bursts at greater distances. Finally, we predict a joint detection rate for the Fermi Gamma-ray Burst Monitor and the Advanced LIGO and Virgo detectors of 0.1–1.4 per year during the 2018–2019 observing run and 0.3–1.7 per year at design sensitivity.","author_count":1153,"contributors":["Abbott, B. P.","Abbott, R.","Abbott, T. D.","Acernese, F.","Ackley, K.","Adams, C.","Adams, T.","Addesso, P.","Adhikari, R. X.","Adya, V. B.","Affeldt, C.","Afrough, M.","Agarwal, B.","Agathos, M