{"affno":"","first":"Dakai","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Dakai","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fuqiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Fuqiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hui","key":"panpau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Hui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Han","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","name":"Liang, Han","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kui","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","locid":"0036bb1c-f950-43e7-87d8-d27fd0ffdb94","name":"Wu, Kui","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jianxing","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Jianxing","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28522810"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-017-02405-9","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"2121","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019928026"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-48040008-b823-4904-a0c9-2f02f5489f0c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Integrative analysis of genomic sequencing data reveals higher prevalence of LRP1B mutations in lung adenocarcinoma patients with COPD","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-436444","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Air pollutions from transportation sector have become a serious urban environmental problem, especially in developing countries with expending urbanization. Cleaner technologies advancement and optimal regulation on the transporting behaviors and related design in infrastructures is critical to address above issue. To understand the spatial and temporal emissions pattern within transportation lays the foundation for design on better infrastructures and guidance on low-carbon transportation behaviors. The feasibility of Global Positioning System (GPS) and emerging big data analysis technique enable the in-depth analysis on this topic, while to date, applications had been rather few. With this circumstance, this paper analyzed the taxi's energy consumption and emissions and their spatial-temporal distribution in Shanghai, one of the most famous mega cities in China, applying big data analysis on GPS data of taxies. Spatial and temporal features of energy consumptions and pollutants emissions were further mapped with geographical information system (GIS). Results highlighted that, spatially, the energy consumption and emission presented a distribution of dual-core cyclic structure, in which, two hubs were identified. One was the city center, the other was Hongqiao transport hub, the activities and emission was more concentrated in the west par of Huangpu River. Temporally, the highest activity and emission moment was 9–10AM, the second peak occurred in 7–8PM, which were both the traffic rush period. The lowest activity/emission moment was 3–4AM. Causal mechanism for such distribution was further investigated, so as to improve the driving behaviors. Through the exploration of spatial and temporal emissions distribution of taxis via big dada technique, this paper provided enlightening insights to policy makers for better understanding on the travel patterns and related environmental implications in Shanghai metropolis, so as to support better planning on infrastructures system, demand side management and the promotion on low-carbon life styles.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ren, Jingzheng","Luo, Xiao","Dong, Liang","Dou, Yi","Zhang, Ning","Li, Ye","Sun, Lu","Yao, Shengyong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-601026"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jinan University","National Institute for Environmental Studies (NIES)","The University of Tokyo","Tongji University","shijiazhuang Tiedao University"],"keyword":["Big data mining","GPS","Shanghai"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis on spatial temporal features of taxis emissions from big data informed travel patterns a case of shanghai china","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84973582097","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-601026","identifier":[{"id":"84973582097","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-614274c5-6a66-477c-8955-1da982cec8ee"],"keyword":["Big data mining","GPS","Shanghai","Spatial-temporal emissions distribution","Taxi travel pattern"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09CA78C05B6BA424EA03DEE00CC58B36"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation, SDU Engineering Operations Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"tongji university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tongji University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"national institute for environmental studies","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"National Institute for Environmental Studies (NIES)","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"jinan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Jinan University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"jp","key":"the university of tokyo","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"The University of Tokyo","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"shijiazhuang tiedao university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"shijiazhuang Tiedao University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingzheng","key":"renpau","last":"Ren","locid":"0fabc81a-5853-4ac7-96a2-bfaefb164136","name":"Ren, Jingzheng","orcid":"0000-0002-9690-5183","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"luopau","last":"Luo","name":"Luo, Xiao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Liang","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Liang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"doupau","last":"Dou","name":"Dou, Yi","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ning","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ye","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ye","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lu","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Lu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Shengyong","key":"yaopau","last":"Yao","name":"Yao, Shengyong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jclepro.2016.05.161","issn":["09596526"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Cleaner Production","pages":"926-935","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cleaner Production","volume":"142"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84973582097"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-614274c5-6a66-477c-8955-1da982cec8ee"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Analysis on spatial-temporal features of taxis' emissions from big data informed travel patterns : a case of Shanghai,China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-601026","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Although several lung cancer susceptibility loci have been identified, much of the heritability for lung cancer remains unexplained. Here 14,803 cases and 12,262 controls of European descent were genotyped on the OncoArray and combined with existing data for an aggregated genomewide association study (GWAS) analysis of lung cancer in 29,266 cases and 56,450 controls. We identified 18 susceptibility loci achieving genome-wide significance, including 10 new loci. The new loci highlight the striking heterogeneity in genetic susceptibility across the histological subtypes of lung cancer, with four loci associated with lung cancer overall and six loci associated with lung adenocarcinoma. Gene expression quantitative trait locus (eQTL) analysis in 1,425 normal lung tissue samples highlights RNASET2, SECISBP2L and NRG1 as candidate genes. Other loci include genes such as a cholinergic nicotinic receptor, CHRNA2, and the telomere-related genes OFBC1 and RTEL1. Further exploration of the target genes will continue to provide new insights into the etiology of lung cancer.","author_count":62,"contributors":["McKay, James D.","Hung, Rayjean J.","Han, Younghun","Zong, Xuchen","Carreras-Torres, Robert","Christiani, David C.","Caporaso, Neil E.","Johansson, Mattias","Xiao, Xiangjun","Li, Yafang","Byun, Jinyoung","Dunning, Alison","Pooley, Karen A.","Qian, David C.","Ji, Xuemei","Liu, Geoffrey","Timofeeva, Maria N.","Bojesen, Stig E","Wu, Xifeng","Marchand, Loic Le","Albanes, Demetrios","Bickeböller, Heike","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Bush, William S.","Tardon, Adonina","Rennert, Gad","Teare, M. Dawn","Field, John K.","Kiemeney, Lambertus A.","Lazarus, Philip","Haugen, Aage","Lam, Stephen","Schabath, Matthew B.","Andrew, Angeline S.","Shen, Hongbing","Hong, Yun Chul","Yuan, Jian Min","Bertazzi, Pier Alberto","Pesatori, Angela C.","Ye, Yuanqing","Diao, Nancy","Su, Li","Zhang, Ruyang","Brhane, Yonathan","Leighl, Natasha","Johansen, Jakob S.","Mellemgaard, Anders","Saliba, Walid","Haiman, Christopher A.","Wilkens, Lynne R.","Rafnar, Thorunn","Thorgeirsson, Thorgeir E","Reginsson, Gunnar W.","Brennan, Paul","Landi, Maria Teresa","Amos, Christopher I"],"cuid":["S02-096.67-021743"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["SpiroMeta Consortium"],"country":["Canada","China","France","Germany","Israel","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","South Korea","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carlos III Health Institute (ISCIII) (CIBER)","Case Western Reserve University","Dartmouth College","Harvard University","International Agency for Research on Cancer","Moffitt Cancer Center","Nanjing Medical University","National Institute of Occupational Health","National Institutes of Health","National Institutes of Health (NIH)","Radboud University Nijmegen","Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute, Mount Sinai Hospital, Toronto","Seoul National University","Technion-Israel Institute of Technology","Umeå University","University of British Columbia","University of Cambridge","University of Göttingen","University of Hawai'i at Mānoa","University of Hawaii at Manoa","University of Liverpool","University of Milan","University of Oviedo","University of Pittsburgh","University of Sheffield","University of South Florida","University of Southern California","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Toronto","Vanderbilt University","Washington State University Pullman","Washington State University Spokane"],"keyword":["Architecture","Consortium","Crohns disease","Genome wide association","Imputation","Metaanalysis","Telomere length","Variants"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-