{"abstract":"This special issue of Catalysis Today with the theme “Sustain-able Energy” results from a great success of the session “Catalytic Technologies Accelerating the Establishment of Sustainable and Clean Energy”, one of the two sessions of the 1st International Symposium on Catalytic Science and Technology in Sustainable Energy and Environment, held in Tianjin, China during October8–10, 2014. This biennial symposium offers an international forum for discussing and sharing the cutting-edge researches and the most recent breakthroughs in energy and environmental technologies based on catalysis principles.A total of 29 invited contributions from the authors who madeoral and poster (very limited number) presentations are includedin this special issue. A wide spectrum of topics is covered, whichcan be broadly categorized as: Clean Fossil Fuels Renewable Fuels Efficient Catalytic Energy Processors Finally, we gratefully acknowledge all the authors and reviewers of the manuscripts and the editorial team of Elsevier, without whom the special issue would not have been possible.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Wang, Yuxin","Xiao, Feng-Shou","Seshan, Kulathu K.","Jensen, Anker Degn","Li, Yongdan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356966"],"event":{"end":"2014-10-10","place":"Tianjin, cn","start":"2014-10-08","title":"1st International Symposium on Catalytic Science and Technology in Sustainable Energy and Environment","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tianjin University","University of Twente","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preface catalysis today special issue of catalysis today with the theme sustainable energy","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dbp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85044316429","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356966","identifier":[{"id":"000364863000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85044316429","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-af694621-9aa4-435e-9bc2-784f28b02a75"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1FE322DAA969B95E5F4BF0B1A598E23D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tianjin university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tianjin University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"university of twente","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Twente","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CHEC Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuxin","key":"wangped","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yuxin","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Feng-Shou","key":"xiaoped","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Feng-Shou","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kulathu K.","key":"seshanped","last":"Seshan","name":"Seshan, Kulathu K.","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anker Degn","key":"jensenped","last":"Jensen","locid":"cbdc5a0f-1286-4071-bb03-0e1be55ff36f","name":"Jensen, Anker Degn","orcid":"0000-0002-7341-4859","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongdan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Yongdan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cattod.2015.10.007","pages":"245","status":"p","title":"Catalysis Today","volume":"259"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044316429"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-af694621-9aa4-435e-9bc2-784f28b02a75"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Preface: Catalysis Today : Special issue of Catalysis Today with the theme “Sustainable Energy”","type":"Book Preface, Encycl. Entry","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356966","year":"2016","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In pressure-induced reversible structural transitions, the term \"reversible\" refers to the recovery of the virgin structure in a material upon complete decompression. Pressure-induced amorphous-to-crystalline transitions have been claimed to be reversible, but evidence that amorphous material recovers its virgin amorphous structure upon complete depressurization has been lacking. In amorphous As2Se3 (a-As2Se3) chalcogenide, however, we report a novel reversible amorphous-to-crystalline transition that provides compelling experimental evidence that upon complete decompression, the recovered amorphous phase is structurally the same as that of the virgin (as-cast) amorphous phase. Combining the experimental results with ab initio molecular dynamics simulations, we elucidate that the amorphization is mediated by a surplus of total free energy in the high-pressure face-centered cubic phase as compared to the virgin amorphous phase and that the structural recovery to the virgin amorphous phase is a consequence of an enhancement in covalent bonding character over interlayer forces upon complete decompression. Furthermore, we observed a two-dimensional to three-dimensional network transition under compression and its reversibility upon decompression.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Ahmad, Azkar Saeed","Lou, Hong Bo","Lin, Chuan Long","Li, Ai Guo","Yang, Ke","Glazyrin, K.","Liermann, H. P.","Franz, Hermann","Ståhl, Kenny","Cui, Shuo","Bureau, Bruno","Zhang, Dong-Xian","Wang, Xiao-Dong","Cao, Qing-Ping","Greer, A. Lindsay","Jiang, Jian-Zhong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-377459"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","German Electron Synchrotron","University of Cambridge","Université de Rennes","Zhejiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reversible devitrification in amorphous as sub 000000000002 sub se sub 000000000003 sub under pressure","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.94.195211","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-377459","identifier":[{"id":"84997706283","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f38eb1ba-4a15-4c22-8d52-255611c8b6ec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B3C1C5726916F34E6A1D36D309A5E3E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127704943/Reversible_devitrification.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.94.195211","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"german electron synchrotron","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Electron Synchrotron","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, X-ray Crystallography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"université de rennes","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université de Rennes","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Azkar Saeed","key":"ahmadpau","last":"Ahmad","name":"Ahmad, Azkar Saeed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong Bo","key":"loupau","last":"Lou","name":"Lou, Hong Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chuan Long","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Chuan Long","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ai Guo","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Ai Guo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ke","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Ke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"K.","key":"glazyrinpau","last":"Glazyrin","name":"Glazyrin, K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"H. P.","key":"liermannpau","last":"Liermann","name":"Liermann, H. P.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hermann","key":"franzpau","last":"Franz","name":"Franz, Hermann","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kenny","key":"ståhlpau","last":"Ståhl","locid":"3c26b45b-2fa8-44f0-bc8f-0fdbb7afd6da","name":"Ståhl, Kenny","orcid":"0000-0002-4459-3026","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuo","key":"cuipau","last":"Cui","name":"Cui, Shuo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Bruno","key":"bureaupau","last":"Bureau","name":"Bureau, Bruno","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dong-Xian","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Dong-Xian","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Dong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiao-Dong","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qing-Ping","key":"caopau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Qing-Ping","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"A. Lindsay","key":"greerpau","last":"Greer","name":"Greer, A. Lindsay","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian-Zhong","key":"jiangpau","last":"Jiang","name":"Jiang, Jian-Zhong","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1103/physrevb.94.195211","issn":["1550235X","24699950"],"issn_org":["24699950"],"issue":"19","journal":"Physical Review B","paperid":"195211","publisher":"American Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Physical Review B","volume":"94"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84997706283"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f38eb1ba-4a15-4c22-8d52-255611c8b6ec"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Reversible devitrification in amorphous As<sub>2</sub> Se<sub>3</sub> under pressure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-377459","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Type 2 diabetes (T2D) has been reported to be associated with an elevated risk of breast cancer. It is unclear, however, whether this association is due to shared genetic factors. METHODS: We constructed a genetic risk score (GRS) using risk variants from 33 known independent T2D susceptibility loci and evaluated its relation to breast cancer risk using the data from two consortia, including 62,328 breast cancer patients and 83,817 controls of European ancestry. Unconditional logistic regression models were used to derive adjusted odds ratios (ORs) and 95 % confidence intervals (CIs) to measure the association of breast cancer risk with T2D GRS or T2D-associated genetic risk variants. Meta-analyses were conducted to obtain summary ORs across all studies. RESULTS: The T2D GRS was not found to be associated with breast cancer risk, overall, by menopausal status, or for estrogen receptor positive or negative breast cancer. Three T2D associated risk variants were individually associated with breast cancer risk after adjustment for multiple comparisons using the Bonferroni method (at p < 0.001), rs9939609 (FTO) (OR 0.94, 95 % CI = 0.92-0.95, p = 4.13E-13), rs7903146 (TCF7L2) (OR 1.04, 95 % CI = 1.02-1.06, p = 1.26E-05), and rs8042680 (PRC1) (OR 0.97, 95 % CI = 0.95-0.99, p = 8.05E-04). CONCLUSIONS: We have shown that several genetic risk variants were associated with the risk of both T2D and breast cancer. However, overall genetic susceptibility to T2D may not be related to breast cancer risk.","author_count":118,"contributors":["Zhao, Zhiguo","Wen, Wanqing","Michailidou, Kyriaki","Bolla, Manjeet K","Wang, Qin","Zhang, Ben","Long, Jirong","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Schmidt, Marjanka K","Milne, Roger L","García-Closas, Montserrat","Chang-Claude, Jenny","Lindstrom, Sara","Bojesen, Stig E","Ahsan, Habibul","Aittomäki, Kristiina","Andrulis, Irene L","Anton-Culver, Hoda","Arndt, Volker","Beckmann, Matthias W","Beeghly-Fadiel, Alicia","Benitez, Javier","Blomqvist, C