{"abstract":"Lung cancer is the leading cause of mortality and 5-year survival rate is very low worldwide. Recent studies show that vascular endothelial growth factor receptor-3 (VEGFR-3) signaling pathway contributes to lung cancer progression. So we hypothesize that an oral DNA vaccine that targets VEGFR-3 carried by attenuated Salmonella enterica serovar typhimurium strain SL3261 has impacts on lung cancer progression. In this study, the oral VEGFR-3-based vaccine-immunized mice showed appreciable inhibition of tumor growth and tumor lymphatic microvessels in lung cancer mice model. Moreover, the oral VEGFR-3-based vaccine-immunized mice showed remarkable increases in both VEGFR-3-specific antibody levels and cytotoxic activity. Furthermore, the oral VEGFR-3-based vaccine-immunized mice showed a significant increase in the levels of T helper type 1 (Th1) cell intracellular cytokine expression (IL-2, IFN-γ, and TNF-α). After inoculation with murine Lewis lung carcinoma (LLC) cells, CD4 + or CD8 + T cell numbers obviously declined in control groups whereas high levels were maintained in the oral VEGFR-3-based vaccine group. These results demonstrated that the oral VEGFR-3-based vaccine could induce specific humoral and cellular immune responses and then significantly inhibit lung carcinoma growth via suppressing lymphangiogenesis.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Chen, Yan","Liu, Xin","Jin, Cong Guo","Zhou, Yong Chun","Navab, Roya","Jakobsen, Kristine Raaby","Chen, Xiao Qun","Li, Jia","Li, Ting Ting","Luo, Lu","Wang, Xi Cai"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-215559"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wang, Xi Cai"],"country":["Canada","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kunming Medical College","University Health Network"],"keyword":["DNA vaccine","Lung cancer","Lymphangiogenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an orally administered dna vaccine targeting vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 000000000003 inhibits lung carcinoma growth","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84941686876","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-215559","identifier":[{"id":"84941686876","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26376999","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-975bc07d-3f64-4e41-9695-287418c98806"],"keyword":["Attenuated Salmonella enterica serovar Typhimurium","DNA vaccine","Lung cancer","Lymphangiogenesis","VEGFR-3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACB149A11054B50B9F965204E3131E0A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"kunming medical college","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Kunming Medical College","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"university health network","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University Health Network","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"chenyanpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"af