{"abstract":"Spoof surface plasmon polaritons based notch filter for ultra-wideband microwave waveguide is proposed. Owing to subwavelength confinement, such a filter has advantage in the structure size without sacrificing the performance. The spoof SPP based notch is introduced to suppress the WLAN and satellite communication interference simultaneously. Both the cutoff frequency and the notch frequency are sensitive to the structure parameters, and the cut-off frequency can reach 20 GHz. An adiabatic transition relying on gradient hole-size and flaring ground is designed to effectively couple energy into spoof SPP waveguide. The result shows its cut-off frequency of 17.4 GHz with the insertion loss better than 3 dB during the whole pass-band, while having more than 20 dB rejections at 5.36 GHz and 9.32 GHz with 10 dB fractional bandwidth 1.07% and 0.74% respectively to avoid the existing WLAN and satellite communication signals. Due to planar structures proposed here, it is easy to integrate in the microwave integrated systems, which can play an important role in the microwave communication circuit and system.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Xiao, Binggang","Li, Sheng-Hua","Xiao, Sanshui"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-323717"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Jiliang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spoof surface plasmon polaritons based notch filter for ultra wideband microwave waveguide","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131068114/Spoof_Surface_Plasmon_Polaritons_Based_Notch_Filter_for_Ultra_wideband_Microwave_Waveguide.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-323717","identifier":[{"id":"84964613693","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-40528ea6-11f6-40e8-8e67-d0c9d412ea04"],"keyword":["Notch band","Spoof surface plasmon polaritons","UWB waveguide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-022CA15C457FC01155EE2AC833CB97C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.optcom.2016.04.019","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/131068114/Spoof_Surface_Plasmon_Polaritons_Based_Notch_Filter_for_Ultra_wideband_Microwave_Waveguide.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china jiliang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Jiliang University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Structured Electromagnetic Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Binggang","key":"xiaobinggangpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Binggang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sheng-Hua","key":"lishenghuapau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Sheng-Hua","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanshui","key":"xiaosanshuipau","last":"Xiao","locid":"c516dded-c5eb-40a6-b2dd-37be55b893c8","name":"Xiao, Sanshui","orcid":"0000-0001-6529-5047","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.optcom.2016.04.019","issn":["00304018","18730310"],"issn_org":["00304018"],"journal":"Optics Communications","pages":"13-17","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Optics Communications","volume":"374"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964613693"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-40528ea6-11f6-40e8-8e67-d0c9d412ea04"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Spoof surface plasmon polaritons based notch filter for ultra-wideband microwave waveguide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-323717","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Sintering and steel production as the main emission sources of polychlorinated dibenzo-p-dioxins and dibenzofurans (PCDD/Fs) may affect environment and human health. The concentrations, profiles, and distributions of PCDD/Fs in soil samples from around four typical sintering and steel production plants in Hebei Province, China, were determined. Forty-six soil samples were collected at distances from 500 to 9000 m from industrial plant chimneys. The concentrations of total 17 2,3,7,8-substituted PCDD/F congeners in the soil samples from sites A, B, C, and D were in the range 11-130, 13-284, 2.6-378, and 21-231 pg/g, respectively, and the internationally accepted toxic equivalent (I-TEQ) concentrations were 0.37-13.2, 0.31-12.1, 0.13-13.7, and 1.60-22.7 pg I-TEQ/g, respectively. Soil ingestion was estimated the major exposure pathway to PCDD/Fs. At current PCDD/F concentrations, the local population will be exposed to low amounts of PCDD/Fs in soil from around the industrial sites, and this exposure will pose potential health risks for the local population living at distances of less than 1000 m from nearest stack but will have no high health risks for people living further away. These results will be helpful when planning measures to control PCDD/F sources. The data will also benefit local environmental monitoring studies and be useful when assessing the risks posed by PCDD/Fs around the industrial sites to the environment and humans.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Han, Ying","Liu, Wenbin","Hansen, Hans Chr. Bruun","Chen, Xuebin","Liao, Xiao","Li, Haifeng","Wang, Mengjing","Yan, Nan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-477660"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"concentrations of and health risks posed by polychlorinated dibenzo i p i dioxins and dibenzofurans around industrial sites in hebei province china","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-477660","identifier":[{"id":"27314421","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84975125440","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8cd60d5f-6307-4f25-a487-bf71674c7c44"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EBCE99367209DEDB51442EE6E223A67"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Environmental Chemistry and Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ying","key":"hanpau","last":"Han","name":"Han, Ying","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wenbin","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Wenbin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans Chr. Bruun","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"9b553aa7-aebe-452e-b36f-b21edcff4e70","name":"Hansen, Hans Chr. Bruun","orcid":"0000-0002-8617-2393","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xuebin","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xuebin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao","key":"liaopau","last":"Liao","name":"Liao, Xiao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Haifeng","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Haifeng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mengjing","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Mengjing","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nan","key":"yanpau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Nan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27314421"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11356-016-7050-1","issn":["09441344","16147499"],"issn_org":["09441344"],"issue":"18","journal":"Environmental Science and Pollution Research","pages":"18742-18752","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science and Pollution Research","title_org":"Environmental science and pollution research international","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84975125440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8cd60d5f-6307-4f25-a487-bf71674c7c44"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Concentrations of and health risks posed by polychlorinated dibenzo-<i>p</i>-dioxins and dibenzofurans around industrial sites in Hebei Province, China","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-477660","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: This study compared in vivo enhanced-depth imaging optical coherence tomography (EDI-OCT) with ex vivo histology of the choroid in human eyes. METHODS: Three eyes in three patients with advanced iris melanoma without posterior segment involvement underwent EDI-OCT less than 24 hours prior to enucleation and, in one eye, immediately after enucleation. Following fixation in 4% buffered formaldehyde and paraffin embedding, serial sections of the whole eye were cut horizontally, mounted, stained with hematoxylin-eosin and digitized. Alignment between histology and EDI-OCT was made on landmarks such as retinal vessel, the foveal depression, ciliary arteries, drusen, and nevi. RESULTS: Intra- and interindividual variations in relative choroidal thickness were comparable between the two modalities. After histologic fixation of the three melanoma eyes, the fullness of the choroidal vessels was reduced and subfoveal choroid thickness reduced to 56%, 45%, and 56%, respectively, of its in vivo thickness on EDI-OCT. CONCLUSIONS: There were no identifiable discrepancies in choroidal structural patterns between clinical EDI-OCT and histologic sections except that after enucleation and histologic fixation choroidal thickness was reduced to roughly half of its in vivo value, a phenomenon that may reflect the high content of blood vessels in the choroid.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Li, Xiao Qiang","Heegaard, Steffen","Kiilgaard, Jens Folke","Munch, Inger Christine","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-522045"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enhanced depth imaging optical coherence tomography of the human choroid in vivo compared with histology after enucleation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.15-18884","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-522045","identifier":[{"id":"84978536050","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27409496","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d73fb467-2a9a-40de-a264-bc2bafbd5ea6"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E4C677FB8F5AC51AC6EAE1418BA62AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.15-18884","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Xiao Qiang","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Qiang","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"e1720fc3-b9d4-4664-8bcc-2394fd476fdd","name":"Heegaard, Steffen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Folke","key":"kiilgaardpau","last":"Kiilgaard","locid":"13c2c03c-a356-4fa4-b819-c4d75cc12646","name":"Kiilgaard, Jens Folke","orcid":"0000-0003-1054-1460","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27409496"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1167/iovs.15-18884","issn":["01460404","02730189"],"issn_org":["01460404"],"issue":"9","journal":"Investigative Ophthalmology & Visual Science","status":"p","title":"Investigative Ophthalmology & Visual Science","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978536050"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d73fb467-2a9a-40de-a264-bc2bafbd5ea6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Enhanced-Depth Imaging Optical Coherence Tomography of the Human Choroid In Vivo Compared With Histology After Enucleation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-522045","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In order to obtain a better understanding of the welding mechanism in contact separation, electrical endurance tests were conducted with AgSnO2 and AgNi contacts on a simulation test device. Waveforms of contact displacement, contact voltage, and current were recorded with LabVIEW during the tests, and changes in a contact gap and heights of pips with increases in operation cycles were observed through charge-coupled device cameras. The resultant test results show that welding in separation is accompanied with a preceding voltage pulse which represents arc rather than contact bounce arc.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Yang, Xiao Cheng","Huang, Jiang","Li, Zhen Biao","Liu, Jin You","Wang, Qian","Hasegawa, Makoto"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065530"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chitose Institute of Science and Technology","Huazhong University of Science and Technology","State Grid Corporation of China"],"keyword":["Electrical contacts"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the preceding voltage pulse and separation welding mechanism of electrical contacts","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84966474611&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-065530","identifier":[{"id":"000378266500002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84966474611","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-354d70fa-2a18-4a38-9484-68aec85c4434"],"keyword":["Arcing","Electrical contacts","Gap length","Welding in separation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D128F203C515798F379934722F28ED0A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"huazhong university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"state grid corporation of china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Grid Corporation of China","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"jp","key":"chitose institute of science and technology","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Chitose Institute of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Cheng","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Xiao Cheng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiang","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jiang","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhen Biao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhen Biao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin You","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jin You","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qian","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"3d0d34fa-554c-4f03-b685-11b630e49ba2","name":"Wang, Qian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Makoto","key":"hasegawapau","last":"Hasegawa","name":"Hasegawa, Makoto","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tcpmt.2016.2552202","issn":["21563950","21563985"],"issn_org":["21563950"],"issue":"6","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Components, Packaging and Manufacturing Technology","pages":"846-853","paperid":"7465799","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Components, Packaging and Manufacturing Technology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84966474611"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-354d70fa-2a18-4a38-9484-68aec85c4434"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Preceding Voltage Pulse and Separation Welding Mechanism of Electrical Contacts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065530","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: An increasing number of studies have been conducted on the use of endoscopic ultrasound (EUS)-guided needle sampling for upper gastrointestinal subepithelial lesions (SEL). However, reported diagnostic efficacy varies greatly.OBJECTIVE: To summarize up current evidences on the diagnostic efficacy of EUS-guided needle sampling for upper GI SEL.METHOD: A reproducible strategy was used to search four databases. Search results were evaluated for eligibility, and the quality of eligible studies was assessed by QUADAS-2. Pooled efficacy of EUS-guided needle sampling in upper GI SEL was calculated. Procedure-related complications, diagnostic errors, and independent factors related to a higher success rate were also recorded and analyzed.RESULTS: Seventeen studies, comprising 978 attempts of EUS-guided needle sampling, were included in a meta-analysis. Pooled diagnostic rate of EUS-guided needle sampling was 59.9 %, with a heterogeneity I (2) of 55.2 %. Subgroup analysis showed no difference in diagnostic rate among fine needle aspiration (FNA), trucut needle biopsy (TCB), and fine needle biopsy (FNB), or among 19-, 22-, and 25-G needles. Subgroup analysis and meta-regression suggested that the cell block method might be correlated with a higher diagnostic rate. Few severe complications were reported. Diagnosis errors were rare.CONCLUSION: EUS-guided needle sampling is a safe, but only moderately effective method for pathology diagnosis of upper GI SEL. Choice of FNA/TCB/FNB, or 19 G/22 G/25 G does not seem to alter the overall diagnostic rate.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Xiao-Cen","Li, Quan-Lin","Yu, Yongfu","Yao, Li-Qing","Xu, Mei-Dong","Zhang, Yi-Qun","Zhong, Yun-Shi","Chen, Wei-Feng","Zhou, Ping-Hong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-149856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic efficacy of endoscopic ultrasound guided needle sampling for upper gastrointestinal subepithelial lesions","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84940055207","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-149856","identifier":[{"id":"84940055207","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26310529","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-23c70a3d-ca56-47a4-b3ea-838125bad354"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-928738A4DF7DD8A33C99DAE69E2CF7BA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Cen","key":"zhangxiaocenpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xiao-Cen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Quan-Lin","key":"liquanlinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Quan-Lin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongfu","key":"yuyongfupau","last":"Yu","locid":"06be533f-163e-454d-bd55-9219a4f5cafa","name":"Yu, Yongfu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Li-Qing","key":"yaoliqingpau","last":"Yao","name":"Yao, Li-Qing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mei-Dong","key":"xumeidongpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Mei-Dong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi-Qun","key":"zhangyiqunpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yi-Qun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Yun-Shi","key":"zhongyunshipau","last":"Zhong","name":"Zhong, Yun-Shi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei-Feng","key":"chenweifengpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Wei-Feng","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ping-Hong","key":"zhoupinghongpau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Ping-Hong","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26310529"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00464-015-4494-1","issn":["09302794","14322218"],"issn_org":["09302794"],"issue":"6","journal":"Surgical Endoscopy","pages":"2431-2441","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Surgical Endoscopy","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940055207"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-23c70a3d-ca56-47a4-b3ea-838125bad354"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Diagnostic efficacy of endoscopic ultrasound-guided needle sampling for upper gastrointestinal subepithelial lesions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-149856","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Hoffmann-Jørgensen, Jørgen","Miao, Yu","Li, Xiao Chun","Xu, Shou Fang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-168050"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Miao, Yu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Henan Normal University","Xinxiang University"],"keyword":["Bernstein s inequality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kolmogorov type law of the logarithm for arrays","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84959081746","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-168050","identifier":[{"id":"84959081746","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-43fab02f-ace3-4335-a525-4d2beb31029f"],"keyword":["Bernstein’s inequality","Independent random variables","Kolmogorov’s inequality","Kolmogorov’s law of the logarithm"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C071A3B65C81321F38619728B67C5779"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"henan normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Henan Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"xinxiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xinxiang University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"hoffmannjørgensenpau","last":"Hoffmann-Jørgensen","locid":"c7359355-02af-4bd1-b876-f9b3438da85e","name":"Hoffmann-Jørgensen, Jørgen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yu","key":"miaopau","last":"Miao","name":"Miao, Yu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao Chun","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiao Chun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Shou Fang","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Shou Fang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10959-014-0574-8","issn":["08949840","15729230"],"issn_org":["08949840"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Theoretical Probability","pages":"32-47","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Theoretical Probability","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959081746"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-43fab02f-ace3-4335-a525-4d2beb31029f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Kolmogorov Type Law of the Logarithm for Arrays","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-168050","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The environmental conditions in the new ranges of introduced plant species are often different from the conditions in their native ranges, and invasive plant species have been assumed to adapt to different environmental conditions by rapid ecological evolution in the invasive range after the introduction. Another interpretation of the change in plant traits after their introduction, however, is ecological fitting, which is based on the inherently high phenotypic plasticity of the species rather than on evolution. The Mediterranean haplotype M1 lineage of the wetland grass Phragmites australis was introduced to the coastal wetlands along the Gulf Coast of North America, where it is exposed to a different climate compared to its original range. The climate in the native range is arid or temperate with dry and hot summers, whereas the climate in the introduced range is warmer and has a higher and more uniform precipitation than that in the native range. This warmer and more humid environment is likely to pose different selection pressures to the plants in the introduced range and thus cause rapid evolutionary change and phenotypic differentiation in the introduced range. Here, we compared phenotypic traits of the M1 lineage from the native and introduced ranges in a common garden experiment to study the processes assisting the successful spread in the introduced range. Overall, the native and introduced groups were similar, but we detected a few phenotypic traits that diverged. Ecological fitting could be the fundamental mechanism by which the P. australis M1 lineage survives and spreads in the introduced Gulf Coast region. However, further research is needed to assess how the diverging traits observed in our study in Denmark (lower photosynthetic rates, lower chlorophylls concentration and higher leaf K concentration for the introduced than for the native genotypes) are expressed in the two ranges.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Guo, Wen Yong","Lambertini, Carla","Guo, Xiao","Li, Xiu Zhen","Eller, Franziska","Brix, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-170900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Guo, Wen Yong"],"country":["China","Czechia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Czech Academy of Sciences","East China Normal University","Qingdao Agricultural University"],"keyword":["Common reed","Ecological fitting","Evolution","Mediterranean","Phragmites australis","Range expansion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phenotypic traits of the mediterranean phragmites australis m000000000001 lineage differences between the native and introduced ranges","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979600081","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-170900","identifier":[{"id":"84979600081","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-48ede551-15ff-436a-b1d4-1b5091924fa2"],"keyword":["Common reed","Delta type","Ecological fitting","Evolution","Gulf Coast","Haplotype M1","Mediterranean","Phragmites australis","Preadaptation","Range expansion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4EAFF4B306749001151EA88D14C6255A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cz","key":"czech academy of sciences","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Czech Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"east china normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"qingdao agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Wen Yong","key":"guowenyongpau","last":"Guo","locid":"0061a6f4-1828-4e8d-899f-759e877791a6","name":"Guo, Wen Yong","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carla","key":"lambertinicarlapau","last":"Lambertini","locid":"539cdc5f-a62e-4b9d-bd32-6316a6003286","name":"Lambertini, Carla","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"guoxiaopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Xiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiu Zhen","key":"lixiuzhenpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiu Zhen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Franziska","key":"ellerfranziskapau","last":"Eller","locid":"15509be6-9a31-4be1-9fab-9bf9db482917","name":"Eller, Franziska","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"brixhanspau","last":"Brix","locid":"4068bdb4-1c13-432c-b420-3991683780b5","name":"Brix, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-2771-2983","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10530-016-1236-9","issn":["13873547","15731464"],"issn_org":["13873547"],"issue":"9","journal":"Biological Invasions","pages":"2551-2561","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"Biological Invasions","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979600081"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-48ede551-15ff-436a-b1d4-1b5091924fa2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Phenotypic traits of the Mediterranean Phragmites australis M1 lineage: differences between the native and introduced ranges","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-170900","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Here we examine the impact of ring conformation on the charge transport characteristics of cyclic pentasilane structures bound to gold electrodes in single molecule junctions. We investigate the conductance properties of alkylated cyclopentasilane cis and trans stereoisomers substituted in the 1,3-position with methylthiomethyl electrode binding groups using both the scanning tunneling microscope-based break junction technique and density functional theory based ab initio calculations. In contrast with the linear ones, these cyclic silanes yield lower conductance values; calculations reveal that the constrained dihedral geometries occurring within the ring are suboptimal for σ-orbital delocalization, and therefore, conductance. Theoretical calculations reproduce the measured conductance trends for both cis and trans isomers and find several distinct conformations that are likely to form stable molecular junctions at room temperature. Due to the weakened σ-conjugation in the molecule, through-space interactions are found to contribute significantly to the conductance. This manuscript details the vast conformational flexibility in cyclopentasilanes and the tremendous impact it has on controlling conductance.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Li, Haixing","Garner, Marc H.","Shangguan, Zhichun","Zheng, Qianwen","Su, Timothy A.","Neupane, Madhav","Li, Panpan","Velian, Alexandra","Steigerwald, Michael L.","Xiao, Shengxiong","Nuckolls, Colin","Solomon, Gemma C.","Venkataraman, Latha"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-504506"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University","Shanghai Normal University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conformations of cyclopentasilane stereoisomers control molecular junction conductance","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c6sc01360k","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-504506","identifier":[{"id":"84983591629","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ba134e05-9c54-46f1-af01-51051813fd61"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-365D3EB83758A68FF226AFAB29939B0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/166006717/Li_2016_Conformations_of_cyclopentasilane.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c6sc01360k","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shanghai normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai Normal University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Haixing","key":"lihaixingpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Haixing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marc Hamilton","key":"garnermarchpau","last":"Garner","locid":"f0a76121-3afd-4e78-8c29-9a9eee1d54f4","name":"Garner, Marc H.","name_org":"Garner, Marc Hamilton","orcid":"0000-0002-7