{"abstract":"Understanding the interactions of drug molecules with biomacromolecules at a micro-scale level is essential to design potent drugs for the treatments of human genome diseases. To unravel the mechanism of binding of aristololactam-β-D-glucoside (ADG) and phenylalanine transfer RNA (tRNAPhe), an integrated computational strategy combining quantum mechanics (QM) calculation, molecular docking and atomistic molecular dynamics (MD) simulation was present in this work. QM calculations were performed to derive the partial charges of ADG, molecular docking was used to determine the binding poses of ADG on the tRNAPhe, and atomistic MD simulations were conducted to examine the thermal stability of five predicted binding poses for the complex of ADG and the tRNAPhe. The binding free energies of the five complexes were then calculated using the molecular mechanics/generalized born surface area approach with the variable internal dielectric constant model. By comparing computed affinities and experimentally-measured values in the binding free energy, we identified a most likely binding structure of ADG and the tRNAPhe. Further analysis of energy of the ADG-tRNA complex revealed that the aristololactam of ADG provides binding specificity to the tRNAPhe, and the D-glucoce contributes to the affinity for binding with the tRNAPhe.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Xiao, Xingqing","Zhao, Binwu","Yang, Li","Liang, Xiaodong","Ren, Yingqian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350461"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","East China University of Science and Technology","North Carolina State University","Wuhan Institute of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"probe the binding mode of aristololactam β d glucoside to phenylalanine transfer rna i in silico i","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85034262630","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350461","identifier":[{"id":"85034262630","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-99fc0c6f-839c-4f10-87ab-a901951cb49e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D9CB63E2B1EFF0E236E20C74061CBAB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"north carolina state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"North Carolina State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"wuhan institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CERE – Center for Energy Ressources Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"east china university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"East China University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xingqing","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Xingqing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Binwu","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Binwu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Li","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Li","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaodong","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","locid":"723584e2-cb7e-488c-a430-f85e705739b3","name":"Liang, Xiaodong","orcid":"0000-0002-2007-546X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yingqian","key":"renpau","last":"Ren","name":"Ren, Yingqian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/slct.201600603","issn":["23656549"],"issue":"17","journal":"ChemistrySelect","pages":"5430-5439","publisher":"Chemistry Europe","status":"p","title":"ChemistrySelect","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034262630"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-99fc0c6f-839c-4f10-87ab-a901951cb49e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Probe the Binding Mode of Aristololactam-β-D-glucoside to Phenylalanine Transfer RNA<i> in Silico </i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-350461","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"With the unique possibilities for controlling light in nanoscale devices, graphene plasmonics has opened new perspectives to the nanophotonics community with potential applications in metamaterials, modulators, photodetectors, and sensors. This paper briefly reviews the recent exciting progress in graphene plasmonics. We begin with a general description for optical properties of graphene, particularly focusing on the dispersion of graphene-plasmon polaritons. The dispersion relation of graphene-plasmon polaritons of spatially extended graphene is expressed in terms of the local response limit with intraband contribution. With this theoretical foundation of graphene-plasmon polaritons, we then discuss recent exciting progress, paying specific attention to the following topics: excitation of graphene plasmon polaritons, electron-phonon interactions in graphene on polar substrates, and tunable graphene plasmonics with applications in modulators and sensors. Finally, we seek to address some of the apparent challenges and promising perspectives of graphene plasmonics. [Front. Phys. 11(2), 117801 (2016) doi:10.1007/s11467-016-0551-z].","author_count":4,"contributors":["Xiao, Sanshui","Zhu, Xiaolong","Li, Bo-Hong","Mortensen, N. Asger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-370178"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["C","Collective excitations surface states","Dispersion relation","Graphene","Light control","Metamaterials","Modulators","Nanophotonic devices and technology","Nanophotonics","Nanoscale devices","Nanosensors","Optical beam modulators","Optical materials","Optical metamaterials","Optical modulation","Optical properties","Optical sensors","Photodetectors","Plasmonics","Plasmons","Polaritons","Reviews","Reviews and tutorial papers resource letters","Sensors","electron phonon interactions","graphene plasmon polaritons"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"graphene plasmon polaritons from fundamental properties to potential applications arxiv","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126596511/art_3A10.1007_2Fs11467_016_0551_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-370178","identifier":[{"id":"84957602148","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-db48c7ef-21ff-48c0-bb02-16472a68ece9"],"keyword":["C","Collective excitations (surface states)","Exchange, correlation, dielectric and magnetic functions, plasmons","Microsensors and nanosensors","Nanophotonic devices and technology","Optical beam modulators","Optical materials","Optical metamaterials","Optical properties of graphene and graphene related materials (thin films, low-dimensional and nanoscale structures)","Photodetectors","Polaritons","Reviews and tutorial papers; resource letters","Sensing and detecting devices","dispersion relation","electron-phonon interactions","graphene","graphene-plasmon polaritons","light control","metamaterials","modulators","nanophotonics","nanoscale devices","nanosensors","optical modulation","optical properties","optical sensors","plasmonics","plasmons","polar substrates","reviews","sensors","spatially extended graphene","tunable graphene plasmonics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C4BDE990C671904FC80811C9E06A295"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126596511/art_3A10.1007_2Fs11467_016_0551_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11467-016-0551-z","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu techni