y":"kraftpeterpau","last":"Kraft","name":"Kraft, Peter","rank":107,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Paul","key":"pharoahpaulpau","last":"Pharoah","name":"Pharoah, Paul","rank":108,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"40","first":"David","key":"hunterdavidpau","last":"Hunter","name":"Hunter, David","rank":109,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Douglas F","key":"eastondouglasfpau","last":"Easton","name":"Easton, Douglas F","rank":110,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wei","key":"zhengweipau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Wei","rank":111,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27551723"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pmed.1002105","issn":["15491277","15491676"],"issn_org":["15491277"],"issue":"8","journal":"PLoS Medicine","pages":"1-18","paperid":"e1002105","status":"p","title":"PLoS Medicine","title_org":"P L o S Medicine (Online)","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84988940556"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f83c46bc-e7a6-4110-ab28-f9a7b671b603"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetically Predicted Body Mass Index and Breast Cancer Risk : Mendelian Randomization Analyses of Data from 145,000 Women of European Descent","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541629","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Only two genome-wide significant loci associated with longevity have been identified so far, probably because of insufficient sample sizes of centenarians, whose genomes may harbor genetic variants associated with health and longevity. Here we report a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of Han Chinese with a sample size 2.7 times the largest previously published GWAS on centenarians. We identified 11 independent loci associated with longevity replicated in Southern-Northern regions of China, including two novel loci (rs2069837-IL6; rs2440012-ANKRD20A9P) with genome-wide significance and the rest with suggestive significance (P < 3.65 × 10 -5). Eight independent SNPs overlapped across Han Chinese, European and U.S. populations, and APOE and 5q33.3 were replicated as longevity loci. Integrated analysis indicates four pathways (starch, sucrose and xenobiotic metabolism; immune response and inflammation; MAPK; calcium signaling) highly associated with longevity (P ≤ 0.006) in Han Chinese. The association with longevity of three of these four pathways (MAPK; immunity; calcium signaling) is supported by findings in other human cohorts. Our novel finding on the association of starch, sucrose and xenobiotic metabolism pathway with longevity is consistent with the previous results from Drosophilia. This study suggests protective mechanisms including immunity and nutrient metabolism and their interactions with environmental stress play key roles in human longevity.","author_count":57,"contributors":["Zeng, Yi","Nie, Chao","Min, Junxia","Liu, Xiaomin","Li, Mengmeng","Chen, Huashuai","Xu, Hanshi","Wang, Mingbang","Ni, Ting","Li, Yang","Yan, Han","Zhang, Jin-Pei","Song, Chun","Chi, Li-Qing","Wang, Han-Ming","Dong, Jie","Zheng, Gu-Yan","Lin, Li","Qian, Feng","Qi, Yanwei","Liu, Xiao","Cao, Hongzhi","Wang, Yinghao","Zhang, Lijuan","Li, Zhaochun","Zhou, Yufeng","Wang, Yan","Lu, Jiehua","Li, Jianxin","Qi, Ming","Bolund, Lars","Yashin, Anatoliy","Land, Kenneth C","Gregory, Simon","Yang, Ze","Gottschalk, William","Tao, Wei","Wang, Jian","Wang, Jun","Xu, Xun","Bae, Harold","Nygaard, Marianne","Christiansen, Lene","Christensen, Kaare","Franceschi, Claudio","Lutz, Michael W","Gu, Jun","Tan, Qihua","Perls, Thomas","Sebastiani, Paola","Deelen, Joris","Slagboom, Eline","Hauser, Elizabeth","Xu, Huji","Tian, Xiao-Li","Yang, Huanming","Vaupel, James W"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-027828"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novel loci and pathways significantly associated with longevity","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep21243","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-027828","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4766491","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26912274","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000370792700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"84959378751","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d10befd6-52d1-4dfe-9507-609a88d1394f","ku-4bb0e175-fa11-402d-9302-465b6ecdbb8b","sdu-0bacd3b6-b646-42b9-9a61-d3defaa38950"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3146FD1644144714B8490A8377961204"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep21243","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/161732548/Novel_loci_and_pathways_significantly_associated_with_longevity.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129761742/Novel_loci_and_pathways_significantly_associated_with_longevity.pdf","ve