{"abstract":"Due to strong mode confinement, long propagation distance, and unique tunability, graphene plasmons have been widely explored in the mid-infrared and terahertz windows. However, it remains a big challenge to push graphene plasmons to shorter wavelengths to integrate graphene plasmon concepts with existing mature technologies in the near-infrared region. We investigate localized graphene plasmons supported by graphene nanodisks and experimentally demonstrate graphene plasmon working at 2 μm with the aid of a fully scalable block copolymer self-assembly method. Our results show a promising way to promote graphene plasmons for both fundamental studies and potential applications in the near-infrared window.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wang, Zhongli","Li, Tao","Almdal, Kristoffer","Mortensen, N. Asger","Xiao, Sanshui","Ndoni, Sokol"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-686150"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["cond mat mes hall","physics optics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental demonstration of graphene plasmons working close to the near infrared window","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124629571/q544_Graphene_plasmons_arxiv.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-686150","identifier":[{"id":"84995687217","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-aca05b9d-7f78-43a8-ab90-5f990335e616","sdu-4082b4f6-9270-4777-bdbc-29140b64b437"],"keyword":["cond-mat.mes-hall","physics.optics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-940B0DADE767760F9F3F0C1C934166CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128792122/q544_Graphene_plasmons_arxiv.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124629571/q544_Graphene_plasmons_arxiv.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Nanostructured Graphene","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Self-Organized Nanoporous Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Nano Optics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongli","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"e03185f1-ee58-4d68-b502-389ba3d77b3a","name":"Wang, Zhongli","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tao","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"fbb38a0d-283c-4595-ad95-9909a4c81844","name":"Li, Tao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristoffer","key":"almdalpau","last":"Almdal","locid":"f7ff938f-94fe-4584-b751-cd218de29a0c","name":"Almdal, Kristoffer","orcid":"0000-0002-5490-9303","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"N. Asger","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"85da0775-0beb-47f2-8cc6-ea4eb9fcad2d","name":"Mortensen, N. Asger","orcid":"0000-0001-7936-6264","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanshui","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"c516dded-c5eb-40a6-b2dd-37be55b893c8","name":"Xiao, Sanshui","orcid":"0000-0001-6529-5047","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sokol","key":"ndonipau","last":"Ndoni","locid":"d425701a-23e9-4d32-a6f2-d1db3114605f","name":"Ndoni, Sokol","orcid":"0000-0002-6854-1909","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1364/ol.41.005345","issn":["01469592","15394794"],"issn_org":["01469592"],"issue":"22","journal":"Optics Letters","pages":"5345-5348","publisher":"Optica Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Optics Letters","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84995687217"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-aca05b9d-7f78-43a8-ab90-5f990335e616","sdu-4082b4f6-9270-4777-bdbc-29140b64b437"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Experimental demonstration of graphene plasmons working close to the near-infrared window","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-686150","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Rural settlements form an important aspect of the urban-rural relationships because of the interactions between rural dwellers and surrounding environment. The activities in the mountainous rural settlements are restricted by a variety of natural and social factors, therefore, a scientific assessment of the spatial and temporal processes is urgent for the urbanization of these regions. For this reason, we selected Shanghang county, which is experiencing rapid urbanization, as a case study for our work. We used high-resolution remote sensing images and DEM data form the years 2004 and 2014, and extracted data on rural settlements, rivers, roads, and slope information, among others. RS, GIS, and Fragstats techniques were used to quantify the spatio-temporal variability in rural settlements. The findings of our study are as follows: (1) spatial pattern of rural settlements did not show a significant change, and these settlements were found to be mainly concentrated in the west and northeast of the Tingjiang River watershed; this was confirmed by the Voronoi model. However, nearest neighbor analysis showed different results, which is more concentrate in 2004 than 2014. (2) Ripley’s K function revealed existence of scale effect in the rural settlement pattern: settlements at a height of less than 65 km showed gathering trends; highest concentrations were found to be at heights of 35 km and 15 km in 2004 and 2014 respectively, and spatial scaling within 30km is more concentrate in 2014. (3) The slopes, river systems, and roads can significantly affect the distribution of the rural settlements. Slope of 10° is the threshold and 80% of rural settlements are spread within 10°, slope of 5° is the most important factor within 10° more than 67% of the rural settlements are distributed within the 2km buffer zone from the river system; more than 98.28% of the settlements are distributed within the 500m buffer zone of the roads, which implies that greater attention should be paid to the role of roads in the urbanization of mountainous regions in future. (4) The rural settlements located in the government township were found to have expanded 4.59 times than in the past, which is the most dramatic change area of town-village landscape in mountainous urbanization. Besides, we proposed that center town-village settlement is the most critical area, and also key development region. We expect our research to provide a methodological reference for the management and evaluation of rural settlements, and theoretical planning, and decision-making for mountainous urbanization in the future.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Yu, Zhaowu","Xiao, Li Shan","Guo, Qing Hai","He, Zhi Chao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394073"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Fujian Normal University","Key Laboratory of Urban Environment and Health","University of Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Landscape pattern"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mountain county rural settlement landscape pattern change and spatial characteristics in rapid mountain urbanization process in fujian province","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-394073","identifier":[{"id":"84973345819","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-01028b4b-c0fd-40c5-89a7-44be1e2a05d6"],"keyword":["Landscape pattern","Mountainous urbanization","Rural settlements","Spatial characteristics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F41AA482BC24D607BF2654AF0075893D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Landscape Architecture and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"key laboratory of urban environment and health","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Key Laboratory of Urban Environment and Health","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"university of chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"fujian normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fujian Normal University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3 4","first":"Zhao Wu","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","locid":"7633a5d8-eb40-4879-94c6-fa240d8d5bcd","name":"Yu, Zhaowu","name_org":"Yu, Zhao Wu","orcid":"0000-0003-4576-4541","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Li Shan","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Li Shan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Qing Hai","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Qing Hai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Zhi Chao","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Zhi Chao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5846/stxb201410302126","issn":["10000933","18722032"],"issn_org":["10000933"],"issue":"10","journal":"Shengtai Xuebao","pages":"3021-3031","status":"p","title":"Shengtai Xuebao","title_org":"Shengtai Xuebao/ Acta Ecologica Sinica","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-01028b4b-c0fd-40c5-89a7-44be1e2a05d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mountain county rural settlement landscape pattern change and spatial characteristics in rapid mountain urbanization process in Fujian province","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394073","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"To investigate large structural clonal mosaicism of chromosome X, we analysed the SNP microarray intensity data of 38,303 women from cancer genome-wide association studies (20,878 cases and 17,425 controls) and detected 124 mosaic X events >2 Mb in 97 (0.25%) women. Here we show rates for X-chromosome mosaicism are four times higher than mean autosomal rates; X mosaic events more often include the entire chromosome and participants with X events more likely harbour autosomal mosaic events. X mosaicism frequency increases with age (0.11% in 50-year olds; 0.45% in 75-year olds), as reported for Y and autosomes. Methylation array analyses of 33 women with X mosaicism indicate events preferentially involve the inactive X chromosome. Our results provide further evidence that the sex chromosomes undergo mosaic events more frequently than autosomes, which could have implications for understanding the underlying mechanisms of mosaic events and their possible contribution to risk for chronic diseases.","author_count":176,"contributors":["Machiela, Mitchell J","Zhou, Weiyin","Karlins, Eric","Sampson, Joshua N.","Freedman, Neal D","Yang, Qi","Hicks, Belynda D","Dagnall, Casey","Hautman, Christopher","Jacobs, Kevin B","Abnet, Christian C","Aldrich, Melinda C.","Amos, Christopher I","Amundadottir, Laufey T.","Arslan, Alan A.","Beane-Freeman, Laura E.","Berndt, Sonja I","Black, Amanda","Blot, William J","Bock, Cathryn H.","Bracci, Paige M.","Brinton, Louise A","Bueno-de-Mesquita, H Bas","Burdett, Laurie","Buring, Julie E","Butler, Mary Ann","Canzian, Federico","Carreón, Tania","Chaffee, Kari G.","Chang, I-Shou","Chatterjee, Nilanjan","Chen, Chu","Chen, Constance","Chen, Kexin","Chung, Charles C","Cook, Linda S","Crous Bou, Marta","Cullen, Michael","Davis, Faith G","De Vivo, Immaculata","Ding, Ti","Doherty, Jennifer","Duell, Eric J","Epstein, Caroline G.","Fan, Jin Hu","Figueroa, Jonine D","Fraumeni, Joseph F.","Friedenreich, Christine M.","Fuchs, Charles S.","Gallinger, Steven","Gao, Yu Tang","Gapstur, Susan M","García-Closas, Montserrat","Gaudet, Mia","Gaziano, J Michael","Giles, Graham","Gillanders, Elizabeth M","Giovannucci, Edward L","Goldin, Lynn","Goldstein, Alisa M","Haiman, Christopher A","Hallmans, Goran","Hankinson, Susan E","Harris, Curtis C","Henriksson, Roger","Holly, Elizabeth A.","Hong, Yun Chul","Hoover, Robert N","Hsiung, Chao A","Hu, Nan","Hu, Zhuo-Wei","Hunter, David J","Hutchinson, Amy","Jenab, Mazda","Johansen, Christoffer","Khaw, Kay-Tee","Kim, Hee Nam","Kim, Yeul Hong","Kim, Young Tae","Klein, Alison P.","Klein, Robert J","Koh, Woon-Puay","Kolonel, Laurence N","Kooperberg, Charles","Kraft, Peter","Krogh, Vittorio","Kurtz, Robert C.","LaCroix, Andrea Z","Lan, Qing","Landi, Maria Teresa","Marchand, Loic Le","Li, Donghui","Liang, Xiaolin","Liao, Linda M.","Lin, Dongxin","Liu, Jianjun","Lissowska, Jolanta","Lu, Lingeng","Magliocco, Anthony M","Malats, Núria","Matsuo, Keitaro","McNeill, Lorna H.","McWilliams, Robert R.","Melin, Beatrice S","Mirabello, Lisa","Moore, Lee","Olson, Sara H","Orlow, Irene","Park, Jae Yong","Patinõ-Garcia, Ana","Peplonska, Beata","Peters, Ulrike","Petersen, Gloria M.","Pooler, Loreall C","Prescott, Jennifer","Prokunina-Olsson, Ludmila","Purdue, Mark P.","Qiao, You Lin","Rajaraman, Preetha","Real, Francisco X.","Riboli, Elio","Risch, Harvey A","Rodríguez-Santiago, Benjamín","Ruder, Avima M","Savage, Sharon A","Schumacher, Fredrick","Schwartz, Ann G.","Schwartz, Kendra L.","Seow, Adeline","Wendy Setiawan, Veronica","Severi, Gianluca","Shen, Hongbing","Sheng, Xin","Shin, Min Ho","Shu, Xiao-Ou","Silverman, Debra T.","Spitz, Margaret R","Stevens, Victoria L","Stolzenberg-Solomon, Rachael","Stram, Daniel O","Tang, Ze Zhong","Taylor, Philip R.","Teras, Lauren R.","Tobias, Geoffrey S.","Van Den Berg, David","Visvanathan, Kala","Wacholder, Sholom","Wang, Jiu Cun","Wang, Zhaoming","Wentzensen, Nicolas","Wheeler, William","White, Emily","Wiencke, John K","Wolpin, Brian M.","Wong, Maria Pik","Wu