rst":"Huanming","key":"yanghuanmingpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Huanming","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenkarstenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","rank":41,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nanshan","key":"zhongnanshanpau","last":"Zhong","name":"Zhong, Nanshan","rank":42,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jun","key":"wangjunpau","last":"Wang","locid":"5dee6edc-2876-496f-a341-4a07933f9928","name":"Wang, Jun","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Qiang","key":"panhammarströmqiangpau","last":"Pan-Hammarström","name":"Pan-Hammarström, Qiang","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jianxing","key":"hejianxingpau","last":"He","name":"He, Jianxing","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jian","key":"wangjianpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jian","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26647728"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms10131","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"10131","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949570896"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f129bf6c-8530-48bf-803f-de7b8e0e6888"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Frequent alterations in cytoskeleton remodelling genes in primary and metastatic lung adenocarcinomas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-537336","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Development of efficient and economical electrochemical systems for water splitting is a key part of renewable energy technology. Amorphous films of tungsten sulfide have been deposited by electrochemical reduction of tetrathiotungstate ions (WS42-) on dealloyed nanoporous gold (NPG) for electrochemical hydrogen evolution reaction (HER). The electrocatalytic performance has been proved to be sensitive to the thickness of the deposited layer, with an optimal deposition time of 600 s identified. The bi-continuous nanoporous morphology of the composites has been confirmed by transmission electron microscopy (TEM), and is beneficial for high exposure of catalytic sites and electrolyte access to the electrode surface. High-resolution TEM (HRTEM) has been employed to characterize the strong adhesion between the ultrathin film (less than 1 nm) and gold skeleton, allowing rapid charge transfer and long-term stability. The measured Tafel slope of 74 mV dec (1) implies an underlying Volmer-Heyrovsky HER mechanism. (C)2015 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Xiao, Xinxin","Engelbrekt, Christian","Li, Zheshen","Si, Pengchao"],"cuid":["S03-099.64-724215"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Si, Pengchao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Key Laboratory for Liquid-Solid Structural Evolution and Processing of Materials","Shandong University"],"keyword":["EDGE SITES","Electrocatalysis","Electrocatalysts","Electrodeposition","Gold","Hydrogen evolution reaction","MoS2","Nanoparticles","Nanoporous gold","Reduced graphene oxide","Supercapacitors","Tungsten sulfide","WS2 NANOSHEETS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrogen evolution at nanoporous gold tungsten sulfide composite film and its optimization","src":["aau","au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electacta.2015.05.048","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work is sponsored by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC, No. 51301096), Shandong Provincial Natural Science Foundation (ZR2013EMQ012) and the Fundamental Research Funds of Shandong University (No. 2014JC017). The work is also financially supported by Danish Council for Independent Research Technology and Production Sciences (DEF-1335-00330) and The Danish Agency for Science, Technology and Innovation for the International Network Programme (4070-00131B). We also appreciate Prof. Yi Ding and Assoc. Prof. Jingdong Zhang for their kind support."],"id":"S03-099.64-724215","identifier":[{"id":"000356674900050","type":"wos"},{"id":"84929648727","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7add556a-63c1-4a29-89a8-ba1ede30fdaa","au-c2750eaf-0907-4cc6-bd75-72ce9a2952df","dtu-5ef16812-c955-400c-9ac0-6684fd2efa31"],"keyword":["EDGE SITES","ELECTROCATALYSTS","ELECTRODEPOSITION","GOLD","HIGHLY-ACTIVE CATALYST","MOS2","NANOPARTICLES","REDUCED GRAPHENE OXIDE","SUPERCAPACITORS","WS2 NANOSHEETS","electrocatalysis","hydrogen evolution reaction","nanoporous gold","tungsten sulfide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-D58643CF3B55CCADF139FD429E935174"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electacta.2015.05.048","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"key laboratory for liquid solid structural evolution and processing of materials","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Key Laboratory for Liquid-Solid Structural Evolution and Processing of Materials","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, NanoChemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy, Department of Physics and Astronomy - Centre for Storage Ring Facilities (ISA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"fd69114c-9434-44ba-b01b-e9ecb3831cae","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"engelbrektpau","last":"Engelbrekt","locid":"a1b586e6-3d4b-4ebc-9037-259adc94bc5a","name":"Engelbrekt, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3679-3666","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zheshen","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"063ebd9e-41f2-4dcc-a04f-3d893fbccb86","name":"Li, Zheshen","orcid":"0000-0002-8381-1620","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengchao","key":"sipau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Pengchao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.electacta.2015.05.048","issn":["00134686","18733859"],"issn_org":["00134686"],"journal":"Electrochimica Acta","pages":"393-398","paperid":"24981","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Electrochimica Acta","volume":"173"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84929648727"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7add556a-63c1-4a29-89a8-ba1ede30fdaa","au-c2750eaf-0907-4cc6-bd75-72ce9a2952df","dtu-5ef16812-c955-400c-9ac0-6684fd2efa31"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Hydrogen evolution at nanoporous gold/tungsten sulfide composite film and its optimization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.64-724215","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Studies of related individuals have consistently demonstrated notable familial aggregation of cancer. We aim to estimate the heritability and genetic correlation attributable to the additive effects of common single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) for cancer at 13 anatomical sites. METHODS: Between 2007 and 2014, the US National Cancer Institute has generated data from genome-wide association studies (GWAS) for 49 492 cancer case patients and 34 131 control patients. We apply novel mixed model methodology (GCTA) to this GWAS data to estimate the heritability of individual cancers, as well as the proportion of heritability attributable to cigarette smoking in smoking-related cancers, and the genetic correlation between pairs of cancers. RESULTS: GWAS heritability was statistically significant at nearly all sites, with the estimates of array-based heritability, hl (2), on the liability threshold (LT) scale ranging from 0.05 to 0.38. Estimating the combined heritability of multiple smoking characteristics, we calculate that at least 24% (95% confidence interval [CI] = 14% to 37%) and 7% (95% CI = 4% to 11%) of the heritability for lung and bladder cancer, respectively, can be attributed to genetic determinants of smoking. Most pairs of cancers studied did not show evidence of strong genetic correlation. We found only four pairs of cancers with marginally statistically significant correlations, specifically kidney and testes (ρ = 0.73, SE = 0.28), diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) and pediatric osteosarcoma (ρ = 0.53, SE = 0.21), DLBCL and chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) (ρ = 0.51, SE =0.18), and bladder and lung (ρ = 0.35, SE = 0.14). Correlation analysis also indicates that the genetic architecture of lung cancer differs between a smoking population of European ancestry and a nonsmoking Asian population, allowing for the possibility that the genetic etiology for the same disease can vary by population and environmental exposures. CONCLU