{"abstract":"Three-dimensional (3D) reconstruction of an organ or tissue from a stack of histologic serial sections provides valuable morphological information. The procedure includes section preparation of the organ or tissue, micrographs acquisition, image registration, 3D reconstruction, and visualization. However, the brightness and contrast through the image stack may not be consistent due to imperfections in the staining procedure, which may cause difficulties in micro-structure identification using virtual sections, region segmentation, automatic target tracing, etc. In the present study, a reference-free method, Sequential Histogram Fitting Algorithm (SHFA), is therefore developed for adjusting the severe and irregular variance of brightness and contrast within the image stack. To apply the SHFA, the gray value histograms of individual images are first calculated over the entire image stack and a set of landmark gray values are chosen. Then the histograms are transformed so that there are no abrupt changes in progressing through the stack. Finally, the pixel gray values of the original images are transformed into the desired ones based on the relationship between the original and the transformed histograms. The SHFA is tested on an image stacks from mouse kidney sections stained with toluidine blue, and captured by a slide scanner. As results, the images through the entire stack reveal homogenous brightness and consistent contrast. In addition, subtle color differences in the tissue are well preserved so that the morphological details can be recognized, even in virtual sections. In conclusion, compared with the existing histogram-based methods, the present study provides a practical method suitable for compensating brightness, and improving contrast of images derived from a large number of serial sections of biological organ.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Chang, Shi-Jie","Li, Shuo","Andreasen, Arne","Sha, Xian-Zheng","Zhai, Xiao-Yue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177829"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Medical University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a reference free method for brightness compensation and contrast enhancement of micrographs of serial sections","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0127855","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177829","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4447386","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26020531","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84932627837","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-550c4059-f597-4fb8-8534-d09a955e73f0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7B6B6D0C65D2EE5B4F0C0AFC89B87788"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0127855","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"china medical university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Medical University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Syd"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shi-Jie","key":"changpau","last":"Chang","name":"Chang, Shi-Jie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuo","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Shuo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Arne","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"e60f073e-4e38-4dfc-94b4-d92fcadd319e","name":"Andreasen, Arne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xian-Zheng","key":"shapau","last":"Sha","name":"Sha, Xian-Zheng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao-Yue","key":"zhaipau","last":"Zhai","locid":"778248b0-1401-40dc-acf7-9dbb1a955fb7","name":"Zhai, Xiao-Yue","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26020531"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0127855","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"5","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84932627837"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-550c4059-f597-4fb8-8534-d09a955e73f0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A reference-free method for brightness compensation and contrast enhancement of micrographs of serial sections","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-177829","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To observe the distribution of advanced glycation end products (AGEs) and their receptor (RAGE) in the stomach of diabetic rats. METHODS: Diabetes mellitus (DM) and control (CON) rats were reared for eight weeks. Fasting plasma glucose (FPG), glycated serum protein (GSP) and gastric layer thickness were measured. The expression of AGEs and RAGE was detected by immunohistochemical staining. RESULTS: The thickness of the mucosa (781.47 µm ± 137.82 µm vs 709.85 µm ± 169.41 µm) and submucosa (233.39 µm ± 134.05 µm vs 109.32 µm ± 44.43 µm) increased significantly in the DM group compared with the CON group (P < 0.05). The expression of AGEs and RAGE in the mucosa (5.66 ± 1.90 vs 2.25 ± 0.52, 2.79 ± 0.54 vs 1.70 ± 0.30) and muscle (37.37 ± 7.38 vs 24.32 ± 4.02, 4.26 ± 0.80 vs 3.59 ± 0.37) layers of the stomach was significantly higher in the DM group than in the CON group (P < 0.05). CONCLUSION: The expression of AGEs and RAGE is up-regulated in the stomach of diabetic rats. The increased levels of AGE and RAGE in gastric tissue may contribute to diabetic gastrointestinal dysfunction. © 2015 Baishideng Publishing Group Inc. All rights reserved. Key Words: Diabetes mellitus; Stomach; Advanced glycation end products; Receptor for advanced glycation end products","author_count":7,"contributors":["Tian, Jia Xing","Zhao, Jingbo","Li, Min","Li, Jun Ling","Cao, Yang","Gregersen, Hans","Tong, Xiao-Lin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-242406"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing University of Chemical Technology","Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","Chongqing University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"糖基化终末产物及其受体在糖尿病大鼠胃组织中的分布 distribution of advanced glycation end products and their receptor in the stomach of diabetic rats","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.wjgnet.com/1009-3079/23/2714.asp","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-242406","identifier":[{"id":"84931366219","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c60b6f80-6214-40ba-a8fe-e9c7a543c9d4"],"keyword":["Diabetes mellitus; Stomach; Advanced glycation end products; Receptor for advanced glycation end products"],"lang":"Chinese","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2729171C386BF088C079F6C785F9D951"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"beijing university of chemical technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing University of Chemical Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of medical sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"chongqing university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chongqing University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jia Xing","key":"tianjiaxingpau","last":"Tian","name":"Tian, Jia Xing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingbo","key":"zhaojingbopau","last":"Zhao","locid":"4061f83c-8088-4b35-a098-771e74594159","name":"Zhao, Jingbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"liminpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Min","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corr