{"abstract":"Human papillomavirus (HPV) integration is a key genetic event in cervical carcinogenesis1. By conducting whole-genome sequencing and high-throughput viral integration detection, we identified 3,667 HPV integration breakpoints in 26 cervical intraepithelial neoplasias, 104 cervical carcinomas and five cell lines. Beyond recalculating frequencies for the previously reported frequent integration sites POU5F1B (9.7%), FHIT (8.7%), KLF12 (7.8%), KLF5 (6.8%), LRP1B (5.8%) and LEPREL1 (4.9%), we discovered new hot spots HMGA2 (7.8%), DLG2 (4.9%) and SEMA3D (4.9%). Protein expression from FHIT and LRP1B was downregulated when HPV integrated in their introns. Protein expression from MYC and HMGA2 was elevated when HPV integrated into flanking regions. Moreover, microhomologous sequence between the human and HPV genomes was significantly enriched near integration breakpoints, indicating that fusion between viral and human DNA may have occurred by microhomology-mediated DNA repair pathways2. Our data provide insights into HPV integration-driven cervical carcinogenesis.","author_count":36,"contributors":["Hu, Zheng","Zhu, Da","Wang, Wei","Li, Weiyang","Jia, Wenlong","Zeng, Xi","Ding, Wencheng","Yu, Lan","Wang, Xiaoli","Wang, Liming","Shen, Hui","Zhang, Changlin","Liu, Hongjie","Liu, Xiao","Zhao, Yi","Fang, Xiaodong","Li, Shuaicheng","Chen, Wei","Tang, Tang","Fu, Aisi","Wang, Zou","Chen, Gang","Gao, Qinglei","Li, Shuang","Xi, Ling","Wang, Changyu","Liao, Shujie","Ma, Xiangyi","Wu, Peng","Li, Kezhen","Wang, Shixuan","Zhou, Jianfeng","Wang, Jun","Xu, Xun","Wang, Hui","Ma, Ding"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-520632"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Alphapapillomavirus","Base Sequence","Cell Line Tumor","Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia","DNA Viral","Down Regulation","Female","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Genome Human","Genome Viral","Genome Wide Association Study","Humans","Middle Aged","Molecular Sequence Data","Papillomavirus Infections","Sequence Analysis DNA","Up Regulation","Uterine Cervical Neoplasms","Virus Integration"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome wide profiling of hpv integration in cervical cancer identifies clustered genomic hot spots and a potential microhomology mediated integration mechanism","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-520632","identifier":[{"id":"25581428","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84926211535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d4e1c2b8-50c2-45c6-b39e-bf9b3e4dc928"],"keyword":["Adult","Alphapapillomavirus","Base Sequence","Cell Line, Tumor","Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia","DNA, Viral","Down-Regulation","Female","Gene Expression Profiling","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Genome, Human","Genome, Viral","Genome-Wide Association Study","Humans","Middle Aged","Molecular Sequence Data","Papillomavirus Infections","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Up-Regulation","Uterine Cervical Neoplasms","Virus Integration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-74EE8569C9F9546A3AB8798BBEC3B3DF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, NNF Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Zheng","key":"huzhengpau","last":"Hu