{"abstract":"The current study investigated the relationship between general intelligence and the three stages of facial expression processing. Two groups of adolescents with different levels of general intelligence were required to identify three types of facial expressions (happy, sad, and neutral faces), which were presented with either inverted or upright orientation. Participants' response times and accuracy were measured and event-related potentials (ERPs) were recorded to evaluate neural dynamic processes. The behavioural results showed that high IQ adolescents exhibited shorter response times than average IQ adolescents during the facial expression identification task. The electrophysiological responses showed that no significant IQ-related differences were found for P1 responses during the early visual processing stage. During the middle processing stage, high IQ adolescents had faster structural encoding of inverted faces (shorter N170 latencies) compared to their average IQ peers, and they also showed better structural encoding of sad faces, with larger vertex positive potential (VPP) amplitudes than for neutral faces. During the late processing stage, adolescents with high IQ showed better attentional modulation, with larger late positive potential (LPP) amplitudes compared to adolescents with average IQ. The current study revealed that adolescents with different intellectual levels used different neural dynamic processes during these three stages in the processing of facial expressions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Liu, Tongran","Xiao, Tong","Li, Xiaoyan","Shi, Jiannong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-050153"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Northeastern University China"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Event related potentials"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neural mechanism of facial expression perception in intellectually gifted adolescents","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neulet.2015.02.062","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-050153","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000352677900005","type":"wos"},{"id":"84924130066","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0053446e-bf2b-413e-9770-4b74a5fbca30"],"keyword":["Adolescents","Event-related potentials","Facial expression perception","﻿General intelligence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7ED9C4C1B8F500C361EF515D2A9A3E56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neulet.2015.02.062","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"northeastern university china","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeastern University China","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Confucius Institute for Innovation and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, I C Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tongran","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Tongran","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tong","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Tong","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoyan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xiaoyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiannong","key":"shipau","last":"Shi","locid":"f50bddd8-fe10-44b0-bd18-69847c92aa6a","name":"Shi, Jiannong","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.neulet.2015.02.062","issn":["01676253","03043940"],"issn_org":["03043940"],"journal":"Neuroscience Letters","pages":"22-26","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Neuroscience Letters","volume":"592"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924130066"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0053446e-bf2b-413e-9770-4b74a5fbca30"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Neural Mechanism of Facial Expression Perception in Intellectually Gifted Adolescents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-050153","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Purpose:This study demonstrates noninvasive prenatal testing (NIPT) for Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD) using a newly developed haplotype-based approach.Methods:Eight families at risk for DMD were recruited for this study. Parental haplotypes were constructed using target-region sequencing data from the parents and the probands. Fetal haplotypes were constructed using a hidden Markov model through maternal plasma DNA sequencing. The presence of haplotypes linked to the maternal mutant alleles in males indicated affected fetuses. This method was further validated by comparing the inferred single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) genotypes to the direct sequencing results of fetal genomic DNA. Prenatal diagnosis was confirmed with amniocentesis, and those results were interpreted in a blinded fashion.Results:The results showed an average accuracy of 99.98% for the total inferred maternal SNPs. With a mean depth of 30× achieved in the 10-Mb target region of each sample, the noninvasive results were consistent with those of the invasive procedure.Conclusion:This is the first report of NIPT for DMD and the first application of a haplotype-based approach in NIPT for X-linked diseases. With further improvements in accuracy, this haplotype-based strategy could be feasible for NIPT for DMD and even other X-linked single-gene disorders.Genet Med advance online publication 05 February 2015Genetics in Medicine (2015); doi:10.1038/gim.2014.207.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Xu, Yan","Li, Xuchao","Ge, Hui-Juan","Xiao, Bing","Zhang, Yan-Yan","Ying, Xiao-Min","Pan, Xiao-Yu","Wang, Lei","Xie, Wei-Wei","Ni, Lin","Chen, Sheng-Pei","Jiang, Wen-Ting","Liu, Ping","Ye, Hui","Cao, Ying","Zhang, Jing-Min","Liu, Yu","Yang, Zu-Jing","Chen, Ying-Wei","Chen, Fang","Jiang, Hui","Ji, Xing"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-413498"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"haplotype based approach for noninvasive prenatal tests of duchenne muscular dystrophy using cell free fetal dna in maternal plasma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-413498","identifier":[{"id":"84931072285","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25654318","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-218ea350-4aeb-4688-8f93-292f100b876b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C48D7C7E53FF7A1D901BBDA599B5DB63"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Molecular Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Yan","key":"xuyanpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Yan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xuchao","key":"lixuchaopau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Xuchao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hui-Juan","key":"gehuijuanpau","last":"Ge","name":"Ge, Hui-Juan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bing","key":"xiaobingpau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Bing","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yan-Yan","key":"zhangyanyanpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yan-Yan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao-Min","key":"yingxiaominpau","last":"Ying","name":"Ying, Xiao-Min","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xiao-Yu","key":"panxiaoyupau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Xiao-Yu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lei","key":"wa