{"abstract":"We established a catalog of the mouse gut metagenome comprising ∼2.6 million nonredundant genes by sequencing DNA from fecal samples of 184 mice. To secure high microbiome diversity, we used mouse strains of diverse genetic backgrounds, from different providers, kept in different housing laboratories and fed either a low-fat or high-fat diet. Similar to the human gut microbiome, >99% of the cataloged genes are bacterial. We identified 541 metagenomic species and defined a core set of 26 metagenomic species found in 95% of the mice. The mouse gut microbiome is functionally similar to its human counterpart, with 95.2% of its Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes (KEGG) orthologous groups in common. However, only 4.0% of the mouse gut microbial genes were shared (95% identity, 90% coverage) with those of the human gut microbiome. This catalog provides a useful reference for future studies.","author_count":38,"contributors":["Xiao, Liang","Feng, Qiang","Liang, Suisha","Sonne, Si Brask","Xia, Zhongkui","Qiu, Xinmin","Li, Xiaoping","Long, Hua","Zhang, Jianfeng","Zhang, Dongya","Liu, Chuan","Fang, Zhiwei","Chou, Joyce","Glanville, Jacob","Hao, Qin","Kotowska, Dorota","Colding, Camilla","Licht, Tine Rask","Wu, Donghai","Yu, Jun","Sung, Joseph Jao Yiu","Liang, Qiaoyi","Li, Junhua","Jia, Huijue","Lan, Zhou","Tremaroli, Valentina","Dworzynski, Piotr","Nielsen, Henrik Bjørn","Bäckhed, Fredrik","Doré, Joël","Le Chatelier, Emmanuelle","Ehrlich, S. Dusko","Lin, John C.","Arumugam, Manimozhiyan","Wang, Jun","Madsen, Lise","Kristiansen, Karsten"],"cuid":["S02-099.27-037112"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Hong Kong","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Chinese University of Hong Kong","King's College London","National Institute for Agronomic Research","Pfizer","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Metagenomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a catalog of the mouse gut metagenome incl author correction","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84943607837","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.27-037112","identifier":[{"id":"000362555700032","type":"wos"},{"id":"84943607837","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26414350","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-c8300b1f-fbbd-4a88-9cb0-85943c5cc06e","ku-39a2454c-b774-44ef-aad9-cc04bdc781e2"],"keyword":["Metagenomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-03D4D44A74828441AB8F3282EC601654"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"bgi group","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI Group","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"pfizer","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pfizer","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical Un