{"abstract":"A kind of dealloyed nanoporous gold (NPG)/ultrathin CuO film nanohybrid for non-enzymatic glucose sensing has been prepared by a simple, in-situ, time-saving and controllable two-step electrodeposition. The three-dimensional and bicontinuous nanoporous structure of the nanocomposites have been characterized by scanning electron microscope (SEM) and transmission electron microscopy (TEM), and the electrochemical tests have been estimated by cyclic voltammetry and single potential step chronoamperometry (SPSC). The optimal NPG/CuO electrode exhibits great electrocatalytic activity towards glucose oxidation and also shows obvious linear response to glucose up to 12 mM with a high sensitivity of 374.0 μA cm-2 mM-1 and a good detection limit of 2.8 μM (S/N=3), as well as strong tolerance against chloride poisoning and interference of ascorbic acid and uric acid.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Xiao, Xinxin","Wang, Meng'En","Li, Hui","Pan, Yichuan","Si, Pengchao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-725988"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Si, Pengchao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Key Laboratory for Liquid-Solid Structural Evolution and Processing of Materials","Shandong Jiaotong University","Shandong University"],"keyword":["Copper oxide","Glucose","Nanoporous gold"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non enzymatic glucose sensors based on controllable nanoporous gold copper oxide nanohybrids","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84898072719&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was sponsored by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC, No. 51301096 ), Shandong Provincial Natural Science Foundation ( ZR2013EMQ012 ), Project Nos. 31370056431211 and 31370070614018 ( 2010TB018 ) from Shandong University and the National 973 Program Project of China ( 2012CB932800 ). We also appreciate Prof. Yi Ding for his kind support."],"id":"S01-000.00-725988","identifier":[{"id":"84898072719","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24840458","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-8b49be85-ab7b-4cf7-8758-a36cd9d3ba9f"],"keyword":["Copper oxide","Glucose","Nanoporous gold","Non-enzymatic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AA533A9E8C44FCC2CEFDBCFD8222EAAD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Applied Supramolecular Chemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"key laboratory for liquid solid structural evolution and processing of materials","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Key Laboratory for Liquid-Solid Structural Evolution and Processing of Materials","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"shandong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"shandong jiaotong university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shandong Jiaotong University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xinxin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","locid":"fd69114c-9434-44ba-b01b-e9ecb3831cae","name":"Xiao, Xinxin","orcid":"0000-0002-0240-0038","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Meng'En","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Meng'En","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hui","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"25b7eb5d-9574-415a-a631-fd2e5d7f547f","name":"Li, Hui","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Yichuan","key":"panpau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Yichuan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pengchao","key":"sipau","last":"Si","name":"Si, Pengchao","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24840458"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.talanta.2014.03.030","issn":["00399140","18733573"],"issn_org":["00399140"],"journal":"Talanta","pages":"366-371","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Talanta","volume":"125"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8b49be85-ab7b-4cf7-8758-a36cd9d3ba9f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Non-enzymatic glucose sensors based on controllable nanoporous gold/copper oxide nanohybrids","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-725988","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Many analyses of the human gut microbiome depend on a catalog of reference genes. Existing catalogs for the human gut microbiome are based on samples from single cohorts or on reference genomes or protein sequences, which limits coverage of global microbiome diversity. Here we combined 249 newly sequenced samples of the Metagenomics of the Human Intestinal Tract (MetaHit) project with 1,018 previously sequenced samples to create a cohort from three continents that is at least threefold larger than cohorts used for previous gene catalogs. From this we established the integrated gene catalog (IGC) comprising 9,879,896 genes. The catalog includes close-to-complete sets of genes for most gut microbes, which are also of considerably higher quality than in previous catalogs. Analyses of a group of samples from Chinese and Danish individuals using the catalog revealed country-specific gut microbial signatures. This expanded catalog should facilitate quantitative characterization of metagenomic, metatranscriptomic and metaproteomic data from the gut microbiome to understand its variation across populations in human health and disease.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Li, Junhua","Jia, Huijue","Cai, Xianghang","Zhong, Huanzi","Feng, Qiang","Sunagawa, Shinichi","Arumugam, Manimozhiyan","Kultima, Jens Roat","Prifti, Edi","Nielsen, Trine","Juncker, Agnieszka","Manichanh, Chaysavanh","Chen, Bing","Zhang, Wenwei","Levenez, Florence","Wang, Juan","Xu, Xun","Xiao, Liang","Liang, Suisha","Zhang, Dongya","Zhang, Zhaoxi","Chen, Weineng","Zhao, Hailong","Al-Aama, Jumana Yousuf","Edris, Sherif","Yang, Huanming","Wang, Jian","Hansen, Torben","Nielsen, Henrik Bjørn","Brunak, Søren","Kristiansen, Karsten","Guarner, Francisco","Pedersen, Oluf","Doré, Joel","Ehrlich, S Dusko","Bork, Peer","Wang, Jun"],"cuid":["S02-089.66-037944"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","BGI Group","BGI Hong Kong Research Institute","European Molecular Biology Laboratory","European Molecular Biology Laboratory, Heidelberg","INRAE","South China University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an integrated catalog of reference genes in the human gut microbiome","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nbt.2942","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.66-037944","identifier":[{"id":"84905730165","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24997786","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-f0604914-10d7-432a-bc84-36c9b615d4ab","ku-b39d4a15-c465-428e-828b-3915444cbb14"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DC578F7062372569EF1C015A9665399B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nbt.2942","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"south china university of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"South China University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"bgi group","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI Group","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"bgi hong kong research institute","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI Hong Kong Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University 