{"abstract":"Rare genetic variants contribute to complex disease risk; however, the abundance of rare variants in human populations remains unknown. We explored this spectrum of variation by sequencing 202 genes encoding drug targets in 14,002 individuals. We find rare variants are abundant (1 every 17 bases) and geographically localized, so that even with large sample sizes, rare variant catalogs will be largely incomplete. We used the observed patterns of variation to estimate population growth parameters, the proportion of variants in a given frequency class that are putatively deleterious, and mutation rates for each gene. We conclude that because of rapid population growth and weak purifying selection, human populations harbor an abundance of rare variants, many of which are deleterious and have relevance to understanding disease risk.","author_count":31,"contributors":["Nelson, Matthew R.","Wegmann, Daniel","Ehm, Margaret G.","Kessner, Darren","St. Jean, Pamela","Verzilli, Claudio","Shen, Judong","Tang, Zhengzheng","Bacanu, Silviu-Alin","Fraser, Dana","Warren, Liling","Aponte, Jennifer","Zawistowski, Matthew","Liu, Xiao","Zhang, Hao","Zhang, Yong","Li, Jun","Li, Yun","Li, Li","Woollard, Peter","Topp, Simon","Hall, Matthew D.","Nangle, Keith","Wang, Jun","Abecasis, Goncalo","Cardon, Lon R.","Zöllner, Sebastian","Whittaker, John C.","Chissoe, Stephanie L.","Novembre, John","Mooser, Vincent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-500854"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","GlaxoSmithKline","University of California at Los Angeles","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an abundance of rare functional variants in 000000000202 drug target genes sequenced in 000000000014 000000000002 people","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1217876","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-500854","identifier":[{"id":"84863541347","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4319976","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"22604722","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b3d94547-2aba-4dbc-989e-22b827c5f3cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DDA38E6049CFCD5ECE08C526718C43F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1126/science.1217876","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1217876","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"glaxosmithkline","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"GlaxoSmithKline","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at los angeles","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Los Angeles","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of north carolina at chapel hill","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"bgi","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"BGI","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of S